[Term]
id: IAO:0000409
name: denotator type
def: "A denotator type indicates how a term should be interpreted from an ontological perspective." []
is_a: IAO:0000102 ! data about an ontology part
property_value: IAO:0000119 "Barry Smith, Werner Ceusters" xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000000
name: molecular dynamics process
def: "A sequence of related actions or operations performed to achieve a specific outcome in a biomolecular simulation study. This encompasses all stages from initial system setup and simulation execution to final data analysis and interpretation." []
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000001
name: software
def: "A set of instructions and data that a computer follows to carry out a task. In this field it covers everything from a program that runs a simulation to a small script that converts one file format into another. It is the top of the branch that every named program in this ontology sits somewhere below. (UNVERIFIED)" []

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000002
name: simulation preparation
def: "A stage of a simulation study in which the molecular system and its environment are assembled and made ready to run. It covers obtaining a structure, adding the atoms and molecules the experimental structure left out, choosing a force field, adding solvent and ions, and settling the system before data is collected. Most simulations that fail, fail here rather than later. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "preparation" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:002156 ! simulation stage

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000003
name: simulation execution
def: "The stage of a biomolecular simulation process where the main simulation runs are performed according to the prepared system and defined parameters to generate trajectory data. This phase involves propagating the system forward in time using algorithms like molecular dynamics or Monte Carlo, under specific ensemble conditions. The goal is typically to sample conformational space, observe dynamic events, or calculate specific properties like free energies." []
synonym: "execution" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:002156 ! simulation stage
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000004
name: simulation analysis
def: "A stage of a simulation study that follows the run, in which the trajectory and energy output are processed into results. It covers everything from measuring a distance to fitting a kinetic model. It is where a simulation becomes a finding rather than a large file. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "analysis" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:002156 ! simulation stage

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000005
name: protonation
def: "A specific step within the preparation process where the ionization states (presence or absence of protons) of ionizable residues (like acids, bases, histidines) and ligands are determined and assigned based on estimated pKa values relevant to the target pH of the simulation. Correct protonation is critical for accurately modeling electrostatic interactions and pH-dependent phenomena. Specialized tools are often used for this task. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000002 ! simulation preparation
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000208 ! thermalization

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000006
name: model
def: "A simplified representation used to study a real-world system, such as a molecule or collection of molecules. In biomolecular simulation, it defines the components (atoms, residues) and their properties needed for computational analysis. This framework allows scientists to simulate and predict the system's behavior. (UNVERIFIED)" []
comment: Distinct from 'MoDEL' (MOLSIM:001001), a named simulation data repository whose name differs from this term only by capitalisation. This term is the general class of representations used in simulation.

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000007
name: force field
def: "A set of mathematical functions and fitted numbers used to compute the potential energy of a system of atoms from their positions alone. It replaces the electrons of quantum mechanics with terms for bonds, angles, rotations and non-bonded contacts. Everything a classical simulation can and cannot describe follows from it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "FF" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000006 ! model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000008
name: lipid force field
def: "A force field specifically designed and parameterized for simulating lipid molecules and lipid bilayers, crucial components of cell membranes. It aims to accurately capture the unique properties of lipids, including their phase behavior and interactions with other molecules. Examples include LIPID14, LIPID17, and parameters within general force fields like CHARMM36m. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000772 ! chemical entity-based force field
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000009
name: protein force field
def: "A force field specifically designed and parameterized for simulating proteins and peptides, focusing on accurately representing amino acid properties and polypeptide chain behavior. These are crucial for studying protein folding, dynamics, and interactions. Many different protein force fields exist, often differing in their parameterization philosophy and target data. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000772 ! chemical entity-based force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000010
name: DNA force field
def: "A force field specifically developed and parameterized for simulating Deoxyribonucleic Acid (DNA) molecules. It focuses on accurately representing the structure, dynamics, and interactions of DNA bases, sugars, and phosphate backbone, including features like sugar pucker and helical parameters. Accurate DNA force fields are essential for studying DNA replication, transcription, and drug binding." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000772 ! chemical entity-based force field
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000011
name: RNA force field
def: "A force field specifically developed and parameterized for simulating Ribonucleic Acid (RNA) molecules. It aims to accurately capture the complex conformational landscape and catalytic potential of RNA. Development often focuses on improving descriptions of sugar pucker, backbone torsions (especially the epsilon and zeta angles), and non-canonical base interactions." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000772 ! chemical entity-based force field
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000012
name: carbohydrates force field
def: "A force field specifically designed and parameterized for simulating carbohydrate molecules (sugars or glycans). It addresses the unique challenges of modeling the flexibility of glycosidic linkages between sugar units and the numerous hydrogen bonding possibilities involving hydroxyl groups. These are important for studying glycoproteins, glycolipids, and polysaccharides like cellulose." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000772 ! chemical entity-based force field
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000013
name: organic molecule force field
def: "A force field parameterised for small organic molecules, covering the wide range of chemistry found in drug-like compounds. It must handle groups no protein or nucleic acid force field was built for. It is used together with a biomolecular force field when a ligand is simulated in a protein. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000772 ! chemical entity-based force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000014
name: water model force field
def: "A force field parameterised for water alone, usually representing a molecule by 3 to 5 interaction points with fixed geometry. Water is most of the atoms in a biomolecular simulation, so the choice affects cost as much as accuracy. No model reproduces every measured property of water, so the choice depends on which properties matter for the study. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000772 ! chemical entity-based force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000015
name: ion force field
def: "A set of parameters specifically developed to describe the interactions of ions (charged atoms or small molecules) within a simulation, typically in conjunction with a specific water model and other biomolecular force fields. These parameters define the ion's charge and non-bonded terms (usually Lennard-Jones parameters for size and interaction strength). Accurate ion parameters are crucial for modeling salt effects, ion channels, and metalloproteins, and often require careful tuning for compatibility with the chosen water model. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000772 ! chemical entity-based force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000016
name: general purpose organic force field
def: "An organic molecule force field designed to give parameters for almost any organic structure, including ones never tested during its development. It achieves that breadth by defining atom types broadly and supplying rules to fill gaps. The parameters it produces are therefore approximate, and are checked rather than trusted for any specific molecule. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "other organic molecules force field" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000772 ! chemical entity-based force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000017
name: minimal basis set
def: "A basis set holding only enough functions to accommodate an atom's electrons in its ground state, with none to spare. Having no spare functions means the electron cloud cannot change shape when a bond forms, so bonding is described poorly. It is used for teaching and for very rough calculations, not for results. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "minimal" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000432 ! quantum mechanics basis set
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000018
name: lipid21
def: "A specific version of a lipid force field, part of the AMBER family, providing parameters optimized for simulating lipids. Released around 2021, it incorporates updates and refinements based on contemporary data and methodologies to improve accuracy in membrane simulations. Its name indicates the originating group (AMBER) and year of major update. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000008 ! lipid force field
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000019 ! lipid14

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000019
name: lipid14
def: "A specific lipid force field parameter set developed for the AMBER simulation package, released around 2014. It provides parameters optimized for simulating a range of common lipid types found in biological membranes. This version aimed to improve upon previous lipid models within the AMBER family. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000008 ! lipid force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000020
name: lipid17
def: "A specific lipid force field parameter set developed for the AMBER simulation package, released around 2017. It was built upon the modularity of LIPID14 and provided an extension of modular phospholipid residues to include anionic head groups and polyunsaturated tails." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000008 ! lipid force field
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000021
name: AMBER ff14SB
def: "A specific protein force field parameter set from the AMBER family (ff), released around 2014, with optimizations primarily for side-chain (S) and backbone (B) torsion angles compared to earlier versions like ff99SB. It was widely adopted for its improved accuracy in representing protein secondary structure and dynamics. It is an all-atom force field." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000132 ! CHARMM36
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000132 ! CHARMM36
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000022
name: TIP3P
def: "A rigid water model with 3 interaction sites, one on each atom, using the measured geometry of an isolated water molecule. It is the cheapest widely used model and the one the AMBER and CHARMM force fields were fitted alongside. It reproduces density well and diffuses about twice as fast as real water, which matters for any rate taken from a simulation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000014 ! water model force field
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000763 ! TIP4P
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000763 ! TIP4P

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000023
name: general AMBER force field
def: "A force field for small organic molecules, built to be used alongside the AMBER protein and nucleic acid parameters. It defines atom types broadly enough to cover almost any organic structure, and supplies rules for filling gaps where no parameter was fitted. That breadth is why its parameters for any particular molecule should be checked rather than trusted. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "GAFF" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000016 ! general purpose organic force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000024
name: general AMBER force field 2
def: "A force field for small organic molecules, refitting the original general AMBER parameters against a larger set of quantum calculations and measurements. It improves the description of rotations and of van der Waals interactions in particular. It is not interchangeable with the first version, so which one was used must be recorded. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "GAFF2" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000016 ! general purpose organic force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000025
name: mol3 format
def: "A text-based molecular structure format, similar to the mol2 format, but designed to include additional records for atomic connectivity. It is used to represent chemical structures with an expanded description of their bonding topology. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001088 ! molecular structure format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000097 ! NetCDF trajectory format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000319 ! standard xyz format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000026
name: analysis method
def: "A method for processing the data a simulation produces and extracting something meaningful from it. It turns a trajectory, which is a list of coordinates at successive times, into a quantity that can be compared with an experiment or with another simulation. Almost nothing useful comes out of a simulation without one. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000140 ! computational method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000027
name: reaction analysis
def: "A specific type of analysis method focused on understanding how chemical reactions occur within the simulated molecular system. It involves characterizing the pathways, transition states, and energy changes associated with the transformation of reactants into products. This helps elucidate reaction mechanisms and kinetics at the molecular level." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000026 ! analysis method
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000028
name: coordinate analysis
def: "A subset of reaction analysis that uses the positions (coordinates) of atoms to describe the progress of a chemical reaction or conformational change. It defines one or more geometric variables, collectively known as reaction coordinates, to map the transition pathway between different molecular states. This analysis helps visualize and quantify the structural changes during a reaction. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000027 ! reaction analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000029
name: direct reaction coordinate analysis
def: "A type of coordinate analysis where the reaction progress is described using simple, intuitive geometric parameters like bond distances, angles, or dihedrals directly involved in the transformation. This provides a straightforward way to monitor specific structural changes assumed to be representative of the reaction pathway." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000028 ! coordinate analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000030
name: obsolete water type
def: "OBSOLETE. Refers to specific parameterizations or types of water models commonly used in biomolecular simulations, often used somewhat interchangeably with 'water model'. Each 'water type' (e.g., SPC, TIP3P, TIP4P-Ew) defines the geometry, number of interaction sites, and associated parameters (charges, Lennard-Jones) for representing water molecules. The choice significantly influences simulation outcomes, particularly solvation effects and dynamics." []
comment: Retired 2026-08-24. Its own definition described it as 'often used somewhat interchangeably with water model', and that is what it was: a second home for water models alongside MOLSIM:000014 water model force field, which holds all 18. Its two children were re-parented rather than replaced, so there is no single successor. MOLSIM:000031 optimal point charges moved to MOLSIM:000014 beside OPC3, and MOLSIM:000476 TIP3P water model was retired as a duplicate of MOLSIM:000022 TIP3P.
is_obsolete: true

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000031
name: OPC
def: "A rigid four-site water model whose partial charges and geometry were optimised together to reproduce bulk properties of liquid water, including the density, the heat of vaporisation and the dielectric constant. It reproduces several of those properties more closely than the older three-site and four-site models at a similar computational cost. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "optimal point charges" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000014 ! water model force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000032
name: box type
def: "Specifies the geometric shape of the simulation cell used under periodic boundary conditions (PBCs), which replicate the central simulation system in three dimensions to mimic a bulk environment and avoid surface effects. The choice of shape (e.g., cubic, truncated octahedron, rhombic dodecahedron) affects the computational efficiency (volume of solvent needed) and how well the unit cell packs space. It determines the distance and geometry for interactions between a particle and its periodic images." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000006 ! model
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000033
name: rhombic dodecahedron
def: "A specific type of simulation box shape corresponding to a dodecahedron with rhombus-shaped faces. It is one of the space-filling polyhedra that is closer to a sphere than a cube, thus often requiring less solvent volume (and fewer solvent molecules) to solvate a roughly spherical solute while maintaining a minimum distance to the periodic images. It can offer computational savings compared to a cubic box of similar minimum image distance." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000032 ! box type
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000034 ! truncated octahedron
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000034
name: truncated octahedron
def: "A specific type of simulation box shape created by cutting off the corners of an octahedron. Like the rhombic dodecahedron, it is a space-filling polyhedron that approximates a sphere more closely than a cube, reducing the required solvent volume for solvating non-cubic solutes under periodic boundary conditions. It offers similar computational efficiency benefits as the rhombic dodecahedron for many systems." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000032 ! box type
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000035
name: hexagonal prism
def: "A simulation box shape consisting of a hexagonal base extruded along a perpendicular axis. This shape is sometimes used for systems with inherent one-dimensional periodicity or symmetry, such as fibers (like DNA) or layered systems, where periodic boundary conditions are naturally applied across the hexagonal faces and along the prism axis. Its use is less common than cubic or truncated octahedral boxes for general globular protein simulations." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000032 ! box type
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000036
name: rectangular/cubic
def: "The simplest simulation box shape, defined by three mutually perpendicular axes (orthogonal box). If all edge lengths are equal, it is cubic; otherwise, it is rectangular (also called orthorhombic or cuboid). While straightforward to implement and visualize, cubic boxes can be inefficient for solvating non-cubic solutes, often requiring significantly more solvent molecules than more spherically approximating shapes like the truncated octahedron to achieve the same minimum distance between periodic images." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000032 ! box type
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000037
name: algorithm
def: "A well-defined sequence of steps or rules designed to perform a specific task or solve a particular problem. In computational science, algorithms provide the precise instructions for a computer to follow to achieve a desired outcome, such as simulating molecular motion or analyzing data. They are the fundamental building blocks of computational methods used in biomolecular simulation and analysis. (UNVERIFIED)" []

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000038
name: thermostat algorithm
def: "An algorithm used in molecular dynamics simulations to control the temperature of the simulated system, ensuring it samples configurations corresponding to a specific target temperature (e.g., for the NVT or NPT ensembles). Thermostats work by adjusting particle velocities or adding/removing kinetic energy in various ways to mimic coupling with an external heat bath. Different thermostat algorithms vary in their theoretical basis, efficiency, and how accurately they reproduce correct statistical mechanics. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000382 ! simulation control algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000039 ! barostat algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000039 ! barostat algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000039
name: barostat algorithm
def: "An algorithm used in molecular dynamics simulations, typically alongside a thermostat, to control the pressure of the simulated system by adjusting the simulation box volume. This allows simulations to be performed under conditions of constant pressure and temperature (NPT ensemble), mimicking typical laboratory conditions. Different barostats vary in how they couple the volume changes to the pressure difference and whether they allow anisotropic box changes. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000382 ! simulation control algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000040
name: Berendsen barostat
def: "A barostat algorithm that weakly couples the system to an external pressure bath by rescaling the simulation box volume and particle coordinates based on the difference between the current instantaneous pressure and the target pressure. Similar to the Berendsen thermostat, it is computationally simple and effective for equilibration but does not rigorously sample the correct NPT ensemble. It allows isotropic or anisotropic pressure coupling. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000039 ! barostat algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000041 ! Monte Carlo barostat
property_value: MOLSIM:002254 "barostat=1" xsd:string {dcterms:source="MOLSIM:000217"}
property_value: MOLSIM:002254 "pcoupl=Berendsen" xsd:string {dcterms:source="MOLSIM:000247"}

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000041
name: Monte Carlo barostat
def: "A barostat algorithm where trial changes to the simulation box volume are attempted periodically during a molecular dynamics simulation using a Monte Carlo acceptance criterion. Accepted moves rescale the box dimensions and particle coordinates. This method correctly samples the NPT ensemble but can be less efficient than continuous barostats for large volume fluctuations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000039 ! barostat algorithm
property_value: MOLSIM:002254 "barostat=2" xsd:string {dcterms:source="MOLSIM:000217"}

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000042
name: Andersen barostat
def: "A barostat algorithm where the simulation box volume is treated as a dynamic variable coupled to a fictitious \"piston\" mass, interacting with the internal pressure of the system. This extended Lagrangian approach allows the volume to fluctuate dynamically around the value corresponding to the target external pressure, correctly generating the NPT ensemble. It typically assumes isotropic volume changes. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000039 ! barostat algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000043
name: Parrinello-Rahman barostat
def: "An extension of the Andersen barostat that allows the simulation box shape and volume to change anisotropically, meaning the lengths of the box edges and the angles between them can fluctuate independently. This is crucial for simulating phase transitions or studying materials under anisotropic stress conditions while correctly sampling the NPT ensemble. It uses a matrix of barostat variables coupled to the pressure tensor. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000039 ! barostat algorithm
property_value: MOLSIM:002254 "pcoupl=Parrinello-Rahman" xsd:string {dcterms:source="MOLSIM:000247"}

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000044
name: Langevin-piston barostat
def: "A barostat algorithm that combines the extended Lagrangian approach (like Andersen or Parrinello-Rahman) with Langevin dynamics applied to the piston/box degrees of freedom. This introduces stochastic and frictional terms to the equation of motion for the box volume, helping to control pressure fluctuations and potentially improving sampling efficiency. It aims to provide robust pressure control while correctly sampling the NPT ensemble. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000039 ! barostat algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000045
name: Langevin thermostat
def: "A Langevin thermostat is a widely used algorithm in molecular dynamics simulations that maintains a constant temperature by mimicking a solvent environment. It modifies Newton's equations of motion by adding two forces to each particle: a frictional drag force that removes kinetic energy, and a random, stochastic force that adds kinetic energy." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000038 ! thermostat algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000046 ! Berendsen thermostat
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000046 ! Berendsen thermostat
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986
property_value: MOLSIM:002254 "ntt=3" xsd:string {dcterms:source="MOLSIM:000217"}

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000046
name: Berendsen thermostat
def: "A thermostat algorithm that weakly couples the system to an external heat bath by rescaling particle velocities at each step based on the difference between the current instantaneous temperature and the target temperature. While computationally simple and effective at bringing the system to the target temperature, it does not rigorously generate configurations from the correct canonical (NVT) ensemble. It is often used for equilibration phases rather than production simulations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000038 ! thermostat algorithm
property_value: MOLSIM:002254 "ntt=1" xsd:string {dcterms:source="MOLSIM:000217"}
property_value: MOLSIM:002254 "tcoupl=berendsen" xsd:string {dcterms:source="MOLSIM:000247"}

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000047
name: Andersen thermostat
def: "A thermostat algorithm that maintains temperature by introducing stochastic collisions between randomly selected particles and fictitious heat bath particles. When a particle \"collides,\" its velocity is reassigned from a Maxwell-Boltzmann distribution corresponding to the target temperature. This method correctly generates configurations from the canonical (NVT) ensemble. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000038 ! thermostat algorithm
property_value: MOLSIM:002254 "ntt=2" xsd:string {dcterms:source="MOLSIM:000217"}
property_value: MOLSIM:002254 "tcoupl=andersen" xsd:string {dcterms:source="MOLSIM:000247"}

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000048
name: Nosé-Hoover thermostat
def: "A deterministic thermostat algorithm that controls temperature by introducing an extended degree of freedom (a thermostat variable) that dynamically couples to the physical system's kinetic energy. This extended variable evolves according to its own equation of motion, causing the physical system's temperature to fluctuate around the target value in a way consistent with the canonical (NVT) ensemble. It avoids the stochastic elements of Langevin or Andersen thermostats. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "Nose-Hoover" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000038 ! thermostat algorithm
property_value: MOLSIM:002254 "tcoupl=nose-hoover" xsd:string {dcterms:source="MOLSIM:000247"}

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000049
name: constraint algorithm
def: "An algorithm used in molecular dynamics simulations to fix certain geometric parameters, most commonly bond lengths involving light atoms like hydrogen. By constraining these fast vibrations, longer simulation time steps can be used, significantly speeding up the simulation while having minimal impact on slower, large-scale motions. These algorithms iteratively adjust particle positions or use analytical solutions to satisfy the constraint conditions. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000037 ! algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000074 ! similarity calculation algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000050
name: SHAKE algorithm
def: "An iterative constraint algorithm widely used in molecular dynamics to fix bond lengths. It adjusts the positions of atoms involved in a constraint at the end of a time step until the constraint condition (e.g., fixed bond distance) is satisfied within a defined tolerance. It handles coupled constraints involving multiple atoms connected together. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000049 ! constraint algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000051 ! RATTLE algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000051
name: RATTLE algorithm
def: "A constraint algorithm similar to SHAKE but designed for velocity-Verlet type integrators, ensuring that both positions and velocities satisfy the constraint conditions at the end of each time step. It involves solving constraint equations for positions first, then using those positions to solve for constrained velocities. This maintains consistency between positions and velocities under constraint. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000049 ! constraint algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000052
name: LINCS algorithm
def: "A constraint algorithm that holds bond lengths fixed by correcting the positions after each integration step, solving the constraint equations directly rather than by repeated adjustment. Being non-iterative makes it fast and makes its cost predictable. It is the constraint algorithm GROMACS uses by default. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "LINCS" EXACT []
synonym: "linear constraint solver algorithm" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000049 ! constraint algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000053
name: electrostatic interaction algorithm
def: "An algorithm designed to efficiently calculate the long-range electrostatic forces between charged particles (atoms) in molecular simulations, which is computationally demanding due to the N-squared complexity if all pairs are considered directly. These methods employ various approximations or techniques like grid-based calculations, truncation schemes, or multipole expansions to reduce the computational cost while maintaining acceptable accuracy. They are essential for simulating realistic biomolecular systems. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000384 ! force calculation algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001724 ! Treecode algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000054
name: particle mesh Ewald
def: "A highly efficient grid-based algorithm for calculating long-range electrostatic interactions in periodic systems, based on the Ewald summation technique. It splits the calculation into a short-range part computed directly in real space and a long-range part computed efficiently in reciprocal space using Fast Fourier Transforms (FFTs) on a grid. PME is a standard method for accurate electrostatics in biomolecular simulations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "PME" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000428 ! Ewald summation

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000055
name: reaction field
def: "An approximate method for handling long-range electrostatic interactions where direct interactions are calculated only up to a certain cutoff distance. The effect of charges beyond the cutoff is approximated by embedding the cutoff sphere within a continuous dielectric medium representing the solvent. While computationally cheaper than PME, its accuracy depends on the system and parameters chosen. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "RF" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000053 ! electrostatic interaction algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000056 ! particle-particle particle-mesh

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000056
name: particle-particle particle-mesh
def: "An efficient algorithm for calculating long-range forces (like electrostatic or gravitational) in particle simulations, conceptually similar to Particle Mesh Ewald (PME). It splits the force calculation into a short-range part computed directly between nearby particles (particle-particle) and a long-range part computed using a grid and Fast Fourier Transforms (particle-mesh). PPPM is widely used in both astrophysics and molecular simulation for its performance and accuracy. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "P3M" EXACT []
synonym: "PPPM" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000053 ! electrostatic interaction algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000057
name: interaction type
def: "Refers to the classification of forces or potential energy contributions that describe how particles (atoms, ions, coarse-grained beads) affect each other within a simulation's model or force field. These types determine the structure, dynamics, and thermodynamics of the simulated system according to the chosen model." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000006 ! model
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000058
name: long range interaction
def: "An interaction between particles where the force or potential energy diminishes slowly with increasing distance, typically decaying as r^−n where n≤3 (e.g., electrostatic interactions decaying as 1/r). Because their influence extends significantly far, these interactions necessitate special computational techniques (like Particle Mesh Ewald (PME) or Ewald sums) in simulations using periodic boundary conditions to accurately account for contributions beyond a simple distance cutoff. They are crucial for the behavior of charged or polar molecules in condensed phases. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000057 ! interaction type
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000059 ! short range interaction

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000059
name: short range interaction
def: "An interaction between particles where the force or potential energy decreases rapidly with increasing distance, becoming negligible beyond a certain range (typically a few molecular diameters). Van der Waals interactions (often modeled with Lennard-Jones potentials decaying as 1/(r^6) for attraction) are the primary example. These interactions can often be computationally truncated using a cutoff radius in simulations without significant loss of accuracy, improving efficiency. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000057 ! interaction type

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000060
name: specific interaction
def: "An interaction whose strength and occurrence depend critically on the specific chemical identities, geometries, and relative orientations of the interacting partners. These often involve directional components and chemical complementarity, such as hydrogen bonds, salt bridges (ionic interactions), or π-stacking, playing key roles in molecular recognition, binding specificity, and defined structural motifs. They contrast with more general, less directional interactions like isotropic Van der Waals forces. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000057 ! interaction type

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000061
name: non specific interaction energy
def: "An interaction energy arising from forces that depend little on the chemical identity or the orientation of the groups involved, chiefly dispersion attraction and excluded-volume repulsion. These forces act between almost any pair of atoms, so they set overall cohesion and packing rather than specific recognition. They are what drives the hydrophobic effect. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000057 ! interaction type

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000062
name: non-covalent interaction
def: "An interaction between atoms, ions, or molecules that does not involve the sharing of valence electrons to form a covalent bond. These interactions, including Van der Waals forces, electrostatic interactions (encompassing hydrogen bonds, salt bridges, dipole interactions), π-effects, and hydrophobic effects, govern molecular recognition, self-assembly, folding, and the stability of biomolecular complexes. Though individually weaker than covalent bonds (typically 0.1-10 kcal/mol vs >50 kcal/mol), their cumulative effect is critical for biological structure and function. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000057 ! interaction type

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000063
name: covalent interaction
def: "An interaction in which atoms share valence electrons, forming the bonds that hold a molecule together. It is far stronger than any non-bonded interaction, which is why bonds do not break at ordinary temperatures. A classical force field represents it as a fixed connection rather than describing the sharing. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000057 ! interaction type
property_value: skos:closeMatch NCIT:C41573

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000064
name: Van der Waals interaction
def: "A short-range non-covalent interaction between atoms or molecules arising from temporary fluctuations in electron distribution causing transient dipoles (London dispersion forces) and interactions involving permanent or induced multipoles, counteracted by strong short-range repulsion due to overlapping electron clouds (Pauli exclusion principle). Commonly modeled using potentials like the Lennard-Jones 6-12 potential. These interactions determine molecular size, shape, packing efficiency, and contribute to binding affinity. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000062 ! non-covalent interaction

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000065
name: solvation model
def: "A model that represents the effect of the surrounding solvent on a solute in a simulation. It may include individual solvent molecules explicitly, or replace them with a continuous medium carrying averaged properties. The choice sets both the cost of the simulation and which solvent effects can appear in the result. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000006 ! model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000066
name: explicit solvent model
def: "A solvation model where individual solvent molecules (e.g., water molecules represented by a specific water model like TIP3P or SPC/E) are explicitly included in the simulation system alongside the solute molecule(s). This approach provides the most detailed, atomistic representation of solute-solvent interactions, capturing specific hydrogen bonding patterns, local solvent structure, and dynamic effects. However, it significantly increases the system size and computational expense due to the large number of solvent particles that must be simulated. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000065 ! solvation model
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000068 ! implicit solvent model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000067
name: obsolete water model
def: "OBSOLETE. Within the context of solvation models, this typically refers to the use of an explicit solvent model where the solvent is specifically water, represented using a particular force field parameter set (e.g., TIP3P, SPC/E, TIP4P-Ew). This distinguishes it from implicit solvation approaches or explicit simulations using non-aqueous solvents. The term emphasizes that water molecules are being directly simulated using a chosen set of parameters defining their interactions." []
comment: Retired 2026-08-24. It named a water model but held none: all 18 sit under MOLSIM:000014 water model force field, which its own definition pointed at by naming TIP3P, SPC/E and TIP4P-Ew as the parameter sets involved. The distinction it was reaching for, explicit solvation with water specifically, is already carried by MOLSIM:000066 explicit solvent model, whose definition names the same models. It was also asserted disjoint from MOLSIM:000066, which was wrong, since explicit water is a kind of explicit solvent rather than something separate from it.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: MOLSIM:000014

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000068
name: implicit solvent model
def: "A solvation model that approximates the average effect of the solvent environment without explicitly representing individual solvent molecules. Instead, the solvent is treated as a continuous medium characterized by macroscopic properties, primarily its dielectric constant (ϵ) to account for electrostatic screening, and sometimes surface tension to account for nonpolar effects like cavity formation. Common examples include Generalized Born (GB) models and methods based on solving the Poisson-Boltzmann (PB) equation, often combined with a surface area term (SASA); these significantly reduce computational cost compared to explicit solvent. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000065 ! solvation model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000069
name: hybrid solvent model
def: "A solvation modeling approach that combines elements of both explicit and implicit solvent representations within the same simulation. Typically, a limited number of explicit solvent molecules are retained in a specific region of interest deemed critical (e.g., the active site of an enzyme, the first solvation shell around a solute), while the bulk solvent further away is represented using an implicit continuum model. This strategy aims to capture detailed local solvent effects accurately while maintaining computational efficiency by treating the less critical bulk solvent implicitly. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000065 ! solvation model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000070
name: coarse grained solvent model
def: "A solvent model designed for compatibility with coarse-grained (CG) solute force fields, where the solvent representation is also simplified to match the reduced resolution of the solute. This can involve explicit CG solvent particles where each particle represents multiple (e.g., 3-4) real water molecules (like MARTINI water), or implicit CG solvent models that adapt continuum concepts to the coarse-grained scale. These models drastically reduce the number of degrees of freedom associated with the solvent, enabling simulations of very large systems or very long timescales. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000065 ! solvation model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000071
name: machine learning solvent model
def: "An emerging class of solvation models where the complex relationship between a solute's structure/properties and its solvation free energy (or related solvent effects) is learned using machine learning (ML) algorithms. These algorithms are trained on large datasets generated from high-fidelity sources like explicit solvent simulations, quantum mechanical calculations, or experimental data. ML solvent models aim to achieve high accuracy approaching that of the training data but at a significantly reduced computational cost, potentially bridging the gap between fast implicit models and expensive explicit models. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000065 ! solvation model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000072
name: quantum mechanical solvent model
def: "A solvation model where the electronic structure of the solvent, or its interaction with the solute, is treated using quantum mechanics (QM). This can range from embedding a QM description of the solute within a classical solvent model (either implicit or explicit) using QM/MM techniques, to treating a number of explicit solvent molecules quantum mechanically along with the solute, or using implicit solvent models derived from QM principles (like the SMD model). These models capture electronic polarization, charge transfer, and other quantum effects involving the solvent, providing high accuracy but at a very high computational cost, reserved for specific problems like chemical reactions in solution. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000065 ! solvation model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000073
name: generalized Born
def: "A specific type of implicit solvent model that provides an analytical approximation to the electrostatic component of the solvation free energy, based on the Born model for solvation of a spherical ion. It calculates effective Born radii for each atom in the solute, representing the degree of solvent exposure, and uses these radii in a formula that approximates the electrostatic polarization energy typically calculated by solving the more complex Poisson-Boltzmann equation. GB models are computationally much faster than PB methods, making them popular for applications like MD simulations or energy minimization, often paired with a surface area term (GBSA). (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "GB" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000068 ! implicit solvent model
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000270 ! Poisson-Boltzmann surface area
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000270 ! Poisson-Boltzmann surface area

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000074
name: similarity calculation algorithm
def: "An algorithm used to quantify the degree of resemblance between two objects, often molecules represented by chemical fingerprints or structural features, or between simulation data like conformations or trajectories. These methods employ various mathematical formulas (metrics or coefficients) to compute a numerical score indicating similarity or distance. They are widely used in cheminformatics, drug discovery, and simulation analysis. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000037 ! algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000075
name: Tanimoto similarity algorithm
def: "An algorithm that measures how similar 2 molecules are by comparing the sets of features each carries, as the number of features they share divided by the number either one has. The result runs from 0 for no shared features to 1 for identical sets. It is the standard measure used with molecular fingerprints, where the features are substructures present in the molecule. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000074 ! similarity calculation algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000076 ! Tversky index algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000076
name: Tversky index algorithm
def: "A molecular similarity measure that compares two molecular structures by calculating their overlap while allowing asymmetric weighting through parameters α and β. The measure ranges from 0 (completely different) to 1 (identical), and can be adjusted to emphasize either the reference or query molecule in the comparison. It is particularly useful in molecular screening as it can identify both substructure and superstructure relationships between molecules. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000074 ! similarity calculation algorithm
property_value: IAO:0000116 "General form, for reference: T(A,B) = |A n B| / (alpha*|A - B| + beta*|B - A| + |A n B|), where A and B are the feature sets of the two molecules being compared. alpha weights features unique to A (the reference) and beta weights features unique to B (the query or fit molecule); alpha = beta = 1 reduces to the Tanimoto coefficient, and alpha = beta = 0.5 gives the Dice coefficient. The named variants below differ only in their fixed alpha/beta values, which each of their definitions states. Note this text is a plain-string note: no OWL consumer renders mathematical notation, so it is written to be readable as-is rather than as LaTeX. Requested in GitHub issue #1." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000077
name: Dice coefficient algorithm
def: "A similarity calculation method used to compare two sets (e.g., features in molecular fingerprints), closely related to the Tanimoto coefficient and Jaccard index. It measures the overlap between the sets, normalized by the average size of the two sets. It is often used in information retrieval and cheminformatics as an alternative similarity metric. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000074 ! similarity calculation algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000078
name: Euclidean distance
def: "A type of statistical property representing the straight-line distance between two points in a multi-dimensional space, which may represent molecules in a property space or conformations by atom coordinates. It is calculated as the square root of the sum of squared differences between corresponding coordinates or features. Lower Euclidean distance implies higher similarity in the context of the chosen space. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001403 ! statistical property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000079
name: Manhattan distance
def: "A type of statistical property representing the distance between two points in a multi-dimensional space, calculated as the sum of the absolute differences of their coordinates. The Manhattan distance is an alternative to the Euclidean distance for measuring similarity in clustering and data analysis. This is also known as the city block distance. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001403 ! statistical property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000080
name: distance
def: "A type of `structural property` that represents the separation between two specified atoms or centers of mass. It is a fundamental geometric measure used to monitor interactions like hydrogen bonds, salt bridges, or the separation between molecular components. Analysis outputs frequently report `distance` values over time. This value is commonly referred to as `dist` in analysis scripts. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000001 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label length unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000081
name: Hamming distance algorithm
def: "A similarity calculation method specifically used for comparing two strings or bit vectors (like binary molecular fingerprints) of equal length. It counts the number of positions at which the corresponding symbols or bits are different. A lower Hamming distance indicates higher similarity between the binary representations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000074 ! similarity calculation algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000082
name: Jaccard index algorithm
def: "A similarity calculation method used for comparing two sets, defined as the size of the intersection divided by the size of the union of the sets. It is identical to the Tanimoto coefficient when applied to binary data (like molecular fingerprints). It provides a normalized measure of overlap between feature sets, ranging from 0 (no overlap) to 1 (identical sets). (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000074 ! similarity calculation algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000083
name: overlap coefficient algorithm
def: "A similarity calculation method that measures the overlap between two sets, defined as the size of the intersection divided by the size of the smaller of the two sets. Unlike Tanimoto/Jaccard, it reaches 1 if one set is a subset of the other. It is useful for assessing containment or sub-structure relationships. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000074 ! similarity calculation algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000084
name: fit Tversky combo
def: "A comprehensive molecular similarity measure that combines FitTversky shape matching with FitColorTversky chemical feature matching into a single metric. This measure emphasizes the database (fit) molecule's characteristics through its high β parameter value (0.95), making it particularly useful for identifying compounds where the query molecule is a substructure of database molecules. Like RefTverskyCombo, it produces scores typically ranging from 0 to 2, providing a balanced assessment of both geometric shape and chemical functionality similarities. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000076 ! Tversky index algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000085 ! ref Tversky

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000085
name: ref Tversky
def: "A specialized variant of the Tversky Index that uses fixed parameters with the alpha (α) value of 0.95, and beta (β) value of 0.05 to heavily weight the reference molecule in the comparison. This asymmetric weighting makes it particularly effective at finding molecules that contain the reference structure as a substructure. RefTversky is commonly used in virtual screening to identify compounds that preserve key structural features of a reference molecule. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000076 ! Tversky index algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000086
name: combo score algorithm
def: "A general term for a similarity score obtained by combining results from multiple different similarity calculation methods or metrics. The rationale is often to capture different aspects of similarity (e.g., structural, feature-based) into a single, potentially more informative score. The specific combination formula and constituent metrics define the particular combo score. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000074 ! similarity calculation algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000087
name: optimal transformation path algorithm
def: "An algorithm designed to find the best path or connection between states or nodes according to some defined criteria, such as minimum cost, shortest distance, or maximum flow. These algorithms are used in various contexts, including finding minimum energy pathways for reactions, constructing minimum spanning trees for clustering, optimizing network routes, or solving complex search problems. They employ different strategies ranging from exact graph traversals to heuristic searches. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000037 ! algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000088
name: Kruskal's algorithm
def: "A greedy algorithm used to find a Minimum Spanning Tree (MST) for a connected, undirected graph with weighted edges. An MST connects all vertices together with the minimum possible total edge weight. Kruskal's algorithm iteratively adds the lowest-weight edge that does not form a cycle until all vertices are connected." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000087 ! optimal transformation path algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000089 ! Prim's algorithm
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000089
name: Prim's algorithm
def: "An algorithm that finds the cheapest set of connections joining every node of a network, by starting from one node and repeatedly adding the cheapest link to a node not yet reached. The result is a tree touching every node with no redundant links. In this field it is used to build the shortest paths connecting conformations in a clustering. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000087 ! optimal transformation path algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000090
name: Dijkstra's algorithm
def: "An algorithm for finding the shortest path between a starting node and all other nodes in a graph with non-negative edge weights. It works by iteratively exploring the graph, maintaining the shortest distance found so far to each node, and always extending the path from the node with the current shortest distance. It is fundamental in graph theory and network routing. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000087 ! optimal transformation path algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000091
name: A* search algorithm
def: "An informed search algorithm used for finding the shortest path between a starting node and a target node in a graph, commonly used in pathfinding and planning problems. It extends Dijkstra's algorithm by using a heuristic function to estimate the cost from the current node to the target, guiding the search towards the goal more efficiently. Its performance depends on the quality of the heuristic used. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "A-star search algorithm" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000087 ! optimal transformation path algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000092
name: nearest neighbor algorithm
def: "An algorithm that answers a question about a point by looking at whichever recorded points lie closest to it. It is used to classify, to cluster, and to build lists of which atoms are near enough to interact. It makes no assumption about the shape of the data, only that closeness is meaningful. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000087 ! optimal transformation path algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000093
name: genetic algorithm
def: "A class of heuristic optimization algorithms inspired by the process of natural selection and evolution. They maintain a population of candidate solutions (chromosomes) that evolve over generations through processes like selection, crossover (recombination), and mutation, guided by a fitness function that evaluates solution quality. Genetic algorithms are often used for complex optimization problems where exact methods are infeasible. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000087 ! optimal transformation path algorithm
property_value: skos:exactMatch KISAO_0000506

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000094
name: simulated annealing algorithm
def: "A probabilistic heuristic algorithm used for finding the global optimum of a function in a large search space, inspired by the annealing process in metallurgy. It starts with an initial solution and iteratively explores neighboring solutions, accepting worse solutions with a probability that decreases over time (controlled by a \"temperature\" parameter), allowing it to escape local optima. It is a metaheuristic for global optimization. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000087 ! optimal transformation path algorithm
property_value: skos:exactMatch KISAO_0000503

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000095
name: ant colony optimization algorithm
def: "A probabilistic heuristic algorithm for finding good paths through graphs, inspired by the foraging behavior of ants who deposit pheromones. Artificial ants construct candidate solutions (paths) by moving through the graph, probabilistically choosing edges based on distance and accumulated artificial pheromone trails, which are updated based on the quality of solutions found. It is often applied to combinatorial optimization problems like the Traveling Salesperson Problem. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000087 ! optimal transformation path algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000096
name: network flow algorithm
def: "A class of algorithms designed to solve problems related to flows in networks (graphs where edges have capacities), such as finding the maximum flow possible between a source and a sink node. Examples include the Ford-Fulkerson algorithm and its variations (e.g., Edmonds-Karp). These algorithms are used in logistics, scheduling, network design, and resource allocation problems. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000087 ! optimal transformation path algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000097
name: NetCDF trajectory format
def: "A binary trajectory format based on the NetCDF standard, used by the Amber simulation package. It efficiently stores atomic coordinates, velocities, forces, and periodic box dimensions from a simulation. This is the modern, recommended trajectory format for Amber." []
comment: In the vast majority of scientific applications, including molecular dynamics, climate science, and oceanography, a .nc file is a NetCDF file. There is no difference in the format itself. The .nc extension is simply the most common file name suffix for a file written using the NetCDF data model. (UNVERFIED)
synonym: "AMBER nc format" EXACT []
synonym: "AMBER NetCDF trajectory format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000844 ! NetCDF format
is_a: MOLSIM:001090 ! molecular trajectory format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000159 ! mdcrd format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000098
name: ligand state
def: "Refers to the specific characteristics of a ligand molecule, particularly in the context of its interaction with a receptor molecule (like a protein). This encompasses various aspects, including whether it is bound or unbound, its specific binding pose or conformation, its protonation or tautomeric form, and its electronic state." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000006 ! model
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000099
name: bound state
def: "The state in which a ligand molecule is physically associated with its receptor molecule, typically residing within a specific binding site or pocket, stabilized by non-covalent interactions. Simulations often aim to characterize the structure, dynamics, and interaction energy of the ligand within the bound state, or calculate the free energy difference between the bound and unbound states (binding free energy)." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000098 ! ligand state
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000100 ! unbound state
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000100
name: unbound state
def: "The state in which a ligand molecule is not associated with the receptor molecule, typically solvated freely in the surrounding solvent or located far from the receptor's binding site. Defining the unbound state is necessary for calculating binding free energies, as it serves as the reference state relative to the bound state. It represents the ligand and receptor separated and independently solvated." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000098 ! ligand state
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000101
name: transition state
def: "In chemical kinetics and simulation, the transition state refers to a specific, high-energy, transient molecular configuration along the reaction coordinate connecting two stable states (e.g., reactant and product, or bound and unbound states). It is connected to the energy barrier that must be overcome for the transition to occur. While challenging to simulate directly due to its short lifetime, characterizing the transition state is crucial for understanding reaction mechanisms and rates, often studied using specialized simulation techniques or QM methods." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002255 ! molecular state
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000102
name: metastable state
def: "A state of a system that is locally stable (residing in a minimum on the potential energy surface) but has a higher free energy than the globally stable state. The system can persist in a metastable state for a significant time if the energy barrier to reach a more stable state is high. Examples in biomolecular systems include misfolded protein conformations, transiently bound ligand poses, or specific intermediate states along a functional cycle." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002255 ! molecular state
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000103
name: encounter complex
def: "A transient state occurring early in the binding process where the ligand and receptor molecules first come into close proximity and make non-specific contacts, largely driven by diffusion, before potentially rearranging into a specific, stable bound state. The encounter complex represents a collection of loosely associated configurations, often characterized by significant residual motion and non-optimal interactions, preceding the formation of the final bound pose." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000098 ! ligand state
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000104
name: solvated state
def: "A general state referring to a molecule (either ligand or receptor, or the complex) being surrounded by solvent molecules (typically a water buffer in biological contexts). This term emphasizes the presence and influence of the solvent on the molecule's structure, dynamics, and energetics. Both the bound and unbound states are typically solvated states, and solvation effects are crucial components of binding free energies and conformational preferences." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002255 ! molecular state
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000105
name: conformational state
def: "A specific three-dimensional arrangement or shape adopted by a flexible molecule, such as a protein or ligand. Molecules can typically exist in multiple conformational states, corresponding to different local minima on their potential energy surface, separated by energy barriers. Simulations are often used to explore the accessible conformational states, their relative populations, and the transitions between them, which are essential for molecular function and binding." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002255 ! molecular state
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000106
name: protonation state
def: "The condition of a molecule defined by which of its acidic and basic groups currently carry a proton. It fixes the charge on the molecule and therefore how it interacts with everything around it. It depends on the acidity of the surroundings, so a group buried in a protein may differ from the same group in water. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001210 ! system setup parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000107
name: tautomeric state
def: "One of several forms of a molecule that differ by the position of a hydrogen atom and an accompanying shift of a double bond, and which interconvert readily. The forms are genuinely different molecules for a simulation, because their bonds and charges differ. Choosing the wrong one for a ligand is a common and silent source of error. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001210 ! system setup parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000108
name: excited state
def: "An electronic state of a molecule where one or more electrons have been promoted to higher energy levels than in the ground electronic state, typically following the absorption of light (photoexcitation). Excited states have different electron distributions, geometries, and reactivity compared to the ground state and are central to photochemistry and spectroscopy (like fluorescence). Simulating excited states requires quantum mechanical methods (like TD-DFT or CASSCF) as classical force fields are typically parameterized only for the ground electronic state. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002255 ! molecular state

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000109
name: method
def: "A method represents the overall strategy or plan that specifies how a scientific objective is to be achieved. In the context of biomolecular science, this high-level concept encompasses both the physical procedures of an experimental method and the abstract protocols of a computational method. Defining the specific method is crucial for establishing the provenance and reproducibility of a result, as it dictates whether the evidence was generated through physical observation or theoretical calculation. (UNVERIFIED)" []

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000110
name: Euler integrator
def: "An integration algorithm that computes the next position and velocity from the current ones and the current force alone. It is the simplest possible scheme and the easiest to reason about. It is not used in practice, because the energy of a system integrated this way drifts steadily upward. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001691 ! integration algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001692 ! Beeman integrator

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000111
name: obsolete correlation coefficient
def: "OBSOLETE. A type of statistical property that measures the strength and direction of the linear association between two variables. It is a value between -1 and 1, where 1 indicates a perfect positive correlation and -1 indicates a perfect negative correlation. The correlation coefficient is widely used to identify relationships between different properties in a simulation. This is often reported as r or rho." []
comment: Obsoleted 2026-07-29: duplicated STATO:0000142. STATO is the canonical OBO home for statistics; reused in place of this term. Its four children were re-parented under STATO:0000142 in the same edit - retiring a parent necessarily re-points every child that named it.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: STATO:0000142

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000112
name: obsolete Pearson's correlation coefficient
def: "OBSOLETE. Pearson's correlation coefficient (often denoted as 'r') measures the strength and direction of the linear relationship between two continuous variables. It assumes the data are approximately normally distributed and calculates the covariance of the two variables divided by the product of their standard deviations. It is perhaps the most widely used measure of linear correlation." []
comment: Obsoleted 2026-07-29: duplicated STATO:0000280. STATO is the canonical OBO home for statistics; reused in place of this term.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: STATO:0000280

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000113
name: tilt orientation
def: "A specific type of `orientation` descriptor that represents the cosine of the rotation of a vector orthogonal to a given axis." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001352 ! molecular orientation
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000114
name: HOLE
def: "HOLE is a computer program used to analyze the dimensions and shape of internal pathways or tunnels within a biomolecular structure. It operates by computationally squeezing a flexible sphere along a channel axis to determine the maximum pore radius at every point without overlapping the surrounding atoms." []
xref: https://doi.org/10.1016/S0263-7855(97)00009-X
is_a: MOLSIM:000245 ! tunnel predictor tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000115 ! MOLE
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000115
name: MOLE
def: "MOLE is a software algorithm designed to automatically locate and characterize channels, tunnels, and pores within protein structures. It utilizes a Voronoi diagram approach to efficiently map the void space inside a molecule and identify paths connecting internal cavities to the surface." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000245 ! tunnel predictor tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000116
name: bootstrap analysis
def: "A statistical method that estimates how uncertain a computed quantity is by drawing many new samples from the existing data, with repetition allowed, and recomputing the quantity from each. The spread of those recomputed values estimates the spread the original would have shown across repeated experiments. It needs no assumption about how the data are distributed, which is why it suits simulation output. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000349 ! resampling method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000117
name: Markov state model analysis
def: "A data analysis method that divides the conformations visited in simulations into discrete states and counts the transitions between them, assuming the next state depends only on the current one and not on the path taken there. That assumption lets many short simulations be stitched into a picture of behaviour far longer than any of them. From it come the slow timescales, the populations of the states, and the routes between them. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "MSM" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000300 ! free energy and molecular dynamics analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000118
name: Jensen-Shannon divergence analysis
def: "A statistical measure of how different 2 probability distributions are, bounded between 0 and 1 and giving the same answer whichever distribution is taken first. Those 2 properties are what it adds to the underlying relative entropy measure, which is unbounded and asymmetric. It is used to compare the conformations sampled by 2 simulations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000400 ! statistical analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000119
name: Kullback-Leibler divergence
def: "A statistical measure of how much information is lost when one probability distribution is used in place of another. It is not symmetric: the value depends on which distribution is treated as the reference. It is 0 only when the 2 are identical and has no upper limit, which is why the symmetric bounded version is often preferred. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001403 ! statistical property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000120
name: dimensionality reduction technique analysis
def: "A statistical method that re-expresses data with many variables in terms of a few, chosen to keep as much of the structure as possible. A protein trajectory has 3 coordinates per atom, which cannot be looked at directly. Reducing it to 2 or 3 numbers per frame is what makes it possible to see where the system went. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000400 ! statistical analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000121
name: principal component analysis
def: "A statistical method that finds the directions along which data vary most, and re-expresses the data in terms of the few largest of them. Applied to a trajectory, the largest directions are the collective motions that account for most of the movement. A protein with thousands of coordinates can then be described by 2 or 3 numbers per frame. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "PCA" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000120 ! dimensionality reduction technique analysis
property_value: skos:closeMatch OBI:0200051

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000122
name: data analysis technique
def: "A data analysis technique is a specific computational method used to extract meaningful scientific insights from the raw data generated by a simulation. These techniques can range from simple calculations, like measuring the distance between two atoms over time, to complex statistical methods that identify large-scale molecular motions. Applying these techniques is the crucial step that transforms a trajectory of atomic coordinates into an understandable story about the molecule's behavior." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000026 ! analysis method
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000123
name: clustering analysis
def: "Clustering analysis encompasses algorithms designed to partition a dataset into distinct groups or clusters, such that data points within the same cluster are more similar to each other than to those in other clusters based on chosen features. In molecular simulation, clustering is frequently applied to trajectory data to identify distinct conformational states visited by the system. Various algorithms exist, differing in how similarity and clusters are defined (e.g., k-means, hierarchical clustering)." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000917 ! structural analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000124
name: statistical test analysis
def: "A statistical test is a specific procedure used within the framework of hypothesis testing to decide whether to reject or fail to reject the null hypothesis. It involves calculating a test statistic (a value derived from the sample data) and comparing it to a critical value or calculating a p-value (the probability of observing the data, or more extreme data, if the null hypothesis were true). Examples include t-tests, chi-squared tests, and ANOVA. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000348 ! hypothesis testing analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000125
name: Kolmogorov-Smirnov test analysis
def: "A statistical test that judges whether 2 sets of values come from the same distribution, by measuring the largest gap between their cumulative distributions. It assumes nothing about the shape of either distribution, which is why it suits simulation data. It is used to check whether 2 simulations sampled the same conformations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000124 ! statistical test analysis
property_value: skos:closeMatch STATO:0000083

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000126
name: confidence intervals analysis
def: "A confidence interval provides a range of values, calculated from sample data (e.g., simulation results), that is estimated to contain the true underlying value of a population parameter (e.g., the true average energy) with a specified probability or confidence level (e.g., 95%). It quantifies the uncertainty associated with estimating a parameter from limited or noisy data. Wider intervals indicate greater uncertainty. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000400 ! statistical analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000127
name: error metrics analysis
def: "A statistical method that measures how far predicted values lie from observed ones. Which measure to use depends on what a large error should cost: squaring the differences makes outliers dominate, taking their size does not. Reporting more than one is usual, because each hides something the others show. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000400 ! statistical analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000128
name: standard error of the mean analysis
def: "A statistical measure giving how far a computed average is likely to lie from the true average, based on how much the data scatter and how many independent samples there are. It shrinks as more independent data is added, unlike the spread of the data itself, which does not. For a trajectory the count of independent samples is far smaller than the number of frames, which is why it must be estimated by block averaging. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "SEM" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000127 ! error metrics analysis
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000129 ! root mean square error analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000129
name: root mean square error analysis
def: "An error metric giving the typical size of the difference between predicted and observed values, computed by squaring the differences, averaging them and taking the square root. Squaring first makes large errors count disproportionately, so a single bad prediction moves it noticeably. It is in the same units as the quantity itself, which makes it directly interpretable. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "RMSE" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000127 ! error metrics analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000130
name: mean absolute error analyisis
def: "An error metric giving the average size of the difference between predicted and observed values, ignoring sign. Because it does not square the differences, every error counts in proportion to its size and one large error does not dominate. It is the measure to prefer when outliers are expected and should not be allowed to control the score. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "MAE" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000127 ! error metrics analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000131
name: mean squared error analysis
def: "An error metric giving the average of the squared differences between predicted and observed values. It is the quantity most fitting procedures minimise, because squaring makes it smooth and easy to differentiate. Its units are the square of the quantity's, which is why the square root is usually reported instead. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "MSE" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000127 ! error metrics analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000132
name: CHARMM36
def: "A widely used all-atom force field parameter set from the CHARMM family, optimized for proteins, lipids, nucleic acids, and carbohydrates. Developed by the MacKerell Lab at the University of Maryland, it provides the mathematical parameters (atomic charges, masses, bond lengths, and angles) necessary to calculate the physical forces dictating the structure and dynamics of biomolecules. It represents a significant update over earlier CHARMM versions (like CHARMM22/27), incorporating improved parameters derived from high-level quantum calculations and experimental data. The 'm' variant (CHARMM36m) includes further refinements, particularly for proteins." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000133
name: cross-validation errors analysis
def: "A statistical method that measures how well a model predicts data it was not fitted to, by repeatedly holding part of the data back, fitting on the rest, and testing on the held-back part. A model can always be made to fit the data it was built from, so testing on that data proves nothing. This is the standard guard against that mistake. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000135 ! convergence and uncertainty quantification analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000134
name: bootstrapped error estimates analysis
def: "A validation method that puts an uncertainty on a result by resampling the data it came from and recomputing it many times. It is used to show that a conclusion does not rest on a few particular data points. A result whose value changes substantially across resamples is not a result. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "BSE" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000353 ! validation analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000135
name: convergence and uncertainty quantification analysis
def: "A data analysis method that judges whether a simulation has sampled enough for its results to be stable, and puts an error estimate on those results. It works from time series of the quantity of interest, or by resampling the data statistically. Without both parts, a reported value has no stated reliability. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000400 ! statistical analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000136
name: block averaging analysis
def: "A statistical method that estimates the uncertainty of an average taken from a trajectory, by dividing the data into blocks and looking at how the block averages scatter. It is needed because successive frames of a trajectory resemble each other, so the usual formula for the uncertainty of a mean underestimates it badly. Enlarging the blocks until the estimate stops changing gives the honest figure. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000135 ! convergence and uncertainty quantification analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000137
name: hysteresis analysis
def: "A data analysis method that compares results obtained while a parameter or collective variable is changed in one direction with those obtained while it is changed back, and reports the difference between them. A large difference means the system did not stay near equilibrium, or that sampling was insufficient. Showing that the difference is small is part of demonstrating that a free energy calculation has converged. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000135 ! convergence and uncertainty quantification analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000138
name: convergence metrics analysis
def: "A data analysis method that computes quantitative measures of whether a simulation has sampled enough for its results to have stopped changing. Measures include the stability of a running average, the size of fluctuations in a key property, and the number of transitions observed between states. Which measure is appropriate depends on the kind of simulation and on what is being calculated. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000135 ! convergence and uncertainty quantification analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000139
name: overlap metrics analysis
def: "A data analysis method that measures how far the configurations sampled in neighbouring simulation windows or thermodynamic states coincide. Enough overlap is a precondition for combining the windows with WHAM or MBAR; too little makes the combined free energy unreliable. It is checked before the free energy profile is computed, not after. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000135 ! convergence and uncertainty quantification analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000140
name: computational method
def: "A computational method is a procedure that uses computers to study a scientific problem. As a type of method, it encompasses the specific set of calculations and theoretical models used to simulate molecular behavior or analyze resulting data, distinct from experimental or purely theoretical approaches. These methods are defined by their underlying algorithms and the parameters specified in input files, such as an AMBER mdin or GROMACS mdp file. This is a high-level concept, often found in methods sections of papers as \"computational methods,\" \"in silico approach,\" or \"simulation protocol.\" (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000109 ! method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000141
name: theoretical approach
def: "A method consisting of the physical principles and mathematical framework a calculation is built on, such as quantum mechanics or classical mechanics with an empirical potential. It sits above the algorithm and the software, and fixes what the calculation is able to represent at all. Two methods sharing an approach can still differ in every other respect. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000109 ! method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000142
name: predictive index analysis
def: "A statistical metric rating how well a model's predictions support a decision, by weighting each pair of compounds by how much getting their order wrong would cost. Ordering 2 very different compounds wrongly counts more heavily than ordering 2 similar ones wrongly. It is used where a model guides a choice rather than predicting a value. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000127 ! error metrics analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000143
name: ligand pairs selection criteria
def: "A criterion applied when choosing which pairs of compounds to compare in a relative free energy study. The choice determines whether the calculation converges at all, because a pair differing by one atom behaves quite differently from a pair differing by a ring. Its subclasses cover similarity, affinity range, data quality and practicality. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: IAO:0000030 ! information content entity

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000144
name: structural similarity
def: "A ligand selection criterion favouring pairs of molecules that share a common core and differ only by small changes. Such pairs can be transformed into one another alchemically with few atoms changing, which is what makes the calculation converge. Choosing dissimilar pairs is the most common reason a relative free energy calculation fails. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000143 ! ligand pairs selection criteria
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000145 ! chemical similarity

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000145
name: chemical similarity
def: "A ligand selection criterion favouring molecules that resemble each other in chemical character, such as polarity, charge and hydrogen bonding, rather than in how their atoms are connected. Two molecules built on different frameworks can still behave alike by this measure. It is used when the aim is to replace a scaffold rather than to modify one. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000143 ! ligand pairs selection criteria

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000146
name: binding affinity range
def: "A ligand selection criterion requiring the measured binding strengths of the chosen compounds to fall within a stated range, or to differ by no more than a stated amount. A pair whose affinities differ enormously gives a free energy difference that is large and easy to predict, which tests nothing. A pair too close together cannot be distinguished from calculation error. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000143 ! ligand pairs selection criteria

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000147
name: structural and chemical diversity
def: "A ligand selection criterion requiring the chosen set as a whole to span a range of structures and chemistries, even though individual pairs within it should be similar. A set of near-identical compounds tests a method over a narrow region and says nothing about its general reliability. The 2 requirements apply at different levels: similarity within a pair, diversity across the set. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000143 ! ligand pairs selection criteria

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000148
name: experimental data availability
def: "This practical criterion emphasizes selecting ligands for which reliable experimental data, particularly binding affinity measurements (like Ki, Kd, or IC50), already exist. Having high-quality experimental data is essential for validating the computational predictions and assessing the accuracy of the methods used. Availability of structural data (e.g., co-crystal structures) is also highly valuable." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000143 ! ligand pairs selection criteria
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000149
name: chemical properties
def: "A ligand selection criterion based on computed or measured properties of the compounds, such as molecular weight, lipophilicity, charge and the number of rotatable bonds. These properties predict how difficult a compound will be to simulate as well as how drug-like it is. A charged or very flexible compound needs far more sampling than a neutral rigid one. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000143 ! ligand pairs selection criteria

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000150
name: structural change
def: "A ligand selection criterion based on how large and of what kind the difference between 2 candidate compounds is. Changing a single atom converges quickly; changing a ring or a charge does not. The size of the change is the best single predictor of whether a relative free energy calculation will succeed. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "structural changes" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000143 ! ligand pairs selection criteria

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000151
name: computational feasibility
def: "A ligand selection criterion asking whether the calculations a candidate would require can be completed with the time and computing available. A charged or highly flexible ligand may need many times the sampling of a neutral rigid one. It is applied before the calculation, since discovering the answer afterwards wastes the whole effort. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000143 ! ligand pairs selection criteria

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000152
name: relevance to drug discovery
def: "A ligand selection criterion favouring molecules and modifications that bear on an ongoing drug discovery project or a stated therapeutic aim. It is a judgement about purpose rather than about chemistry, so it cannot be computed. It is recorded because it explains why a particular set of compounds was chosen. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000143 ! ligand pairs selection criteria

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000153
name: structural data quality
def: "A ligand selection criterion based on how good the experimental structure of the complex is, judged by resolution, how well the model fits the data, and whether the ligand is clearly resolved. A poorly resolved ligand may be placed wrongly, and a calculation started from it inherits that error. It is assessed before the structure is used, not after a result looks wrong. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000143 ! ligand pairs selection criteria

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000154
name: stability in simulations
def: "A ligand selection criterion based on whether the compound stays bound and in a consistent pose during a trial simulation. A ligand that drifts out of its site, or flips between poses, gives a free energy that depends on how long the run was. Testing it with a short simulation before committing to a full calculation is cheaper than discovering it afterwards. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000143 ! ligand pairs selection criteria

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000155
name: ligand efficiency
def: "A measure relating how tightly a compound binds to how many heavy atoms it has, usually as binding energy divided by that count. It exists because binding strength rises almost automatically with size, so a large weak binder can look better than a small efficient one. Optimising a small efficient compound usually ends better than optimising a large inefficient one. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000143 ! ligand pairs selection criteria

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000156
name: GROMACS mdp format
def: "The GROMACS mdp format is the specific simulation parameter format used by the GROMACS software package. The file, which typically has a \".mdp\" extension, contains a series of keyword-value pairs that control every aspect of the simulation run, from the integrator and time step to the thermostat and pressure coupling methods. For GROMACS users, creating and editing the mdp file is the primary way to define the simulation protocol." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002065 ! simulation parameter format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000469 ! AMBER mdin format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000157
name: simulation framework
def: "A reusable software platform or environment that provides a basic structure and set of tools or libraries for developing applications or performing complex tasks within a specific domain. In biomolecular simulation, a framework might offer standardized ways to set up simulations, manage data, integrate different tools, or build custom analysis workflows, providing a higher level of abstraction than individual tools or scripts. Examples could include workflow management systems (like Galaxy, KNIME adapted for simulation) or simulation setup environments (like CHARMM-GUI). (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "framework" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000001 ! software
property_value: dcterms:source https://doi.org/10.1002/jcc

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000158
name: simulation and modeling software
def: "A software program that builds, runs or analyses a computational model of a physical system. It is the category the simulation engines, the modelling suites and the analysis packages all belong to. What separates it from other software is that its subject is a model of something real. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000001 ! software

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000159
name: mdcrd format
def: "A text-based file format from the Amber software that stores the movement of atoms over time from a simulation. It contains a series of snapshots, or frames, where each frame lists the x, y, and z coordinates of every atom at a specific time point. It may also store the x, y, and z simulation box sizes." []
synonym: "AMBER mdcrd format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001090 ! molecular trajectory format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393
property_value: skos:exactMatch format:3878

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000160
name: molecular dynamics engine
def: "Application programs specifically designed to perform molecular dynamics (MD) simulations, which calculate the motion of atoms and molecules over time based on classical mechanics and a chosen force field. These packages typically include capabilities for system preparation, simulation execution (often optimized for high-performance computing), and basic trajectory analysis. Examples include AMBER, GROMACS, NAMD, CHARMM, Desmond, and LAMMPS." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001851 ! simulation engine
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000161 ! quantum chemistry engine
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000161
name: quantum chemistry engine
def: "A software program that solves for the arrangement of electrons in atoms and molecules using quantum mechanics. It implements methods such as Hartree-Fock, density functional theory and the correlated methods built on them. It is what supplies an energy and a set of forces when a force field is not accurate enough. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001851 ! simulation engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000162
name: docking tool
def: "A computational tool used to predict the preferred binding orientation and affinity (scoring) of one molecule (typically a small ligand) to another (usually a larger receptor like a protein or nucleic acid). Docking tools employ search algorithms to explore possible binding poses within a target site and use scoring functions to estimate the binding strength for each pose. Widely used in drug discovery and understanding molecular recognition, examples include AutoDock, Vina, Glide, GOLD, and DOCK." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001850 ! modeling and setup tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000172 ! topology and parameterization tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000163
name: visualization tool
def: "A software program that draws molecular structures, surfaces, densities and trajectories as interactive 3-dimensional images. It lets a person look at a system rather than only measure it. Many faults in a prepared system, such as a molecule sitting half outside its box, are obvious on sight and invisible to any numerical check. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000001 ! software

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000164
name: analysis tool
def: "Software designed to process raw data generated from biomolecular simulations (like trajectories, energy files) to calculate specific quantitative properties and extract meaningful insights. Analysis tools implement algorithms for calculating metrics like RMSD, RMSF, radius of gyration, hydrogen bonds, interaction energies, principal components (PCA), free energy estimations (MM/PBSA), clustering, etc. Examples include cpptraj (AmberTools), GROMACS analysis utilities, MDAnalysis (Python library), and specialized scripts or programs." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000001 ! software
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000165
name: data processing tool
def: "A tool focused on manipulating, converting, filtering, or extracting information from data files. This can involve tasks like converting file formats, extracting specific columns or frames, merging datasets, calculating simple statistics, or preparing data for input into other analysis or visualization tools." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000001 ! software
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000166
name: file conversion tool
def: "A specific type of data processing tool dedicated to converting molecular structure, trajectory, or data files from one format to another (e.g., PDB to MOL2, XTC to netcdf)." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000165 ! data processing tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:002099 ! metadata extraction tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000167
name: automation script
def: "A script specifically designed to automate a series of steps in a workflow that would otherwise need to be performed manually. In simulations, this could involve automatically setting up multiple simulation replicas, submitting jobs to a computing cluster, checking job status, and organizing output files, thereby reducing manual effort and potential errors. Workflow management systems often rely heavily on automation scripts. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001802 ! script
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000168 ! data analysis script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000168
name: data analysis script
def: "A script written to perform specific analysis tasks on data generated from simulations, often going beyond the standard capabilities of packaged analysis tools or requiring custom calculations. Examples include scripts to calculate specific geometric parameters over time, parse log files for specific energy terms, perform advanced statistical analysis or time-series analysis on trajectory data, or generate data for custom plots." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001802 ! script
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000169
name: workflow script
def: "A script that defines and executes an entire sequence of computational tasks constituting a specific workflow, often involving multiple steps like data preparation, running simulations (potentially submitting to clusters), performing analysis, and summarizing results. These scripts orchestrate the execution of various tools and other scripts, manage intermediate data, and handle dependencies between steps, ensuring the entire process runs smoothly and reproducibly. Tools like Snakemake or Nextflow help in creating robust workflow scripts. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001802 ! script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000170
name: software component
def: "A reusable part of a larger software system that provides a defined set of functions to whatever calls it. Unlike a program, it is not run on its own; it is built into something else. A library that reads a file format is the usual example. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000001 ! software

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000171
name: software development and management tool
def: "A software program that helps in writing, building, testing or maintaining other software, rather than in doing any science itself. Compilers, version control systems and test frameworks belong here. They appear in this ontology because a simulation result depends on which versions of which tools produced it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000001 ! software

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000172
name: topology and parameterization tool
def: "A software program that works out which atom type each atom belongs to and which force field parameters therefore apply, producing the topology a simulation needs. The assignment is made from the molecule's connectivity and chemistry. A wrong assignment produces a system that simulates normally and represents the wrong molecule. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001850 ! modeling and setup tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000173
name: quantum mechanics
def: "A physical theory describing how matter behaves at the scale of atoms and subatomic particles, where energy and angular momentum take discrete values. It is what chemical bonding and molecular electronic structure are explained by. In this field its equations are solved approximately to predict molecular properties. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "QM" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000141 ! theoretical approach

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000174
name: STO-2G
def: "A minimal basis set in which each atomic orbital is approximated by 2 Gaussian functions added together. Gaussians are used because the integrals they require can be computed quickly, while the orbital shape they imitate cannot. With only 2 the imitation is poor, so it is used to demonstrate the method rather than to obtain results. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000017 ! minimal basis set
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000214 ! STO-3G

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000175
name: Gaussian
def: "A comprehensive and widely used quantum chemistry software package, primarily focused on electronic structure calculations using ab initio methods, Density Functional Theory (DFT), and semi-empirical methods. While its core strength is QM, Gaussian can perform ONIOM (QM/MM) calculations and some limited molecular mechanics (MM) computations, making it potentially usable in biomolecular contexts, especially for parameterization or high-accuracy active site studies, but it's not typically used as a primary classical MD engine like AMBER or GROMACS. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000161 ! quantum chemistry engine
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000176 ! GAMESS
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000176 ! GAMESS
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000179 ! Q-Chem

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000176
name: GAMESS
def: "A quantum chemistry engine providing a broad range of wavefunction-based and density functional methods, distributed freely for academic use. Two separately maintained programs share the name, developed in the United States and the United Kingdom, and their inputs are not interchangeable. Which one produced a result therefore has to be recorded. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000161 ! quantum chemistry engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000177
name: Psi4
def: "An open-source suite of quantum chemistry software specializing in high-accuracy ab initio methods (like coupled cluster and symmetry-adapted perturbation theory) alongside standard methods like HF and DFT. Psi4 is known for its modern codebase (Python and C++), user-friendly input, extensive libraries, and focus on accuracy and efficient algorithms for correlated wavefunction calculations. It's increasingly popular in the academic community for demanding electronic structure calculations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000161 ! quantum chemistry engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000178
name: Orca
def: "A versatile and powerful quantum chemistry software package, freely available for academic use, offering a wide range of methods including DFT, HF, semi-empirical, MPn, coupled cluster, and multi-reference methods. Orca is known for its robustness, efficiency (especially for DFT), user-friendliness, and ability to handle large molecules, making it very popular for diverse applications in computational chemistry, including biomolecular-relevant calculations like QM/MM or spectroscopy. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000161 ! quantum chemistry engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000179
name: Q-Chem
def: "A comprehensive quantum chemistry software package offering a wide range of methods, including Hartree-Fock, DFT, coupled-cluster, and QM/MM capabilities. Like Gaussian, its primary focus is quantum mechanical electronic structure calculations. While it can be used for QM/MM simulations relevant to biomolecular systems, it's not typically used for large-scale classical MD simulations in the way dedicated MD packages are. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000161 ! quantum chemistry engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000180
name: Quantum ESPRESSO
def: "An integrated suite of open-source software for quantum mechanical electronic structure calculations and materials modeling, primarily based on Density Functional Theory (DFT), plane waves, and pseudopotentials. While extremely powerful for condensed matter physics and materials science, and capable of ab initio MD (Born-Oppenheimer MD), its typical application domain and methods (plane waves) differ from those commonly used for classical MD or QM/MM studies of large solvated biomolecules in packages like AMBER or GROMACS. It is more suited for periodic systems. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000161 ! quantum chemistry engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000181
name: NWChem
def: "A versatile open-source computational chemistry software package developed by Pacific Northwest National Laboratory (PNNL), designed for high-performance computing. It offers a broad range of capabilities, including classical MD simulation, various quantum mechanical methods (DFT, Hartree-Fock, coupled cluster), and hybrid QM/MM methods. Its ability to handle both MD and QM makes it suitable for complex biomolecular simulations requiring multi-scale approaches on large parallel computers. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000161 ! quantum chemistry engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000182
name: Molpro
def: "A high-accuracy quantum chemistry software package primarily focused on sophisticated ab initio wavefunction-based methods, particularly multi-reference methods (CASSCF, CASPT2, MRCI) and high-level coupled cluster calculations (CCSD(T), etc.), alongside standard HF and DFT. Molpro is renowned for its capabilities in calculating highly accurate energies, properties, and potential energy surfaces, often used for benchmarking or studying systems where electron correlation is challenging, including complex transition metal systems or photochemical processes. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000161 ! quantum chemistry engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000183
name: Chronus Quantum
def: "An object-oriented quantum chemistry software package focused on developing and implementing novel electronic structure theories, particularly methods for electron correlation and response properties (e.g., for spectroscopy). It serves both as a research platform for method development and an application for advanced QM calculations. It provides a modern framework for tackling challenging quantum chemical problems. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000161 ! quantum chemistry engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000184
name: QuTiP
def: "A Python library for simulating quantum systems that exchange energy with their surroundings, rather than being isolated. Its subject is quantum optics and quantum information rather than molecular structure. It appears here because such calculations sometimes accompany spectroscopic work on molecules. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000161 ! quantum chemistry engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000185
name: π-π interaction
def: "A non-covalent interaction occurring between aromatic rings, arising from a combination of electrostatic interactions between their quadrupole moments (electron-rich faces vs electron-poorer edges) and Van der Waals (dispersion) forces. The preferred geometry (e.g., stacked, parallel-displaced, T-shaped) depends on the specific aromatic systems and influences the interaction strength. They are important in protein structure (stacking of Phe, Tyr, Trp, His residues) and the stability of DNA/RNA helices (base stacking). (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "π-π interactions" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000064 ! Van der Waals interaction

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000186
name: hydrophobic interaction
def: "The observed tendency for nonpolar molecules or molecular groups to associate with each other when in an aqueous (water) environment, effectively minimizing their disruptive contact with water molecules. This phenomenon is primarily entropically driven by the favorable increase in the entropy of water molecules that are released from ordered \"cages\" (solvation shells) around the nonpolar surfaces when they aggregate. It is a major driving force for protein folding (burying hydrophobic residues), membrane formation, and ligand binding." []
synonym: "hydrophobic interactions" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000062 ! non-covalent interaction
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000187
name: electrostatic interaction
def: "An interaction between charged or polar groups arising from the attraction and repulsion of their charges. It reaches much further than any other non-bonded interaction, falling off only in proportion to distance for 2 ions. That long reach is why a periodic simulation needs a special method to compute it rather than simply cutting it off. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "electrostatic interactions" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000062 ! non-covalent interaction

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000188
name: cation-π interaction
def: "A specific type of non-covalent electrostatic interaction involving the attractive force between a cation (a positively charged ion, e.g., Na+,K+,Lys+,Arg+) and the electron-rich face of an aromatic π-system (like benzene, or the side chains of Phe, Tyr, Trp, His). The cation is attracted to the negative electrostatic potential above and below the plane of the aromatic ring, which arises from its quadrupole moment. These interactions contribute significantly to protein structure stabilization and molecular recognition, including ligand binding. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "cation-π interactions" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000187 ! electrostatic interaction
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000189 ! hydrogen bond

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000189
name: hydrogen bond
def: "A specific, directional non-covalent interaction formed between a hydrogen atom covalently bonded to a highly electronegative atom (the donor, D, typically N, O, or F) and another nearby electronegative atom (the acceptor, A, also typically N, O, or F) which possesses a lone pair of electrons. Represented as D-H···A, it has characteristics of both electrostatic attraction (between the partially positive H and partially negative A) and weak orbital overlap/covalency." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000187 ! electrostatic interaction
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000190
name: backbone hydrogen bond
def: "Hydrogen bonds formed specifically between the atoms of the polypeptide backbone in proteins or peptides. The most common form involves the amide hydrogen (N-H group) of one residue acting as the donor and the carbonyl oxygen (C=O group) of another residue (often i→i+4 in helices or between strands in sheets) acting as the acceptor." []
synonym: "backbone hydrogen bonds" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000189 ! hydrogen bond
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000191 ! side-chain hydrogen bond
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000191
name: side-chain hydrogen bond
def: "Hydrogen bonds where at least one of the participating atoms (either the donor hydrogen attached to its electronegative atom, or the acceptor electronegative atom) belongs to an amino acid side chain, rather than exclusively involving backbone atoms. These interactions can occur between two side chains, or between a side chain and the backbone, contributing to the stability of the protein's tertiary and quaternary structure, protein-ligand interactions, and enzyme active site chemistry." []
synonym: "side-chain hydrogen bonds" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000189 ! hydrogen bond
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000192
name: backbone-side chain hydrogen bond
def: "Hydrogen bonds formed specifically between an atom on the polypeptide backbone (either the amide N-H donor or the carbonyl C=O acceptor) and an atom within an amino acid side chain (acting as acceptor or donor, respectively). These interactions directly link the regular backbone structure to the specific side chain identities and conformations, playing crucial roles in stabilizing protein folds (tertiary structure) and positioning side chains for function." []
synonym: "backbone-side chain hydrogen bonds" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000189 ! hydrogen bond
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000193
name: peptidic bond
def: "A covalent bond joining the carbonyl carbon of one amino acid to the nitrogen of the next, formed with the loss of a water molecule. Its partial double-bond character holds the 6 atoms around it flat and makes rotation about it slow. That rigidity is why a protein backbone has only 2 freely rotating angles per residue. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000063 ! covalent interaction
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000194 ! disulfide bridge

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000194
name: disulfide bridge
def: "A specific type of covalent bond formed by the oxidation of the thiol (-SH) groups of two cysteine amino acid residues, creating a sulfur-sulfur bond (-S-S-). These bonds can form between cysteines within the same polypeptide chain (intramolecular) or between different chains (intermolecular), acting as strong cross-links that significantly stabilize the folded tertiary or quaternary structure of many proteins, particularly extracellular ones. Formation and breakage of disulfide bridges are important biochemical processes. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "disulfide bridges" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000063 ! covalent interaction

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000195
name: thermodynamic ensemble
def: "A theoretical statistical mechanics construct representing a probability distribution for the state of a system, defined by a specific set of macroscopic variables held constant (e.g., NVT, NPT). In molecular simulation, it dictates the thermodynamic conditions and integration rules applied to generate a trajectory. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "ensemble" EXACT []
synonym: "statistical ensemble" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000006 ! model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000196
name: canonical ensemble
def: "A statistical ensemble representing systems where the number of particles (N), the system volume (V), and the temperature (T) are held constant; hence often called the NVT ensemble. The system is considered to be in thermal contact with an infinitely large heat bath at temperature T, allowing energy exchange. Simulations performed in the NVT ensemble generate configurations according to the Boltzmann probability distribution appropriate for that temperature, making it suitable for studying equilibrium properties under constant temperature and volume conditions. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "NVT ensemble" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000195 ! thermodynamic ensemble
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000197 ! isothermal-isobaric ensemble

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000197
name: isothermal-isobaric ensemble
def: "The isothermal-isobaric ensemble (often called the NPT ensemble) is a statistical mechanical framework for a system with a fixed number of particles (N), constant temperature (T), and constant pressure (P). Unlike canonical ensembles, volume (V) is allowed to fluctuate, making it ideal for modeling real-world condensed-phase laboratory conditions." []
synonym: "NPT ensemble" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000195 ! thermodynamic ensemble
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000198
name: microcanonical ensemble
def: "A statistical ensemble representing completely isolated systems, where the number of particles (N), the system volume (V), and the total energy (E) are all held constant; hence often called the NVE ensemble. There is no exchange of energy or particles with the surroundings. Simulations performed in the NVE ensemble directly follow Newtonian laws of motion (integrating Hamilton's equations), and conservation of total energy serves as a key check of simulation stability and accuracy, but it's less commonly used for equilibrium sampling compared to NVT or NPT as temperature can fluctuate. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "NVE ensemble" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000195 ! thermodynamic ensemble

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000199
name: grand canonical ensemble
def: "A statistical ensemble representing open systems where the chemical potential (μ), the system volume (V), and the temperature (T) are held constant; hence often called the μVT ensemble. The system can exchange both energy (with a heat bath at T) and particles (with a particle reservoir at chemical potential μ). Simulations in this ensemble are useful for studying systems where the number of particles can change, such as adsorption phenomena, phase equilibria (vapor-liquid), or systems involving chemical reactions where concentrations are fixed rather than particle numbers. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "µVT ensemble" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000195 ! thermodynamic ensemble

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000200
name: protein structure determination method
def: "Protein structure determination methods refer to the experimental techniques used to obtain high-resolution three-dimensional atomic coordinates of protein molecules. These methods provide the foundational structural data used in biomolecular simulations, structure-based drug design, and understanding protein function. The primary techniques include X-ray crystallography, NMR spectroscopy, and cryo-electron microscopy." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000304 ! experimental method
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000201
name: X-ray crystallography
def: "X-ray crystallography is an experimental technique that determines the three-dimensional structure of molecules, particularly proteins, by analyzing the diffraction pattern produced when X-rays are scattered by a crystalline form of the molecule. The diffraction pattern contains information about the arrangement of electrons, allowing calculation of an electron density map into which the atomic structure can be built. It is capable of providing very high-resolution structural information. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "X-ray" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000200 ! protein structure determination method
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000202 ! nuclear magnetic resonance
property_value: skos:closeMatch NCIT:C17672

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000202
name: nuclear magnetic resonance
def: "Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (NMR) spectroscopy is an experimental technique used to determine protein structures, typically in solution, by exploiting the magnetic properties of atomic nuclei. It measures distances between specific pairs of atoms (primarily hydrogens using the Nuclear Overhauser Effect) and torsion angle restraints based on spin-spin coupling. These experimentally derived restraints are then used to calculate an ensemble of structures consistent with the data." []
synonym: "NMR" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000200 ! protein structure determination method
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986
property_value: skos:closeMatch CHMO:0000591

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000203
name: cryogenic electron microscopy
def: "Cryogenic electron microscopy (Cryo-EM) is an experimental technique that determines the structure of molecules and complexes by imaging samples rapidly frozen in a thin layer of vitreous (non-crystalline) ice using an electron microscope. Sophisticated image processing techniques are used to average images of thousands or millions of individual particles to reconstruct a high-resolution three-dimensional density map. Cryo-EM is particularly powerful for large, flexible complexes that are difficult to crystallize. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "Cryo-EM" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000200 ! protein structure determination method
property_value: skos:exactMatch CHMO:0002413

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000204
name: ligand charge model
def: "A computational methodology or protocol used to assign partial atomic charges to the atoms of a small molecule (ligand), typically for use within a classical molecular mechanics force field during simulations of its interaction with a biomolecule (like a protein or nucleic acid). Since electrostatic interactions are crucial for molecular recognition and binding affinity, accurate and consistent charge assignment is critical. Different models (e.g., RESP, AM1-BCC, Mulliken, Löwdin) exist, often aiming to reproduce the quantum mechanically derived electrostatic potential around the molecule or fit to experimental data, with varying levels of theory, complexity, and computational cost. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000006 ! model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000205
name: AM1-BCC
def: "A widely used method for assigning atom-centered partial charges to organic molecules, particularly suitable for general force fields like GAFF (stands for Austin Model 1 - Bond Charge Correction). It involves a two-step process: first, charges are calculated using the computationally inexpensive semi-empirical AM1 quantum mechanical method; second, empirical Bond Charge Corrections (BCCs) are added to these initial charges based on atom and bond types to make them better reproduce the electrostatic potential obtained from higher-level QM calculations (typically HF/6-31G*). AM1-BCC aims to provide a balance between speed and accuracy for charging diverse organic ligands. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000204 ! ligand charge model
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000206 ! restrained electrostatic potential
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000206 ! restrained electrostatic potential

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000206
name: restrained electrostatic potential
def: "A popular method for deriving high-quality partial atomic charges for molecules, frequently used in conjunction with the AMBER force fields. It involves calculating the quantum mechanical electrostatic potential (ESP) on a grid of points around the molecule (typically using Hartree-Fock or DFT methods), and then fitting atom-centered point charges to reproduce this ESP using a least-squares algorithm. Crucially, 'restraints' (typically hyperbolic penalties) are applied during the fitting process to prevent unrealistically large charges on buried atoms and ensure transferability, often performed in multiple stages for chemical equivalence. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "RESP" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000204 ! ligand charge model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000207
name: custom script
def: "A script written by a researcher for one specific purpose in their own project, rather than distributed as part of a tool. It exists because no available program did quite what was needed. It is worth recording because a result may depend on it entirely, and it is usually the least documented part of a workflow. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001802 ! script
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000208
name: thermalization
def: "A step within the preparation or equilibration phase where the system's temperature is gradually raised or adjusted to the desired target temperature for the production simulation. This is typically done by coupling the system to a thermostat while velocities are assigned or rescaled. Proper thermalization ensures the system reaches the correct kinetic energy distribution before equilibration or production runs. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "heating" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000002 ! simulation preparation

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000209
name: equilibration
def: "A crucial phase in simulation preparation, following initial setup and minimization/thermalization, where the system is simulated under the target ensemble conditions (e.g., NVT or NPT) for a period to allow it to relax and reach a stable state. Key properties like temperature, pressure, density, potential energy, and RMSD are monitored to ensure the system is well-equilibrated before starting the production simulation intended for data collection. This phase allows the system to 'forget' its initial, potentially artificial starting configuration." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000002 ! simulation preparation
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000210
name: umbrella sampling
def: "A specific simulation execution technique used to enhance sampling along a chosen reaction coordinate or order parameter, often for calculating the potential of mean force (PMF) or free energy profile associated with a process like ligand unbinding or a conformational change. It involves running multiple simulations, each confined ('biased') by a potential (the 'umbrella') to sample a specific window along the coordinate, with subsequent analysis required to unbias the results and reconstruct the overall profile. It falls under the category of enhanced sampling methods." []
synonym: "US" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000003 ! simulation execution
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000211 ! production
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000211
name: production
def: "A stage of a simulation run in which data is collected, after the system has been prepared and allowed to settle. It is run under the conditions the study is about, for long enough that averages taken from it stop drifting. Only this part of a trajectory is normally analysed; the settling period before it is discarded. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000003 ! simulation execution

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000212
name: free energy calculation
def: "A type of simulation execution specifically designed to compute the free energy difference between two states (e.g., bound vs unbound, state A vs state B) or the free energy profile along a reaction coordinate. Common methods include Free Energy Perturbation (FEP), Thermodynamic Integration (TI), Umbrella Sampling (for PMFs), and sometimes methods based on endpoint analysis like MM/PBSA or MM/GBSA (though these are technically post-processing analyses estimating free energy). These calculations are computationally demanding but crucial for understanding binding affinities, reaction barriers, and relative stabilities. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000003 ! simulation execution

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000213
name: adaptive steered molecular dynamics
def: "An enhanced sampling simulation technique that enhances traditional steered molecular dynamics (SMD) to calculate binding affinities, mechanical unfolding pathways, and free energy profiles (e.g., Potential of Mean Force) in biomolecules. It works by breaking long pulling processes into a series of stages or windows along a specific reaction coordinate." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000003 ! simulation execution
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000214
name: STO-3G
def: "A minimal basis set in which each atomic orbital is approximated by 3 Gaussian functions added together. Gaussians are used because the integrals they require can be computed quickly, while the orbital shape they imitate cannot. It is by far the most used member of the family and appears in almost every textbook example. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000017 ! minimal basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000215
name: STO-4G
def: "A minimal basis set in which each atomic orbital is approximated by 4 Gaussian functions added together. Gaussians are used because the integrals they require can be computed quickly, while the orbital shape they imitate cannot. More Gaussians give a better imitation and no extra flexibility, because the number of orbitals is unchanged. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000017 ! minimal basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000216
name: visualization
def: "A process that turns molecular structures, trajectories and simulation data into pictures or animations. It is how a system is checked before a run, watched during one, and understood afterwards. Many errors in a prepared system are obvious on sight and invisible in any numerical check. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000004 ! simulation analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000217
name: AMBER
def: "A widely used package of biomolecular simulation software, encompassing both a suite of programs (AmberTools) for simulation preparation, analysis, and modeling, and a high-performance simulation engine (pmemd) for running MD and free energy calculations. AMBER is associated with a popular family of force fields (e.g., ff14SB, GAFF) and is extensively used for simulating proteins, nucleic acids, lipids, and organic molecules. It includes capabilities for classical MD, QM/MM, and various advanced simulation techniques." []
synonym: "AmberMD" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001664 ! software suite
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000218
name: AmberTools
def: "The freely available component of the AMBER software package, containing numerous programs and utilities for biomolecular simulation tasks excluding the main high-performance simulation engine (pmemd). AmberTools includes programs for system setup (tleap), trajectory analysis (cpptraj), structure preparation (antechamber), energy minimization and basic MD simulation (sander), QM calculations (sqm), free energy analysis (mmpbsa), and many others. It provides the essential infrastructure for preparing, analyzing, and modeling simulations run with AMBER or other programs." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001664 ! software suite
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000491 ! SYBYL
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000219
name: amber.sh
def: "This likely refers to a shell script used within the AMBER software ecosystem, possibly for setting up environment variables, running specific AmberTools programs, or launching simulations. It represents a specific script file used to execute or configure parts of the AMBER software suite. Its exact function would depend on the specific context or script content. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001570 ! metalpdb2mol2.py

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000220
name: protonation tool
def: "A software program that decides which acidic and basic groups in a structure carry a proton at a stated acidity. It predicts this from the local environment of each group, since experimental structures rarely show hydrogens. The answer changes the charge of the system and so changes everything a simulation does. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000490 ! structure preparation tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000240 ! pKa tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000221
name: PDB2PQR
def: "A widely used software tool (available as a web server and standalone package) that automates many common tasks in preparing biomolecular structures (from PDB files) for continuum electrostatics calculations or simulations. Its core functions include adding missing heavy atoms, adding and optimizing hydrogen atom positions, assigning charges and radii from a chosen force field, and determining residue protonation states at a specified pH using the PROPKA algorithm internally. It outputs the structure in PQR format (PDB with Charge and Radius)." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000223 ! generic protonation tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001600 ! reduce
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000222
name: ligand protonation tool
def: "A protonation tool specifically focused on determining the most likely ionization and tautomeric states of small molecule ligands, often in the context of drug discovery or protein-ligand binding studies. Predicting ligand protonation can be challenging due to diverse functional groups and potential binding site environmental effects." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000220 ! protonation tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000223 ! generic protonation tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000223
name: generic protonation tool
def: "A protonation tool designed for general use on biomolecular structures, typically proteins or nucleic acids obtained from sources like the PDB, to add hydrogens and determine appropriate protonation states for titratable residues at a given pH. These tools often focus on standard amino acids and sometimes common cofactors. PDB2PQR is a classic example of such a tool." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000220 ! protonation tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000224
name: Epik
def: "A software program in the Schrödinger suite that predicts which protonation and tautomeric forms of a small molecule are present at a given acidity, and how much each is favoured. It is run before docking or simulation, since the form chosen determines the molecule's charge and hydrogen bonding. It reports several forms with penalties rather than a single answer. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000222 ! ligand protonation tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000225
name: membrane packing tool
def: "A computational tool specifically designed to generate realistic initial configurations of lipid bilayers, often including embedded proteins, for use in membrane simulations. These tools arrange lipid molecules (and potentially cholesterol, solvent) according to specified lipid types, compositions, and area per lipid, ensuring proper packing density and avoiding steric clashes, which is challenging to do manually. Examples include PACKMOL-Memgen, CHARMM-GUI's Membrane Builder, and InflateGRO. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001556 ! system setup tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000259 ! topology and coordinate generation tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000226
name: PACKMOL-Memgen
def: "A specific tool or script that likely utilizes the general packing capabilities of PACKMOL (a program for creating initial configurations of molecules in defined regions) specifically for generating lipid bilayer structures for membrane simulations. Memgen might refer to a set of routines or scripts that work with PACKMOL to arrange lipids correctly around a pre-positioned membrane protein or to build pure bilayers with specific properties, automating the membrane generation process. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000225 ! membrane packing tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001927 ! CHARMM-GUI

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000227
name: membrane protein orientation tool
def: "A computational tool designed to predict or determine the likely orientation and transmembrane embedding depth of a protein structure within a lipid bilayer. Correctly positioning a membrane protein in the bilayer is a critical first step for setting up realistic membrane protein simulations. These tools often use algorithms based on hydrophobicity analysis, sequence features, or structural properties to find the most favorable position relative to the hydrophobic core and hydrophilic headgroup regions of the membrane." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001850 ! modeling and setup tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000228
name: memembed
def: "A specific computational tool or algorithm designed to predict the optimal orientation and insertion depth of a membrane protein within a lipid bilayer. It works from a knowledge-based statistical potential." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000227 ! membrane protein orientation tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000466 ! orientations of proteins in membranes
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000229
name: resolution-based simulation method
def: "A simulation method classified by how much structural detail it keeps, from every atom represented separately to many atoms grouped into 1 particle. The choice is the main control on what a simulation costs and on what can be seen in its result. A grouped model runs far longer and further, but nothing smaller than a group can be observed in it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "simulation type" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000308 ! simulation method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000230
name: all-atom molecular dynamics
def: "All-atom molecular dynamics (AA-MD) is a simulation technique where every individual atom in the molecular system, including hydrogen atoms and explicit solvent molecules, is represented. The motion of each atom is simulated over time by numerically integrating Newton's equations of motion using forces derived from a classical force field. This approach provides high structural detail but is computationally intensive, limiting accessible timescales and system sizes." []
synonym: "AA-MD" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000229 ! resolution-based simulation method
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000231
name: interaction energy model
def: "A model specifying which contributions make up the total potential energy of a system and what functional form each takes. It is the structure of a force field, as distinct from the numbers filling it. Two force fields with the same structure and different numbers behave differently; 2 with different structures cannot share numbers at all. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000006 ! model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000232
name: bond interaction energy
def: "A component of the potential energy stored in the stretching or compression of covalent bonds away from their preferred length. It is usually modelled as a spring, which rises steeply for small departures and never lets the bond break. That is why an ordinary force field cannot describe a chemical reaction. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000231 ! interaction energy model
is_a: MOLSIM:001294 ! energy
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000233 ! gravitational interaction energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000233
name: gravitational interaction energy
def: "A potential energy arising from the gravitational attraction between masses. At the scale of molecules it is smaller than the electrostatic interaction by roughly 36 orders of magnitude, so no molecular simulation includes it. The term exists for completeness in the list of fundamental interactions. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000231 ! interaction energy model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000234
name: electromagnetic interaction energy
def: "A potential energy arising from electromagnetic forces, covering both the attraction and repulsion between charges and the weaker interactions between magnetic moments. Every chemical interaction is ultimately of this kind, including bonding and dispersion. In a force field it appears explicitly as the electrostatic term and implicitly in all the others. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000231 ! interaction energy model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000235
name: nuclear interaction energy
def: "A potential energy arising from the strong and weak nuclear forces, which act only within an atomic nucleus over distances of about a femtometre. They hold the nucleus together and govern radioactive decay. They never appear in a molecular simulation, which treats each nucleus as a single unchanging particle. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000231 ! interaction energy model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000236
name: weighted histogram analysis method analysis
def: "A free energy analysis method that combines histograms from several biased simulations, such as the windows of an umbrella sampling run, into a single unbiased free energy profile. It solves self-consistently for the free energy offset of each window, which is what removes the bias. It needs the sampled ranges of neighbouring windows to overlap. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "WHAM" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000353 ! validation analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000237
name: potential of mean force analysis
def: "The Potential of Mean Force (PMF) method calculates the free energy profile of a system as a function of one or more specific coordinates, often called reaction coordinates or order parameters. It essentially describes the effective potential energy governing the system's behavior along those chosen coordinates, including entropic effects averaged over all other degrees of freedom. PMFs are crucial for understanding reaction mechanisms, binding processes, and conformational changes." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000615 ! free energy calculation analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000238
name: trajectory approach analysis
def: "A free energy analysis method distinguished by how many simulations its snapshots come from: 1 simulation of the complex, or separate simulations of the complex, the free receptor and the free ligand. The single-trajectory choice cancels internal energy terms and is cheaper, but it cannot capture conformational change on binding. The choice affects both cost and accuracy, so it must be recorded with the result. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000262 ! molecular mechanics Poisson Boltzmann surface area analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000239
name: single trajectory
def: "The single trajectory approach, often used in MM/PBSA and MM/GBSA calculations, involves running only one molecular dynamics simulation of the protein-ligand complex. Snapshots of the complex, the protein alone, and the ligand alone are then extracted directly from this single trajectory for endpoint free energy calculations. This reduces the computational cost compared to running three separate simulations but assumes the conformations sampled in the complex are representative for the free states." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000238 ! trajectory approach analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000240
name: pKa tool
def: "A computational tool specifically designed to predict the pKa values of ionizable groups (acidic or basic sites) within a molecule, typically amino acid residues in a protein or functional groups in a ligand. The pKa value indicates the pH at which a group is 50% protonated/deprotonated. These tools use various methods, ranging from simple empirical rules to sophisticated calculations involving continuum electrostatics (solving Poisson-Boltzmann equation) or QM methods, to estimate how the molecular environment shifts the intrinsic pKa of a group. PROPKA is a well-known example." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000490 ! structure preparation tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000241
name: PROPKA
def: "A widely used, fast empirical method and software tool for predicting the pKa values of ionizable residues in proteins and protein-ligand complexes. PROPKA uses information about the local structural environment (hydrogen bonds, desolvation, interactions with charged groups) to estimate shifts from standard reference pKa values, providing quick and often reasonably accurate pKa predictions crucial for determining protonation states at a given simulation pH. It's often integrated into other tools like PDB2PQR. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000240 ! pKa tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000242
name: MMPBSA.py
def: "A specific implementation of the MM/PBSA and MM/GBSA methods, distributed as a Python script within the AmberTools software suite. It reads trajectory files (from AMBER or other packages) and calculates binding free energies by computing the MM energy components (using sander or other external programs), the electrostatic solvation energy (using PB or GB solvers), and the nonpolar solvation energy (SASA-based), and combining them according to the MM/PBSA or MM/GBSA schemes. It automates this popular but approximate free energy estimation procedure. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000460 ! molecular mechanics Poisson-Boltzmann surface area tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000461 ! molecular mechanics Poisson-Boltzmann surface area module

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000243
name: in-silico mutagenesis tool
def: "A computational tool that allows researchers to simulate the effects of mutations (changing one amino acid residue to another) on the structure, stability, dynamics, or binding affinity of a protein. These tools typically take a protein structure, allow the user to specify mutations, and then use algorithms (often based on molecular mechanics energy functions, rotamer libraries, or machine learning) to model the structural changes and estimate the impact on stability (ddG) or other properties." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001850 ! modeling and setup tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000244
name: FoldX
def: "A popular empirical force field and associated software tool specifically designed for rapid calculation of protein stability changes upon mutation (in silico mutagenesis). FoldX uses an energy function that includes terms relevant to protein folding stability (like VdW interactions, solvation energy, hydrogen bonds, electrostatics, entropy) to estimate the folding free energy of a protein structure and, importantly, the change in folding free energy (ΔΔG) caused by single or multiple point mutations. It's widely used for predicting mutation effects and in protein design. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000243 ! in-silico mutagenesis tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000245
name: tunnel predictor tool
def: "A computational tool designed to identify and characterize pathways, channels, or tunnels within the structure of a macromolecule, typically a protein enzyme. These tunnels often connect a buried active site to the protein surface and are important for ligand entry/egress, solvent access, or product release. Tools like CAVER use geometric algorithms to find voids and pathways within the protein structure based on atomic coordinates. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000164 ! analysis tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000251 ! trajectory processing tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000246
name: CAVER
def: "A software tool for identifying and analyzing tunnels and channels in protein structures. CAVER uses computational geometry algorithms to explore the void space within a protein (or dynamic snapshots from a simulation) and simulates the introduction of probes to map the surface and the cavities of a target. It provides information on the location, dimensions (bottleneck radius), curvature, and physicochemical properties of identified tunnels." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000245 ! tunnel predictor tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000247
name: GROMACS
def: "A highly popular, versatile, and extremely fast open-source software package primarily designed for classical molecular dynamics simulations of biomolecules like proteins, lipids, and nucleic acids. Known for its computational efficiency, particularly on parallel architectures (CPUs and GPUs), GROMACS supports various force fields (including AMBER, CHARMM, OPLS, GROMOS families via ports), simulation protocols, enhanced sampling methods, and includes extensive tools for trajectory analysis. It is widely used in the academic and industrial research community. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001664 ! software suite

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000248
name: CHARMM
def: "A versatile and long-established software package for molecular simulation, encompassing molecular mechanics (MM) and dynamics (MD), as well as capabilities for QM/MM and complex modeling tasks (stands for Chemistry at HARvard Macromolecular Mechanics). CHARMM is associated with its own widely used force field family (e.g., CHARMM36) and provides extensive functionalities for preparing, running, and analyzing simulations, particularly for proteins, lipids, nucleic acids, and carbohydrates. Both a free academic version and a licensed version exist." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001664 ! software suite
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000249
name: ion parameterization
def: "The set of numbers defining how an ion interacts non-covalently in a force field, being its charge, its size and its interaction strength. Ions are hard to parameterise because a single set cannot match every measured property at once. The choice therefore depends on what the simulation is meant to reproduce. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000006 ! model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000250
name: Li and Merz 12-6
def: "A set of van der Waals parameters for common single-atom ions, fitted for the standard 12-6 form of the potential. Separate versions were fitted to reproduce different target properties, because no single set reproduces hydration free energy and ion-water distance at once. Which version was used must be recorded, since they are not interchangeable. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000249 ! ion parameterization

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000251
name: trajectory processing tool
def: "An analysis tool specifically focused on reading, processing, manipulating, and analyzing molecular dynamics trajectory files. These tools provide functionalities to read various trajectory formats, select specific atoms or frames, perform calculations over time (like RMSD, distances, angles), calculate average structures, remove solvent, re-image periodic boundaries, and write out modified trajectories or extracted data." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000164 ! analysis tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000252
name: CPPTRAJ
def: "A powerful command-line trajectory analysis program, distributed with AmberTools, capable of processing trajectories from many simulation packages (AMBER, GROMACS, NAMD, CHARMM, etc.) and performing a wide variety of analyses. Its capabilities include calculating structural metrics (RMSD, radius of gyration, distances, angles, dihedrals), analyzing hydrogen bonds, performing principal component analysis (PCA), clustering, calculating interaction energies, grid analysis, and extensive data manipulation and output options. It is a central tool for analyzing simulation data in the AMBER ecosystem and beyond." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000251 ! trajectory processing tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001579 ! pytraj
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000253
name: clustering algorithm
def: "An algorithm used in data analysis to group a set of objects (e.g., molecular conformations, data points) such that objects in the same group (cluster) are more similar to each other than to those in other groups. Clustering algorithms use various criteria and methods (e.g., distance-based, density-based, hierarchical) to identify inherent structures or patterns within unlabeled data. They are essential tools for exploring and understanding complex datasets. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000037 ! algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000254
name: hierarchical agglomerative bottom-up algorithm
def: "A specific type of clustering algorithm that builds a hierarchy of clusters starting with each data point as its own cluster and iteratively merging the two closest clusters until only one cluster (containing all points) remains. This process creates a tree-like structure (dendrogram) that can be cut at different levels to obtain different numbers of clusters. It provides a nested partitioning of the data based on similarity. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000253 ! clustering algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001707 ! DBSCAN clustering algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000255
name: static molecular interaction prediction modeling
def: "A modelling method that predicts how molecules will bind from their fixed structures alone, without simulating them moving. It scores how well 2 shapes fit together and how favourable the contacts are, rather than following the binding as it happens. It is fast enough to test millions of candidate molecules, which no simulation-based method can do. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000305 ! modeling method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000256
name: protein-protein docking analysis
def: "A computational method that predicts the structure of a complex formed when 2 proteins bind, given the structure of each on its own. It searches over the ways the 2 surfaces can meet and scores each arrangement. It is harder than docking a small molecule, because the contact area is far larger and both partners may change shape. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000255 ! static molecular interaction prediction modeling

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000257
name: endpoint free energy tool
def: "A software program that estimates a binding or solvation free energy from the initial and final states of a process alone, without simulating any path between them. It combines molecular mechanics energies with a continuum solvation model and a surface area term. It is much cheaper than an alchemical calculation and correspondingly less rigorous. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001564 ! free energy analysis tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001968 ! alchemical analysis tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000258
name: Antechamber
def: "A specific program, typically distributed as part of the AmberTools suite, designed to automatically assign atom types and calculate partial atomic charges for organic molecules, preparing them for use with molecular mechanics force fields like GAFF (General AMBER Force Field). Antechamber reads common molecular file formats and generates topology and parameter files needed for subsequent energy minimization or molecular dynamics simulations using programs like SANDER or PMEMD from the AMBER package. It is a crucial tool for preparing non-standard residues or ligands for simulation." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000172 ! topology and parameterization tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000259
name: topology and coordinate generation tool
def: "A tool used in the preparation stage of a simulation to generate the molecular topology file (defining atom types, bonds, angles, dihedrals, charges, non-bonded parameters according to a force field) and initial coordinate file for the system to be simulated. These tools typically take structural information (like a PDB file) and force field definitions as input and assemble the complete system description required by the simulation engine. tleap in AmberTools is a classic example. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001556 ! system setup tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000260
name: tleap
def: "A core program within the AmberTools suite used for building the topology (parameter) files and initial coordinate files for simulations with AMBER. Tleap reads force field definition files, structural fragments (like amino acid residues or solvent molecules), and user-provided structure files (e.g., PDB), then connects units (e.g., solvating a protein), adds counterions, and writes out the prmtop (topology) and inpcrd (coordinate) files necessary to run simulations with SANDER or PMEMD. It is an essential setup tool in the AMBER workflow. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "LEaP" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000259 ! topology and coordinate generation tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001584 ! xleap

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000261
name: binding free energy calculation analysis
def: "Binding free energy encompasses computational techniques specifically designed to estimate the Gibbs free energy change (ΔGbind) associated with the non-covalent binding of two molecules. Calculating binding free energy is crucial for predicting molecular interactions, understanding binding affinity in drug design, and validating docking poses. These methods range from approximate endpoint methods to more rigorous alchemical transformations." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000615 ! free energy calculation analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000262
name: molecular mechanics Poisson Boltzmann surface area analysis
def: "A free energy analysis method that estimates a binding free energy from snapshots of the bound and free states by adding 3 terms: the molecular mechanics energy in vacuum, the polar solvation free energy from the Poisson-Boltzmann equation, and a non-polar term scaled from the solvent-accessible surface area. It uses only the end states, so it needs no path of intermediates. That makes it much cheaper than an alchemical calculation and correspondingly less rigorous. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "MM/PBSA" EXACT []
synonym: "MMPBSA" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000326 ! endpoint free energy analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000263
name: molecular mechanics generalized Born surface area analysis
def: "A free energy analysis method that estimates a binding free energy in the same way as the Poisson-Boltzmann variant, but computes the polar solvation term with the generalized Born approximation instead of solving the Poisson-Boltzmann equation. The approximation is much faster and usually close enough for ranking related ligands. The molecular mechanics and surface-area terms are unchanged. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "MM/GBSA" EXACT []
synonym: "MMGBSA" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000326 ! endpoint free energy analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000264
name: linear interaction energy analysis
def: "A free energy analysis method that estimates a binding free energy from the change in the average electrostatic and van der Waals interaction energies of a ligand with its surroundings between the bound and the free state. The 2 changes are combined with empirical scaling coefficients rather than computed from first principles. It needs 1 simulation of the complex and 1 of the ligand in solution, which is far fewer than an alchemical route. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "LIE" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000326 ! endpoint free energy analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000265
name: alchemical free energy analysis
def: "A free energy analysis method that computes a free energy difference by simulating a reversible path between 2 states through intermediates that need not be physically realisable. The energy function is changed gradually along the path, for example turning a ligand's interactions off, and the free energy is recovered from how the system responds. Free energy perturbation and thermodynamic integration are the 2 standard ways of doing it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000261 ! binding free energy calculation analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000266
name: free energy perturbation analysis
def: "Free Energy Perturbation (FEP) is an alchemical method for calculating free energy differences between two states (A and B) by simulating a series of intermediate states that gradually transform A into B. The free energy change between adjacent intermediate states (λ and λ+Δλ) is calculated using the Zwanzig equation, which involves ensemble averaging the energy difference exponentiated. Summing the free energy changes over all intermediate steps yields the total free energy difference between A and B." []
synonym: "FEP" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000265 ! alchemical free energy analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000267
name: CHAP
def: "The Channel Annotation Package (CHAP) is a specialized software tool used to analyze the functional properties of pores and channels in membrane proteins. It calculates a detailed pore radius profile combined with a hydrophobicity profile to estimate the free energy barriers for water and ion permeation. This analysis allows researchers to visualize solvent behavior inside the pore and determine the conductive state of ion channels." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000245 ! tunnel predictor tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000268
name: binding free energy estimator 2 analysis
def: "Binding Free Energy Estimator 2 (BFEE2) is a comprehensive computational workflow designed to calculate protein-ligand binding free energies with 'chemical' accuracy. Its packages automate a rigorous multi-step process that includes enhanced sampling of the ligand's binding pose and the use of alchemical or geometrical free energy methods to compute the final affinity." []
synonym: "BFEE2" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000261 ! binding free energy calculation analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000269
name: non-equilibrium free energy analysis
def: "A free energy analysis method that recovers an equilibrium free energy difference from simulations deliberately driven away from equilibrium, by applying a fluctuation theorem to the work done. Many fast, irreversible transformations are run between the 2 states and the work distribution is analysed with Jarzynski's equality or Crooks' theorem. It can be cheaper than the equilibrium alchemical route because each transformation is short. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "NEQ" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000261 ! binding free energy calculation analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000270
name: Poisson-Boltzmann surface area
def: "A method (often abbreviated PB/SA) for calculating the free energy of solvation by combining two components: the electrostatic contribution calculated by numerically solving the Poisson-Boltzmann (PB) equation, and the non-polar contribution estimated as being proportional to the solvent-accessible surface area (SASA) of the solute. The PB equation provides a more rigorous treatment of continuum electrostatics than GB models by accounting for solute shape and charge distribution within a dielectric medium, while the SASA term models the cost of creating the solute cavity in the solvent and attractive solute-solvent van der Waals interactions. This method is often used for post-processing simulation trajectories to estimate binding free energies. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "PBSA" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000068 ! implicit solvent model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000271
name: generalized Born surface area
def: "A method (often abbreviated GB/SA) for calculating the free energy of solvation, similar to PB/SA, but using a Generalized Born (GB) model instead of the Poisson-Boltzmann equation to compute the electrostatic contribution. It combines the GB electrostatic energy with a non-polar energy term proportional to the solvent-accessible surface area (SASA). GBSA offers a computationally much cheaper alternative to PB/SA for estimating solvation free energies, suitable for use during simulations or large-scale analyses, though potentially less accurate depending on the GB implementation and system. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "GBSA" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000068 ! implicit solvent model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000272
name: radii set
def: "A defined collection or list that assigns specific atomic radius values to different atom types (defined by element, hybridization state, and sometimes chemical environment). These radii are used in various computational molecular modeling contexts, such as calculating molecular surfaces (like Van der Waals surface or Solvent Accessible Surface Area - SASA), estimating molecular volumes, defining cavities, or as parameters within implicit solvent models (e.g., determining effective Born radii for GB models or defining the dielectric boundary for PB models). Different radii sets exist (e.g., Bondi Van der Waals radii, radii optimized for solvation calculations like PARSE), derived from different physical principles or empirical fitting procedures. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000006 ! model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000273
name: bondi
def: "A set of van der Waals radii covering most of the periodic table, compiled by Bondi in the 1960s from crystallographic contact distances and gas-phase properties. It is the reference set most later radii sets were derived from by modification. It was not fitted for use in any solvation model. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000272 ! radii set
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000274 ! mbondi
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000274 ! mbondi

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000274
name: mbondi
def: "A set of van der Waals radii derived from the Bondi set with adjustments for particular atom types, chiefly hydrogen. The adjustments were made so that generalized Born solvation energies better match Poisson-Boltzmann ones. The prefix stands for modified. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000272 ! radii set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000275
name: mbondi2
def: "A specific version ('version 2') of modified Bondi radii, developed primarily for use within the AMBER simulation package, particularly in conjunction with specific Generalized Born (GB) implicit solvent models (like GB models with igb=2 or igb=5 in AMBER). These radii have been empirically optimized by adjusting values (especially for hydrogens, C, N, O, S, P) relative to the original Bondi set or earlier mbondi sets to yield improved accuracy in reproducing experimental solvation free energies of small molecules and potentially biomolecular energetics when using those particular GBSA methods. They represent a parameter set tuned for a specific computational model. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000272 ! radii set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000276
name: enthropic contributions mode analysis
def: "A thermodynamics analysis method that estimates the entropy term of the free energy from the vibrational modes of a system. It approximates entropy from how the system vibrates about an average structure, rather than counting states directly. Normal mode analysis and the quasiharmonic approximation are the 2 usual routes. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000309 ! entropy analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000277
name: quasiharmonic analysis
def: "A dynamics analysis method that estimates vibrational entropy from a trajectory by treating atoms as oscillating harmonically about their average positions. It diagonalises the mass-weighted covariance matrix of the atomic fluctuations to obtain effective frequencies, which are then put through the standard harmonic oscillator formulas. Unlike normal mode analysis it uses the sampled motion rather than a single minimum, so it captures anharmonic breadth as an effective frequency. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "QHA" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000276 ! enthropic contributions mode analysis
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000278 ! normal mode analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000278
name: normal mode analysis
def: "A dynamics analysis method that computes the vibrational modes and frequencies of a molecule by treating its motion as harmonic about a single energy minimum. It builds the matrix of second derivatives of the potential energy at that minimum and diagonalises it, giving collective modes as eigenvectors and their frequencies from the eigenvalues. Those frequencies are what a vibrational entropy estimate is built from. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "NMA" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000276 ! enthropic contributions mode analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000279
name: 1 trajectory approach
def: "A trajectory approach for end-point binding free energy calculations in which only the complex is simulated, and the receptor and ligand structures are taken from that same trajectory. Because every structure comes from 1 simulation, the internal energies of the parts cancel exactly, which removes most of the statistical noise. The price is that neither part can relax into the shape it would take on its own, so any real conformational change on binding is missed. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000238 ! trajectory approach analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000280
name: 3 trajectory approach
def: "A trajectory approach for end-point binding free energy calculations in which the complex, the free receptor and the free ligand are each simulated separately. Each component is therefore sampled in the state it is actually in, which captures any conformational change on binding. The cost is 3 simulations instead of 1, and much larger statistical noise, because the internal energies no longer cancel. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000238 ! trajectory approach analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000281
name: thermodynamic integration similarity calculation tool
def: "A type of utility program used to help set up a thermodynamic integration (TI) free energy calculation. It assesses the similarity between the starting and ending molecules of a planned alchemical transformation, often by calculating the overlap of their potential energies. The results from this tool are used to design an optimal pathway with an appropriate number of intermediate steps, which is crucial for ensuring the TI calculation will be accurate and reliable. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001556 ! system setup tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000282
name: ROCS
def: "A software program that compares molecules by overlaying their 3-dimensional shapes and chemical features rather than their bond connectivity. Two molecules built on different scaffolds can occupy the same space and bind the same site, which a structure comparison would miss. It is used to search for such replacements. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "rapid overlay of chemical structures" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000281 ! thermodynamic integration similarity calculation tool
is_a: MOLSIM:001684 ! match analysis tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000283 ! AMBER-FEW

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000283
name: AMBER-FEW
def: "This likely refers to FEW (Free Energy Workflow), a tool or set of scripts designed to automate and manage free energy calculations (like FEP or TI) specifically using the AMBER simulation package. Such workflows typically handle tasks like setting up the simulation legs (lambda windows), running the simulations, collecting data, and performing the final free energy analysis, aiming to simplify and standardize complex free energy calculation protocols within the AMBER environment. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000281 ! thermodynamic integration similarity calculation tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000284
name: OpenCalphad
def: "An open-source software library for thermodynamic calculations using the CALPHAD method, which models phase equilibria in multi-component systems from fitted Gibbs energy expressions. It is used in materials science and metallurgy to compute phase diagrams. It is a thermodynamic modelling tool rather than a molecular simulation one. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000281 ! thermodynamic integration similarity calculation tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000285
name: Brick-CFCMC
def: "This likely refers to a tool or module implementing the Continuous Fractional Component Monte Carlo (CFCMC) method, possibly within a specific software framework ('Brick'). CFCMC is an advanced Monte Carlo simulation technique used for calculating chemical potentials and free energies, particularly useful for phase equilibria or solvation free energy calculations, by allowing molecules to be gradually inserted or deleted via a fractional intermediate state. It's a specialized free energy calculation method distinct from standard TI or FEP. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000281 ! thermodynamic integration similarity calculation tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000286
name: thermodynamic integration approach
def: "A free energy analysis method distinguished by how a thermodynamic integration calculation is arranged: how the path between the states is built, how the intermediate states are spaced, and how the atoms of the 2 states are mapped onto each other. The choices affect cost and convergence but not the quantity being computed. Its subclasses each fix 1 of those choices. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000355 ! thermodynamic integration analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000287
name: standard thermodynamic integration
def: "A thermodynamic integration approach in which independent simulations are run at a set of fixed values of the coupling parameter and the results integrated numerically. Each simulation is independent of the others, so they can all be run at once. It is the arrangement every other variant is compared against. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000286 ! thermodynamic integration approach
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000288 ! extended thermodynamic integration

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000288
name: extended thermodynamic integration
def: "Extended Thermodynamic Integration likely refers to modifications or extensions of the standard TI protocol designed to handle more complex transformations, improve sampling efficiency, or apply TI in broader contexts beyond simple λ-coupling. This might include approaches combining TI principles with non-equilibrium work measurements, using specialized integration schemes along multiple reaction coordinates, or applying advanced sampling techniques at intermediate λ states. The specific meaning depends heavily on the context in which it is used. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000286 ! thermodynamic integration approach

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000289
name: dual-topology approach
def: "A thermodynamic integration approach in which the atoms of both states are present in the system at once, with each set coupled to the rest according to the coupling parameter and invisible to the other. It handles changes in connectivity that a single set of atoms cannot represent. It costs more, because both states are simulated throughout. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000286 ! thermodynamic integration approach

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000290
name: single-topology approach
def: "A thermodynamic integration approach in which 1 set of atoms has its types, charges and van der Waals parameters changed along the path, with atoms present in only 1 state grown or shrunk to nothing. It keeps the atom count fixed throughout. It is compact but awkward when the 2 states have different connectivity. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000286 ! thermodynamic integration approach

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000291
name: 1-step soft-core approach
def: "A thermodynamic integration approach that uses a soft-core potential to cover the whole transformation in 1 window, or very few. The soft-core form keeps the energy finite as atoms appear and disappear, which is what makes so few windows possible. It saves simulation time at the cost of relying heavily on the soft-core form being well behaved. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000286 ! thermodynamic integration approach

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000292
name: multi-step approach
def: "A thermodynamic integration approach that divides the path between the 2 states into several discrete windows, each sampled separately. Dividing it keeps the change between neighbouring windows small enough for the samples to overlap. It is the standard arrangement, and the alternative of a single window is a special case. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000286 ! thermodynamic integration approach

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000293
name: Hamiltonian replica exchange
def: "A thermodynamic integration approach in which the simulations at different coupling values run in parallel and periodically swap configurations, with the swap accepted or rejected by a Metropolis criterion. Swapping lets a configuration travel along the whole path, which relieves sampling bottlenecks at any single value. It converges faster than independent windows for the same total simulation time. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000286 ! thermodynamic integration approach

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000294
name: conveyor belt thermodynamic integration
def: "A thermodynamic integration approach in which several replicas move together along the coupling parameter, keeping a fixed spacing between them as the whole set advances. Coupling their movement means the path is traversed as a unit rather than sampled at fixed points. It is intended to reduce the number of replicas needed for a given accuracy. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "CBTI" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000286 ! thermodynamic integration approach

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000295
name: optimization of alchemical pathways
def: "A thermodynamic integration approach that chooses the number and the spacing of the intermediate coupling values so as to minimise the statistical error for a given amount of simulation. Even spacing is wasteful, because the integrand changes much faster near the end points than in the middle. The spacing may be fixed in advance or adjusted as the calculation runs. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000286 ! thermodynamic integration approach

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000296
name: free energy workflow
def: "A workflow that sets up, runs and analyses a free energy calculation as one automated sequence. It manages the many coupling states, their simulations and the collection of their output, which is otherwise done by hand and easily got wrong. It is what makes a campaign over many ligands practical. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "FEW" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000167 ! automation script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000298
name: thermodynamic integration extrapolation approach
def: "This category encompasses variants of TI calculations where the full integral ∫ 0 1 ⟨∂H/∂λ⟩λ dλ is estimated based on simulation data obtained only at or near the endpoints (λ=0 and λ=1) or at a very limited number of intermediate points, using some form of extrapolation. These approaches aim to significantly reduce the computational cost associated with simulating many intermediate λ states. The accuracy critically depends on the validity of the extrapolation scheme used for the specific system. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000355 ! thermodynamic integration analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000299
name: thermodynamic integration with linear extrapolation
def: "A thermodynamic integration approach that samples the integrand only at or near the 2 end points and assumes it varies linearly between them. Assuming linearity removes every intermediate simulation, which is where nearly all the cost lies. It is only valid where the integrand really is close to linear, which is uncommon. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000298 ! thermodynamic integration extrapolation approach
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000356 ! thermodynamic integration without linear extrapolation

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000300
name: free energy and molecular dynamics analysis
def: "Analysis techniques and calculated properties that are particularly characteristic of or frequently applied to data generated from molecular dynamics (MD) simulations, especially those aimed at calculating free energies or characterizing structural dynamics. These methods help interpret the complex time-series data produced by MD. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000400 ! statistical analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000301
name: Bennett acceptance ratio analysis
def: "A free energy analysis method that estimates the free energy difference between 2 thermodynamic states by combining the forward and reverse work distributions sampled in both. For a given amount of simulation data it gives the lowest-variance estimate available. It handles exactly 2 states; the multi-state generalisation is a separate term. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "BAR" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000300 ! free energy and molecular dynamics analysis
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000302 ! multi-state Bennett acceptance ratio analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000302
name: multi-state Bennett acceptance ratio analysis
def: "A free energy analysis method that combines data from simulations run at many thermodynamic states at once, and returns the free energy difference between any pair of them together with equilibrium averages. It uses every sample from every state rather than only neighbouring pairs, which is what makes it statistically optimal. It generalises the 2-state Bennett acceptance ratio. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "MBAR" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000300 ! free energy and molecular dynamics analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000303
name: linear dependence evaluation analysis
def: "A mathematical technique used to determine if a set of variables or vectors (e.g., descriptive coordinates or components from data analysis) are linearly related, meaning one can be expressed as a combination of the others. In simulation analysis, this is often used to check for redundancy in sets of collective variables or principal components derived from trajectory data. Identifying such dependencies can help simplify models or analysis. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000383 ! mathematical analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000304
name: experimental method
def: "An experimental method is a procedure carried out in a laboratory to make observations and gather data about the real world. As a type of method, it provides real-world data, such as a structure from X-ray crystallography or dynamics from nuclear magnetic resonance, which serves as a crucial input for validation of a computational simulation." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000109 ! method
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000305
name: modeling method
def: "A modeling method is a computational technique used to to predict, refine, and simulate 3D molecular arrangements. As a type of computational method, it typically involves predicting a static structure or interaction pose without simulating its dynamic behavior over time, such as in protein-ligand docking. These methods often employ search algorithms and scoring functions to evaluate and rank potential conformations based on criteria like shape complementarity and interaction energy." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000140 ! computational method
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000306
name: statistical package
def: "A software program built for statistical analysis, data handling, plotting and reporting. It is not specific to molecular simulation, but simulation output is data like any other and is often analysed in one. R and similar environments are the usual examples. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000164 ! analysis tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000307
name: R
def: "A widely used free software environment and programming language specifically designed for statistical computing and graphics. R provides a vast collection of packages contributed by users worldwide, covering nearly every area of statistical analysis, data visualization, and data science. In biomolecular simulation analysis, R is frequently used for plotting results (energy profiles, RMSD timeseries), performing statistical analysis on sampled properties, clustering conformations, and developing custom analysis workflows. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000306 ! statistical package
is_a: MOLSIM:001659 ! programming language
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001660 ! NAB
property_value: skos:closeMatch SWO:0000415

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000308
name: simulation method
def: "A computational method that reproduces how a system changes over time by advancing its state in small steps according to physical laws. It covers molecular dynamics and the enhanced sampling schemes built on it, and it produces a trajectory rather than a single answer. The choice of method fixes which physical laws apply and how the state is advanced. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000140 ! computational method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000309
name: entropy analysis
def: "A thermodynamics analysis method that estimates the contribution of disorder to the free energy of a molecular system. It works from the system's vibrational modes or from the spread of conformations in a trajectory, most often through normal mode analysis or the quasiharmonic approximation. The result is the term that must be subtracted from an energy to give a free energy. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000610 ! thermodynamics analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000310
name: obsolete plan specification
def: "OBSOLETE. A plan specification is a document or set of rules that describes how a study or experiment should be designed and carried out. As a type of information content entity, it represents the formal design of a computational experiment, such as the ligand pairs selection criteria for a relative binding free energy study. This specification outlines the rationale and criteria for selecting systems and parameters before the simulation or analysis is performed, ensuring a systematic and reproducible approach. This concept is often described in publications in sections titled \"Experimental Design,\" \"Study Protocol,\" \"Selection Criteria,\" or \"Computational Strategy.\"" []
comment: Retired 2026-08-12 as part of the COB alignment. IAO:0000104 plan specification says the same thing and is reached from IAO:0000030 information content entity, which MOLSIM already adopted. This retirement waited until the branch was cleaned: MOLSIM:000310 previously held four children of which three were not plans, and those moved to MOLSIM:002251 atom selection specification and MOLSIM:002252 selection criteria. Its one remaining child, MOLSIM:002155 simulation protocol, was re-parented onto IAO:0000104 in the same change.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: IAO:0000104

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000311
name: RMSD analysis
def: "A calculation that measures how much a molecule's shape has changed compared to a reference structure by quantifying the root-mean-square deviation of atomic coordinates after optimal superposition. This can be performed against a single static starting structure over time (1D trajectory), or calculated for every pair of frames in a simulation to produce a frame-to-frame comparative matrix, often displayed as a 2D heat map (2D RMSD analysis). It is the most common procedure for assessing simulation stability, monitoring conformational transitions, and serving as a metric for clustering algorithms." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000917 ! structural analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000312
name: RMSF analysis
def: "RMSF analysis is a calculation that identifies which parts of a molecule are the most flexible or wobbly. As a type of structural analysis, this method quantifies the mobility of individual atoms or residues by calculating the root-mean-square fluctuation of their positions around the time-averaged structure from a trajectory. The resulting per-residue RMSF values are directly comparable to crystallographic B-factors and are used to identify flexible loops, termini, or side chains." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000917 ! structural analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000313
name: distance RMSD analysis
def: "Distance RMSD analysis is a way to compare two molecular shapes based on their internal distances, without needing to align them first. As a type of structural analysis, this method calculates the root-mean-square deviation of a matrix of internal, pairwise atomic distances between two conformations, providing a metric of structural similarity that is independent of overall rotation and translation. This is particularly useful for comparing highly flexible molecules or for clustering based on internal conformational changes rather than global alignment." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000917 ! structural analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000314
name: radius of gyration analysis
def: "Radius of gyration analysis is a calculation that measures how compact or spread out a molecule is. As a type of structural analysis, this method quantifies the overall size and shape of a molecule or atomic selection by calculating the root-mean-square distance of its atoms from their common center of mass. Monitoring the radius of gyration over time is a standard procedure to track large-scale conformational changes, such as protein folding, unfolding, or domain movements." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000917 ! structural analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000315
name: ramachandran plot data
def: "A structural property consisting of the pair of backbone rotation angles for each residue in a protein. Plotted against each other across many residues, the pairs cluster into a few regions and leave most of the plot empty, because the remaining combinations put atoms on top of one another. A residue falling in an empty region is a sign that the structure is wrong there. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "Rama plot" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000316
name: potential of mean force
def: "A potential of mean force is an energy profile that shows how much energy it takes to move a molecule from one place to another. As a type of free energy, the Potential of Mean Force (PMF) is an output_data_descriptor that represents the free energy of a system as a function of one or more specific geometric coordinates, known as reaction coordinates. The PMF describes the energetic landscape along a pathway, with its minima representing stable states and its maxima corresponding to transition state energy barriers. This is commonly referred to in analysis outputs and publications as \"PMF,\" \"free energy profile,\" \"Potential of Mean Force,\" or \"pmf.dat.\"" []
synonym: "PMF" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001314 ! free energy property
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000317
name: JSON format
def: "JSON (JavaScript Object Notation) is a textual data interchange format with a simple syntax and low parsing cost. It is human-readable and it has a flexible structure. The JSON format is widely used and it is natively supported for parsing and serialization in most mainstream programming languages." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000910 ! general data format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000318 ! YAML format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393
property_value: skos:exactMatch format:3464

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000318
name: YAML format
def: "A text data format that records structured data using indentation to show nesting, with no brackets or closing tags. It is easy for a person to read and edit, which is why configuration and workflow files use it. Its reliance on indentation also means a misplaced space changes the meaning. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000910 ! general data format
property_value: skos:exactMatch format:3750

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000319
name: standard xyz format
def: "A standardized, minimalistic text-based file format used to store the Cartesian coordinates of atoms. It typically consists of a header line (atom count), a comment line, and one line per atom containing the element symbol and X, Y, Z positions. It may contain multiple frames (i.e. trajectory). The XYZ file format is widely supported by many programs, although many slightly different XYZ file formats coexist (Tinker XYZ, UniChem XYZ, etc.)." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001088 ! molecular structure format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000320
name: TOML format
def: "A text data format for configuration files, built from key and value pairs grouped into named sections. Its rules are deliberately narrow, so a file has only one possible reading. That is its advantage over more flexible formats, where the same text can be interpreted more than one way. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000910 ! general data format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000321
name: pickle format
def: "A binary data format that stores Python objects exactly as they exist in memory, so they can be written to a file and restored later. It preserves structures no general format can express. It can only be read back by Python, and reading one from an untrusted source can execute code, so it is unsuitable for exchange. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000910 ! general data format
property_value: skos:exactMatch format:4002

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000322
name: xvg format
def: "A text-based data file format generated by GROMACS analysis tools, designed for plotting 1D or 2D graphs. It contains tabular numerical data alongside metadata and formatting commands intended to be read directly by the Grace (xmgrace) plotting program." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000590 ! plot data format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000591 ! agr format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000323
name: element type
def: "An atom type that classifies an atom based strictly on its atomic number (number of protons in its nucleus), defining its fundamental chemical element. In structure files, it is typically represented by its standard IUPAC one- or two-letter chemical symbol (e.g., C, O, Fe)." []
synonym: "atomic element" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001763 ! atom type
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001764 ! neural network atom type
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000324
name: force field atom type
def: "An atom type assigned by a specific molecular mechanics force field that dictates the atom's non-bonded and bonded interaction parameters. It encodes not only the element, but also the atom's hybridization state, local chemical environment, and connectivity (e.g., distinguishing between an sp3 aliphatic carbon and an sp2 aromatic carbon). (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "mechanics atom type" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001763 ! atom type

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000325
name: monte carlo simulation
def: "A stochastic simulation method that relies on repeated random sampling to explore the configurational space of a molecular system. Unlike molecular dynamics, which integrates equations of motion over time, Monte Carlo generates a sequence of states by proposing random trial moves (such as atom displacements or molecular rotations) and accepting or rejecting them based on a thermodynamic probability criterion, typically the Metropolis algorithm. It is widely used for calculating equilibrium thermodynamic properties and sampling conformational ensembles. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "MC" EXACT []
synonym: "MC simulation" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000308 ! simulation method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000326
name: endpoint free energy analysis
def: "An endpoint free energy method is a computational approach that estimates the free energy difference between two states by analyzing simulations performed only at the beginning and end points of a process. Unlike more rigorous alchemical methods, it does not simulate the intermediate transformation pathway. Methods like MM/PBSA and MM/GBSA are popular endpoint methods that combine molecular mechanics energies with continuum solvent models to estimate binding free energies from trajectories of the bound and unbound states. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000265 ! alchemical free energy analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000327
name: active site focusing analysis
def: "Active site focusing is a strategy used in some endpoint free energy methods to improve the calculation by concentrating on the most important region of the system. This might involve performing the energy analysis only for residues within a certain distance of the binding site, or using a more detailed model for that region. For experts, this approach aims to reduce computational noise and focus the calculation on the energetic contributions that are most relevant to the binding event." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000262 ! molecular mechanics Poisson Boltzmann surface area analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000328
name: system setup modeling
def: "A system setup method is a procedure used to prepare a molecular system for a simulation. This involves all the steps required to build a complete and chemically correct model, such as adding solvent molecules, placing ions, and ensuring the correct atom ordering. For experts, these methods are critical for creating a valid starting point that accurately reflects the intended experimental conditions of the simulation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000305 ! modeling method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000329
name: ion placement analysis
def: "An ion placement method is a specific procedure used during system setup to add ions, such as sodium or chloride, to the simulation box. The primary purpose is usually to neutralize the total charge of the system and to mimic a specific salt concentration." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000328 ! system setup modeling
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000330
name: ion concentration calculation analysis
def: "An ion concentration calculation method is the procedure used to determine the exact number of positive and negative ions that need to be added to a simulation box to achieve a target salt concentration. This calculation must account for the volume of the box and the number of counter-ions already added to neutralize the solute molecule. For experts, accurately performing this calculation is a mandatory step for preparing a system that correctly models the desired ionic strength. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000329 ! ion placement analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000331
name: force field component
def: "One of the individual terms a force field's energy is built from, such as the bond, angle, rotation, van der Waals or electrostatic term. Each covers a distinct kind of interaction and their sum is the total energy. They are fitted together, which is why terms from different force fields cannot be mixed. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000006 ! model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000332
name: SCF convergence algorithm
def: "An optimization algorithm that drives the iterative solution for a molecule's electrons towards a stable answer. Simple repetition often oscillates between 2 near-solutions instead of settling, particularly for metals and open-shell systems. These algorithms extrapolate from previous iterations to break that oscillation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000407 ! optimization algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000408 ! energy minimization algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000333
name: level shifting algorithm
def: "A technique that helps a self-consistent field calculation converge by artificially raising the energy of the unoccupied orbitals. Widening the gap between occupied and unoccupied orbitals stops electrons moving between them from one iteration to the next, which is what causes oscillation. The shift is reduced to zero before the final answer is taken. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000332 ! SCF convergence algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000334
name: fit color Tversky
def: "A similarity measure that specifically compares the chemical features and atom types between molecules, focusing on their functional groups and chemical properties rather than their shape. This measure evaluates the similarity of atomic properties and chemical functionalities between molecules, making it valuable for identifying compounds with similar chemical behavior. It complements shape-based similarity measures in molecular comparison workflows. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000076 ! Tversky index algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000335
name: restrained subset dynamics
def: "Restrained subset dynamics is a simulation method where restraining potentials are applied to only a specific part, or subset, of the molecular system. This allows the selected atoms to be held fixed or guided, while the rest of the system is free to move and respond dynamically." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000364 ! restrained simulation method
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000336
name: multiscale simulation method
def: "A simulation method that combines 2 or more levels of description within one system, such as quantum mechanics for a reacting group and a force field for everything else. The expensive description is applied only where it is needed. The difficulty is always the boundary, where the 2 descriptions must be joined without introducing artefacts. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000308 ! simulation method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000337
name: Mulliken charge analysis
def: "A method that assigns charge to atoms by dividing each basis function's electron population between the atoms its functions are centred on, splitting shared contributions equally. It is the cheapest such method and requires no fitting. Its values depend strongly on the basis set used, so they are unreliable for anything beyond a rough comparison. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000674 ! charge analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000338
name: isotropic position scaling barostat
def: "A pressure control algorithm that holds pressure steady by scaling all 3 box dimensions by the same factor, so the box changes size but not shape. It suits a system with no preferred direction, such as a protein in water. It is the wrong choice for a membrane, where the plane of the bilayer and the direction across it behave differently. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000039 ! barostat algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000339
name: numerical integration
def: "A numerical method that advances a differential equation forward in small steps, because no exact solution can be written down. The equations of motion for more than 2 interacting particles are of that kind, so every molecular dynamics simulation is doing this. The size of the step controls both the accuracy and the cost. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000340 ! integration analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000340
name: integration analysis
def: "A class of mathematical techniques specifically used in molecular dynamics simulations to numerically solve the equations of motion governing particle movement. These algorithms approximate the positions and velocities of atoms at future discrete time steps based on the forces acting upon them at the current step. They are fundamental for generating the trajectory of the molecular system over time. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000383 ! mathematical analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000341
name: auto-correlation analysis
def: "Auto-correlation analysis examines the correlation of a time series (a sequence of data points ordered in time, e.g., from a simulation) with lagged versions of itself. It helps identify repeating patterns, seasonality, or the characteristic timescale (memory) over which values in the series are statistically dependent. The primary output is the Auto-Correlation Function (ACF)." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000342 ! correlation analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000342
name: correlation analysis
def: "A dynamics analysis method that measures the statistical relationship between fluctuating quantities recorded during a simulation. It covers both how a single property relates to itself after a delay and how 2 different properties vary together or in opposition. The results reveal which motions are linked and over what timescales. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000400 ! statistical analysis
is_a: MOLSIM:000939 ! dynamics analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000343
name: anisotropic position scaling barostat
def: "An anisotropic position scaling barostat is a pressure control algorithm that allows the lengths of the three simulation box vectors to fluctuate independently to maintain a constant pressure tensor. This allows the shape of the simulation box to change, which is necessary for simulating systems that are not uniform in all directions, such as lipid membranes or solid crystals." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000039 ! barostat algorithm
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000344
name: Welch's T-test analysis
def: "A statistical test that judges whether 2 groups have different averages, without assuming they scatter by the same amount. The older form of the test assumes equal scatter, which independent simulations rarely have. It is the form to use when comparing runs of different lengths or from different conditions. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000124 ! statistical test analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000345
name: auto-correlation coefficients analysis
def: "Auto-correlation coefficients are the numerical values that make up the Auto-Correlation Function (ACF) at different time points (τ). Each coefficient measures the linear correlation between the time series and the same series shifted by τ time steps." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000341 ! auto-correlation analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000346
name: partial auto-correlation coefficients analysis
def: "A statistical method that measures how strongly a series relates to itself a given number of steps back, after removing everything explained by the steps in between. Plain autocorrelation cannot distinguish a real long-range relationship from one carried indirectly through the intervening points. Removing the intermediate effect is what this adds. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000345 ! auto-correlation coefficients analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000347
name: regression analysis
def: "A statistical method that fits a relationship between an outcome and one or more explanatory quantities. It gives both the shape of the relationship and how much of the variation it accounts for. It is how a simulated quantity is checked against a measured one across a set of systems rather than one at a time. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000400 ! statistical analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000348
name: hypothesis testing analysis
def: "A statistical method that judges whether an observed difference is larger than would be expected from sampling alone. It computes how likely the observed result would be if there were no real difference, and that likelihood is compared against a chosen threshold. It answers whether a difference is real, not whether it is large enough to matter. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000400 ! statistical analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000349
name: resampling method
def: "A statistical method that estimates how uncertain a result is by repeatedly drawing new samples from the data already collected and recomputing the result from each. It replaces an assumption about how the data are distributed with computation. That makes it usable where no standard formula applies, which is most of simulation output. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000400 ! statistical analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000350
name: small angle x-ray scattering
def: "An experimental technique that measures the X-rays scattered at small angles by a sample in solution, and from that pattern infers the overall size and shape of the molecules in it. Because it works in solution it reports on the ensemble actually present, not on 1 crystallised conformation. It gives low-resolution shape rather than atomic positions. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "SAXS" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000990 ! small-angle scattering

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000351
name: obsolete similarity and divergence analysis
def: "OBSOLETE. Similarity and divergence measures are mathematical quantities used to compare two probability distributions, datasets, or sequences, quantifying how similar or different they are. Similarity measures indicate closeness (higher values mean more similar), while divergence measures quantify the difference or 'distance' between them (higher values mean more different). These are used in various fields including information theory, statistics, and bioinformatics (e.g., comparing conformational ensembles)." []
comment: Retired 2026-08-13. It held a single child, MOLSIM:000118 Jensen-Shannon divergence analysis, which now sits directly under MOLSIM:000400 statistical analysis beside correlation analysis and hypothesis testing analysis. Three faults made it worth removing rather than renaming: the label joined two ideas with and, which reviewers raised as a pattern in August 2026; it grouped one term, so it explained nothing; and its definition described similarity and divergence measures, meaning quantities, while the class was labelled an analysis and parented under statistical analysis. The same shape as MOLSIM:000918 global structure analysis, retired on 2026-08-08.
is_obsolete: true

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000352
name: binpos format
def: "The binpos (\"binary position\") format is binary file format from Amber that stores atomic coordinate frames (i.e. a trajectory) from a molecular dynamics simulation." []
synonym: ".binpos" EXACT []
synonym: "Scripps binpos format" EXACT []
synonym: "Scripps Research Institute BinPos" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001090 ! molecular trajectory format
property_value: IAO:0000116 "The Scripps Research Institute is named upstream as the originator of the format. Recorded here rather than in the definition, which was verified on 2026-09-18 without it. Source: EDAM 1.25, class format_3885 BinPos (http://edamontology.org/format_3885)." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393
property_value: skos:exactMatch format:3885

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000353
name: validation analysis
def: "A method used to check whether the results or models generated by biomolecular simulations are accurate, physically realistic, and reliable. These techniques assess the quality of simulation outputs by comparing them against known experimental data or established theoretical principles. Their goal is to ensure the simulation provides a meaningful representation of the molecular system being studied. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000400 ! statistical analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000354
name: obsolete p-value
def: "OBSOLETE. A type of statistical property that represents the probability of obtaining results at least as extreme as the observed results, assuming that the null hypothesis is true. A small p-value (typically < 0.05) is used to argue that the observed result is statistically significant. It is a fundamental concept in hypothesis testing. This is a standard output of statistical tests." []
comment: Obsoleted 2026-07-29: duplicated STATO:0000700. STATO is the canonical OBO home for statistics; reused in place of this term.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: STATO:0000700

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000355
name: thermodynamic integration analysis
def: "A free energy analysis method that computes the free energy difference between 2 states by simulating a series of intermediate states along a coupling parameter and integrating the average derivative of the energy with respect to that parameter. The path between the states does not have to be physically realisable, only reversible. The formula belongs in an editor note rather than in the definition, where mathematical notation does not render. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "TI" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000265 ! alchemical free energy analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000356
name: thermodynamic integration without linear extrapolation
def: "A thermodynamic integration approach in which the integrand is sampled at intermediate values of the coupling parameter rather than only at the end points, so the integral is computed from the sampled curve. Sampling the middle costs a simulation at each intermediate state and removes the assumption that the curve is a straight line. It is the arrangement nearly all thermodynamic integration uses. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000298 ! thermodynamic integration extrapolation approach

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000357
name: visualization analysis
def: "A visualization method is a technique used to create a graphical representation of molecular data, allowing scientists to see and interact with their results. This includes generating 3D images of molecules, animating simulation trajectories, or plotting data in the form of 2D graphs. For researchers, visualization is an indispensable method for understanding complex structural information and communicating findings. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000026 ! analysis method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000358
name: worm plot visualization analysis
def: "A worm plot is a visualization method that displays a collection of superimposed molecular structures from a simulation or an NMR ensemble. Each structure is typically represented as a smooth tube or \"worm\" tracing the path of the protein backbone. This method provides a clear visual impression of the conformational variability and dynamic fluctuations within the molecular ensemble. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000357 ! visualization analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000359
name: helical density map visualization analysis
def: "A helical density map is a visualization method used to represent the three-dimensional distribution of atoms within a helical structure, averaged over time from a simulation. It creates a 3D grid where the value at each point represents the probability of finding an atom, which can then be displayed as a contoured surface. This method is particularly useful for analyzing the average structure and packing of molecules like DNA or alpha-helical proteins. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000357 ! visualization analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000360
name: Laplacian mapping ion placement analysis
def: "A computational method for placing ions, like sodium or chloride, into a simulation box containing a charged molecule like a protein. It works by calculating the electrostatic potential around the molecule and then using a mathematical operator, the Laplacian, to identify the most electrostatically favorable positions for the ions to be placed. This approach is more physically realistic than simply placing ions randomly, as it positions them in regions where they are most likely to be found, such as near oppositely charged amino acid residues." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000329 ! ion placement analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000361
name: adaptively biased molecular dynamics
def: "An enhanced sampling simulation technique that enhances traditional biased molecular dynamics to calculate binding affinities, mechanical unfolding pathways, and free energy profiles (e.g., Potential of Mean Force) in biomolecules. It applies an evolving, position-dependent energy bias to help the system escape local minima along a specific reaction coordinate." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000362
name: driven adaptively biased molecular dynamics
def: "Driven adaptively biased molecular dynamics (d-ABMD) is an enhanced sampling technique that combines two approaches to explore a specific molecular process. It uses an adaptive biasing potential, like in metadynamics, to overcome energy barriers, while simultaneously applying an external \"driving\" force to guide the system along a predefined reaction coordinate. This dual approach is particularly effective for efficiently calculating the free energy profile of a complex conformational change that is too slow to occur spontaneously." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000361 ! adaptively biased molecular dynamics
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000363
name: redox potential replica-exchange molecular dynamics
def: "Redox potential replica-exchange molecular dynamics is a specialized version of the REMD method where the different parallel simulations are run at different electrochemical redox potentials, rather than different temperatures. This allows the system to efficiently sample different oxidation states in a simulation that is coupled to an electron bath." []
synonym: "redox potential REMD" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000858 ! replica-exchange molecular dynamics
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000364
name: restrained simulation method
def: "A restrained simulation is a type of simulation where an additional, artificial energy potential is applied to guide the system's motion. These restraints can be used to force a molecule to adopt a certain conformation, to prevent it from moving too far, or to incorporate experimental data into the simulation. Restraints are a powerful tool for targeted sampling, structure refinement, and calculating potentials of mean force." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000308 ! simulation method
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000365
name: electron microscopy map restraint method
def: "An electron microscopy map restraint method is a simulation technique where the simulation is guided by a three-dimensional density map obtained from an electron microscopy experiment. An additional energy term is added that penalizes conformations where the simulated atoms do not fit well into the experimental density. For structural biologists, this method is a powerful tool for refining low-resolution experimental structures into high-resolution, physically realistic atomic models." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000364 ! restrained simulation method
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000366
name: finite-difference analysis
def: "A numerical method that solves a differential equation by replacing each derivative with the difference between values at nearby grid points. The continuous problem becomes a large set of simultaneous equations, one per grid point. It is how the Poisson-Boltzmann equation is solved for a molecular shape. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000367 ! numerical analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000367
name: numerical analysis
def: "A branch of mathematics concerned with computing approximate answers to problems that cannot be solved exactly. Almost every step of a simulation rests on it, because the equations of motion and the integrals of statistical mechanics have no closed-form solutions for a real molecule. Its central concern is how large the approximation error is and whether it accumulates. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000026 ! analysis method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000368
name: immersed interface analysis
def: "A numerical method for solving a differential equation across a boundary where the solution or its derivative jumps, such as the surface between a solute and continuum solvent. It modifies the finite-difference stencil near the boundary to take the known jump conditions into account, instead of smoothing over them. In this field it is used to solve the Poisson-Boltzmann equation accurately at the molecular surface. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000367 ! numerical analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000369
name: low-mode conformational search
def: "An enhanced sampling method that generates new conformations by displacing a structure along its slowest collective modes rather than at random. Those modes are the directions in which the molecule moves most easily, so displacing along them reaches genuinely different conformations at low energy cost. Random displacement mostly produces strained structures that are immediately rejected. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000370
name: constant pH replica-exchange molecular dynamics
def: "A simulation method that runs several constant pH simulations in parallel, each at a different pH or temperature, and periodically swaps configurations between them. The swaps let a configuration stuck in one protonation state escape by way of conditions where that state is unfavourable. It converges protonation populations far faster than a single constant pH run. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000858 ! replica-exchange molecular dynamics

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000371
name: NMR analysis
def: "NMR analysis in a simulation context refers to the methods used to calculate NMR-related properties from a molecular dynamics trajectory. This allows for a direct comparison between the simulation results and experimental data from Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (NMR) spectroscopy. This includes calculating observables like J-couplings, nuclear Overhauser effects (NOEs), and relaxation times, which are crucial for validating the accuracy of the simulation." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000917 ! structural analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000372
name: r-6 weighted distance averaging analysis
def: "The r-6 weighted distance averaging is a specific calculation method used in NMR analysis to compute an effective distance from a simulation trajectory that can be directly compared to an experimental nuclear Overhauser effect (NOE). Because the NOE intensity is proportional to the inverse sixth power of the distance between two protons, a simple average of the distance is incorrect. For experts, performing this <r⁻⁶>⁻¹/⁶ averaging is the physically correct way to back-calculate NOE-derived distances from a dynamic ensemble of structures." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000371 ! NMR analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000373
name: replica-exchange self-guided Langevin dynamics
def: "This is an enhanced sampling method that combines the replica-exchange method with self-guided Langevin dynamics (SGLD). It runs multiple SGLD simulations in parallel, typically at different temperatures, and attempts to swap their coordinates. This combination aims to leverage the accelerated local exploration of SGLD with the global barrier-crossing capability of replica-exchange for very efficient conformational sampling." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000858 ! replica-exchange molecular dynamics
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000374
name: force field parameterization modeling
def: "A force field parameterization method is the systematic procedure used to derive the numerical values, or parameters, for a force field. This process involves fitting the parameters of the force field's energy functions to reproduce high-quality data, which can come from quantum mechanical calculations or experimental measurements. For experts, the parameterization method is the core of force field development and determines the accuracy and domain of applicability of the resulting model. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000305 ! modeling method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000375
name: Seminario method modeling
def: "A parameterization method that derives bond and angle force constants from the matrix of second derivatives of the energy computed quantum mechanically. It projects that matrix onto each bond and angle direction in turn, which separates contributions that a simple fit would confuse. It is the standard way parameters are obtained for a molecule no existing force field covers. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000374 ! force field parameterization modeling

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000376
name: temperature replica-exchange molecular dynamics
def: "Temperature replica-exchange molecular dynamics is the standard and most common form of the REMD method. It involves running multiple parallel simulations at a range of different temperatures and attempting to swap their coordinates. This is a robust and widely used method for enhancing the sampling of systems with complex energy landscapes, such as in protein folding simulations." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000858 ! replica-exchange molecular dynamics
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000377
name: well-tempered adaptively biased molecular dynamics
def: "Well-Tempered Adaptively Biased Molecular Dynamics (WT-ABMD) is an enhanced sampling technique in computational chemistry. It merges the features of adaptively biased molecular dynamics (ABMD) and well-tempered metadynamics to calculate the free energy surface of complex molecular systems while avoiding over-exploration of high-energy states." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000361 ! adaptively biased molecular dynamics
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000378
name: Z-matrix parameterization modeling
def: "A parameterization method in which the molecule's geometry is expressed in internal coordinates, as bond lengths, angles and rotations, and parameters are fitted in those terms. Fitting in internal coordinates makes each parameter correspond to one geometric feature. It is more laborious than fitting in Cartesian coordinates and gives parameters that are easier to interpret and transfer. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000374 ! force field parameterization modeling

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000379
name: ZLM density fitting
def: "A density fitting method that expands the electron density in spherical harmonic functions centred on each atom, so that electron repulsion integrals can be computed more cheaply. Fitting the density rather than computing every integral exactly is what makes large density functional calculations affordable. The error it introduces is small and controllable. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000367 ! numerical analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000380
name: force interpolation analysis
def: "A force interpolation method is a numerical technique used in some simulation algorithms to estimate the forces on atoms without calculating them directly at every step. This is often done by calculating the forces on a coarser grid and then interpolating these forces to the actual atomic positions. For experts, this method can be used in some multiple-time-stepping algorithms to reduce the computational cost of the force calculation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000367 ! numerical analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000381
name: adaptive thermostat
def: "A temperature control algorithm that changes its own coupling strength as the simulation proceeds. Strong coupling is wanted while a system is still far from its target and unwanted once it has settled, and a fixed setting cannot do both. It adjusts so that the early phase is fast and the later dynamics are left alone. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000038 ! thermostat algorithm
property_value: MOLSIM:002254 "ntt=6" xsd:string {dcterms:source="MOLSIM:000217"}
property_value: MOLSIM:002254 "ntt=7" xsd:string {dcterms:source="MOLSIM:000217"}
property_value: MOLSIM:002254 "ntt=8" xsd:string {dcterms:source="MOLSIM:000217"}

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000382
name: simulation control algorithm
def: "An algorithm that governs how a simulation advances and how its physical conditions are held steady. It covers the integrator that moves the atoms forward in time, and the thermostats and barostats that keep temperature and pressure at their targets. These are the algorithms that determine what ensemble a simulation actually samples. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000037 ! algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000383
name: mathematical analysis
def: "The use of defined mathematical procedures to process data and extract quantities from it. It covers fitting, transforming, integrating and differentiating the output of a simulation. It is distinguished from the domain-specific analyses by making no assumption about what the numbers represent. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000367 ! numerical analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000384
name: force calculation algorithm
def: "An algorithm that computes the force on every atom at each step, from the positions of the atoms and the force field. It dominates the cost of a simulation, because the non-bonded part must consider a great many pairs. Almost every optimisation in a simulation engine is aimed at this step. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000382 ! simulation control algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000385
name: Mulliken Ewald summation
def: "An Ewald summation method in which the charge distribution is represented by charges assigned to atoms by Mulliken population analysis rather than by fixed force field charges. It allows a quantum mechanical charge distribution to be handled by the standard periodic electrostatics machinery. The accuracy is limited by how well atom-centred charges can stand in for the real distribution. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000428 ! Ewald summation

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000386
name: QM-QM derivative calculation analysis
def: "A numerical method for computing energy derivatives in a calculation with more than one quantum layer, such as a high-accuracy method inside a cheaper one. The derivatives of each layer must be combined so that the force on a shared atom is consistent. Getting the combination wrong produces forces that do not match the energy, and a simulation that drifts. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000367 ! numerical analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000387
name: QM Ewald treatment
def: "An application of Ewald summation to a system whose charge distribution comes from a quantum mechanical calculation rather than from fixed charges. It is needed because a quantum region in a periodic box interacts with its own images, which must be accounted for rather than ignored. The difficulty is that the charge distribution changes as the calculation proceeds. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000428 ! Ewald summation

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000388
name: QM/MM simulation
def: "A multiscale simulation in which a small chemically active region is described by quantum mechanics and the rest by a force field. It is what allows a reaction inside an enzyme to be modelled, since a force field cannot break bonds and a quantum treatment of the whole protein is impossible. The difficulty is always the boundary, where the 2 descriptions must be joined without artefacts. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "QM/MM" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000308 ! simulation method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000389
name: hot spot adaptive QM/MM
def: "A QM/MM method in which the quantum region follows the chemistry, expanding to include whatever is currently involved in the reaction. It differs from a solvent-adaptive scheme in that the region moves with the reactive event rather than merely exchanging solvent. It suits a reaction whose site shifts along a chain or across a surface. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000388 ! QM/MM simulation

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000390
name: isotropic periodic sum method
def: "A general term for a method that calculates the long-range forces in a simulation with periodic boundary conditions, assuming the system is uniform in all directions. It involves summing up the interactions between a particle and all of its periodic images in a way that correctly accounts for the infinite, repeating nature of the simulated system. Standard algorithms like the Ewald sum or Particle Mesh Ewald (PME) are specific implementations of this principle, which is essential for accurately modeling the electrostatics of a bulk liquid. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000053 ! electrostatic interaction algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000391
name: semi-isotropic position scaling barostat
def: "A semi-isotropic position scaling barostat is a pressure control algorithm that couples the scaling of the x and y dimensions of the simulation box together, while allowing the z dimension to fluctuate independently. This method is specifically designed for simulating planar systems like lipid bilayers, where the pressure in the plane of the membrane is different from the pressure perpendicular to it." []
synonym: "semi-isotropic pressure scaling barostat" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000039 ! barostat algorithm
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000392
name: direct sum Coulomb method
def: "An electrostatic method that computes the force between every pair of charged atoms explicitly and adds them all up. It is exact for a system with no periodic images, and its cost grows with the square of the number of atoms. That growth is why it is used only for small or non-periodic systems. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000053 ! electrostatic interaction algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000393
name: self-guided Langevin dynamics
def: "Self-guided Langevin dynamics (SGLD) is an enhanced sampling method that accelerates conformational searching by adding a memory-dependent guiding force to the standard equations of motion. This guiding force is calculated from a local average of the forces the system has recently experienced, effectively pushing the system to explore new regions faster. SGLD enhances sampling by reducing random fluctuations and promoting more directed exploration of the potential energy surface." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000394
name: generalized Langevin equation self-guided Langevin dynamics
def: "A simulation method that adds a guiding force built from a running average of the system's recent motion, so that slow collective movements are amplified while fast local ones are not. Amplifying the slow motions lets a simulation cross barriers it would otherwise take far longer to reach. Results must be corrected afterwards to recover the unbiased distribution. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000393 ! self-guided Langevin dynamics

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000395
name: accelerated molecular dynamics
def: "Accelerated molecular dynamics is a special type of simulation whose scope is to overcome the timescale limitations of classical molecular dynamics. It works by adding a \"boost\" to the system's energy, effectively lowering the energy barriers that separate different molecular conformations. For experts, aMD is an enhanced sampling method that adds a non-negative, history-independent bias potential when the system's potential energy is below a certain threshold, allowing for the recovery of canonical averages through energetic reweighting." []
synonym: "aMD" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000843 ! molecular dynamics
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000396
name: Gaussian accelerated molecular dynamics
def: "Gaussian accelerated molecular dynamics (GaMD) is an enhanced sampling method that speeds up simulations by adding a boost potential that has a Gaussian distribution. This method smooths the potential energy surface, allowing the system to more easily escape from local energy minima." []
synonym: "GaMD" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000397
name: ligand Gaussian accelerated molecular dynamics
def: "Ligand Gaussian accelerated molecular dynamics is a specific application of the GaMD method focused on enhancing the sampling of a ligand's movement and conformational changes. The boost potential is applied in a way that specifically accelerates the dynamics of the ligand, its binding site, or both." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000396 ! Gaussian accelerated molecular dynamics
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000398
name: dual-boost ligand Gaussian accelerated molecular dynamics
def: "Dual-boost ligand Gaussian accelerated molecular dynamics (Dual-boost LiGaMD) is a variant of the GaMD method where two separate boost potentials are applied simultaneously to enhance the sampling of ligand binding and unbinding pathways. For example, one boost is applied to the dihedral angles of the ligand to enhance its conformational sampling, while a second boost is applied to the total potential energy of the system to accelerate its overall dynamics." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000397 ! ligand Gaussian accelerated molecular dynamics
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000399
name: peptide Gaussian accelerated molecular dynamics
def: "Peptide Gaussian accelerated molecular dynamics is a specific application of the GaMD method tailored to enhance the conformational sampling of peptides. The boost potential is applied to accelerate the slow folding and conformational transition events that are characteristic of flexible peptide molecules." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000396 ! Gaussian accelerated molecular dynamics
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000400
name: statistical analysis
def: "A method that uses probability theory to collect, summarise and draw conclusions from data. It is what puts an uncertainty on a value and what decides whether a difference between 2 results is real. Simulation output is a sample, so nothing taken from it is complete without one. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000367 ! numerical analysis
property_value: skos:closeMatch operation:2238

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000401
name: dual-boost peptide Gaussian accelerated molecular dynamics
def: "Dual-boost peptide Gaussian accelerated molecular dynamics (Dual-boost PepGaMD) is a variant of GaMD where two separate boost potentials are applied simultaneously to enhance the sampling of peptides. One boost is typically applied to the peptide's dihedral angles to accelerate local conformational changes, while the second is applied to the total system potential to overcome larger energy barriers." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000399 ! peptide Gaussian accelerated molecular dynamics
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000402
name: ligand Gaussian accelerated molecular dynamics 3
def: "Ligand Gaussian accelerated molecular dynamics 3 (GaMD3) is a recent and refined version of an enhanced sampling method used to accelerate the simulation of ligand binding and unbinding events. It applies a smoothly varying boost potential to the system's energy landscape, allowing the ligand to escape from deep binding pockets and explore different conformations more rapidly. This third-generation implementation includes improved algorithms for updating the boost potential, aiming for more robust and efficient sampling of complex ligand dynamics." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000397 ! ligand Gaussian accelerated molecular dynamics
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000403
name: protein-protein interaction Gaussian accelerated molecular dynamics
def: "This is an application of the GaMD method specifically designed to enhance the sampling of protein-protein binding and unbinding events. The boost potential is applied to the potential energy of the entire complex to accelerate the slow association and dissociation processes." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000396 ! Gaussian accelerated molecular dynamics
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000404
name: dual-boost protein-protein interaction Gaussian accelerated molecular dynamics
def: "Dual-boost protein-protein interaction Gaussian accelerated molecular dynamics (Dual-boost PPI-GaMD) is a variant of GaMD where two separate boost potentials are applied simultaneously to enhance the sampling of protein-protein interfaces. One boost is typically applied to the protein protein interface to accelerate local conformational changes, while the second is applied to the total system potential to overcome larger energy barriers." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000403 ! protein-protein interaction Gaussian accelerated molecular dynamics
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000405
name: multiply-targeted molecular dynamics
def: "Multiply-targeted molecular dynamics is an enhanced sampling technique that biases a simulation to explore the conformational space between several known target structures simultaneously. Unlike standard targeted MD which pulls a molecule from one state to another, this method encourages the system to visit a collection of different functional states. This is useful for characterizing the pathways that connect multiple known conformations of a protein, such as its active and inactive forms." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000862 ! targeted molecular dynamics
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000406
name: partial nudged elastic band
def: "A Partial Nudged Elastic Band (PNEB) is a computational method used to calculate the minimum energy path for structural transitions. Unlike traditional NEB, it applies the nudging algorithm only to a user-defined subset of atoms while allowing the remaining atoms to optimize freely. This reduces computational costs and supports complex environments like explicit solvents." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000856 ! nudged elastic band
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000407
name: optimization algorithm
def: "An algorithm that searches for the input values giving the best score under some measure, usually the lowest or highest value of a function. In this field the function is almost always an energy and the inputs are atomic positions. The difficulty is that such a search finds the nearest good answer rather than the best one anywhere. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000037 ! algorithm
property_value: skos:closeMatch KISAO_0000552

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000408
name: energy minimization algorithm
def: "An optimization algorithm that adjusts atomic positions to lower the energy of a structure until it reaches a nearby minimum. It moves downhill only, so it settles in the nearest low point rather than the lowest one. It is run on a freshly built system to remove overlaps that would otherwise make the first simulation steps explode. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000407 ! optimization algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000409
name: XMIN minimization algorithm
def: "A family of minimization algorithms that build up an approximation to the curvature of the energy surface from the slopes seen at successive steps, rather than computing it directly. Reusing past steps this way gives most of the speed of a curvature-based method at the cost of a slope-based one. It is the minimizer AmberTools offers for large systems. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000408 ! energy minimization algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001712 ! downhill simplex minimizer algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000410
name: lambda-scheduling free energy analysis
def: "A lambda-scheduling free energy method is a technique where the alchemical transformation between two states is performed in a single, continuous simulation run. This is achieved by slowly and continuously changing the coupling parameter, lambda, according to a predefined schedule over the course of the simulation. For experts, this non-equilibrium approach can be computationally efficient, and the free energy can be estimated from the work performed during the transformation using fluctuation theorems. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000615 ! free energy calculation analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000411
name: hybrid solvent replica-exchange molecular dynamics
def: "Hybrid solvent replica-exchange molecular dynamics is a specialized version of the REMD method where the different parallel simulations use different solvent models. For example, some replicas might use an implicit solvent model, which allows for very fast sampling, while others use a more accurate explicit solvent model. Swapping between these replicas allows the simulation to combine the sampling efficiency of implicit solvent with the accuracy of explicit solvent." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000858 ! replica-exchange molecular dynamics
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000412
name: reservoir replica-exchange molecular dynamics
def: "Reservoir replica-exchange molecular dynamics is an efficient variant of the REMD method for simulations with a very large number of replicas. Instead of attempting swaps between all adjacent pairs, it attempts swaps between a master simulation and a large \"reservoir\" of simulations running at different temperatures. This can significantly improve the efficiency of the exchange process when a very wide temperature range needs to be sampled." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000858 ! replica-exchange molecular dynamics
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000413
name: replica-exchange umbrella sampling
def: "Replica-exchange umbrella sampling is an enhanced sampling method that combines two powerful techniques to calculate free energy profiles. It runs multiple umbrella sampling simulations in parallel, each restraining the system to a different window along a reaction coordinate, and periodically attempts to swap the coordinates between these simulations. This combination helps to overcome slow conformational sampling within each umbrella window, leading to faster convergence of the potential of mean force." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000414
name: replica-exchange with arbitrary degree of freedom
def: "Replica-exchange with an arbitrary degree of freedom is a powerful generalization of the standard replica-exchange simulation method. Instead of running parallel simulations at different temperatures, this technique allows them to be run along any user-defined variable, such as a reaction coordinate, a force field parameter, or a pH value. By attempting to swap these variables between replicas, the method can dramatically enhance sampling and map out a system's response to a wide range of conditions in a single set of simulations." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000415
name: EMIL free energy analysis
def: "A free energy calculation analysis that computes an absolute free energy by thermodynamic integration from a realistic atomistic model to a simplified reference model whose free energy can be solved exactly. The Einstein Molecule model is used for the solute, in which each atom is held in place by a harmonic potential so that the reference free energy has a closed-form solution. EMIL is the name of the module that implements this in AMBER, and its authors call the underlying method Thermodynamic Integration relative to an Exact Solution. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000615 ! free energy calculation analysis
property_value: IAO:0000119 "Berryman J.T. Absolute free energies for biomolecules in implicit or explicit solvent. Physics Procedia, 2014. States that the AMBER implementation of this method is called EMIL." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000119 "Berryman J.T. and Schilling T. Free energies by thermodynamic integration relative to an exact solution, used to find the handedness-switching salt concentration for DNA. J. Chem. Theory Comput. 9(1):679-686, 2013." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000416
name: constant pH molecular dynamics
def: "A simulation method in which acidic and basic groups can gain or lose a proton during the run, rather than being fixed at the start. Their protonation is coupled to a chosen acidity, so the populations that result are those at that pH. It matters because a fixed assignment made before the simulation may be wrong, and a wrong charge changes everything downstream. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "CpHMD" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000843 ! molecular dynamics

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000417
name: continuous constant pH molecular dynamics
def: "A constant pH method in which the degree of protonation of each titratable group is a continuous quantity that moves under its own equation of motion, rather than switching between protonated and deprotonated. Because it changes smoothly, no jump has to be accepted or rejected and the simulation never stops to attempt one. The cost is that intermediate values do not correspond to any real chemical state and must be kept away from. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000416 ! constant pH molecular dynamics

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000418
name: lambda-dynamics free energy analysis
def: "Lambda-dynamics is a free energy calculation method where the coupling parameter, lambda, is treated as a dynamic variable that evolves in time, just like an atomic coordinate. A fictitious mass is assigned to lambda, and its \"motion\" along the transformation pathway is simulated, allowing it to sample different intermediate states." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000615 ! free energy calculation analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000419
name: PME continuous constant pH molecular dynamics
def: "A continuous constant pH method formulated to work with particle mesh Ewald electrostatics. The difficulty it solves is that changing a charge continuously changes the total charge of the system, which the Ewald treatment assumes is fixed. Without this reformulation, constant pH and the standard long-range electrostatics could not be used together. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000417 ! continuous constant pH molecular dynamics

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000420
name: variational free energy profile analysis
def: "A variational free energy profile method is a class of techniques for finding the minimum free energy path between two states. These methods work by optimizing a trial pathway to minimize a functional that represents the free energy, based on a variational principle. For experts, methods like the string method are a type of variational approach for identifying the most probable transition pathway and the associated free energy barrier. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000615 ! free energy calculation analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000421
name: weighted thermodynamic perturbation theory analysis
def: "A free energy analysis method that improves on plain free energy perturbation by applying a weighting function to the sampled configurations. The weighting concentrates effort where the 2 states overlap least, which is where plain perturbation converges worst. It is used when the states are too dissimilar for the unweighted estimator to be reliable. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000615 ! free energy calculation analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000422
name: generalized weighted thermodynamic perturbation theory
def: "A free energy analysis method that extends weighted thermodynamic perturbation theory to a broader family of weighting functions. The generalisation lets the weighting be chosen to suit the pair of states rather than taken from a fixed form. It targets the same problem, which is poor overlap between the states being compared. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000421 ! weighted thermodynamic perturbation theory analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000423
name: multidimensional replica-exchange molecular dynamics
def: "Multidimensional replica-exchange molecular dynamics is an extension of the REMD method where exchanges are performed along more than one variable simultaneously. For example, parallel simulations could be run at different temperatures and different pH values, with swaps attempted in both the temperature and pH dimensions." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000858 ! replica-exchange molecular dynamics
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000424
name: transition state search algorithm
def: "An optimization algorithm that locates a first-order saddle point on a potential energy surface, where the energy is at a maximum along 1 direction and a minimum along all others. It differs from a minimiser in having to climb in a chosen direction rather than descend in every one. The saddle point it finds is the transition state that sets a reaction barrier. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000407 ! optimization algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000425
name: dimer method algorithm
def: "A transition state search algorithm that uses 2 closely spaced copies of a structure to find the direction in which the energy curves downwards most, then moves uphill along it to a saddle point. It needs only first derivatives of the energy, never the full matrix of second derivatives. That makes it usable on systems too large for methods that build the whole Hessian. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000424 ! transition state search algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000426
name: grid inhomogeneous solvation theory analysis
def: "A data analysis method that computes the local density, energy and entropy of water on a 3-dimensional grid around a solute, from a simulation with explicit solvent. It assigns thermodynamic quantities to positions rather than to the system as a whole. That is what allows individual hydration sites to be identified and their contribution to solvation free energy to be quantified. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000974 ! solvent analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000427
name: 3D-mapping analysis
def: "An analysis method that builds a 3-dimensional map showing which regions around a molecule matter for its function, by computing a chosen property at each point of a grid. What the map shows depends on the property: where a probe binds favourably, where solvent is held, or where charge accumulates. It turns a per-point calculation into a picture that can be inspected. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000974 ! solvent analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000428
name: Ewald summation
def: "An electrostatic method that computes the total electrostatic energy of a periodically repeating system by splitting the calculation into a short-range part summed directly and a long-range part summed in reciprocal space. The split works because each part converges quickly where the other does not. Without it, the sum over periodic images does not converge at all. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000053 ! electrostatic interaction algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000429
name: Lennard-Jones particle mesh Ewald
def: "An algorithm that computes the long-range part of the van der Waals interaction using the same grid-based reciprocal space treatment that particle mesh Ewald applies to electrostatics. Van der Waals forces are usually just cut off at a distance, which introduces a small systematic error in density and surface tension. This removes that error at modest extra cost. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000053 ! electrostatic interaction algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000430
name: non-bonded potential
def: "The part of a force field describing interactions between atoms not joined by a bond, comprising the electrostatic term and the van der Waals term. Every atom in principle interacts with every other, so this part dominates the cost of a simulation. Nearly all the effort of making simulations fast goes into computing it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000331 ! force field component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000431
name: improper torsion potential
def: "The part of a force field that keeps 4 atoms flat, or preserves a centre's handedness, using a term with a single preferred value rather than a repeating one. The 4 atoms are not in a chain, which is what makes it improper. It exists because the other terms have no way to forbid a planar group from folding. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000331 ! force field component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000432
name: quantum mechanics basis set
def: "A set of mathematical functions, often resembling atomic orbitals, used in quantum chemical calculations to represent the spatial distribution of electrons within a molecule (molecular orbitals). The choice and size of the basis set significantly impact the accuracy and computational cost of a simulation; larger, more flexible basis sets generally yield more accurate results but require more computer resources. These functions serve as the building blocks for constructing the calculated electronic wavefunction. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000173 ! quantum mechanics
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000827 ! Moeller-Plesset

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000433
name: Altona & Sundaralingam pucker analysis
def: "A structural analysis method that describes the shape of a 5-membered ring, such as the ribose sugar of a nucleotide, using 2 numbers: the phase angle of pseudorotation and the puckering amplitude. The phase angle says which atoms lie out of the plane and in which direction, and the amplitude says by how much. Together they place a sugar in a named conformational family such as C2'-endo or C3'-endo. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000927 ! pucker analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000434
name: Cremer & Pople pucker analysis
def: "A structural analysis method that describes the shape of any non-planar ring using a set of numbers derived from how far each atom sits out of the ring's mean plane. It applies to rings of any size, where the older 2-parameter treatment covers 5-membered rings only. For a 6-membered ring it gives 3 numbers that place it on a sphere of possible shapes. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000927 ! pucker analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000435
name: kernel modified molecular dynamics
def: "A simulation method in which the forces are adjusted using a function borrowed from machine learning that measures how similar 2 configurations are. The adjustment pushes the system away from configurations it has already visited. That is what encourages it to explore rather than settle. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000843 ! molecular dynamics

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000436
name: data format
def: "A data format defines the specific rules and conventions used to structure, store, and exchange data, particularly within computer files. In biomolecular simulation, this refers to the various standardized ways that information like molecular structures, simulation parameters, or results are organized. Understanding these formats is essential for using simulation software and sharing data. (UNVERIFIED)" []

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000437
name: simulation input format
def: "A data format that provides the necessary data, settings, or instructions required to initiate a computational task. This format provides the instructional input for simulation or analysis software. It is distinct from formats that describe molecular structure or results. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001085 ! molecular data format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000438
name: script format
def: "A data format for a file containing a sequence of commands or code in a specific language. These scripts are designed to be executed by a program to automate a workflow or a series of analysis steps." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001085 ! molecular data format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000439
name: simulation log format
def: "A simulation log format is a text-based file structure that records the progress and key information generated during a computer simulation or calculation. It typically includes a copy of the input settings, step-by-step updates on energy and temperature, performance timings, and any warnings or error messages. This format is the primary source for monitoring a simulation's stability, diagnosing problems, and extracting averaged thermodynamic properties after the run is complete." []
synonym: "output log format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001085 ! molecular data format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000440
name: NMR data format
def: "A category of data formats for files containing information derived from Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (NMR) experiments. These formats are used to store and exchange experimental data, such as structural restraints, that can be used in simulations." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000436 ! data format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393
property_value: skos:closeMatch format:3824

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000441
name: simulation state format
def: "A data format for a file that stores a complete snapshot of a simulation's state at a specific time. This includes coordinates, velocities, and other state variables sufficient to resume the run. These formats are often binary for efficiency." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001085 ! molecular data format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000442
name: Molden format
def: "A text data format that stores the results of a quantum chemistry calculation for visualization, holding atomic coordinates together with the basis functions and coefficients that describe the molecular orbitals. Because it carries the orbitals themselves rather than only a picture of them, a viewer can render orbitals, electron density and vibrational modes from it. It is read by many visualization programs, not only the one it is named after. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:010022 ! quantum chemistry format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001114 ! site-site functionals format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000443
name: xyzv format
def: "A simple text-based file format for storing data that exists at various points in 3D space. Each line in the file specifies an x, y, and z coordinate, followed by the data value at that point. It is a straightforward, human-readable format for representing sparse or irregular grid data. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000909 ! volumetric data format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000468 ! MRC format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000444
name: tleap input format
def: "A script file format for the tleap program in AmberTools, used to build a molecular system for simulation. It contains a sequence of commands to load molecular structures, apply force fields, add solvent, and save the final topology and coordinate files. This format is a fundamental part of the system preparation stage in an Amber workflow. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000438 ! script format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000469 ! AMBER mdin format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000469 ! AMBER mdin format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000867 ! CHARMM input format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000445
name: mmCIF format
def: "The mmCIF format (.cif or .mmcif) is the standard archival format for macromolecular structures used by the Protein Data Bank (PDB), superseding the legacy PDB format. It uses a flexible, dictionary-based syntax (CIF) with key-value pairs and loop structures to store atomic coordinates, connectivity, experimental details, and extensive metadata. It is better suited for handling large, complex structures and diverse experimental data." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001088 ! molecular structure format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000446 ! PDB format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393
property_value: skos:exactMatch format:1477

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000446
name: PDB format
def: "The PDB format (.pdb) is the long-standing, fixed-column text format traditionally used for storing protein and nucleic acid structures from the Protein Data Bank. It includes records for metadata, atomic coordinates, and optionally connectivity. While still widely compatible with visualization and simulation software, it is considered obsolete since it has limitations for very large structures and complex metadata compared to the newer mmCIF format." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001088 ! molecular structure format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393
property_value: skos:exactMatch format:1476

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000447
name: identifier
def: "An identifier is a unique name, code, or label assigned to a specific entity, data record, or concept to distinguish it unambiguously from others within a given context. In scientific databases and computational workflows, identifiers (like accession numbers or unique IDs) are crucial for referencing, retrieving, and linking specific pieces of information accurately. They serve as unique addresses for data points or objects. (UNVERIFIED)" []
property_value: skos:closeMatch IAO:0020000

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000448
name: obsolete protein database ID
def: "OBSOLETE. A protein database ID is a unique alphanumeric code assigned to each entry in a public protein structure or sequence database, such as the Protein Data Bank (PDB ID, e.g., '1TIM') or UniProt (accession number, e.g., 'P00761'). These identifiers serve as the standard way to reference and retrieve specific protein structures or sequence information." []
comment: Retired 2026-08-07 on review by orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393. Two objections, both accepted. First, the Protein Data Bank is not a protein database: it holds nucleic acids, protein-nucleic acid complexes and other assemblies, so the label and definition made a claim that is simply false. Second, a PDB entry identifies a deposited structure while a UniProt accession identifies a sequence record, so grouping them said less than it appeared to. Its two children, MOLSIM:000686 PDB ID and MOLSIM:000687 UniProt ID, were re-parented to MOLSIM:000447 identifier alongside the other identifiers. No IAO:0100001 successor, because there is no single term that replaces it; this is the same shape as the other retired grouping terms whose children were re-parented instead. Note the term had been verified by orcid:0000-0003-4177-3619 before this review.
is_obsolete: true

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000449
name: electrostatic damping function
def: "A function that reduces the electrostatic interaction between 2 charges as they approach very closely. Without it, a polarizable model can reach a state where 2 induced dipoles reinforce each other without limit and the energy diverges. Damping prevents that failure, which is called polarization catastrophe. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "tinker-exponential damping" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000430 ! non-bonded potential

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000450
name: hydrogen bond analysis
def: "Hydrogen bond analysis is a structural analysis method used to identify and quantify the hydrogen bonds that are formed and broken during a simulation. The analysis typically uses a set of geometric criteria, such as a maximum distance between the donor and acceptor atoms and a minimum angle, to define when a hydrogen bond exists." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000917 ! structural analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000451
name: isotropically distributed ensemble analysis
def: "A structural analysis method that tests whether the orientations of the structures in a collection are spread evenly over all directions. It computes the distribution of orientations and looks for any preferred alignment. It is used to confirm that a simulation has not introduced an artificial bias in rotational motion, which some theoretical treatments assume is absent. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000939 ! dynamics analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000452
name: isotropic reorientational eigenmode dynamics analysis
def: "A dynamics analysis method that breaks the tumbling of a molecule in solution into a set of independent rotational modes. Each mode has its own timescale, so the overall rotation can be described by a few numbers instead of a full trajectory. The result can be compared directly with NMR relaxation measurements. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000939 ! dynamics analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000453
name: nucleic acid structure analysis
def: "Nucleic acid structure analysis is a specialized type of structural analysis that calculates a set of parameters describing the detailed geometry of a DNA or RNA helix, known as the helical parameters. This includes parameters that describe the geometry of individual base pairs as well as the relationship between adjacent base pairs, such as twist, roll, and slide." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000917 ! structural analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393
property_value: skos:closeMatch operation:2481

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000454
name: native contact analysis
def: "A structural analysis method that tracks how many of the atom pairs in contact in a reference folded structure are also in contact at each point in a trajectory. The reference set is taken from the native state and the result is reported as the fraction of it that is present. That fraction is a common single-number measure of how far folding has progressed. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000917 ! structural analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000455
name: time-lagged independent component analysis
def: "A statistical method that finds the directions in which a system changes most slowly, rather than those in which it varies most. It does this by looking at how coordinates relate to themselves after a delay rather than at the same instant. The slowest motions are usually the functionally important ones, and they are not always the largest. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "tICA" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000120 ! dimensionality reduction technique analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000456
name: wavelet analysis
def: "A method that decomposes a signal into contributions at different frequencies, while keeping track of when each occurred. A standard frequency analysis says which frequencies are present over the whole record but not when. That matters for a trajectory, where a motion may appear only during part of the run. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000939 ! dynamics analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000457
name: wavelet analysis feature extraction
def: "A method that identifies events in a signal from the output of a wavelet decomposition, by finding where energy at a given frequency appears or disappears. It picks out transitions rather than describing the signal as a whole. In a trajectory it marks the moments at which a molecule changed its mode of motion. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000456 ! wavelet analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000458
name: fluorescence spectroscopy
def: "Fluorescence spectroscopy is an experimental technique that measures the light emitted by a substance after it has absorbed light. A molecule absorbs light at one wavelength, promoting it to an excited electronic state, and then emits light at a longer, lower-energy wavelength as it relaxes back down. This technique is highly sensitive and is widely used to study molecular conformation, binding, and dynamics by monitoring changes in the fluorescence signal." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001008 ! spectroscopy
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000459
name: rtp format
def: "A data format used by GROMACS that defines a reusable template for one residue, giving its atoms, their charges and the bonds between them. It is what lets a topology be built automatically from a sequence rather than written out atom by atom. It is the GROMACS counterpart of the CHARMM residue topology file. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "GROMACS rtp format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001091 ! molecular topology format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000472 ! AMBER topology format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000460
name: molecular mechanics Poisson-Boltzmann surface area tool
def: "A computational tool or script that implements the MM/PBSA (Molecular Mechanics / Poisson-Boltzmann Surface Area) method for estimating free energy changes, typically ligand binding affinities or solvation free energies. This approach involves calculating molecular mechanics energies (MM), electrostatic solvation free energies using the Poisson-Boltzmann (PB) equation, and non-polar solvation free energies using a term proportional to the Solvent Accessible Surface Area (SASA), usually averaged over snapshots from an MD trajectory. It's an endpoint free energy method, computationally cheaper than FEP or TI but generally considered less rigorous. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "MMPBSA tool" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000257 ! endpoint free energy tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000462 ! molecular mechanics generalized Born surface area tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000461
name: molecular mechanics Poisson-Boltzmann surface area module
def: "A molecular mechanics Poisson-Boltzmann surface area tool that is built into a larger simulation or modelling package rather than run on its own. It uses that package's own energy routines and Poisson-Boltzmann solver, which is what distinguishes it from a standalone script such as MMPBSA.py. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "MMPBSA module" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000460 ! molecular mechanics Poisson-Boltzmann surface area tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000462
name: molecular mechanics generalized Born surface area tool
def: "A computational tool or script that implements the MM/GBSA (Molecular Mechanics / Generalized Born Surface Area) method for estimating free energy changes, analogous to MM/PBSA. The key difference is that MM/GBSA uses a Generalized Born (GB) model instead of the more computationally expensive Poisson-Boltzmann (PB) equation to calculate the electrostatic contribution to the solvation free energy. Like MM/PBSA, it combines MM energies, GB electrostatic solvation energy, and a SASA-based nonpolar term, averaged over simulation snapshots, providing a faster but often less accurate estimation of binding or solvation free energies compared to rigorous methods. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "MMGBSA tool" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000257 ! endpoint free energy tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000463
name: ref Tversky combo
def: "A comprehensive molecular similarity measure that combines both shape-based RefTversky and chemical feature-based RefColorTversky scores into a single metric. This combined measure provides a more complete assessment of molecular similarity by considering both geometric shape and chemical functionality simultaneously. The resulting score typically ranges from 0 to 2, though it can occasionally exceed this range due to the field-based nature of shape matching. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000076 ! Tversky index algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000464
name: STO-6G
def: "A minimal basis set in which each atomic orbital is approximated by 6 Gaussian functions added together. It is the most faithful imitation in the family and still minimal, so it remains unsuitable for real work. Adding Gaussians improves the shape of each orbital and never lets the electron cloud change shape as a bond forms. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000017 ! minimal basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000465
name: NModelGB
def: "NModelGB is a specific implementation of a Generalized Born (GB) implicit solvent model, likely used within a particular simulation package. It provides a specific set of equations and parameters for calculating the electrostatic contribution to the solvation free energy. The \"NModel\" designation distinguishes this particular variant from other GB models available to the user. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000462 ! molecular mechanics generalized Born surface area tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000466
name: orientations of proteins in membranes
def: "OPM database (Orientations of Proteins in Membranes) is both a database and a web server/tool providing pre-calculated transmembrane orientations and positions for experimentally determined membrane protein structures found in the PDB. OPM uses a computational approach based on minimizing the calculated transfer free energy from water to the lipid bilayer to determine the most likely membrane boundaries and protein position relative to the bilayer center. It's a valuable resource for obtaining initial membrane protein placements for simulations." []
synonym: "OPM" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000227 ! membrane protein orientation tool
is_a: MOLSIM:001119 ! database web server
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001673 ! Glycoprotein Builder
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000467
name: Forster resonance energy transfer
def: "Förster Resonance Energy Transfer (FRET) is a specific phenomenon in fluorescence spectroscopy where an excited donor fluorophore non-radiatively transfers its energy to a nearby acceptor fluorophore. The efficiency of this energy transfer is extremely sensitive to the distance between the two molecules, making it a \"spectroscopic ruler.\"" []
synonym: "FRET" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000458 ! fluorescence spectroscopy
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986
property_value: skos:exactMatch CHMO:0000062

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000468
name: MRC format
def: "A binary file format used to store three-dimensional images or maps, common in electron microscopy. It is the standard format for storing 3D density maps in cryo-electron microscopy (cryo-EM) and is also used in X-ray crystallography. This format is essential for the visualization and analysis of volumetric data in structural biology. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000909 ! volumetric data format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000469
name: AMBER mdin format
def: "A text-based format containing control parameters for the Amber sander and pmemd programs, organized in Fortran namelists. It specifies simulation conditions like timestep, duration, and temperature/pressure coupling algorithms. This format dictates how the molecular dynamics simulation is performed." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002065 ! simulation parameter format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000470
name: mdout format
def: "A text-based log format generated by Amber's simulation engines that provides a detailed record of the simulation's progress. It contains energy components, thermodynamic properties, and performance timings printed at regular intervals. This format is essential for monitoring simulation stability and extracting averaged properties. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "AMBER mdout format" EXACT []
synonym: "AMBER out format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000439 ! simulation log format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000593 ! CPPTRAJ standard output format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000593 ! CPPTRAJ standard output format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000879 ! ADF output format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000471
name: AMBER restart format
def: "A format that stores the complete state of an Amber simulation, including atomic coordinates, velocities, and periodic box dimensions. It is used to save the simulation state at a specific point in time, allowing the run to be resumed exactly. The format can be either ASCII-based (.rst7) or binary NetCDF-based (.ncrst)." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000441 ! simulation state format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000880 ! RKF format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000890 ! GAUSSIAN chk format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000472
name: AMBER topology format
def: "The Amber molecular dynamics topology file (.prmtop or .parm7) contains all the static information about the molecular system needed for an Amber simulation, excluding coordinates. This includes atom definitions (names, types, masses, charges), molecular connectivity (bonds, angles, dihedrals), force field parameters for all interaction terms, and non-bonded interaction rules. It is generated by programs like tleap and used together with a coordinate file (.inpcrd, .rst7)." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001091 ! molecular topology format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000898 ! itp format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000473
name: ac format
def: "A file format generated by the Antechamber program in AmberTools that contains a molecule's structure and atomic properties. It typically stores atom types and partial charges assigned during the parameterization process for a small molecule. This format serves as an intermediate in preparing non-standard molecules for simulation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001088 ! molecular structure format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000474
name: protein-ligand docking analysis
def: "A computational method that predicts how a small molecule sits in a binding site on a protein, and scores how well it binds. It searches over positions and shapes of the molecule and rates each by a scoring function. It is fast enough to screen large libraries, and its scores rank candidates far better than they predict real binding strengths. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000255 ! static molecular interaction prediction modeling

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000475
name: coarse-grained molecular dynamics
def: "A molecular dynamics method that integrates the equations of motion for a coarse-grained model rather than an all-atom one. Fewer and smoother interactions permit a timestep 10 or more times longer, which together with the smaller particle count is where its speed comes from. Its trajectory cannot be interpreted below the size of 1 site. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "CG-MD" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000229 ! resolution-based simulation method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000476
name: obsolete TIP3P water model
def: "OBSOLETE. A specific, widely used 3-point water model type characterized by its simplicity and computational efficiency (Transferable Intermolecular Potential 3-Point). It places charges on the oxygen and two hydrogen atoms and represents water as a rigid molecule with experimentally derived geometry. While computationally fast, it is known to have limitations in reproducing some properties of real water (like the temperature of maximum density or dielectric constant) compared to more complex models." []
comment: Retired 2026-08-24 as a duplicate. MOLSIM:000022 TIP3P describes the same rigid three-site model with charges on the oxygen and two hydrogens, and sits with the other 18 water models under MOLSIM:000014 water model force field. This one sat under the parallel MOLSIM:000030 water type branch, which was retired in the same change.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: MOLSIM:000022

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000477
name: CHELPG charge analysis
def: "A method that assigns charge to atoms by fitting point charges to reproduce the molecule's electrostatic potential at points on a grid outside it. Fitting to the potential is what makes the resulting charges suitable for a force field, since that potential is what other molecules feel. Charges on buried atoms are poorly determined, because the potential outside barely depends on them. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000674 ! charge analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000478
name: molecular surface analysis
def: "Molecular surface analysis is a category of analysis methods used to calculate and characterize the surface of a molecule. This includes calculating properties like the total surface area, identifying pockets and cavities, and mapping properties like electrostatic potential onto the surface." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000917 ! structural analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986
property_value: skos:closeMatch operation:3351

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000479
name: Connolly surface analysis
def: "A Connolly surface calculation is a specific algorithm used to compute the solvent-accessible surface of a molecule, which is the surface traced out by the center of a probe sphere as it rolls over the molecule. It is a widely used method for defining the boundary between a molecule and the surrounding solvent." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000478 ! molecular surface analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000480
name: covariance matrix analysis
def: "A covariance matrix calculation is an analysis method that quantifies the correlated motions of atoms in a simulation. The resulting matrix describes how the displacement of each atom is correlated with the displacement of every other atom. For experts, calculating and diagonalizing the covariance matrix is the central step in Principal Component Analysis (PCA), which is used to identify the dominant, large-scale collective motions of a protein or other macromolecule. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000939 ! dynamics analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000481
name: obsolete 2D RMSD analysis
def: "OBSOLETE. A 2D RMSD analysis is a method where the Root-Mean-Square Deviation (RMSD) is calculated for multiple frames in a simulation trajectory with respect to a reference structure. The reference structure is usually the first frame in the trajectory or an average structure of the whole simulation. The results are typically visualized as a two-dimensional plot, where each point represents the RMSD between one frame and the reference structure." []
comment: Retired as redundant with 'RMSD analysis' (MOLSIM:000311), which shares the same parent and the same underlying principle. The 2D frame-to-frame form is now covered explicitly by that term's definition. Reported and approved by the term verifier in GitHub issue #45.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: MOLSIM:000311

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000482
name: lipid SCD order parameter calculation analysis
def: "A lipid SCD order parameter calculation is a specific analysis method used to quantify the orientational order of the carbon-hydrogen bonds in the acyl tails of lipid molecules in a membrane simulation. The SCD parameter measures the motional restriction of these bonds relative to the membrane normal. Calculating these order parameters and comparing them to experimental values from NMR is a primary method for validating the accuracy of a membrane simulation." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000917 ! structural analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000483
name: 3D reference interaction site analysis
def: "An analysis method that computes where solvent molecules are likely to sit around a solute by solving integral equations of liquid-state theory on a 3-dimensional grid. It gives a solvent distribution without simulating solvent molecules moving, so no sampling problem arises. What it cannot give is any individual solvent molecule's behaviour over time. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000615 ! free energy calculation analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000484
name: adaptive solvent QM/MM
def: "A QM/MM method in which solvent molecules pass between the quantum and the classical region as they diffuse, rather than being assigned once. A fixed assignment would either trap particular water molecules in the quantum region or cut them as they moved out. The method exists because solvent does not stay put. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000388 ! QM/MM simulation

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000485
name: split-valence basis set
def: "A basis set that represents each valence orbital with 2 or more functions of different spatial extent, while keeping a single function for each core orbital. The extra valence functions let the electron cloud expand or contract as bonding requires, which a minimal set cannot. Splitting only the valence shell concentrates the added cost where bonding happens. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "split-valence" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000432 ! quantum mechanics basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000486
name: 3-21G
def: "A split-valence Gaussian basis set describing each core orbital with 3 contracted primitives and each valence orbital with 2 functions, built from 2 and 1 primitives. It is small enough for large molecules and crude enough that its geometries are only approximate. It is used for a quick first optimisation before a better basis set is applied. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000487 ! 4-21G

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000487
name: 4-21G
def: "A split-valence Gaussian basis set describing each core orbital with 4 contracted primitives and each valence orbital with 2 functions. It differs from the 3-primitive version only in the description of the core, which barely affects bonding. It is rarely used today. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000488
name: harmonic improper torsion potential
def: "An improper torsion potential in which the energy rises with the square of the departure from a single preferred value. Unlike the repeating cosine form it has one minimum, which is what makes it suitable for holding a group flat. The AMBER force fields use a cosine form for the same purpose, so the 2 conventions are not interchangeable. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000431 ! improper torsion potential

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000489
name: Lennard-Jones potential
def: "A potential energy function representing the van der Waals interaction between 2 atoms, with a steep repulsion at short range and a weaker attraction falling off with the sixth power of distance. The attraction has a physical basis in dispersion; the repulsion is chosen for computational convenience rather than derived. It is the form almost every force field uses. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000430 ! non-bonded potential

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000490
name: structure preparation tool
def: "A software program that prepares, corrects and checks a molecular structure before it is used in a simulation. Its tasks include adding atoms the experimental structure does not contain, choosing between alternative positions where the data was ambiguous, and reporting geometry that cannot be right. Experimental structures nearly always need this, because crystallography rarely sees hydrogens and often misses flexible loops. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001850 ! modeling and setup tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000491
name: SYBYL
def: "A comprehensive commercial molecular modeling software suite developed by Certara, widely used in drug discovery and computational chemistry. SYBYL offers extensive tools for structure building and manipulation, conformational analysis, pharmacophore modeling, QSAR, docking, scoring, and visualization, along with molecular mechanics and dynamics capabilities. It provides an integrated environment for many structure preparation and modeling tasks relevant to biomolecular simulation setup, particularly in pharmaceutical research. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001664 ! software suite

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000492
name: Swiss PDB viewer
def: "A visualization and analysis program for protein structures that also performs measurement, superposition and simple modelling. It can build a model of one protein on the structure of a related one, and submit that model for refinement. It is now distributed under the name DeepView, which should be kept as an exact synonym of this term. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "DeepView" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000490 ! structure preparation tool
is_a: MOLSIM:002041 ! molecular structure visualization tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000493 ! Pymol

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000493
name: Pymol
def: "A very popular, powerful, and widely used open-source (with some subscription features) molecular visualization system, known for producing high-quality 3D images of molecules and biological macromolecules. PyMOL allows detailed structure inspection, analysis (measurements, surfaces, electrostatics), creating publication-quality figures and animations, and includes scripting capabilities for automation. It is an indispensable tool for visualizing simulation setups and trajectories, although its structure manipulation capabilities are less extensive than dedicated modeling suites. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002041 ! molecular structure visualization tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000494
name: minimization
def: "Minimization is a computational step that relaxes a molecular structure to remove any bad clashes between atoms. As a stage of the preparation process, energy minimization is a procedure that adjusts the atomic coordinates to find a nearby local minimum on the potential energy surface, thereby removing steric strain from the initial model. This is achieved by using algorithms like steepest descent or conjugate gradient to iteratively reduce the net forces on the atoms until a convergence criterion, such as grms_tol, is met. This process is referred to in log files and inputs with terms like \"MINIMIZATION,\" \"ntmin=1,\" \"emtol,\" and \"ncyc.\" (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000002 ! simulation preparation

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000495
name: parse radii
def: "An empirically derived set of atomic radii developed by Sitkoff, Sharp, and Honig in the 1990s, specifically optimized for use in continuum electrostatic calculations, particularly Poisson-Boltzmann (PB) calculations aimed at reproducing experimental solvation energies (PARSE stands for \"Parameters for Solvation Energy\"). These radii define the boundary between the low-dielectric solute molecule and the high-dielectric solvent continuum in PB theory. They differ significantly from standard Van der Waals radii (like Bondi's) as they are optimized to implicitly account for various energetic contributions within that specific theoretical framework (PB/SA). (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000272 ! radii set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000496
name: pyMBAR
def: "A Python library that implements the multi-state Bennett acceptance ratio estimator for combining data from simulations at several thermodynamic states. It returns free energy differences between any pair of those states together with equilibrium averages. It is the reference implementation most other tools call. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001566 ! software library
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001567 ! FFTW

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000497
name: computational method statistical measure analysis
def: "A statistical metric used to judge how well a computational method performs, rather than to describe the system being studied. Error measures, correlation measures and ranking measures all belong here. They are what a method is validated against before its predictions are relied on. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000348 ! hypothesis testing analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000498
name: predictive index of Pearman analysis
def: "A statistical metric that rates how useful a model's predictions are for making a decision, by weighting each pair of compounds by how much choosing wrongly between them would cost. It counts a wrong ordering of 2 very different compounds more heavily than of 2 similar ones. It is used where a model is meant to guide a choice rather than reproduce a number. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000497 ! computational method statistical measure analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000499
name: accuracy of ddG prediction metrics measurements analysis
def: "A data analysis method that measures how closely predicted relative binding free energies match experimental ones for the same set of ligand pairs. It reports error measures such as root mean square error and mean absolute error, and agreement measures such as the Pearson correlation and the Kendall rank correlation. The rank measures matter most when the purpose is to order ligands rather than to predict a number. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000348 ! hypothesis testing analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000500
name: mechanical embedding QM/MM
def: "A QM/MM scheme in which the quantum region is computed in isolation and its interaction with the surroundings is treated entirely by the force field. The quantum region therefore never feels the charges around it, so its electron distribution does not respond to its environment. It is the simplest scheme and the least accurate where the environment is polar. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000388 ! QM/MM simulation

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000501
name: 4-31G
def: "A split-valence Gaussian basis set describing each core orbital with 4 contracted primitives and each valence orbital with 2 functions built from 3 and 1 primitives. It was an early step towards the widely used 6-31G family and is superseded by it. It is retained because older published work used it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000502
name: linear correlation significance determination analysis
def: "A statistical mathematical technique used to assess whether an observed linear relationship (correlation) between two variables, calculated from simulation data, is statistically meaningful. It evaluates the probability that such a correlation could have occurred simply by random chance if no true underlying relationship existed. This helps researchers confidently interpret potential connections found in simulation results. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000400 ! statistical analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000503
name: determination by p-value analysis
def: "A common specific method for linear correlation significance determination (and statistical testing in general) that involves calculating a probability value, the p-value. The p-value represents the probability of observing the calculated correlation, or a stronger one, assuming that there is actually no real correlation (the null hypothesis). A small p-value (typically below a threshold like 0.05) leads to the conclusion that the observed correlation is statistically significant and unlikely due to chance. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000400 ! statistical analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000505
name: 6-21G
def: "A split-valence Gaussian basis set describing each core orbital with 6 contracted primitives and each valence orbital with 2 functions. The larger core description makes it more accurate than its 3-primitive and 4-primitive relatives for core-dependent properties and no better for bonding. It is rarely used today. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000506
name: 6-31G
def: "A split-valence Gaussian basis set that describes each core orbital with 6 contracted primitives and each valence orbital with 2 functions, an inner one contracted from 3 primitives and an outer one from a single primitive. It is one of the most widely used basis sets in quantum chemistry, because it is far more accurate than a minimal basis set while staying cheap enough for routine work. It is also the starting point most polarization and diffuse variants are built on. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000509
name: QM generalized Born treatment
def: "A multiscale method that describes a solute quantum mechanically while representing the surrounding solvent with a generalized Born continuum model. The quantum region can then respond electronically to the solvent without any solvent molecules being simulated. It is used where reactivity matters but explicit solvent would be too expensive. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000388 ! QM/MM simulation

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000510
name: time-averaged restraint simulation
def: "A time-averaged restraint simulation is an advanced simulation method where the restraining potential is applied not to the instantaneous structure, but to the average of a an experimental one over a period of time. This is particularly useful for incorporating experimental data, like from NMR, which is also an average over time and a molecular ensemble. For experts, this method provides a more physically meaningful way to enforce experimental restraints that reflect the dynamic nature of the molecule." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000364 ! restrained simulation method
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000511
name: 6-311G
def: "A split-valence Gaussian basis set that describes each core orbital with 6 contracted primitives and each valence orbital with 3 functions of different spatial extent, contracted from 3, 1 and 1 primitives. The extra valence function gives more freedom than a double-split set, so it is more accurate for the same molecule. It is usually used together with polarization and diffuse functions rather than on its own. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000512
name: LANL08
def: "A set of effective core potentials and matching valence basis sets developed at Los Alamos National Laboratory for calculations on heavier elements. The potential replaces the chemically inert inner electrons with a single function, which cuts cost and folds in some relativistic effects, while the valence basis describes the electrons that form bonds. It is the successor to the older LANL2 family. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000513
name: LANL08(f)
def: "A set of effective core potentials and valence basis sets from the Los Alamos LANL08 family, with f type polarization functions added on the heavy atoms the potential covers. The f functions give more freedom in describing electron distribution, which matters for bonding in molecules containing heavier elements. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000514
name: LANL2-[6s4p4d2f]
def: "A Los Alamos effective core potential paired with a valence basis contracted to 6 s-type, 4 p-type, 4 d-type and 2 f-type functions. The potential replaces the inner electrons, and the large valence contraction gives far more flexibility than the standard double-zeta basis of the same family. It is used for heavier elements where the standard basis is too small to describe bonding accurately. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000515
name: LANL2DZ ECP
def: "A Los Alamos effective core potential paired with a double-zeta valence basis, for elements from the third row onwards. The potential replaces the inner electrons with a single function, which cuts cost and folds in some relativistic effects. It is the most widely used effective core potential basis combination. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000516
name: LANL2DZ+1d1f
def: "A Los Alamos effective core potential with a double-zeta valence basis, carrying 1 extra d type and 1 extra f type polarization function on the heavy atoms the potential covers. The higher angular momentum functions give the valence basis more freedom, which improves the description of bonding for heavier elements. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000517
name: LANL2DZ+2s2p2d2f
def: "A Los Alamos effective core potential with a double-zeta valence basis, carrying 2 additional s, p, d and f functions on the heavy atoms the potential covers. The additions give far more freedom in describing valence electrons than the standard double-zeta set. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000518
name: LANL2DZdp ECP
def: "A Los Alamos effective core potential with a double-zeta valence basis, carrying d type polarization functions on the heavy atoms the potential covers and p type polarization functions on hydrogen. The added polarization functions improve molecular geometries and interaction energies markedly over the unpolarized version. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000519
name: LANL2DZdp ECP Polarization
def: "A Los Alamos effective core potential with a double-zeta valence basis, carrying d type polarization functions on the heavy atoms the potential covers and p type polarization functions on hydrogen. The added polarization functions improve molecular geometries and interaction energies markedly over the unpolarized version. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000520
name: LANL2TZ
def: "A Los Alamos effective core potential paired with a triple-zeta valence basis set, using 3 functions per valence orbital. The extra valence function makes it more flexible and more accurate than the double-zeta member of the same family, at a higher cost. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000521
name: LANL2TZ(f)
def: "A Los Alamos effective core potential with a triple-zeta valence basis set, with f type polarization functions added on the heavy atoms the potential covers. The f functions describe electron correlation and polarization around heavier elements more accurately than the unaugmented set. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000522
name: cc-pVDZ
def: "A correlation-consistent basis set giving 2 functions per valence orbital with a set of polarization functions. It is the smallest member of its family and the cheapest at which correlated methods give meaningful results. It is used as the lowest point of an extrapolation towards the complete basis set limit. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000523
name: cc-pVTZ
def: "A correlation-consistent basis set that gives 3 functions per valence orbital together with polarization functions up to f type. It is the level at which correlated calculations first become reliably useful. It is the most widely used member of the family. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000524
name: cc-pVQZ
def: "A correlation-consistent basis set that gives 4 functions per valence orbital together with polarization functions up to g type. It is used where a triple-zeta result is not converged enough, and as one point in an extrapolation to the complete basis set limit. Its cost restricts it to modest-sized molecules. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000525
name: cc-pV5Z
def: "A correlation-consistent basis set that gives 5 functions per valence orbital together with polarization functions up to h type. It is built for benchmark calculations that need to come very close to the complete basis set limit for correlation energy. Its cost restricts it to small systems. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000526
name: cc-pV6Z
def: "A correlation-consistent basis set that gives 6 functions per valence orbital together with polarization functions up to i type. It is 1 step larger than the quintuple-zeta set and buys a further small step towards the complete basis set limit. In practice it is feasible only for atoms and diatomic molecules. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000527
name: cc-pV8Z
def: "A correlation-consistent basis set that gives 8 functions per valence orbital together with very extensive polarization functions. It exists to study how results converge towards the complete basis set limit, rather than to be used in ordinary work. Its cost restricts it to single atoms and diatomic molecules. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000528
name: cc-pV9Z
def: "A correlation-consistent basis set that gives 9 functions per valence orbital together with polarization functions of very high angular momentum. It is among the largest sets ever constructed in this family and serves only to extrapolate towards the complete basis set limit. It is too expensive for any molecular calculation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000529
name: cc-pVDZ-RI
def: "An auxiliary basis set built to be paired with the correlation-consistent double-zeta orbital basis in resolution-of-identity or density fitting calculations. It approximates products of orbital basis functions rather than representing orbitals itself. Pairing it with a different orbital basis degrades the approximation it was fitted for. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000530
name: cc-pVTZ-RI
def: "An auxiliary basis set built to be paired with the correlation-consistent triple-zeta orbital basis in resolution-of-identity or density fitting calculations. It approximates products of orbital basis functions so integrals can be evaluated faster. It is not used to represent orbitals. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000531
name: cc-pVQZ-RI
def: "An auxiliary basis set built to be paired with the correlation-consistent quadruple-zeta orbital basis in resolution-of-identity or density fitting calculations. It carries the extra functions that fitting products of the larger orbital basis requires. Its purpose is speed, not accuracy. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000532
name: cc-pV5Z-RI
def: "An auxiliary basis set built to be paired with the correlation-consistent quintuple-zeta orbital basis in resolution-of-identity or density fitting calculations. It is not used to represent orbitals; it approximates products of them so that integrals can be evaluated faster. Without it, calculations at that orbital basis size are often impractical. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000533
name: cc-pV6Z-RI
def: "An auxiliary basis set built to be paired with the correlation-consistent sextuple-zeta orbital basis in resolution-of-identity or density fitting calculations. It approximates products of orbital basis functions rather than the orbitals themselves. It is what allows benchmark calculations at that orbital basis size to run at all. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000534
name: cc-pCVDZ
def: "A correlation-consistent basis set at double-zeta level that adds tight functions, of large exponent, to describe correlation involving the core electrons. Standard valence sets assume the core is inert, which is a poor approximation for properties that depend on core-valence correlation. It is the smallest member of the family and the cheapest at which the effect can be seen at all. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000535
name: cc-pCVTZ
def: "A correlation-consistent basis set at triple-zeta level that adds tight functions, of large exponent, to describe correlation involving the core electrons. Standard valence sets assume the core is inert, which is a poor approximation for properties that depend on core-valence correlation. It is the level at which core-valence correlation is usually first worth its cost. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000536
name: cc-pCVQZ
def: "A correlation-consistent basis set at quadruple-zeta level that adds tight functions, of large exponent, to describe correlation involving the core electrons. Standard valence sets assume the core is inert, which is a poor approximation for properties that depend on core-valence correlation. It is used for benchmark work where core-valence correlation must be converged rather than merely included. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000537
name: cc-pCV5Z
def: "A correlation-consistent basis set at quintuple-zeta level that adds tight functions describing correlation involving the core electrons, without diffuse functions. It is used for benchmark work where core-valence correlation must be converged. Its size restricts it to very small systems. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000538
name: cc-pCV6Z
def: "A correlation-consistent basis set at sextuple-zeta level that adds tight functions describing correlation involving the core electrons, without diffuse functions. It is among the largest such sets in existence and approaches the complete basis set limit for the core-valence contribution. Its size restricts it to atoms and diatomic molecules. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000539
name: cc-pV(D+d)Z
def: "A correlation-consistent double-zeta basis set carrying 1 extra energy-optimised d type polarization function beyond the standard set. The extra function was added because the standard double-zeta set was found short of d functions for the second-row elements sodium to argon. For first-row elements it behaves like the ordinary double-zeta set. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000540
name: cc-pV(T+d)Z
def: "A correlation-consistent triple-zeta basis set carrying 1 extra optimised d type polarization function beyond the standard set. It describes polarization and correlation for the second-row elements sodium to argon more completely than the ordinary triple-zeta set. For other elements the 2 are equivalent. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000541
name: cc-pV(Q+d)Z
def: "A correlation-consistent quadruple-zeta basis set carrying 1 extra optimised d type polarization function beyond the standard set. It is used for benchmark-quality results on the second-row elements sodium to argon, where d function flexibility limits accuracy. For other elements the 2 are equivalent. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000542
name: cc-pV(5+d)Z
def: "A correlation-consistent quintuple-zeta basis set carrying 1 extra optimised d type polarization function beyond the standard set. It is used in high-level benchmark work on small molecules containing the second-row elements sodium to argon. For other elements the 2 are equivalent. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000543
name: cc-pV(6+d)Z
def: "A correlation-consistent sextuple-zeta basis set carrying 1 extra optimised d type polarization function beyond the standard set. It is a highly specialised set for work on the second-row elements sodium to argon near the complete basis set limit. For other elements the 2 are equivalent. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000544
name: aug-cc-pVDZ
def: "A correlation-consistent basis set giving 2 functions per valence orbital, with 1 diffuse function added at each angular momentum present. The diffuse functions matter for anions, weakly bound complexes and response properties. It is the smallest basis set at which such properties can be attempted. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000545
name: aug-cc-pVTZ
def: "A correlation-consistent basis set giving 3 functions per valence orbital, with a set of diffuse functions added. It is the usual working choice where both correlation and diffuse character matter. It is large enough to be trusted and small enough for molecules of a few dozen atoms. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000546
name: aug-cc-pVQZ
def: "A correlation-consistent basis set giving 4 functions per valence orbital with a set of diffuse functions added at each angular momentum. The diffuse functions matter for anions, weakly bound complexes and response properties. It is a common point in an extrapolation towards the complete basis set limit. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000547
name: aug-cc-pV5Z
def: "A correlation-consistent basis set that gives 5 functions per valence orbital and adds a set of diffuse functions. The diffuse functions matter when electron density reaches far from the nuclei, as in an anion or a weakly bound complex. It is a benchmark-level set and its cost limits it to very small systems. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000548
name: aug-cc-pV6Z
def: "A correlation-consistent basis set that gives 6 functions per valence orbital and adds a set of diffuse functions. It is one of the largest standard augmented sets available. It is used to study convergence, or for properties that need extreme accuracy in both correlation and diffuse electron density. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000549
name: aug-cc-pV8Z
def: "A correlation-consistent basis set that gives 8 functions per valence orbital and adds a set of diffuse functions. It is a research set used almost only on atoms and diatomic molecules, to study how properties sensitive to diffuse electrons converge. It is not usable for molecular calculations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000550
name: aug-cc-pV9Z
def: "A correlation-consistent basis set that gives 9 functions per valence orbital and adds a set of diffuse functions. Like the octuple-zeta version it is a research set for atoms and diatomic molecules only. It is not usable for molecular calculations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000551
name: aug-cc-pVDZ-RI
def: "An auxiliary basis set built to be paired with the diffuse-augmented correlation-consistent double-zeta orbital basis in resolution-of-identity or density fitting calculations. It carries the extra functions needed to fit products involving the diffuse part of that basis. Pairing it with a different orbital basis degrades the approximation it was fitted for. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000552
name: aug-cc-pVTZ-RI
def: "An auxiliary basis set built to be paired with the diffuse-augmented correlation-consistent triple-zeta orbital basis in resolution-of-identity or density fitting calculations. It carries the extra functions needed to fit products involving the diffuse part of that basis. Pairing it with a different orbital basis degrades the approximation it was fitted for. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000553
name: aug-cc-pVQZ-RI
def: "An auxiliary basis set built to be paired with the diffuse-augmented correlation-consistent quadruple-zeta orbital basis in density fitting calculations. It carries the extra functions needed to fit products involving the diffuse part of that basis. Its purpose is speed, not accuracy. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000554
name: aug-cc-pV5Z-RI
def: "An auxiliary basis set built to be paired with the diffuse-augmented correlation-consistent quintuple-zeta orbital basis in resolution-of-identity or density fitting calculations. It carries the extra functions needed to fit products involving the diffuse part of that orbital basis. Its purpose is speed, not accuracy. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000555
name: aug-cc-pV6Z-RI
def: "An auxiliary basis set built to be paired with the diffuse-augmented correlation-consistent sextuple-zeta orbital basis in resolution-of-identity or density fitting calculations. It is required in practice, because calculations at that orbital basis size are otherwise not feasible. Its purpose is speed, not accuracy. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000556
name: aug-cc-pCVDZ
def: "A correlation-consistent basis set at double-zeta level that adds both diffuse functions and tight functions describing correlation involving the core electrons. Standard valence sets assume the core is inert, which fails for properties that depend on it. It is the smallest combination that carries both additions. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000557
name: aug-cc-pCVTZ
def: "A correlation-consistent basis set at triple-zeta level that adds both diffuse functions and tight functions describing correlation involving the core electrons. Standard valence sets assume the core is inert, which fails for properties that depend on it. It is the usual working choice where a system needs diffuse character and core-valence correlation at once. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000558
name: aug-cc-pCVQZ
def: "A correlation-consistent basis set at quadruple-zeta level that adds both diffuse functions and tight functions describing correlation involving the core electrons. Standard valence sets assume the core is inert, which fails for properties that depend on it. It is used where both effects must be converged rather than merely present. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000559
name: aug-cc-pCV5Z
def: "A correlation-consistent basis set at quintuple-zeta level that adds both diffuse functions and tight functions describing correlation involving the core electrons. Standard valence sets assume the core is inert, which fails for properties that depend on it. It is a benchmark set whose cost restricts it to small systems. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000560
name: aug-cc-pCV6Z
def: "A correlation-consistent basis set at sextuple-zeta level that adds both diffuse functions and tight functions describing correlation involving the core electrons. Standard valence sets assume the core is inert, which fails for properties that depend on it. It is among the largest standard basis sets in existence and is confined to atoms and diatomic molecules. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000561
name: aug-cc-pV(D+d)Z
def: "A correlation-consistent double-zeta basis set that adds both a set of diffuse functions and 1 extra optimised d type polarization function. It is meant for the second-row elements sodium to argon in situations that also need diffuse functions, such as anions and weakly bound complexes. It combines 2 separate corrections to the standard double-zeta set. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000562
name: aug-cc-pV(T+d)Z
def: "A correlation-consistent triple-zeta basis set that adds both a set of diffuse functions and 1 extra optimised d type polarization function. It targets the second-row elements sodium to argon where both diffuse electron density and d orbital flexibility matter, such as anions and intermolecular complexes. It is the triple-zeta member of that combined family. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000563
name: aug-cc-pV(Q+d)Z
def: "A correlation-consistent quadruple-zeta basis set that adds both a set of diffuse functions and 1 extra optimised d type polarization function. It is used for benchmark results on systems containing the second-row elements sodium to argon whose properties depend on both corrections. It is large enough that its use is restricted to small systems. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000564
name: aug-cc-pV(5+d)Z
def: "A correlation-consistent quintuple-zeta basis set that adds both a set of diffuse functions and 1 extra optimised d type polarization function. It is a specialised benchmark set for the second-row elements sodium to argon in processes that also need diffuse functions. It is close to the complete basis set limit for those elements. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000565
name: aug-cc-pV(6+d)Z
def: "A correlation-consistent sextuple-zeta basis set that adds both a set of diffuse functions and 1 extra optimised d type polarization function. It is among the largest combinations available and is used only for extreme benchmark work on very small systems containing the second-row elements sodium to argon. Both corrections apply to those elements alone. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000566
name: aug-cc-pwCVDZ
def: "A correlation-consistent double-zeta basis set that adds diffuse functions together with tight functions weighted towards core-valence correlation. The weighting concentrates the added functions where core and valence electrons actually correlate, rather than describing the core itself. It suits a small system needing both diffuse character and core-valence correlation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000567
name: aug-cc-pwCVTZ
def: "A correlation-consistent triple-zeta basis set that adds diffuse functions together with weighted core-valence correlating functions. It is the level at which core-valence effects are usually first worth their cost. Both additions are needed for properties sensitive to diffuse electrons in systems where the core cannot be treated as inert. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000568
name: aug-cc-pwCVQZ
def: "A correlation-consistent quadruple-zeta basis set that adds diffuse functions together with weighted core-valence correlating functions. It is used for high-accuracy work where both effects must be converged rather than merely present. Its size restricts it to small molecules. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000569
name: aug-cc-pwCV5Z
def: "A correlation-consistent quintuple-zeta basis set that adds diffuse functions together with weighted core-valence correlating functions. It is a benchmark set used to approach the complete basis set limit. Its cost restricts it to atoms and very small molecules. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000570
name: aug-pc-0
def: "A polarization-consistent basis set at the lowest level of the pc-n family, with diffuse functions added. The family is built so results improve smoothly as the level rises, which makes extrapolation to the limit reliable. This level is the starting point of that sequence rather than a basis for production work. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000571
name: aug-pc-1
def: "A polarization-consistent basis set at the first level of the pc-n family, with diffuse functions added. The level corresponds roughly to polarized double-zeta quality. It is the smallest member of the family used for real calculations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000572
name: aug-pc-2
def: "A polarization-consistent basis set at the second level of the pc-n family, with a set of diffuse functions added. The second level corresponds to polarized triple-zeta quality, and the family is built so that results converge smoothly as the level rises. The diffuse functions make it suitable for anions, intermolecular interactions and polarizabilities. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000573
name: aug-pc-3
def: "A polarization-consistent basis set at the third level of the pc-n family, with a set of diffuse functions added. The third level corresponds to polarized quadruple-zeta quality. It is used where both high accuracy and a correct description of diffuse electron density are needed. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000574
name: aug-pc-4
def: "A polarization-consistent basis set at the fourth level of the pc-n family, with a set of diffuse functions added. The fourth level corresponds to polarized quintuple-zeta quality and is the largest in common use in this family. It is a benchmark set for small systems whose properties depend on diffuse electrons. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000575
name: Ahlrichs Coulomb fitting
def: "An auxiliary basis set developed by the Ahlrichs group to fit the Coulomb part of the electron repulsion in a density fitting calculation. Fitting only the Coulomb term, rather than the whole 2-electron integral set, gives most of the speed-up at very little cost in accuracy. It is matched to the Karlsruhe orbital basis sets. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000576
name: Ahlrichs Polarization
def: "A set of polarization functions, of higher angular momentum than the atom occupies in its ground state, developed by the Ahlrichs group for the Karlsruhe basis sets. Polarization functions let the electron density distort away from atomic symmetry, which is what bonding requires. Without them a basis set cannot describe a bond angle correctly. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000577
name: Ahlrichs pvDZ
def: "A basis set from the Ahlrichs group giving 2 functions per valence orbital together with polarization functions. The polarization functions let the electron cloud distort away from atomic symmetry, which is what bonding requires and which the unpolarized member of the family cannot do. It is the smallest basis set in that family suitable for real calculations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000578
name: Ahlrichs VDZ
def: "A basis set from the Ahlrichs group giving 2 functions per valence orbital and no polarization functions. Without polarization functions the electron cloud cannot distort away from atomic symmetry, so bond angles are poorly described. It is used as a starting point rather than for results. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000579
name: Ahlrichs VTZ
def: "A basis set from the Ahlrichs group giving 3 functions per valence orbital and no polarization functions. The extra valence function improves the radial description while leaving the angular one unchanged. Like its double-zeta counterpart it is normally used with polarization functions added. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000485 ! split-valence basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000580
name: plane-wave
def: "A type of quantum mechanics basis set consisting of periodic sine and cosine functions (waves) defined by their direction and wavelength. Plane waves are particularly well-suited for calculations on periodic systems like crystals or surfaces, often used in conjunction with Density Functional Theory and pseudopotentials. Their systematic improvability by increasing the number of waves (controlled by an energy cutoff) is a key advantage in solid-state simulations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000432 ! quantum mechanics basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000581
name: real-space
def: "A method that represents electronic wavefunctions or densities as values on a grid of points in ordinary 3-dimensional space, rather than as coefficients of basis functions. Accuracy is then improved by making the grid finer, which is a single adjustable control. It parallelises well, because each point depends mostly on its neighbours. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000432 ! quantum mechanics basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000582
name: intrinsic reaction coordinate analysis
def: "A coordinate analysis technique that defines the reaction path as the minimum energy path connecting reactants and products through the transition state on the potential energy surface. This path follows the steepest descent direction (in terms of energy) down from the transition state towards both the reactant and product basins. It is considered a more rigorous definition of the reaction pathway at zero Kelvin. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000028 ! coordinate analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000583
name: intrinsic reaction coordinate maximum analysis
def: "An analysis method that locates the highest point along the lowest-energy path joining reactant and product. That point is the transition state, and its height above the reactant is the reaction barrier. Finding it is what turns a computed path into a predicted rate. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000582 ! intrinsic reaction coordinate analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000584
name: surface analysis
def: "A form of reaction analysis focused on characterizing the features of the potential energy surface (PES), which maps the system's energy as a function of its atomic coordinates. This analysis identifies critical points like energy minima (stable states), saddle points (transition states), and intersections between surfaces that govern molecular stability and reactivity. It helps visualize the energetic landscape explored during reactions or conformational changes." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000027 ! reaction analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000585
name: conical intersection point analysis
def: "A critical feature identified through surface analysis representing a point in molecular geometry where two electronic potential energy surfaces of the same spin-symmetry become degenerate (have the same energy). These points act as funnels facilitating rapid, non-adiabatic transitions between electronic states, crucial for understanding photochemical reactions and relaxation processes. Their location and properties dictate the efficiency and outcome of such electronic transitions. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000584 ! surface analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000586
name: saddle analysis
def: "A saddle point on a potential energy surface is a stationary point (where forces are zero) that corresponds to an energy maximum along one direction (the reaction pathway) and an energy minimum along all other directions. It represents the highest energy barrier that must be overcome during a chemical transformation. Locating saddle points is key to identifying transition states and calculating activation energies for reactions. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000584 ! surface analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000587
name: minimum crossing analysis
def: "A minimum crossing point, often Minimum Energy Crossing Point (MECP), is the molecular geometry where two potential energy surfaces corresponding to different electronic spin states (e.g., singlet and triplet) intersect at the lowest possible energy. These points are crucial for understanding pathways of spin-forbidden reactions or intersystem crossing events. Locating MECPs helps analyze transitions between different spin manifolds. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000584 ! surface analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000588
name: pathway analysis
def: "A form of reaction analysis aimed at identifying and characterizing the sequence of intermediate states and transition states that connect reactants to products, effectively mapping the reaction pathway. This can involve exploring multiple possible routes, using algorithms to find minimum energy paths, or analyzing trajectories from reaction dynamics simulations." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000027 ! reaction analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986
property_value: skos:closeMatch operation:3928

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000589
name: trace gradient extremal analysis
def: "A specific computational technique sometimes used in pathway analysis to find reaction paths or other significant paths on a potential energy surface by following trajectories associated with gradient extremals. This approach can potentially identify pathways connecting different energy minima without necessarily locating the transition states first. It serves as an alternative method for exploring the connections within a complex energy landscape. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000588 ! pathway analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000590
name: plot data format
def: "A category for file formats designed to store numerical data in a specific structure that is easily parsed and read by graphing or plotting software (e.g., Grace, Gnuplot). These are structured data files typically containing columns of numbers and plotting directives." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000436 ! data format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000591
name: agr format
def: "A text-based data file format for the Grace/Xmgrace plotting program. It contains numerical data along with commands that specify the appearance of the graph, such as titles, labels, and colors. This format allows for the creation of complex, publication-quality plots. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000590 ! plot data format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000594 ! Gnuplot data format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000592
name: stripped topology format
def: "A file format that represents a molecular system's topology after certain atoms, typically solvent or ions, have been removed. This format is created to simplify analysis by focusing only on the solute, while retaining the necessary parameter information for calculations. It is commonly used in post-processing steps like MM/PBSA free energy calculations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001091 ! molecular topology format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000593
name: CPPTRAJ standard output format
def: "A text data format in which cpptraj writes time-series results by default, as columns of numbers with the frame or time in the first column and the calculated values in the rest. It is space-delimited and carries no header structure beyond a comment line, so plotting and analysis programs read it directly. Files are commonly given the extension .dat. (UNVERIFIED)" []
comment: Typically with .dat extension, but could be using other file extension.
is_a: MOLSIM:000439 ! simulation log format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000594
name: Gnuplot data format
def: "A data file format designed to be used with the Gnuplot plotting program. It typically consists of columns of numerical data in a simple text-based layout that Gnuplot can easily parse and visualize. This format is widely used for generating scientific graphs and plots from raw data. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "gnu format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000590 ! plot data format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000595
name: XPLOR format
def: "A file format associated with the XPLOR-NIH software, used for representing 3D grid data. It is a text-based format that defines a grid and the data values at each point, often used for electron density maps. This format is a common way to store volumetric data in crystallography and NMR. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000590 ! plot data format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000596
name: grid format
def: "A file format for representing data that is distributed over a three-dimensional grid. Originating from the XPLOR-NIH software, it is used to store volumetric data like electron density or potential maps. This format is used in structural biology to visualize grid-based properties around a molecule." []
synonym: ".grid" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000590 ! plot data format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000597
name: DX format
def: "A file format for the OpenDX (Data Explorer) visualization program, used to represent 3D grid-based data. It stores scalar or vector data on a regular grid, making it suitable for visualizing properties like electrostatic potential or molecular density. This format is a common output for scientific programs that generate volumetric data. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "OpenDX format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000590 ! plot data format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000598
name: mdvel format
def: "A data format that stores the velocity of every atom of a system at each saved step of an AMBER simulation. It records velocities where a trajectory format records positions. It is needed for analyses such as velocity autocorrelation that cannot be done from coordinates alone. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "AMBER mdvel format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001090 ! molecular trajectory format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000599
name: AMBER REM log format
def: "A log file format that records the progress of an Amber replica exchange molecular dynamics simulation. The main file extension for Amber REM (Replica Exchange Molecular Dynamics) log files is .log, typically named as rem.log, according to the Amber documentation and tutorial resources. This log file tracks exchanges, replica temperatures, and relevant statistics for the REMD process. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "Amber Replica Exchange Log" EXACT []
synonym: "rem.log" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000439 ! simulation log format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000600
name: AMBER eigenvector format
def: "A file format that holds the eigenvectors and eigenvalues produced by principal component analysis, normal mode analysis or quasiharmonic analysis in AMBER. The vectors come from diagonalising a covariance or mass-weighted covariance matrix, and are used in essential dynamics analysis of molecular simulations. There is no required extension: the file is usually called evecs.dat or evecs.out, and its layout is standardised so that AMBER tools such as cpptraj and ptraj can read and write it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "evecs.dat" EXACT []
synonym: "evecs.out" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000439 ! simulation log format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000601
name: cpout format
def: "An output file format produced during constant pH molecular dynamics in AMBER, holding pH-dependent state changes, lambda values, protonation fractions and statistics for titratable groups. These files are produced as a result of the simulation or post-simulation analysis, not used to initiate or restart simulations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: ".cpout" EXACT []
synonym: "AMBER cpout format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000439 ! simulation log format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000602
name: geometry optimization analysis
def: "A computational procedure within structural analysis used to find the atomic coordinates corresponding to a stationary point, typically a local minimum, on the potential energy surface, representing a stable or equilibrium structure. Starting from an initial guess geometry, algorithms iteratively adjust atomic positions to minimize the energy and reduce the forces acting on the atoms until convergence criteria are met. This predicts the most stable three-dimensional structure for a given molecular composition and electronic state. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000917 ! structural analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000603
name: FMO geometry optimization analysis
def: "A specific geometry optimization technique designed for large molecular systems that employs the Fragment Molecular Orbital (FMO) method. The FMO method divides the large system (like a protein or DNA segment) into smaller, manageable fragments, performs quantum mechanical calculations on fragments and fragment pairs, and combines the results to approximate the properties (energy, gradient) of the entire system. This fragmentation allows for efficient geometry optimization of very large biomolecules at a quantum mechanical level. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000602 ! geometry optimization analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000604
name: single point energy analysis
def: "An energy analysis calculation that determines the potential energy of a molecular system for a single, fixed geometric arrangement of its atoms (a specific 'snapshot' or structure), without performing geometry optimization or simulating dynamics. This provides the energy value for that particular conformation according to the chosen theoretical method (e.g., force field or quantum mechanical level). It's often used to compare the relative energies of different pre-defined structures." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000950 ! energy analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000605
name: high accuracy energies analysis
def: "A data analysis method that computes potential energies with a high-level and computationally expensive treatment, such as coupled cluster theory or density functional theory with a large basis set. It is applied to a few chosen structures, typically optimised minima, transition states or representative conformations, rather than to a whole trajectory. The values serve as benchmarks for reaction barriers, binding energies and conformational stabilities obtained more cheaply. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000950 ! energy analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000606
name: energy decomposition analysis
def: "An energy analysis technique designed to partition the total interaction energy between two or more interacting molecular fragments (e.g., in a complex) into physically meaningful components based on the underlying quantum mechanical or molecular mechanical framework. Common components include electrostatics, exchange-repulsion (Pauli repulsion), polarization (induction), and charge transfer (or dispersion in some schemes), providing insights into the nature of the forces driving the interaction. Different EDA schemes exist (e.g., Morokuma, SAPT, FMO-EDA). (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000950 ! energy analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000607
name: force analysis
def: "A structural analysis technique that involves calculating the forces acting on each atom for a given molecular configuration. These forces represent the negative gradient of the potential energy and indicate the direction and magnitude of the tendency for atoms to move to lower the system's energy. Analyzing forces is crucial for geometry optimization (where forces are minimized), understanding structural strain, and driving molecular dynamics simulations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000917 ! structural analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000608
name: CCP4 map format
def: "A binary data format that stores 3-dimensional volumetric data on a regular grid, most often electron density from X-ray crystallography or a map from cryogenic electron microscopy. It is the format structural biology tools read and write by default for such maps. It lets the shape of a protein or nucleic acid be seen and interpreted. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: ".ccp4" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000909 ! volumetric data format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000609
name: cmatrix format
def: "A binary file format that stores pre-calculated pairwise distances between structures. It has no mandatory extension, but .cmatrix is the conventional one. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: ".cmatrix" EXACT []
synonym: "CPPTRAJ pairwise distance cache format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:010020 ! molecular trajectory analysis format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001040 ! distance matrix format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000610
name: thermodynamics analysis
def: "A type of analysis, often performed using data from simulations or specialized calculations complementary to MD, focused on determining the thermodynamic properties governing molecular systems. This includes calculating state functions like enthalpy, entropy, and particularly free energy, which dictate stability, equilibrium constants, and the spontaneity of molecular processes. Such analysis provides insights into the energetic driving forces behind biomolecular behavior. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000026 ! analysis method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000611
name: thermal property analysis
def: "A subset of thermodynamics analysis specifically dealing with how a system's properties change with temperature or involve heat exchange. This includes calculating quantities like heat capacity (how much energy is needed to raise the temperature), coefficients of thermal expansion, or enthalpy changes associated with specific processes. These properties are important for understanding temperature dependence and energy balance in molecular systems. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000610 ! thermodynamics analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000612
name: thermochemical analysis
def: "A specific type of thermal properties analysis focused on quantifying the heat absorbed or released during chemical reactions or phase transitions, often involving the calculation of enthalpies of formation, reaction enthalpies, or activation enthalpies. Typically employing quantum mechanical methods or specialized simulation setups, this analysis provides fundamental data on the energetics of chemical transformations. It helps predict reaction feasibility and energy output/input. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000611 ! thermal property analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000613
name: prep format
def: "A text data format used by AMBER to define a new molecular building block, giving its atoms, their types and charges, the bonds between them and its geometry. It is how a residue that no standard library contains is introduced. It is written by the parameter assignment tools rather than by hand. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: ".prep" EXACT []
synonym: ".prepi" EXACT []
synonym: "AMBER prep format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001091 ! molecular topology format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000614
name: OFF format
def: "A text data format used by AMBER to store a library of molecular building blocks together with their force field parameters and geometry. Unlike the prep format, which defines one block, a single file holds many. It is the format the standard residue libraries are distributed in. (UNVERIFIED)" []
comment: AMBER lib format
synonym: ".off" EXACT []
synonym: "AMBER Object File Format" EXACT []
synonym: "AMBER off format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001091 ! molecular topology format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000615
name: free energy calculation analysis
def: "A thermodynamics analysis method that computes the free energy of a system, or more often the free energy difference between 2 states such as bound and unbound or folded and unfolded. Free energy combines energy and disorder, so it, rather than energy alone, decides which state a process settles into. Obtaining it usually needs enhanced sampling, because the states of interest are separated by barriers. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000610 ! thermodynamics analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000616
name: free state FMO analysis
def: "A specific computational task within a free energy calculation framework that uses the Fragment Molecular Orbital (FMO) method to determine the energy and properties of a molecule in its unbound ('free') state. This is often required when calculating binding free energies, where the energy of the isolated components serves as a reference point (G free). Employing FMO makes such quantum mechanical calculations feasible for the large molecules often involved in biomolecular binding events. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000615 ! free energy calculation analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000617
name: Gaussian fluctuation free energy analysis
def: "A free energy analysis method that estimates free energy differences by assuming the system's fluctuations about its average state follow a multi-dimensional Gaussian distribution. That assumption reduces the calculation to the mean and covariance of the sampled coordinates, which is cheap. Its accuracy depends entirely on how well the assumption holds for the system in question. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000615 ! free energy calculation analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000618
name: PC+ correction analysis
def: "A free energy analysis method that adjusts a computed binding free energy using an empirical term based on the number and kind of charged atoms at the interface. It exists because continuum solvent models systematically misjudge the cost of desolvating charged groups. It is applied after the main calculation rather than inside it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000615 ! free energy calculation analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000619
name: universal correction analysis
def: "A free energy analysis method that adds a fixed entropic penalty to a computed binding free energy to represent the translational and rotational freedom a ligand loses on binding. The penalty is taken from prior work rather than computed for the system at hand. It supplies a term that end-point methods otherwise omit entirely. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "UC Correction" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000615 ! free energy calculation analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000620
name: density-functional based tight-binding
def: "A semi-empirical quantum method derived from density functional theory by expanding its energy about a reference density and tabulating the resulting integrals in advance. Tabulating them removes almost all the cost while keeping a quantum description. It is 2 to 3 orders of magnitude faster than the theory it comes from. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "DFTB" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000803 ! semi-empirical method
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000804 ! all-valence-electron restricted

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000621
name: self-consistent-charge density-functional based tight-binding
def: "A tight binding method that solves for the atomic charges self-consistently, so each atom's charge responds to the others rather than being fixed. Adding that step corrects the description of polar and charged systems, which the non-self-consistent form handles badly. It is the form nearly all current tight binding work uses. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "SCC-DFTB" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000620 ! density-functional based tight-binding

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000622
name: third-order self-consistent-charge density-functional based tight-binding
def: "A tight binding method that carries the expansion of the energy one order further than the self-consistent charge form, adding a term for how an atom's response to charge itself changes with charge. That term corrects the description of charged and hydrogen-bonded systems, which the lower order handles poorly. It is the form recommended for biomolecular work. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "DFTB3" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000621 ! self-consistent-charge density-functional based tight-binding

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000623
name: quantum interaction
def: "An interaction that cannot be described correctly without quantum mechanics, because it depends on the wave nature of electrons or on energy taking discrete values. Bond formation, charge transfer and dispersion are all of this kind. A classical force field represents their effects approximately with fitted terms rather than describing them. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000057 ! interaction type

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000624
name: hyperfine coupling
def: "A quantum mechanical interaction representing the coupling between the magnetic moment associated with the spin of an electron and the magnetic moment of a nearby atomic nucleus. This interaction leads to small shifts and splittings ('hyperfine structure') in atomic and molecular energy levels, which are observable in high-resolution spectroscopy, particularly Electron Paramagnetic Resonance (EPR) for species with unpaired electrons, and also in NMR. It provides valuable information about the electron distribution (spin density) near the nucleus and thus molecular structure. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000626 ! spin effect
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000625 ! spin-orbit coupling

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000625
name: spin-orbit coupling
def: "A relativistic quantum mechanical interaction between a particle's intrinsic spin angular momentum and its orbital angular momentum (due to its motion, e.g., an electron orbiting a nucleus). This coupling mixes electronic states and becomes increasingly significant for electrons in atoms with high atomic number (heavy atoms). Spin-orbit coupling influences electronic energy levels, causes splitting of spectral lines (fine structure), and facilitates transitions between states of different spin multiplicity (e.g., intersystem crossing in photochemistry, important for phosphorescence). (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000626 ! spin effect

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000626
name: spin effect
def: "A physical effect arising from the intrinsic angular momentum carried by electrons and atomic nuclei. Spin gives each particle a magnetic moment, and the interactions between those moments are what produce magnetic resonance signals and fine structure in spectra. A calculation that ignores spin cannot reproduce them. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000623 ! quantum interaction

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000627
name: density functional theory
def: "A quantum mechanical method that obtains the energy and other properties of a system from its electron density rather than from the many-electron wavefunction. The density depends on 3 spatial coordinates however many electrons there are, which is what makes the method affordable for large systems. Its accuracy rests on the approximate functional chosen to relate density to energy. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "DFT" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000173 ! quantum mechanics

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000628
name: electrostatic embedding QM/MM
def: "A QM/MM scheme in which the partial charges of the classical region enter the quantum calculation directly, so the quantum region's electron distribution responds to its surroundings. That response is what captures how a protein environment alters the chemistry inside an active site. It costs more than the mechanical scheme and is markedly more accurate. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000388 ! QM/MM simulation

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000629
name: QM/MM Ewald summation
def: "An Ewald summation method for a periodic system in which part is described quantum mechanically and the rest by a force field. It must handle 3 kinds of interaction: within the quantum region, within the classical region, and between them. Getting the third right is what distinguishes it, because the 2 descriptions represent charge differently. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "Ewald for QM/MM" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000428 ! Ewald summation

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000630
name: multilayer QM/MM
def: "A QM/MM method using more than 2 levels of description, such as an expensive quantum method for a reacting group, a cheaper quantum method around it, and a force field beyond that. Each boundary must be handled separately, so the arrangement is more delicate than a 2-level one. It is used where the reacting region is small but its immediate surroundings still need quantum treatment. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000388 ! QM/MM simulation

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000631
name: difference-based adaptive solvation QM/MM
def: "A QM/MM method that lets solvent molecules move between the quantum and the classical region during a simulation, deciding the boundary from the difference in energy between the 2 descriptions. Solvent near a reacting centre is therefore treated quantum mechanically only while it is near. A fixed boundary would either trap the wrong molecules inside or cut bonds as they diffuse across it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000484 ! adaptive solvent QM/MM

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000632
name: adaptive buffered force-mixing
def: "A QM/MM method in which the boundary moves as the simulation proceeds, with a buffer zone where forces from the quantum and classical descriptions are blended. The blending prevents the jump in force that an abrupt reassignment would cause as a molecule crosses. It is what lets solvent diffuse in and out of a quantum region during a run. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000388 ! QM/MM simulation

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000633
name: surface potential analysis
def: "A structural analysis method that computes a field, most often the electrostatic potential, and displays it on the surface of a molecule. Colouring the surface by potential shows at a glance which regions would attract a positive or a negative partner. It is how electrostatic complementarity between 2 binding partners is judged. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000584 ! surface analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000634
name: electrostatic potential calculation analysis
def: "An analysis method that computes the electrostatic potential a molecule's charge distribution produces at points around it. Mapped onto the molecular surface, it shows where an approaching charge would be attracted or repelled. It is how a binding site is judged to be electrostatically complementary to a ligand. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000633 ! surface potential analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000635
name: frequency analysis
def: "An analysis method, typically based on quantum mechanics or molecular mechanics, used to calculate the vibrational frequencies and corresponding normal modes (patterns of atomic motion) of a molecule, usually performed at a stationary point on the potential energy surface (like an energy minimum or transition state). These frequencies can be compared to experimental vibrational spectra (e.g., IR, Raman) to validate the structure or force field. The analysis also helps confirm the nature of the stationary point (minimums have all real frequencies, transition states have one imaginary frequency). (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000026 ! analysis method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000636
name: anharmonic vibrational corrections analysis
def: "A refinement within frequency analysis that goes beyond the standard harmonic approximation (which assumes vibrations occur in a perfectly parabolic potential well) to account for the true, anharmonic shape of the potential energy surface. Calculating these corrections yields more accurate vibrational frequencies that better match experimental observations, particularly for large-amplitude motions or systems with significant vibrational coupling. This improves the quantitative interpretation of vibrational spectra and thermodynamic properties derived from frequencies. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000635 ! frequency analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000637
name: semi-empirical Born-Oppenheimer molecular dynamics
def: "A simulation method in which the forces at each step come from a fast approximate quantum mechanical calculation, solved fully at each new geometry. Being quantum, it can describe bonds being made and broken, which a force field cannot. Being approximate, it is fast enough to run for a useful length of time. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "SEBOMD" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000843 ! molecular dynamics

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000638
name: hybrid ReaxFF/AMBER molecular dynamics
def: "A simulation method combining a reactive force field for the region where bonds form and break with a conventional force field for everything else. The reactive treatment costs far more, so confining it to a small region makes a large system affordable. The boundary between the 2 must be placed where no bond will cross it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000843 ! molecular dynamics

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000639
name: polarizable force field
def: "A force field that represents how a molecule's charge distribution is distorted by the electric field around it, rather than fixing the charges in advance. It matters where the environment changes markedly, as when a ligand moves from water into a protein interior. It costs several times more, because the induced response must be solved for at every step. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "fluctuating charge model" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000007 ! force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000640
name: polarizable Gaussian multipole force field
def: "A polarizable force field in which each atom carries a multipole expansion built from Gaussian-shaped charge distributions, and responds to the field around it. Using distributed shapes rather than points lets the model describe how charge density overlaps between close atoms. It targets the short-range region where point-charge models are least reliable. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000639 ! polarizable force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000641
name: empirical dispersion correction
def: "A correction added to a quantum chemistry calculation to supply the weak long-range attraction that most density functionals omit. The functionals fail here because the attraction arises from correlated fluctuations they do not describe. The correction is a fitted term depending on the atoms and their separation, and it is what makes density functional theory usable for stacking and binding. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "D3 dispersion model" EXACT []
synonym: "grimme dispersion correction" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001463 ! QM/MM model component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000642
name: Gaussian-shaped constraint simulation
def: "A Gaussian-shaped constraint simulation is a type of restrained simulation where the artificial potential used to guide the system has the mathematical form of a Gaussian function. This provides a smooth, harmonic-like restraint near the target value but becomes weaker further away." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000364 ! restrained simulation method
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000643
name: Lorentz-Berthelot mixing modeling
def: "A rule for obtaining the van der Waals parameters between 2 different atom types from the parameters of each alone, averaging their sizes and taking the geometric mean of their interaction strengths. Without such a rule every pair of atom types would need its own fitted parameters. The rule is a convenience rather than physics, which is why some pairs need an explicit override. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000374 ! force field parameterization modeling

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000644
name: HF/6-31G RESP
def: "A protocol for deriving atomic charges in which the electrostatic potential is computed at the Hartree-Fock level with the 6-31G* basis set, then point charges are fitted to it with a restraint pulling buried charges towards zero. That combination is not the most accurate available; it is used because it systematically overestimates polarity by about the amount a simulation in fixed-charge water requires. It is the convention the AMBER force fields were built on, so charges for a new molecule must follow it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000204 ! ligand charge model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000645
name: SIRAH force field
def: "A coarse-grained force field for proteins and nucleic acids whose beads are chosen to preserve the chemical character and the directionality of interactions such as hydrogen bonds. It keeps more chemical detail than a purely shape-based mapping, at a higher cost. It can be combined with explicit coarse-grained water. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000736 ! coarse-grained force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000646
name: empirical metal center parameterization modeling
def: "An empirical metal center parameterization is a method for deriving force field parameters for a metal ion and its coordination site by fitting them to reproduce experimental data. This can include data such as crystal structures, vibrational frequencies, or binding energies for a set of known metal complexes. For experts, this approach is often necessary for metal ions because standard, general-purpose parameterization methods can fail to capture their complex electronic and bonding behavior. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000374 ! force field parameterization modeling

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000647
name: hybrid solvent MM-PBSA analysis
def: "A free energy analysis method that estimates binding free energy using explicit water molecules near the solute and a continuum model for the bulk. It keeps the specific water-mediated contacts that a continuum model cannot represent, while avoiding the cost of explicit solvent everywhere. The energies are then combined in the usual molecular mechanics Poisson-Boltzmann surface area way. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000262 ! molecular mechanics Poisson Boltzmann surface area analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000648
name: BAR/PBSA analysis
def: "A free energy analysis method that combines the Bennett acceptance ratio estimator with the molecular mechanics Poisson-Boltzmann surface area treatment of solvation. It aims to keep the rigour of an alchemical estimator where it matters most while using a continuum model for the rest. The division between the 2 parts is what distinguishes it from either method alone. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000615 ! free energy calculation analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000649
name: kinetic map analysis
def: "Kinetic map analysis is a method used to visualize the network of transitions between different conformational states that a molecule visits during a simulation. It represents the molecular states as nodes and the transitions between them as connections, often colored or weighted by their probability or rate. This provides a clear and intuitive map of the dominant pathways for conformational change, helping to understand the mechanism and timescales of processes like ligand binding or protein folding." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000939 ! dynamics analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000650
name: commute map analysis
def: "Commute map analysis is a method used to identify how different parts of a molecule are dynamically connected, even if they are far apart. It transforms complex molecular coordinates into a mathematical space where the Euclidean distance between points directly corresponds to the commute time (the mean time it takes for a molecule to transition between two conformations and back). This analysis helps to uncover long-range communication networks within a protein that are essential for its function, such as in allosteric regulation." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000939 ! dynamics analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000651
name: entropic decomposition analysis
def: "A thermodynamics analysis method that splits the total entropy change of a process into separate contributions. The split may be by kind of motion, into translational, rotational and vibrational parts, or by component, into solute and solvent. It shows which source of disorder drives a process, for example whether binding is favoured by the release of ordered water. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000309 ! entropy analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000652
name: molecular reconstruction from distribution functions analysis
def: "An advanced analysis method that attempts to generate a three-dimensional model of a molecule or a molecular complex using statistical information about its structure. It takes one or more distribution functions, such as the pairwise distances between atoms obtained from a simulation or experiment, and uses an optimization algorithm to find a 3D structure that is consistent with those distributions. This technique can be used to build structural models from sparse or low-resolution data. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000917 ! structural analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000653
name: polar decomposition analysis
def: "A structural analysis method that separates the change in shape of a group of atoms between 2 conformations into a pure rotation and an internal deformation. It does this by factorising the matrix that maps one set of coordinates onto the other. It answers whether a domain has turned as a rigid body or genuinely changed shape. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000610 ! thermodynamics analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000654
name: path integral molecular dynamics
def: "A simulation method that includes quantum behaviour of the atomic nuclei themselves, by replacing each nucleus with a ring of connected copies. The spread of the ring represents the uncertainty in the particle's position, which is large for light atoms. It matters for hydrogen, where treating the nucleus as a point misplaces bond lengths and reaction barriers. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000843 ! molecular dynamics

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000655
name: replica-exchange free energy perturbation
def: "Replica-exchange free energy perturbation is an enhanced sampling method that combines replica-exchange with an alchemical free energy calculation. It runs multiple simulations in parallel, each at a different intermediate state (lambda value) of the alchemical transformation, and periodically attempts to swap the lambda values between replicas." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000656
name: constant redox potential molecular dynamics
def: "A simulation method in which groups can gain or lose an electron during the run, coupled to a chosen electrode potential. It is the redox counterpart of constant pH simulation and uses the same machinery. It is used for proteins whose function involves moving electrons, where the oxidation state is not fixed in advance. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000843 ! molecular dynamics

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000657
name: X-ray refinement
def: "X-ray refinement is the computational process of building and optimizing an atomic model of a molecule to fit the experimental data from an X-ray crystallography experiment. It is an iterative procedure where the atomic coordinates are adjusted to best match the calculated electron density map, while simultaneously ensuring that the model has realistic chemical geometry, such as proper bond lengths and angles. This process is the final and crucial step in determining a high-resolution crystal structure." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000201 ! X-ray crystallography
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000658
name: grid binning analysis
def: "A structural analysis method that divides the simulation box into a regular 3-dimensional grid of cells and counts how often atoms of a chosen type fall in each cell across a trajectory. The counts give the average spatial density of those atoms. It is the usual way to map where water or ions gather around a solute. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000917 ! structural analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000659
name: periodic boundary imaging
def: "A fundamental trajectory post-processing step used to correct the visual representation of molecules in a periodic system. When a molecule crosses a periodic boundary, it can appear 'broken' or jump across the box in the raw output. This procedure translates the atomic coordinates back into the primary simulation box, implicitly fixing broken 'image bonds' to ensure target molecules remain whole and centered. This is a mandatory prerequisite for correct visualization and accurate calculation of some structural properties." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001767 ! trajectory post-processing
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000660
name: LES trajectory splitting analysis
def: "A trajectory processing method that separates the single combined trajectory written by a locally enhanced sampling run into 1 trajectory per copy of the duplicated region. Locally enhanced sampling simulates several copies of one part of a molecule at once, and their coordinates are interleaved in the output. Splitting them is required before each copy can be analysed or the copies averaged. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000939 ! dynamics analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000661
name: structure modification modeling
def: "A structure modification method is a computational procedure that alters the atomic coordinates or composition of a molecular structure file. This includes a wide range of operations such as adding or deleting atoms, rotating or translating molecules, or building new polymeric chains. For researchers, these methods are the fundamental tools used to build, edit, and prepare molecular models for simulation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000305 ! modeling method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000662
name: ion randomization analysis
def: "An ion randomization method is a procedure for placing ions in a simulation box by randomly swapping their positions with existing solvent molecules. This is often done after an initial, simpler placement to ensure the ions are well-distributed throughout the solvent. This method helps to create a more disordered and realistic initial distribution of ions, avoiding potential artifacts from placing them in a regular grid." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000329 ! ion placement analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000663
name: cell replication analysis
def: "A cell replication method is a procedure used in system setup to create a larger system, known as a supercell, by duplicating the original simulation unit cell in one or more dimensions. This is commonly used in materials science simulations to model bulk crystals or surfaces from a smaller repeating unit. For experts, this method is the standard way to construct a periodic system that is large enough to minimize finite-size artifacts. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000328 ! system setup modeling

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000664
name: coordinate scaling modeling
def: "A coordinate scaling method is a structure modification method that multiplies all the atomic coordinates in a system by a specific scaling factor. This is used to uniformly expand or contract the entire system. For experts, this can be a step in adjusting the density of a system or in some barostat algorithms that control pressure by scaling the box and the coordinates within it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000305 ! modeling method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000665
name: velocity assignment analysis
def: "A velocity assignment method is the procedure used to give atoms their initial speeds and directions at the beginning of a molecular dynamics simulation. These velocities are typically chosen from a random distribution, such as the Maxwell-Boltzmann distribution, that corresponds to the desired starting temperature of the system. For experts, this step is crucial for initiating the thermal motion of the system before the equilibration phase. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000328 ! system setup modeling

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000666
name: volumetric map generation analysis
def: "An analysis method that computes a value at every point of a 3-dimensional grid covering a region of a simulation. The values may be how often solvent is found at each point, or the electrostatic potential there. The result is a map that can be viewed as a surface or a cloud rather than read as a number. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000917 ! structural analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000667
name: topology stripping analysis
def: "A topology stripping method is a procedure used to remove a subset of atoms, typically solvent and ions, from a molecular topology file. This is most often done during post-processing to create smaller topology files for the receptor and ligand alone, which are needed for MM/PBSA or MM/GBSA free energy calculations. For experts, this method is an essential step in the workflow for preparing files for endpoint free energy analysis. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000328 ! system setup modeling

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000668
name: force field parameter update modeling
def: "A force field parameter update method is a procedure for modifying or adding to an existing set of force field parameters. This is often done by reading a small file containing new or revised parameters that override the default values loaded from the main force field library. For experts, this method is the standard way to use parameters for a non-standard ligand or to apply a specific correction to the force field without having to edit the core parameter files. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000374 ! force field parameterization modeling

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000669
name: average structure calculation analysis
def: "An average structure calculation is a structural analysis method that computes the average coordinates of all atoms over a simulation trajectory. This provides a single, representative structure that reflects the central conformation of the system during the simulation. It is important to note that this average structure may not be a physically realistic conformation itself, especially if the molecule is highly flexible." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000917 ! structural analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000670
name: coordinate centering analysis
def: "Coordinate centering is a structural analysis method, often performed as a pre-processing step, that translates the coordinates of a molecular system so that its center of mass is at the origin of the coordinate system. This is a standard procedure to ensure that the molecule remains in the center of the simulation box for easier analysis and visualization." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000917 ! structural analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000671
name: closest solvent analysis
def: "An analysis method that identifies which solvent molecules lie nearest a solute, and follows them over time. It is used to reorder a trajectory so that the same water molecules stay near the solute in the output, or to count how long an individual water stays in contact. It answers which solvent molecules matter, rather than how much solvent there is. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000974 ! solvent analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000672
name: trajectory frame filtering
def: "Trajectory frame filtering is a data processing step where a simulation trajectory is selectively reduced in size by removing certain frames based on a specific criterion. This could involve discarding an initial equilibration period or keeping only those frames where a molecule adopts a particular shape. This filtering is a common procedure used to focus an analysis on a specific time period or a subset of conformations that are most relevant to the scientific question." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000939 ! dynamics analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000673
name: electronic structure analysis
def: "A type of analysis method focused on examining the electronic properties of a molecule derived from its quantum mechanical description, such as the wavefunction or electron density. This includes analyzing the distribution of electrons (charge, spin density), the nature of molecular orbitals, chemical bonding characteristics, and electronic response properties like polarizability. It provides fundamental insights into chemical reactivity, spectroscopy, and intermolecular forces. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000026 ! analysis method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000674
name: charge analysis
def: "A specific electronic structure analysis technique used to partition the total electron density of a molecule and assign partial atomic charges to individual atoms. Various schemes exist (e.g., Mulliken, Löwdin, Hirshfeld, Natural Population Analysis, ESP-derived charges), each with different theoretical underpinnings, providing insights into charge distribution, polarity, and electrostatic interaction sites. These charges are often used to parameterize classical force fields or interpret reactivity. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000673 ! electronic structure analysis
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000675 ! wavefunction property analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000675
name: wavefunction property analysis
def: "An electronic structure analysis method that directly calculates molecular properties as expectation values using the computed quantum mechanical wavefunction or density matrix. This can include properties like dipole and multipole moments, electron density at specific points (e.g., bond critical points in QTAIM), spin densities, or electric field gradients, providing detailed information about the molecule's electronic state and interactions. It leverages the full information contained within the wavefunction. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000673 ! electronic structure analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000676
name: orbital analysis
def: "A form of electronic structure analysis that investigates the molecular orbitals (MOs) of a system, which represent the energy levels and spatial distributions of electrons within the molecule based on quantum mechanics. Common analyses include visualizing frontier orbitals (HOMO, LUMO), examining orbital compositions (e.g., atomic orbital contributions), analyzing orbital energies for insights into ionization potential or electron affinity, and relating MOs to chemical bonding, reactivity, and electronic transitions. It helps rationalize chemical behavior based on electron distribution in orbitals. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000673 ! electronic structure analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000677
name: polarization analysis
def: "An electronic structure analysis technique that examines how the electron distribution of a molecule is distorted (polarized) in response to an external electric field or the field generated by nearby molecules. This involves calculating the induced dipole moment and the polarizability tensor, which quantify the molecule's susceptibility to charge redistribution. Understanding polarization is crucial for accurately describing intermolecular interactions, solvation effects, and responses to electromagnetic fields. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000673 ! electronic structure analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000678
name: atom order fixing analysis
def: "An atom order fixing method is a procedure used to reorder the atoms in a structure file to ensure they match the order expected by a corresponding topology file. Inconsistencies in atom ordering are a common source of errors when preparing systems for simulation. For experts, this is a critical sanity check and correction step to ensure that the coordinates and parameters are correctly matched for every atom. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000328 ! system setup modeling

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000679
name: obsolete image bond fixing analysis
def: "OBSOLETE. Image bond fixing is a post-processing step applied to simulation trajectories to correct the visual representation of molecules in a periodic system. When a molecule crosses a periodic boundary, it can appear \"broken\" in the raw output, with parts of it on opposite sides of the simulation box. This procedure identifies such cases and translates the atomic coordinates to make the molecule appear whole, which is essential for correct visualization and many types of analysis." []
comment: Retired as redundant with its former parent 'periodic boundary imaging' (MOLSIM:000659), of which it was the only child. Bond fixing is an implicit outcome of imaging, and that term's definition now states so. Reported and approved by the term verifier in GitHub issue #45.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: MOLSIM:000659

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000680
name: atom selection analysis
def: "An atom selection method is the procedure or syntax used to specify a particular group of atoms within a molecular system for an analysis or modification. This is typically done using a text-based selection language that allows users to choose atoms based on properties like name, residue, or position." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000328 ! system setup modeling
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000681
name: Gaussian electrostatic model force field
def: "A polarizable force field that represents charge as smeared-out Gaussian distributions rather than as points, with both permanent and induced multipole terms. Smearing the charge removes the artificial divergence that point charges give at very short range. It is markedly more accurate and more expensive than a point-charge treatment. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "GEM force field" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000639 ! polarizable force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000682
name: AMBER ff19SB
def: "Amber ff19SB is a modern and widely used set of rules, or a force field, for accurately simulating the structure and movement of proteins. The AMBER ff19SB protein force field is a recent refinement of the ff14SB lineage, incorporating updated quantum mechanical calculations for backbone dihedral angle parameters to improve the description of protein secondary structure balance. It is considered a state-of-the-art choice for all-atom protein simulations, offering high fidelity for studying protein folding, dynamics, and interactions." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000683
name: vector analysis
def: "A structural analysis method that measures the direction of vectors defined within a molecule, such as a bond vector or the normal to a plane, and how those directions change. It covers both the orientation of a single vector over time and the angle between 2 of them. It is how the orientation and rotational behaviour of specific groups is quantified. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000917 ! structural analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000684
name: atom remapping analysis
def: "An atom remapping method is a procedure used to systematically change the properties of atoms in a topology file, such as their atom types or charges. This is often required when converting a system from one force field to another or when applying specific corrections. For experts, this is an advanced manipulation used in force field development or for setting up non-standard simulations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000328 ! system setup modeling

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000685
name: ab-initio method
def: "A quantum chemistry method that solves the electronic Schrödinger equation using only fundamental physical constants and the identities of the atoms, with no parameters fitted to experiment. Hartree-Fock and the correlated methods built on it, such as Møller-Plesset perturbation theory and coupled cluster, belong here. The absence of fitted parameters is what lets accuracy be improved systematically rather than by re-tuning. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000141 ! theoretical approach

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000686
name: PDB ID
def: "A PDB ID is the unique four-character alphanumeric code (e.g., '1TIM', '6M0J') where the first character is always numeric. Every PDB id is assigned to a experimentally determined biomolecular structure deposited in the Protein Data Bank (PDB). This identifier serves to reference and retrieve PDB data. However these identifiers are now deprecated in favor of the Extended PDB ID." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000447 ! identifier
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393
property_value: skos:exactMatch data:1127

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000687
name: UniProt ID
def: "A UniProt ID, more formally known as a UniProt Accession Number (e.g., 'P00761', 'Q8WZ42'), is the stable and unique identifier assigned to a protein sequence record in the UniProt Knowledgebase (UniProtKB). This ID provides access to comprehensive information about a protein, including its sequence, function, annotations, and cross-references to other databases. It serves as a primary key for protein sequence and functional data." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000447 ! identifier
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393
property_value: skos:exactMatch data:2291

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000688
name: data source
def: "Any origin from which data used in a biomolecular study is obtained, whether a database, a document, a laboratory record or a person. It covers where a structure, a parameter or a measurement came from. Recording it is what lets a claim in a dataset be traced back and checked. (UNVERIFIED)" []
comment: How this branch is built. The classes here are KINDS of data source, for example protein structural database, pathway database, or simulation data repository. Each real, named resource is then added as an individual of one of those classes, not as a class of its own. PDB, UniProt, ChEMBL, Reactome, MoDEL and AlphaFold DB are individuals in this way. This is on purpose: a named database is one single thing in the world, not a kind of thing, so it fits better as an individual. Please keep this pattern, and do not turn these individuals into classes as a tidy-up. Two things to know. First, individuals are not copied into the OBO-format file (see the release-format note in the ontology header). Second, most OBO ontologies use classes for everything, so a reviewer may ask why we did this.

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000689
name: database source
def: "An organized, typically electronic, collection of structured information or data that can be easily accessed, managed, and updated. In biomolecular sciences, databases store vast amounts of information like molecular structures, sequences, experimental results, and simulation trajectories. They serve as central repositories for the research community. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000688 ! data source

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000690
name: primary database
def: "A type of database that archives original data directly submitted by researchers or generated through primary experimental efforts. These databases are foundational resources, providing the raw material (e.g., atomic coordinates, gene sequences) upon which further analysis and knowledge discovery are built. Examples include repositories for protein structures or DNA sequences." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000689 ! database source
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000703 ! secondary database
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000691
name: structural database
def: "A primary database specializing in the storage and dissemination of three-dimensional (3D) atomic coordinate data for biological macromolecules like proteins and nucleic acids. These databases are essential for understanding molecular function, designing drugs, and providing starting points for simulations. The Protein Data Bank (PDB) is a prime example." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000690 ! primary database
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000695 ! sequence database
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000692
name: protein structural database
def: "A structural database specifically focused on archiving and distributing 3D atomic coordinates and associated experimental data for proteins and their complexes. These resources are critical for researchers studying protein architecture, function, and interactions. The PDB is the foremost example in this category. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000691 ! structural database
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000693 ! nucleic acid structural database

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000693
name: nucleic acid structural database
def: "A structural database dedicated to collecting and providing 3D atomic coordinates and related information for nucleic acids such as DNA and RNA, including their various forms and complexes. These databases support research into gene regulation, RNA function, and nucleic acid-drug interactions. The Nucleic Acid Database (NDB) is a key example." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000691 ! structural database
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000694
name: electron microscopy database
def: "A structural database that archives 3D maps and associated metadata derived from electron microscopy experiments, particularly cryo-electron microscopy (cryo-EM), which is used to determine the structure of large biomolecular assemblies. It complements X-ray crystallography and NMR databases by providing structural information for systems often intractable by other methods. The Electron Microscopy Data Bank (EMDB) is the main repository. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000691 ! structural database

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000695
name: sequence database
def: "A primary database that stores and organizes linear sequences of amino acids (for proteins) or nucleotides (for DNA/RNA). These databases are fundamental for comparative genomics, evolutionary studies, identifying functional motifs, and linking sequence to structure and function. Examples include GenBank for nucleic acids and UniProtKB for protein sequences." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000690 ! primary database
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393
property_value: skos:closeMatch MI:0683

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000696
name: protein sequence database
def: "A sequence database specifically focused on collecting, annotating, and distributing protein amino acid sequences and associated functional information. These resources are vital for understanding protein evolution, function, and for identifying proteins from experimental data. UniProtKB is a comprehensive example." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000695 ! sequence database
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000697 ! nucleic acid sequence database
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000697
name: nucleic acid sequence database
def: "A sequence database dedicated to archiving and providing access to DNA and RNA nucleotide sequences from various organisms, including genes, genomes, and transcripts. These databases are cornerstones of genomics and molecular biology research. GenBank, ENA, and DDBJ are major international examples." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000695 ! sequence database
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000698
name: small molecule database
def: "A primary database that curates information about small chemical compounds, including their structures, properties, and biological activities. These resources are crucial for drug discovery, cheminformatics, and understanding ligand-protein interactions. PubChem and ChEBI are prominent examples. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000690 ! primary database

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000699
name: chemical structure database
def: "A small molecule database primarily focused on storing and providing access to 2D and 3D chemical structures, identifiers, and physicochemical properties of diverse chemical compounds. These are fundamental for chemical information retrieval and computational chemistry. PubChem Compound and ZINC are key examples. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000698 ! small molecule database
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000700 ! drug information database

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000700
name: drug information database
def: "A small molecule database specifically curating information about drugs, including their chemical properties, pharmacological actions, targets, and therapeutic uses. These resources are vital for pharmacology, drug development, and clinical research. DrugBank is a well-known example. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000698 ! small molecule database

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000701
name: spectroscopic database
def: "A primary database that archives experimental data obtained from various spectroscopic techniques, such as Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (NMR), mass spectrometry, or infrared spectroscopy, applied to biological molecules. These databases allow for the reanalysis of raw or processed spectral data and aid in structural and functional characterization. The Biological Magnetic Resonance Data Bank (BMRB) is an example for NMR data." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000690 ! primary database
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000702
name: NMR data repository
def: "A spectroscopic database specifically designed to store, organize, and disseminate experimental data from Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (NMR) studies of biomolecules. This includes raw spectral data, assigned chemical shifts, coupling constants, and derived structural constraints, complementing 3D coordinate depositions. The BMRB is the principal repository." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000701 ! spectroscopic database
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000703
name: secondary database
def: "A type of database that derives its content from analyzing, curating, or integrating information from one or more primary databases, often providing value-added annotations or classifications. These databases help researchers interpret primary data by, for example, grouping proteins into families or classifying structures. Pfam (protein families) and SCOP (structural classification) are examples." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000689 ! database source
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000704
name: protein family and domain database
def: "A secondary database that classifies proteins into families and identifies conserved domains based on sequence similarity, structural features, or functional annotations. These resources help predict protein function and understand evolutionary relationships. Examples include Pfam, InterPro, and SMART. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000703 ! secondary database
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000705 ! structural classification database

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000705
name: structural classification database
def: "A secondary database that organizes known protein structures into a hierarchical classification based on their evolutionary relationships and structural similarities, such as folds and superfamilies. These classifications provide insights into protein architecture and evolution. SCOP and CATH are prominent examples. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000703 ! secondary database

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000706
name: pathway database
def: "Databases that curate and represent information about biological pathways, such as metabolic, signaling, or regulatory networks, detailing the interactions between molecules. These resources help understand complex biological processes and the roles of individual components. KEGG and Reactome are widely used examples." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000703 ! secondary database
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000707
name: bioactivity database
def: "A secondary (or sometimes primary) database that collects and organizes experimental data on the biological activity of chemical compounds, particularly their interactions with protein targets (e.g., binding affinity, inhibition constants). These are crucial for drug discovery and chemical biology research. ChEMBL and BindingDB are key examples. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000703 ! secondary database

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000708
name: knowledge-based database
def: "A specialized type of database designed to store complex, structured, and unstructured information, often integrating data from multiple sources and using ontologies or controlled vocabularies to represent knowledge explicitly. Knowledge bases aim to provide a comprehensive understanding of specific biological entities or systems, facilitating inference and discovery. UniProtKB is a prime example in the protein domain. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000689 ! database source

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000709
name: repository database
def: "A type of database primarily focused on the storage, preservation, and dissemination of datasets, often associated with specific types of studies, computational outputs, or large-scale projects. Repositories ensure data accessibility and reusability for the scientific community. Examples include those for simulation trajectories or predicted protein structures." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000689 ! database source
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000710
name: simulation data repository
def: "A repository specifically designed to store, share, and allow re-analysis of data generated from biomolecular simulations, such as molecular dynamics trajectories and analysis results. These resources promote reproducibility and enable new discoveries from existing simulation data. MDposit and MDrepo are examples." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000709 ! repository database
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000711 ! predicted structure repository
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000711
name: predicted structure repository
def: "A repository that archives and provides access to computationally predicted three-dimensional structures of proteins, often generated by large-scale initiatives or community efforts. These resources offer structural hypotheses for proteins lacking experimental structures. The AlphaFold DB is a prominent example." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000709 ! repository database
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000712
name: metabolomics repository
def: "A repository dedicated to storing and disseminating datasets from metabolomics experiments, which involve the comprehensive study of small molecules (metabolites) within cells, tissues, or organisms. These resources support systems biology and biomarker discovery. MetaboLights is an example. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000709 ! repository database

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000713
name: literature database
def: "A database that indexes and provides access to bibliographic information from scientific journals, conference proceedings, and other scholarly publications. These are essential tools for researchers to find relevant scientific articles and stay updated on research findings. PubMed and Scopus are widely used examples." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000689 ! database source
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393
property_value: skos:closeMatch MI:0445

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000714
name: tool web server
def: "A web server that runs a computation on data the user supplies, rather than returning records it already holds. The user uploads a structure, the server computes something from it, and the result comes back. That is what separates it from a database server, which retrieves rather than computes. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001671 ! web server
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001119 ! database web server

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000715
name: prediction data format
def: "A data format that holds the direct output of a prediction program, such as a predicted structure, a predicted binding site, or a predicted functional annotation. It covers the result as the program wrote it, before any curation or deposition into a public repository. A coordinate file from a local homology modelling run is an example. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001085 ! molecular data format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000716
name: UCSF ChimeraX
def: "A visualization and analysis program for molecular structures, built to handle very large data such as cryogenic electron microscopy maps and whole virus capsids. It is the successor to Chimera, rewritten for modern graphics hardware. Its speed on large structures is what distinguishes it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "ChimeraX" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000490 ! structure preparation tool
is_a: MOLSIM:002041 ! molecular structure visualization tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000717
name: obsolete experimental data source
def: "OBSOLETE. Refers to data obtained directly from a specific laboratory experiment. This can include data reported in a scientific publication for which no separate database entry exists, or unpublished results from ongoing research." []
comment: Retired 2026-09-18. MOLSIM:000688 data source sorted its children by 3 different questions at once: what kind of resource it is, how the data was produced, and who may see it. Only the first is a kind of source, so a private unpublished PDB entry belonged under all 3. The 2 facets are now recorded by the MOLSIM:002274 data source descriptor branch instead. Raised in review by orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393; neither this term nor its former children had a single instance.
is_obsolete: true

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000718
name: obsolete scientific publication source
def: "OBSOLETE. A published research article, review, book chapter, or conference proceeding that serves as the source of specific data, findings, or methodologies. When data is cited directly from a publication without an associated database entry, the publication itself is considered the data source. This is common for specific measurements or observations not typically archived elsewhere." []
comment: Retired 2026-09-18 in favour of IAO:0000310 document, which is now imported and attached under MOLSIM:000688 data source. The term duplicated a concept IAO already models, and its own definition enumerated exactly IAO's document types. Part of the data source refactor asked for in review by orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393, which removed the facets experimental and private from the hierarchy and left it sorting sources by what kind of resource they are.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: IAO:0000310

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000719
name: obsolete unpublished experimental result source
def: "OBSOLETE. Data or findings originating from a laboratory experiment that have not yet been published or formally disseminated to the public or scientific community. This category covers preliminary results, ongoing research data, or information shared through informal channels before formal publication or deposition." []
comment: Retired 2026-09-18. MOLSIM:000688 data source sorted its children by 3 different questions at once: what kind of resource it is, how the data was produced, and who may see it. Only the first is a kind of source, so a private unpublished PDB entry belonged under all 3. The 2 facets are now recorded by the MOLSIM:002274 data source descriptor branch instead. Raised in review by orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393; neither this term nor its former children had a single instance.
is_obsolete: true

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000720
name: obsolete private source
def: "OBSOLETE. A data source that is not publicly accessible, such as an internal database maintained by a private company or research institution, or data held privately by an individual researcher. This category is important for acknowledging data origins that cannot be independently verified or accessed by the wider community." []
comment: Retired 2026-09-18. MOLSIM:000688 data source sorted its children by 3 different questions at once: what kind of resource it is, how the data was produced, and who may see it. Only the first is a kind of source, so a private unpublished PDB entry belonged under all 3. The 2 facets are now recorded by the MOLSIM:002274 data source descriptor branch instead. Raised in review by orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393; neither this term nor its former children had a single instance.
is_obsolete: true

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000721
name: obsolete in house database
def: "OBSOLETE. A database developed and maintained within a specific organization (e.g., a pharmaceutical company, a research institute) for its internal use, not generally accessible to the public. These often contain proprietary data, specialized collections, or information tailored to the organization's specific research needs." []
comment: Retired 2026-09-18. MOLSIM:000688 data source sorted its children by 3 different questions at once: what kind of resource it is, how the data was produced, and who may see it. Only the first is a kind of source, so a private unpublished PDB entry belonged under all 3. The 2 facets are now recorded by the MOLSIM:002274 data source descriptor branch instead. Raised in review by orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393; neither this term nor its former children had a single instance. This one has a successor: an in house database is a database, so MOLSIM:000689 database source replaces it.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: MOLSIM:000689

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000722
name: personal communication source
def: "Information or data obtained directly from an individual researcher or expert through informal means such as email, conversation, or unpublished notes, rather than through a formal publication or public database. While sometimes necessary, such sources are typically less verifiable and are often used for supplementary or preliminary information." []
synonym: "private communication source" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000688 ! data source
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000735
name: resolution-based force field
def: "A type of force field classified by the level of structural detail, or resolution, used to represent the system's components. This classification distinguishes between models that represent every atom explicitly versus those that group atoms into larger pseudo-atoms or beads. The resolution impacts the balance between computational efficiency and physical accuracy. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000007 ! force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000736
name: coarse-grained force field
def: "A force field in which groups of atoms are represented by single interaction sites rather than individually. Cutting the number of particles cuts the cost of every step and allows a longer timestep, so much larger systems and much longer times become reachable. What is lost is any detail below the size of a site. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000735 ! resolution-based force field
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000737 ! all-atom force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000737
name: all-atom force field
def: "A force field that explicitly includes parameters for every atom in the simulated system, including hydrogen atoms. This approach provides a high level of detail and aims for greater physical realism compared to coarse-grained models. All-atom simulations are generally more computationally intensive due to the larger number of particles." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000735 ! resolution-based force field
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000738
name: AMBER GLYCAM 06
def: "A specific parameter set within the AMBER family, developed by the GLYCAM group for simulating carbohydrates (glycans). Released around 2006, it provides parameters for common monosaccharides and the glycosidic linkages between them, enabling the study of oligosaccharides and the carbohydrate portions of glycoproteins/glycolipids. It is designed to be compatible with AMBER protein/lipid force fields. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000012 ! carbohydrates force field
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000739 ! AMBER GLYCAM 06 EP

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000739
name: AMBER GLYCAM 06 EP
def: "A force field for carbohydrates in the AMBER family that places extra charged points on the lone pairs of ring and hydroxyl oxygens. Those points direct hydrogen bonding more sharply than a charge on the nucleus can, which matters for sugars because their behaviour is dominated by hydrogen bonds. It is a variant of the GLYCAM06 parameter set rather than a separate force field. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000012 ! carbohydrates force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000740
name: AMBER AMOEBA
def: "A set of ion parameters for the AMOEBA polarizable force field as distributed with the AMBER suite. Because AMOEBA represents charge with atomic multipoles and explicit induced dipoles rather than fixed point charges, ions need parameters fitted for that form. Parameters from a fixed-charge force field cannot be used with it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000015 ! ion force field
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001472 ! bonded metal model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000741
name: AMBER ff02
def: "A specific protein force field parameter set from the AMBER family, representing one of the earlier polarizable force fields. Unlike fixed-charge force fields (like ff99SB), ff02 includes electronic polarizability explicitly, aiming for a more accurate description of electrostatics but at a higher computational cost. Its adoption was less widespread than fixed-charge counterparts." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000742
name: AMBER ff10
def: "A specific protein force field parameter set from the AMBER family, incorporating updates (e.g., to backbone torsions) over ff99SB, developed around 2010. It served as an evolutionary step in the AMBER force field lineage. However, it was largely superseded by subsequent versions like ff12SB and ff14SB. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000743
name: AMBER ff12SB
def: "A specific protein force field parameter set from the AMBER family, representing an update released around 2012. Compared to ff99SB, ff12SB refined quantum-chemical (QM) based side-chain dihedral parameters and updated the backbone φ rotational profile to compensate for biases seen in earlier version. It served as an intermediate improvement before the release of ff14SB." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000744
name: AMBER ff94
def: "An early, widely influential all-atom protein force field parameter set from the AMBER family, released around 1994. It provided a complete set of parameters for proteins and became a benchmark for subsequent developments. While largely superseded by newer versions (ff96, ff99, ff99SB, ff14SB etc.), its development laid crucial groundwork. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000745
name: AMBER ff96
def: "A subsequent refinement of the AMBER ff94 protein force field parameter set, released around 1996. It included adjustments based on accumulated experience and new data, aiming to improve performance compared to ff94. Like ff94, it has been largely replaced by later versions but represents a step in the evolution. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000746
name: AMBER ff99
def: "An important revision of the AMBER protein force field parameter set released around 1999, incorporating significant updates, especially to backbone torsion parameters, compared to ff94/ff96. It aimed to better reproduce secondary structure propensities. Several variants of ff99 exist, addressing specific issues or refining parameters further. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000747
name: AMBER ff99 phi
def: "A specific modification of the AMBER ff99 protein force field. This variant likely involved adjustments targeted at the phi (ϕ) backbone dihedral angle parameters, aiming to correct specific structural biases observed with the original ff99. Such targeted modifications are common in force field development. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000748
name: AMBER ff99bsc0
def: "A force field for nucleic acids, built on the AMBER ff99 parameter set with the alpha and gamma backbone dihedral terms refit by the Barcelona group. The refit removed an irreversible backbone flip that caused DNA simulations to degrade after tens of nanoseconds. It was the first parameter set to make multi-nanosecond DNA simulation stable. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000749
name: AMBER ff99SB
def: "A highly popular and widely used refinement of the AMBER ff99 protein force field, where 'SB' indicates improvements primarily focused on side-chain (S) and backbone (B) dihedral torsion potentials. It corrected some imbalances in secondary structure preference found in ff99. ff99SB served as a robust baseline before the development of ff14SB. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000750
name: AMBER ff99SB ILDN
def: "A force field for proteins, built on the AMBER ff99SB parameter set with the side-chain torsion terms refit for isoleucine, leucine, aspartate and asparagine. The 4 residues were singled out because their rotamer populations disagreed most with NMR measurements. The rest of the parameter set is unchanged. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000751
name: CHARMM 22
def: "An all-atom force field parameter set from the CHARMM family, widely used for protein simulations, often paired with the CMAP (Cross-term energy Correction Map) correction for backbone torsions. Released before CHARMM27 and CHARMM36, it represented a standard for many years. Parameterization relied heavily on fitting to experimental data available at the time. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000752
name: CHARMM 19
def: "An earlier force field parameter set from the CHARMM family, notable for being a 'united-atom' force field for proteins. In this representation, nonpolar hydrogen atoms (e.g., on CH, CH2, CH3 groups) are implicitly included in the heavy atoms they are attached to, reducing the number of particles and computational cost compared to all-atom models." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000753
name: CHARMM 27
def: "An all-atom force field parameter set from the CHARMM family, representing an update and extension of CHARMM22, released around 2000-2001. It included refined parameters for proteins and also incorporated compatible parameters for nucleic acids (DNA, RNA). Like CHARMM22, it was often used with the CMAP correction for proteins. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000754
name: OPEP 1
def: "Specific versions 1 of the OPEP (Optimized Potential for Efficient peptide structure Prediction) coarse-grained force field. OPEP represents each amino acid residue using multiple beads (typically backbone N, H, Cα, C, O and a side-chain bead), aiming to retain chemical specificity while gaining computational efficiency. The different versions likely represent successive refinements and parameter updates. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000755
name: OPEP 2
def: "Specific versions 2 of the OPEP (Optimized Potential for Efficient peptide structure Prediction) coarse-grained force field. OPEP represents each amino acid residue using multiple beads (typically backbone N, H, Cα, C, O and a side-chain bead), aiming to retain chemical specificity while gaining computational efficiency. The different versions likely represent successive refinements and parameter updates. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000756
name: OPEP 3
def: "Specific versions 3 of the OPEP (Optimized Potential for Efficient peptide structure Prediction) coarse-grained force field. OPEP represents each amino acid residue using multiple beads (typically backbone N, H, Cα, C, O and a side-chain bead), aiming to retain chemical specificity while gaining computational efficiency. The different versions likely represent successive refinements and parameter updates. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000757
name: OPEP 4
def: "Specific versions 4 of the OPEP (Optimized Potential for Efficient peptide structure Prediction) coarse-grained force field. OPEP represents each amino acid residue using multiple beads (typically backbone N, H, Cα, C, O and a side-chain bead), aiming to retain chemical specificity while gaining computational efficiency. The different versions likely represent successive refinements and parameter updates. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000758
name: OPLS
def: "A family of force fields whose parameters were fitted to reproduce the measured properties of liquids, such as density and heat of vaporisation, rather than to quantum calculations alone. Fitting to bulk properties is what distinguishes it from the other major families. It covers organic molecules, proteins and nucleic acids. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000759
name: OPLS-AA
def: "A force field of the OPLS family in which every atom including hydrogen is represented separately. It is more accurate than the united-atom version, particularly for aromatic groups and for anything where a hydrogen's position matters. It costs roughly twice as much, because an organic molecule has about twice as many sites. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000760
name: OPLS-UA
def: "A force field of the OPLS family in which non-polar hydrogens are merged into the heavy atom they are bonded to, so that a methyl group is 1 interaction site rather than 4. Merging them cuts the particle count substantially at the cost of any detail those hydrogens carried. It was widely used for organic liquids before all-atom parameters became affordable. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000761
name: OPLS-2001
def: "A specific parameter set version within the OPLS-AA force field family, released around 2001. It contained parameters primarily for proteins and organic liquids available at that time. Subsequent versions like OPLS-2005 updated and expanded upon this set. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000762
name: OPLS-2005
def: "A significant update and expansion of the OPLS-AA force field parameter set, released around 2005. It included refined parameters for proteins, nucleic acids, and a wider range of organic functional groups compared to OPLS-2001. It remains a widely used parameter set within the OPLS family. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000763
name: TIP4P
def: "A rigid water model with 4 sites, the fourth being a massless point near the oxygen carrying that atom's negative charge. Moving the negative charge off the oxygen towards the hydrogens gives a better electrostatic field around the molecule. It costs about 25% more than a 3-site model and reproduces the dielectric constant and the density maximum far better. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000014 ! water model force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000764
name: TIP4P-Ew
def: "A specific variant of the TIP4P water model, optimized for use with Ewald summation methods for calculating long-range electrostatic interactions, which are standard in modern simulations with periodic boundary conditions. The parameters are adjusted to provide good agreement with experimental properties of liquid water (like density, enthalpy of vaporization) under typical simulation conditions (room temperature and pressure). It is a popular choice for biomolecular simulations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000014 ! water model force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000765
name: TIP4P/Ice
def: "A specific variant of the TIP4P water model, parameterized specifically to reproduce the properties of different phases of ice (solid water), as well as liquid water properties. It aims to provide a better description of water's phase diagram, particularly the solid phases, compared to models optimized solely for the liquid state. It is useful for studying freezing, melting, or ice interfaces. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000014 ! water model force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000766
name: TIP4P/2005
def: "A specific variant of the TIP4P water model, released around 2005, re-parameterized to provide improved agreement with a wider range of experimental properties of liquid water over various temperatures and pressures compared to earlier TIP4P versions. It is considered one of the most accurate rigid, non-polarizable 4-point models for general liquid water simulations. It accurately predicts properties like the temperature of maximum density. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000014 ! water model force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000767
name: TIP5P
def: "A rigid water model with 5 sites, adding 2 massless points in the positions the oxygen's lone pairs would occupy. Placing negative charge there makes hydrogen bonding directional in the way real water's is. It reproduces the temperature of maximum density correctly, which simpler models do not, at a further increase in cost. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000014 ! water model force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000768
name: TIP6P
def: "A rigid water model with 6 sites, carrying charges on all 3 atoms, on 2 lone-pair points and on a further point near the oxygen. The extra sites refine the electrostatic field further still. Its cost restricts it to studies of water itself rather than of biomolecules in water. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000014 ! water model force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000769
name: SPC
def: "A rigid water model with 3 interaction sites, one on each atom, and a bond angle set to the ideal tetrahedral value rather than the measured one of an isolated molecule. Widening the angle compensates for the absence of polarization in a fixed-charge model. It is among the oldest models still in use. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000014 ! water model force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000770
name: SPC flexible
def: "A variation of the SPC water model where the normally rigid constraints on bond lengths (O-H) and/or angle (H-O-H) are replaced with flexible harmonic potentials. This allows the water molecule geometry to fluctuate during the simulation, which can affect dynamics and spectroscopic properties. It adds computational overhead compared to rigid SPC. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000014 ! water model force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000771
name: SPC/E
def: "A rigid 3-site water model that keeps the geometry of its predecessor and adds a correction for the energy cost of polarizing a molecule from its gas-phase to its liquid charge distribution. That correction improves the density and the diffusion coefficient markedly. It is a common choice where bulk water properties matter more than compatibility with a particular force field. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000014 ! water model force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000772
name: chemical entity-based force field
def: "A force field specifically developed and parameterized to accurately model a particular class of chemical molecules, such as proteins, lipids, or nucleic acids. Its parameters are tuned based on experimental data and/or quantum mechanical calculations relevant to that molecular type. This specialization aims to improve the accuracy of simulations for specific biomolecular systems. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000007 ! force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000773
name: ADF
def: "A quantum chemistry engine built around density functional theory using Slater-type orbitals rather than the Gaussian functions most programs use. Slater functions have the correct shape at the nucleus, which suits properties that depend on the region near heavy atoms. It is chosen for transition metal and relativistic work for that reason. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000161 ! quantum chemistry engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000774
name: Abalone
def: "Abalone (Abalone II) is a general purpose molecular dynamics and molecular graphics program for simulations of bio-molecules in a periodic boundary conditions in explicit or implicit water models. Mainly designed to simulate the protein folding and DNA-ligand complexes in AMBER force field." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001664 ! software suite
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000775
name: CP2K
def: "An open-source quantum chemistry and solid-state physics software package designed for performing atomistic simulations of solid state, liquid, molecular, periodic, material, crystal, and biological systems. CP2K is particularly known for its efficient DFT calculations using a hybrid Gaussian and Plane Waves (GPW) method and its Quickstep module, enabling QM and QM/MM simulations of large systems, including ab initio MD. It's highly parallelized and versatile for demanding simulations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000161 ! quantum chemistry engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000776
name: CPMD
def: "A quantum chemistry engine for molecular dynamics in which the forces come from a density functional calculation at every step. It avoids re-solving the electronic structure each step by giving the electronic degrees of freedom their own fictitious dynamics. That method is what the program is named after. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000161 ! quantum chemistry engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000777
name: Desmond
def: "A high-performance software package specifically designed for classical molecular dynamics simulations of biological systems, developed by D. E. Shaw Research (DESRES). Desmond is known for its exceptional speed, particularly on GPUs, and its integration with the Schrödinger Materials Science Suite. It supports standard force fields (like CHARMM, AMBER, OPLS) and offers features for system building, simulation execution (including free energy calculations), and analysis, primarily targeting drug discovery and biomolecular research." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000160 ! molecular dynamics engine
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000784 ! LAMMPS
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000778
name: Firefly
def: "A quantum chemistry engine offering a broad range of wavefunction and density functional methods, heavily optimised for Intel processors. It shares its origins and much of its input syntax with GAMESS (US). It was formerly distributed as PC GAMESS, which should be kept as an exact synonym. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000161 ! quantum chemistry engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000779
name: GAMESS-UK
def: "A quantum chemistry software package developed in the UK, distinct from GAMESS-US, though sharing common historical roots. It offers a broad range of ab initio QM methods (HF, MP2, CCSD(T), MCSCF, DFT) and includes capabilities for QM/MM calculations. Like other QM packages, it is primarily used for electronic structure calculations and parameterization rather than large-scale classical MD. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000176 ! GAMESS

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000780
name: GAMESS-US
def: "A widely used, freely available quantum chemistry software package (General Atomic and Molecular Electronic Structure System). It provides a broad range of quantum mechanical methods, from semi-empirical to high-level ab initio (HF, DFT, MP2, CCSD, MCSCF), and includes features for geometry optimization, vibrational analysis, and QM/MM simulations. GAMESS-US is extensively used in computational chemistry research and education for electronic structure calculations relevant to biomolecular systems. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000176 ! GAMESS

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000781
name: GROMOS
def: "A software package for classical molecular dynamics simulation, developed principally at ETH Zürich, covering system setup, simulation and analysis. It is distributed together with the force field family of the same name. The package and the force field are separate things and should not share 1 term. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001664 ! software suite

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000782
name: HyperChem
def: "A commercial molecular modeling software package providing a graphical interface for building, visualizing, and simulating molecular systems. It offers capabilities for molecular mechanics (MM) using various force fields, quantum mechanics (QM) using semi-empirical and ab initio methods, and molecular dynamics (MD) simulations. HyperChem aims to provide an integrated environment for a range of computational chemistry tasks on desktop computers. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001664 ! software suite

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000783
name: Jaguar
def: "A high-performance quantum chemistry software package, part of the Schrödinger Materials Science Suite, known for its speed and accuracy, particularly for DFT calculations. It also offers ab initio methods (like LMP2) and QM/MM capabilities. Jaguar is often used in drug discovery contexts for tasks requiring high-quality QM calculations, such as reaction modeling, property prediction, and parameterization. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000161 ! quantum chemistry engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000784
name: LAMMPS
def: "A highly versatile, open-source classical molecular dynamics simulator developed at Sandia National Laboratories, designed for parallel computing (Large-scale Atomic/Molecular Massively Parallel Simulator). LAMMPS has a very broad application range, extending from biomolecules (using standard force fields like CHARMM, AMBER, OPLS) to materials science, solid-state physics, and coarse-grained simulations, due to its extensive library of potentials and simulation methods. Its flexibility makes it suitable for non-standard simulation setups. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000160 ! molecular dynamics engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000785
name: MOPAC
def: "A widely used semi-empirical quantum chemistry software package (Molecular Orbital PACkage). It implements methods like AM1, PM3, PM6, PM7, which are much faster than ab initio or DFT methods, allowing calculations on larger systems or longer timescales, albeit typically with lower accuracy. MOPAC is often used for rapid geometry optimization, property estimation, or as the QM component in QM/MM calculations where speed is critical. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000161 ! quantum chemistry engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000786
name: NAMD
def: "A highly scalable, parallel molecular dynamics simulation software package developed at the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign, designed specifically for simulating large biomolecular systems on high-performance computers (NAnoscale Molecular Dynamics). NAMD works particularly well with the CHARMM force field (and others like AMBER) and is often used in conjunction with the VMD visualization program for setup and analysis. It is known for its excellent performance on parallel architectures, including GPUs." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000160 ! molecular dynamics engine
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000787
name: SIESTA
def: "An open-source software package for performing electronic structure calculations and ab initio molecular dynamics simulations based on Density Functional Theory (DFT). SIESTA uses localized numerical atomic orbitals as basis sets and efficient pseudopotentials, making it suitable for large systems and parallel computation. While applicable to biomolecules, its strengths are often utilized in materials science and condensed matter physics contexts, similar to Quantum ESPRESSO or VASP. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000161 ! quantum chemistry engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000788
name: Spartan
def: "A commercial molecular modeling and computational chemistry software package featuring an integrated graphical user interface. It provides tools for structure building and visualization, and implements a range of computational methods, including molecular mechanics (MM), semi-empirical methods (like AM1, PM3), Hartree-Fock (HF), Density Functional Theory (DFT), and Møller-Plesset (MPn) calculations. Spartan is widely used in education and research for structure-property relationship studies. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001664 ! software suite

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000789
name: TINKER
def: "A freely available software package for molecular mechanics and dynamics simulations. TINKER provides implementations of various standard force fields (AMBER, CHARMM, OPLS, MMFF) and includes tools for energy minimization, MD simulation, free energy calculations, and structural analysis. It is particularly notable for its implementation of polarizable force fields (e.g., AMOEBA) and its modular design. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001664 ! software suite

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000790
name: Tremolo-X
def: "A molecular dynamics program built for high-performance computing, developed at Fraunhofer SCAI. Its applications are in nanotechnology and materials rather than in biomolecules. It is included here because simulation metadata may name it as the engine that produced a dataset. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000160 ! molecular dynamics engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000791
name: TURBOMOLE
def: "A highly efficient quantum chemistry software package focusing on ab initio methods, particularly Density Functional Theory (DFT) and correlated wavefunction methods (like MP2, CC2, CCSD(T)), optimized for speed and parallel performance. It is widely used for calculations on molecules and clusters, especially for applications requiring high accuracy or large basis sets, such as reaction mechanism studies, spectroscopy, and parameterization tasks relevant to biomolecular simulation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001664 ! software suite

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000792
name: VASP
def: "A quantum chemistry engine for density functional calculations on periodic systems, using plane waves as its basis. Plane waves suit an infinite repeating solid, where atom-centred functions do not. It is the standard tool for solids and surfaces rather than for isolated molecules. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000161 ! quantum chemistry engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000793
name: X-PLOR
def: "A software package primarily used for macromolecular structure determination based on experimental data, particularly X-ray crystallography and NMR spectroscopy data. It incorporates molecular mechanics (energy terms from force fields), molecular dynamics (often used for refinement or simulated annealing protocols), and terms representing the experimental restraints to refine structures consistent with both physics and experimental observations. While it uses MD concepts, its primary goal is structure determination rather than simulating equilibrium dynamics." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001664 ! software suite
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000794
name: Hoover barostat
def: "A pressure control algorithm that treats the volume of the box as an extra degree of freedom with its own equation of motion, following Hoover's formulation. Because the equations are deterministic, the trajectory can be reproduced exactly from the same starting point. It generates the correct constant-pressure ensemble, which the simpler rescaling schemes do not. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000039 ! barostat algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000795
name: M-SHAKE algorithm
def: "A modification of the SHAKE algorithm designed to handle constraints more efficiently in parallel computing environments. It addresses issues related to communication overhead when constraints span across different processors by optimizing the way constraint information is shared and processed. It aims to improve the scalability of constrained simulations on parallel machines. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000049 ! constraint algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000796
name: P-SHAKE algorithm
def: "A constraint algorithm that holds bond lengths fixed using the SHAKE approach, restructured so the work can be divided across processors. The difficulty it addresses is that constraints link atoms which may sit on different processors, so enforcing them needs communication. It targets that communication rather than the constraint mathematics. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000049 ! constraint algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000797
name: SETTLE algorithm
def: "An analytical (non-iterative) constraint algorithm specifically designed for rigid water models like TIP3P or SPC/E, where both bond lengths and the bond angle are fixed. Because the geometry is simple and fixed, the constraint equations for a water molecule can be solved analytically, making SETTLE significantly faster than iterative methods like SHAKE for constraining water. It is highly efficient for simulations with explicit water. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000049 ! constraint algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000798
name: SHAPE algorithm
def: "A constraint algorithm related to SHAKE, often used for fixing distances within rigid clusters of atoms larger than simple bonds or angles. It iteratively adjusts the positions of atoms within the defined rigid body to maintain their relative positions. It extends the concept of bond constraints to more complex rigid units. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000049 ! constraint algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000799
name: WIGGLE algorithm
def: "A constraint algorithm that holds bond lengths fixed while using information about the atoms' velocities as well as their positions to converge faster. Holding bonds fixed removes the fastest vibrations from a system, which is what allows a longer timestep. It is an extension of the SHAKE approach rather than a separate idea. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000049 ! constraint algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000800
name: Nose thermostat
def: "A temperature control algorithm that adds an extra degree of freedom to the system, standing for the heat bath, and lets it exchange energy with the atoms through its own equation of motion. The equations are deterministic and produce exactly the canonical distribution, which simple rescaling does not. Its original form rescales time as well, which the later reformulation removes. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000038 ! thermostat algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000801
name: Nose-Poincare thermostat
def: "A specific mathematical formulation of the Nosé thermostat dynamics based on Poincaré's canonical transformations. It offers insights into the theoretical foundations and conservation laws of the Nosé thermostatting mechanism. It represents a rigorous theoretical framework for this class of deterministic thermostats. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000038 ! thermostat algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000802
name: V-rescale thermostat
def: "A temperature control algorithm that modifies simple weak coupling by adding a random term chosen so the resulting distribution of kinetic energies is the correct one. Weak coupling alone drives every fluctuation towards the mean, which suppresses the spread a real system has. The random term restores it at no extra cost. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000038 ! thermostat algorithm
property_value: MOLSIM:002254 "tcoupl=v-rescale" xsd:string {dcterms:source="MOLSIM:000247"}

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000803
name: semi-empirical method
def: "A category of quantum chemistry calculation methods that bridges the gap between highly accurate but slow ab initio methods and very fast but simple molecular mechanics. It simplifies the complex equations of quantum mechanics (often starting from the Hartree-Fock framework) by neglecting certain terms and using parameters derived from experimental data to approximate others. These methods aim to provide a reasonable balance between computational cost and accuracy for studying molecular properties like geometry and energy. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000173 ! quantum mechanics

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000804
name: all-valence-electron restricted
def: "A semi-empirical method that treats every valence electron explicitly while representing the inner electrons by a fixed core. Including all valence electrons is what lets it describe molecules of any element combination rather than only conjugated ones. It is the level nearly all modern semi-empirical methods work at. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000803 ! semi-empirical method
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000806 ! pi-electron restricted

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000805
name: PPP
def: "A semi-empirical quantum method that treats only the pi electrons of a conjugated system, holding the rest of the molecule fixed as a framework. Restricting the calculation to pi electrons made conjugated molecules computable long before general methods existed. It predicted the absorption spectra of dyes well and cannot describe anything outside the pi system. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000806 ! pi-electron restricted

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000806
name: pi-electron restricted
def: "A semi-empirical method that treats only the pi electrons explicitly, holding the rest of the molecule fixed as a framework. Restricting the calculation this way made conjugated molecules computable on the hardware of the 1950s and 1960s. It cannot describe anything outside the pi system, which is why it is of historical interest only. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000803 ! semi-empirical method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000807
name: AM1
def: "A semi-empirical quantum method built on the NDDO approximation, adding extra Gaussian terms to the core repulsion so that hydrogen bonding is described better than its predecessor manages. Its parameters were adjusted by hand against measured heats of formation and geometries. It remains in wide use, particularly as the basis of fast charge assignment schemes. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000817 ! NDDO
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000808 ! CNDO/2

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000808
name: CNDO/2
def: "A semi-empirical all-valence-electron method that neglects essentially all overlap between electron distributions on different atoms, in its second parameterisation. The severity of that approximation makes it very fast and correspondingly crude. It is of historical interest rather than in current use. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000817 ! NDDO

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000809
name: INDO
def: "A semi-empirical all-valence-electron method that keeps the one-centre electron repulsion integrals between orbitals on the same atom, which the earlier complete-neglect scheme discarded. Keeping them is what lets it describe electron spin distributions and the properties that depend on them. It is the level the MINDO and SINDO families refine. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000817 ! NDDO

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000810
name: Hartree-Fock
def: "A fundamental ab initio quantum chemistry method that approximates the solution to the electronic Schrödinger equation for a multi-electron system. It treats each electron as moving in an average field created by all other electrons, neglecting instantaneous electron correlation but including exact exchange interaction. It serves as a starting point for more sophisticated ab initio methods and is the foundation simplified by semi-empirical approaches. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "HF" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000685 ! ab-initio method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000812
name: restricted open-shell Hartree-Fock
def: "A Hartree-Fock method for systems with unpaired electrons that keeps electrons of opposite spin in the same spatial orbitals wherever they are paired. The constraint means the wavefunction remains an eigenfunction of total spin, with no spin contamination. It is less flexible than the unrestricted method and usually gives a slightly higher energy. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "ROHF" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000810 ! Hartree-Fock
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000813 ! self-consistent field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000813
name: self-consistent field
def: "An iterative computational procedure that solves for a set of molecular orbitals by repeatedly recomputing the average field each electron feels from all the others until the orbitals stop changing. It is how the Hartree-Fock equations, and those of density functional theory, are solved in practice. A calculation that fails to reach that fixed point is said not to have converged. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "SCF" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000810 ! Hartree-Fock

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000814
name: Unrestricted Hartree-Fock
def: "A Hartree-Fock method that lets electrons of opposite spin occupy different spatial orbitals. The extra freedom describes unpaired electrons better than forcing paired orbitals does. The price is that the resulting wavefunction is not an eigenfunction of total spin, so it can be contaminated by states of higher multiplicity. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "UHF" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000810 ! Hartree-Fock

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000815
name: MINDO
def: "A family of semi-empirical all-valence-electron methods that refine the intermediate-neglect approximation with re-fitted parameters, aimed at predicting heats of formation for organic molecules. Successive members are distinguished by a version number. They were superseded by the MNDO and AM1 families. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000809 ! INDO

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000816
name: MNDO
def: "A semi-empirical quantum method built on the NDDO approximation, the first to treat all valence electrons at that level. It described geometries and heats of formation far better than the earlier intermediate-neglect methods. Its known failure is that it underestimates hydrogen bonding severely, which is what the later methods set out to fix. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000817 ! NDDO

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000817
name: NDDO
def: "A semi-empirical approximation scheme that neglects the overlap between atomic orbitals on different atoms, except where both orbitals of a pair sit on the same atom. Dropping those integrals is what makes semi-empirical calculations fast. It underlies the MNDO, AM1 and PM families of methods. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000804 ! all-valence-electron restricted
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000819 ! PM3

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000818
name: PDDG
def: "A modification applied to the MNDO and AM1 semi-empirical methods, adding correction terms that depend on the distance between each pair of atoms. The corrections improve heats of formation markedly, particularly for organic molecules. It changes the parameters and the core repulsion rather than the underlying approximation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000817 ! NDDO

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000819
name: PM3
def: "A semi-empirical quantum method built on the NDDO approximation, with its parameters fitted automatically to a large set of measured molecular properties. The automatic fitting is what distinguishes it from its contemporaries, whose parameters were adjusted by hand. It handles hydrogen bonding better than those and geometries around nitrogen worse. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000804 ! all-valence-electron restricted

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000820
name: PM3MM
def: "A hybrid method that combines the PM3 semi-empirical quantum mechanical treatment for a part of the system (e.g., the active site of an enzyme) with a faster molecular mechanics (MM) force field for the remainder (e.g., the surrounding protein or solvent). This QM/MM approach allows computationally feasible studies of large systems where quantum effects are important locally. It leverages PM3's balance of speed and accuracy for the QM region. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000819 ! PM3

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000821
name: PM6
def: "A semi-empirical quantum method built on the NDDO approximation, parameterised for most of the periodic table rather than for organic elements alone. That coverage is what distinguishes it from its predecessors, which handle few metals. It also revised the core repulsion terms, improving hydrogen bonding and the description of metal complexes. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000819 ! PM3

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000822
name: RM1
def: "A semi-empirical quantum method built on the NDDO approximation, refitting the parameters of AM1 against a larger and more modern set of measurements. It uses the same functional form as its predecessor and differs only in the parameter values. It covers the elements most common in organic and biological molecules. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000804 ! all-valence-electron restricted

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000823
name: SAM1
def: "A semi-empirical quantum method built on the NDDO approximation that computes some of the electron repulsion integrals directly rather than taking them all from parameters. Computing part of them was intended to improve accuracy for hydrogen bonds and transition states. It is much less widely used than its contemporaries. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000804 ! all-valence-electron restricted

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000824
name: SINDO
def: "A semi-empirical all-valence-electron method at the intermediate-neglect level that first orthogonalises the atomic orbitals symmetrically. The orthogonalisation makes the approximations more internally consistent than in the unmodified scheme. It was developed to improve on the earlier intermediate-neglect methods. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000804 ! all-valence-electron restricted

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000825
name: Sparkle/AM1
def: "A modification of the AM1 semi-empirical method specifically parameterized to handle lanthanide elements (rare earth metals). Standard AM1 parameters are not available or reliable for these heavy elements, so Sparkle/AM1 replaces the core description of the lanthanide ion with a point charge dressed by Gaussian functions, adjusted to reproduce structural data. It enables AM1-level calculations on complexes containing lanthanides. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000807 ! AM1

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000826
name: ZANDO
def: "An all-valence-electron semi-empirical method likely based on the INDO or NDDO approximation schemes, developed by Zhidomirov and coworkers. It represents one of the many variations within the semi-empirical framework, likely with specific parameterizations or modifications to the integral approximations aimed at particular applications or accuracy improvements. Note: This method is less common than MNDO/AM1/PMx variants, and specific details might require consulting specialized literature. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000817 ! NDDO

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000827
name: Moeller-Plesset
def: "A post-Hartree-Fock method that recovers electron correlation by treating the difference between the true electronic Hamiltonian and the Hartree-Fock one as a perturbation, and computing energy corrections order by order. Each successive order adds more correlation and costs more. The order used is written as a number after the name. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "MP" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000173 ! quantum mechanics

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000828
name: Moeller-Plesset 2
def: "A Møller-Plesset method truncated at second order, which adds the correlation energy from double excitations out of the Hartree-Fock reference. It is the cheapest way to include electron correlation at all and is widely used for that reason. It describes dispersion reasonably and overestimates it for large systems. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "MP2" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000827 ! Moeller-Plesset
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000829 ! Moeller-Plesset 3

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000829
name: Moeller-Plesset 3
def: "A Møller-Plesset method truncated at third order. It costs substantially more than second order and does not reliably give a better answer, because the perturbation series does not converge smoothly. It is rarely used in practice. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "MP3" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000827 ! Moeller-Plesset

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000830
name: Moeller-Plesset 4
def: "A Møller-Plesset method truncated at fourth order, including single, double, triple and quadruple excitations out of the Hartree-Fock reference. The triple excitations are what make it markedly more accurate than second order and also what make it expensive. It is sometimes written with the excitation levels listed explicitly. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "MP4" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000827 ! Moeller-Plesset

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000831
name: Moeller-Plesset 5
def: "A Møller-Plesset method truncated at fifth order. It includes still higher excitations than fourth order, at a cost that rises steeply with system size. It is used almost only to study how the perturbation series itself behaves. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "MP5" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000827 ! Moeller-Plesset

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000832
name: multi-reference method
def: "A class of advanced quantum mechanics methods required for accurately describing molecules or chemical processes where the electronic structure cannot be well represented by a single dominant electron configuration (as assumed in basic Hartree-Fock theory). These situations often involve stretched bonds, excited states, diradicals, or transition metals, necessitating the use of multiple electronic configurations to capture the essential physics. These methods are typically more computationally demanding than single-reference approaches. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "multi-reference" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000173 ! quantum mechanics

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000833
name: complete active space self-consistent field
def: "A multi-configurational method in which a chosen set of electrons and orbitals, the active space, is treated with every possible configuration among them while the remaining orbitals stay doubly occupied or empty. Choosing that space is the whole art of the method, because its cost grows factorially with its size. It is the most widely used multi-reference starting point. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "CASSCF" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000832 ! multi-reference method
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000834 ! multi-configurational self-consistent field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000834
name: multi-configurational self-consistent field
def: "A quantum chemistry method that optimises the shapes of the molecular orbitals and the weights of several electron configurations at the same time. A single configuration cannot describe a bond being broken or a near-degenerate ground state; several can. It is the starting point for the multi-reference correlated methods. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "MC-SCF" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000832 ! multi-reference method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000835
name: multi-reference coupled cluster with single and double excitations
def: "A quantum chemistry method that applies a coupled cluster treatment with single and double excitations on top of a multi-configurational reference wavefunction. It combines the size consistency of coupled cluster with a reference able to describe bond breaking. It is among the most accurate methods available and among the most expensive. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "MR-CCSD" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000832 ! multi-reference method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000836
name: multi-reference configuration interaction with single and double excitations
def: "A quantum chemistry method that performs a configuration interaction treatment with single and double excitations starting from a multi-configurational reference rather than a single determinant. It recovers dynamic correlation on top of the static correlation the reference already describes. It is not size-consistent, which limits its use on large or dissociating systems. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "MR-CI(SD)" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000832 ! multi-reference method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000837
name: restricted active space self-consistent field
def: "A multi-configurational method that divides the active space into subspaces and limits how many electrons may be excited out of or into each. The restriction keeps the number of configurations manageable where a complete treatment would be too large. It trades some completeness for the ability to use a bigger active space. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "RASSCF" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000832 ! multi-reference method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000838
name: quadratic configuration interaction
def: "A quantum chemistry method developed to account for electron correlation, closely related to the Coupled Cluster (CC) family of methods. It was designed to ensure size-consistency, an important theoretical property meaning the energy of two non-interacting systems is the sum of their individual energies, which is not guaranteed by standard truncated Configuration Interaction (CI). It offers a systematic way to improve upon the Hartree-Fock description. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000173 ! quantum mechanics

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000839
name: QCISD(T)
def: "A quadratic configuration interaction method with single and double excitations that adds a perturbative estimate of triple excitations. The triples correction is what brings the method close to chemical accuracy for many properties. It costs considerably more than the calculation without it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000838 ! quadratic configuration interaction
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000840 ! QCISD

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000840
name: QCISD
def: "A post-Hartree-Fock method that includes single and double excitations in a configuration interaction treatment modified so that the result is size-consistent. Size consistency means the energy of 2 well-separated molecules equals the sum of their separate energies, which plain truncated configuration interaction does not satisfy. Its cost and accuracy are close to those of coupled cluster with single and double excitations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000838 ! quadratic configuration interaction

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000841
name: empirical method
def: "A computational method that uses a simplified energy function whose parameters were fitted to experimental measurements or to more accurate calculations, rather than derived from first principles. The fitting is what makes it fast enough for large systems. It is also its limit: the method is reliable only for systems resembling those it was fitted to. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000141 ! theoretical approach

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000842
name: minimization method
def: "A method that adjusts the positions of atoms to reach a nearby arrangement of lowest energy. It moves downhill from wherever it starts, so it finds the nearest low point rather than the lowest one anywhere. It is run before a simulation to remove the severe atom overlaps that a freshly built system almost always contains. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000841 ! empirical method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000843
name: molecular dynamics
def: "Molecular dynamics (MD) is a computer simulation technique used to study the physical movement of atoms and molecules over time. It calculates the forces between particles using an empirical potential energy function (force field) and then integrates Newton's equations of motion numerically to simulate how the positions and velocities evolve in small time steps. MD simulations provide detailed information about the dynamic behavior, conformational changes, and thermodynamics of molecular systems." []
synonym: "MD" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000308 ! simulation method
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071
property_value: skos:closeMatch operation:2476

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000844
name: NetCDF format
def: "The NetCDF (Network Common Data Form) format, which typically uses the .nc extension, is a set of software libraries and a file format designed for storing and sharing array-oriented scientific data. Developed and maintained by the Unidata program at the University Corporation for Atmospheric Research (UCAR), it is an open standard widely used across many scientific disciplines, such as molecular dynamics. While Amber has adopted NetCDF as its preferred, modern format for storing trajectories and other data, the format itself is not specific to Amber and is a general-purpose standard." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000910 ! general data format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393
property_value: skos:exactMatch format:3650

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000845
name: enhanced sampling
def: "Enhanced sampling encompasses a diverse set of computational techniques used in molecular simulations to accelerate the exploration of a system's possible configurations or states. These methods aim to overcome the timescale limitations of standard simulations, particularly when high energy barriers separate important states or when rare events need to be sampled efficiently. They often involve modifying the potential energy surface, using multiple simulation copies, or applying biasing forces." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000843 ! molecular dynamics
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000846
name: adaptive force bias
def: "An enhanced sampling method that gradually builds up a force opposing the system's own along a chosen coordinate, until the system moves along that coordinate freely. Once the opposing force matches the true one, the barriers along that coordinate have been flattened. The accumulated force is itself the answer, because it gives the free energy profile. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000847 ! canonical adiabatic free energy sampling

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000847
name: canonical adiabatic free energy sampling
def: "Canonical adiabatic free energy sampling refers to enhanced sampling strategies where system parameters or constraints are changed very slowly (adiabatically) during a simulation performed under constant NVT conditions. It splits a system into a \"subsystem\" (the reactive part) and an \"environment\". By introducing fictitious masses and decoupling the subsystem, it allows the subsystem to evolve slowly and adiabatically on the potential of mean force while operating at a much higher temperature than the environment, speeding up rare events without altering the physical ensemble." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000848
name: forward flux simulation
def: "Forward Flux Sampling (FFS) is an enhanced sampling technique specifically designed to calculate rate constants and characterize pathways for rare events, such as transitions between stable molecular states. It involves defining a series of non-overlapping interfaces along a reaction coordinate between the initial and final states. Trajectories are initiated from these interfaces and only propagated forward if they reach the next interface, efficiently focusing computational effort on successful transition paths." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000849
name: locally enhanced sampling
def: "Locally Enhanced Sampling (LES) is a computational method used in molecular dynamics to accelerate the simulation of specific, localized regions of a molecule, such as a ligand binding site or a specific protein segment. It achieves this by introducing multiple non-interacting copies of the \"enhanced\" atoms while proportionately reducing their interaction potentials." []
synonym: "LES" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000850
name: markov chain model
def: "A statistical model of a system that moves between discrete states, in which the next state depends only on the current one and not on how the system arrived there. That assumption is what makes long-timescale behaviour computable from short observations. It holds only if the states are chosen so that everything relevant about the past is captured by which state the system is in. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000851
name: max-flux approach
def: "The max-flux approach in molecular systems typically refers to a variational method used to calculate the most probable reaction pathway during a transition (like conformational changes or chemical reactions). It finds the path that maximizes the diffusive flux of distinct reactive trajectories between two metastable states." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000852
name: metadynamics
def: "Metadynamics is an enhanced sampling technique that accelerates the exploration of complex energy landscapes by adding a history-dependent bias potential along a few chosen collective variables (CVs). Small repulsive energy 'hills' (often Gaussian functions) are periodically deposited at the system's current location in the CV space, discouraging revisiting explored areas and eventually filling up free energy wells. The accumulated bias potential provides an estimate of the free energy surface along the selected CVs." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000853
name: milestoning
def: "Milestoning sampling (or the milestoning algorithm) is an advanced molecular simulation technique designed to calculate the kinetics and thermodynamics of slow, complex processes (such as protein folding or drug binding). It breaks down computationally expensive simulations into multiple, short, independent trajectories between predefined interfaces, or \"milestones\"." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000854
name: multi-state bennett acceptance ratio
def: "A free energy analysis method that combines data from simulations run at many thermodynamic states at once, and returns the free energy difference between any pair of them together with equilibrium averages. It uses every sample from every state rather than only neighbouring pairs, which is what makes it statistically optimal. It generalises the 2-state Bennett acceptance ratio. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000855
name: neural network
def: "A machine learning model built from layers of simple units, each combining its inputs and passing the result on, whose connection strengths are adjusted to fit training data. Given enough units it can represent almost any relationship, which is why it is used where no formula is known. In this field it is used to predict energies and forces, and to find useful coordinates automatically. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "neural networks" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000856
name: nudged elastic band
def: "The Nudged Elastic Band (NEB) method is primarily used to find the Minimum Energy Path (MEP) connecting two known stable states (e.g., reactant and product) on a potential energy surface. It works by optimizing a discrete chain of intermediate structures (images) linking the start and end points. Forces acting on the images perpendicular to the path are minimized, while spring forces along the path ensure continuity, guiding the chain towards the MEP, including the transition state." []
synonym: "NEB" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000857
name: reference potential spatial warping
def: "An enhanced sampling method that speeds up sampling by transforming the coordinates, or modifying the potential energy, using a simpler reference potential as the guide. The transformation flattens barriers that the reference potential also has, leaving the difference between the 2 to be sampled. Results are then corrected back to the true potential. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000858
name: replica-exchange molecular dynamics
def: "Replica-exchange molecular dynamics (REMD), also known as parallel tempering, is an enhanced sampling technique that runs multiple simulations (replicas) of the same system in parallel, typically each at a different temperature. At regular intervals, attempts are made to swap the current configurations between pairs of replicas running at adjacent temperatures, accepted based on a probability criterion. This allows configurations explored at high temperatures (overcoming energy barriers) to diffuse down to lower temperatures, enhancing conformational sampling." []
synonym: "REMD" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000859
name: steered dynamics
def: "Steered Molecular Dynamics (sMD) is a simulation technique where an external, time-dependent force or constraint is applied to manipulate the system, often by pulling on specific atoms or controlling the distance between groups. This forces the system along a chosen pathway, allowing exploration of processes like ligand unbinding or protein monomerization-multimerization that might not occur spontaneously on simulation timescales. sMD trajectories can also be used with fluctuation theorems (like Jarzynski's equality) to estimate equilibrium free energy differences." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000860
name: string method
def: "A computational method that finds the most likely route between 2 stable states of a system, described in terms of a few chosen coordinates. It represents the route as a line of points and repeatedly moves them downhill in energy while keeping them evenly spaced along it. The line settles onto the path the system is most likely to take, which is rarely a straight one. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000861
name: swarm-of-trajectories
def: "The swarm-of-trajectories approach refers to computational strategies that utilize a large number of independent, often relatively short, MD simulations launched from specific initial conditions. This \"swarm\" allows for efficient statistical sampling of pathways, transition probabilities between states, or average forces needed in methods like the String Method or Milestoning. It contrasts with relying on a single, very long trajectory to observe events of interest." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000862
name: targeted molecular dynamics
def: "Targeted Molecular Dynamics (TMD) is a simulation technique used to induce a conformational transition between a known initial structure and a known target structure. It achieves this by adding an extra potential energy term that biases the system to reduce its root-mean-square deviation (RMSD) relative to the target structure over the course of the simulation. TMD provides a plausible pathway for the transition, although not necessarily the minimum energy or most probable one." []
synonym: "TMD" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000863
name: transition path sampling
def: "Transition Path Sampling (TPS) is a powerful simulation technique designed to study rare transition events between stable molecular states by directly sampling the ensemble of reactive pathways connecting them. Starting with one known reactive trajectory, it uses a Monte Carlo sampling in path space (generating new trial paths from old ones) to explore the set of all possible transition mechanisms without needing predefined reaction coordinates. TPS allows for the calculation of rate constants and detailed mechanistic analysis." []
synonym: "TPS" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000864
name: transition state ensemble
def: "The Transition State Ensemble (TSE) refers to the collection of molecular configurations that lie at the top of the highest free energy barrier separating the reactant and product states of a process, such as protein folding or a chemical reaction. Structures within the TSE are equally likely to proceed forward to the product state or revert back to the reactant state (i.e., they have a committor probability of 0.5). Characterizing the structural features of the TSE is key to understanding the mechanism of the transition." []
synonym: "transition state ensembles" EXACT []
synonym: "TSE" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000865
name: transition interface sampling
def: "Transition Interface Sampling (TIS) is a path sampling technique, related to Forward Flux Sampling, used for calculating rate constants of rare events. It involves defining interfaces along an order parameter and then specifically sampling ensembles of trajectories that start in the reactant state and reach a particular interface, or start at one interface and reach the next. By calculating the crossing probabilities between interfaces, TIS reconstructs the overall rate constant." []
synonym: "TIS" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000866
name: ADF input format
def: "An input file format that carries the keywords and data blocks instructing the Amsterdam Density Functional software how to perform a quantum chemical calculation. It specifies details like the desired computational task (e.g., geometry optimization, frequency calculation), the molecular geometry, the choice of density functional and basis set, and other calculation parameters. The format uses specific ADF keywords and block structures (e.g., ATOMS, GEOMETRY). (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000437 ! simulation input format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000868 ! GAMESS input format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000867
name: CHARMM input format
def: "A CHARMM input file is a script containing a sequence of commands written in the CHARMM scripting language, which directs the CHARMM program to perform various tasks. These tasks can range from reading topology and coordinate files, setting up system parameters, running energy minimizations or molecular dynamics simulations, to analyzing results." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000438 ! script format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000868
name: GAMESS input format
def: "An input file format that instructs the GAMESS (US) quantum chemistry program, structured into groups identified by keywords starting with '$', such as $CONTRL, $BASIS and $DATA. Within these groups, keywords specify the type of calculation (e.g., RUNTYP=OPTIMIZE), the theoretical method (e.g., SCFTYP=RHF), basis set, molecular geometry, and other computational details. The format follows specific Fortran namelist-like conventions. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000437 ! simulation input format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000869
name: GAMESS-UK input format
def: "A text data format that specifies a molecular system and the settings for a quantum chemistry calculation to the GAMESS-UK program, using directives such as TITLE, RUNTYPE, GEOMETRY and BASIS. Its keywords and layout differ substantially from those of the separate GAMESS (US) program, so files are not interchangeable between them. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000437 ! simulation input format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000870
name: gjf format
def: "An input file format that instructs the Gaussian quantum chemistry software, carrying the extension .com or .gjf. It characteristically includes a 'route section' (starting with #) containing keywords that define the theoretical method, basis set, and calculation type (e.g., optimization, frequency), followed by a title section, charge and spin multiplicity, and the molecular geometry. The structure is highly standardized within the Gaussian ecosystem. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "GAUSSIAN com format" EXACT []
synonym: "GAUSSIAN gjf format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000437 ! simulation input format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000871
name: GROMACS input format
def: "In GROMACS, the primary molecular dynamics input file usually has an .mdp extension and contains keyword-value pairs defining the simulation parameters. Processed by the grompp tool, it controls aspects like the integration algorithm, timestep, simulation length, temperature and pressure coupling methods, and cutoff schemes. This file dictates how the MD simulation engine (mdrun) will execute the run." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002065 ! simulation parameter format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000872
name: HyperChem hin format
def: "A data format, written with the extension .hin, that is the native way the HyperChem modelling package stores a molecular system. It holds atomic coordinates, connectivity, force field atom types, and settings for a calculation. It serves both as input to the program and as the way a session is saved. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001088 ! molecular structure format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000873
name: Jaguar input format
def: "An input file format that carries the instructions for a quantum chemistry calculation in Jaguar, part of the Schrodinger suite. It uses a specific syntax with data sections delimited by &section_name (e.g., &gen, &zmat) and terminated by &, containing keywords and values controlling the calculation type, method, basis set, and molecular geometry. The structure facilitates setting up various QM tasks. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000437 ! simulation input format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000874
name: MOPAC cartesian format
def: "A data format specifying a molecule's geometry to the MOPAC semi-empirical program as 3 coordinates per atom. Each coordinate carries a flag saying whether it may be optimised or must be held fixed. That per-coordinate control is what distinguishes it from a plain coordinate list. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001088 ! molecular structure format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000875
name: MOPAC internal format
def: "A data format specifying a molecule's geometry to the MOPAC semi-empirical program as bond lengths, angles and rotations. As with its coordinate counterpart, each value carries a flag saying whether it may be optimised. It is the form used when a particular bond or angle must be scanned or held. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001088 ! molecular structure format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000876
name: NAMD configuration format
def: "A NAMD configuration file, typically ending in .namd, contains parameters and commands that control a molecular dynamics simulation run using the NAMD software. It uses a keyword-value pair format, often leveraging Tcl scripting capabilities, to specify input files (structure, coordinates, parameters), simulation conditions (temperature, pressure, duration), and algorithms. This file dictates the entire simulation protocol." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002065 ! simulation parameter format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000877
name: NWChem input format
def: "An NWChem input file (.nw) uses directives and nested blocks to instruct the NWChem software package on performing computational chemistry tasks. It is composed of commands, called directives, which define data (such as basis sets, geometries, and filenames) and the actions to be performed on that data. Directives are processed in the order presented in the input file, with the exception of certain start-up directives (see Input File Structure) which provide critical job control information, and are processed before all other input. Most directives are specific to a particular module and define data that is used by that module only. A few directives (see Top-level Directives) potentially affect all modules, for instance by specifying the total electric charge on the system." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000437 ! simulation input format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000878
name: Q-Chem input format
def: "An input file format that instructs the Q-Chem quantum chemistry program, using data blocks marked by $block_name and $end. Key blocks include $molecule (defining charge, multiplicity, and geometry), $rem (specifying calculation method, basis set, job type via keywords), and potentially others like $basis or $opt. This structure organizes the input required for a wide range of QM calculations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000437 ! simulation input format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000879
name: ADF output format
def: "A text data format in which the Amsterdam Density Functional program records a completed calculation. It holds the input as read back, the convergence history, the final energy with its breakdown into physically meaningful components, and the computed properties. That energy decomposition is what distinguishes it from other quantum chemistry output. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000439 ! simulation log format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000880
name: RKF format
def: "A structured binary file format generated by the Amsterdam Density Functional package, written with the extension .rkf and formerly called ADF Tape41. It stores a comprehensive set of calculation results, including basis set details, molecular orbital coefficients, electron densities, gradients, and potentially Hessians, in a key-value database format. This file is essential for advanced analysis, visualization, and restarting calculations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "ADF rkf format" EXACT []
synonym: "ADF Tape41 format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000441 ! simulation state format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000881
name: CHARMM output format
def: "The CHARMM output file is the main text log generated during a CHARMM run, typically containing an echo of the input script commands interspersed with the results produced by those commands. This includes detailed energy breakdowns, progress information during dynamics or minimization (like step number, time, temperature, pressure, energies), and outputs from analysis routines. It serves as the primary record of the CHARMM job execution." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000439 ! simulation log format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000882
name: GAMESS output format
def: "A text data format, written with the extension .log or .out, in which the GAMESS (US) program records a completed calculation. It holds the input as read back, the basis set and geometry, convergence progress for the SCF or geometry optimisation, final energies, molecular orbital information and calculated properties. It is the file results are extracted from. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000439 ! simulation log format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000883
name: GAMESS-UK output format
def: "A text data format in which the GAMESS-UK program records a completed calculation, including the input as read back, convergence progress, final energies and calculated properties. Its structure and keywords differ from those of the separate GAMESS (US) program, so a parser written for one will not read the other. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000439 ! simulation log format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000884
name: GAUSSIAN log format
def: "A text data format, written with the extension .log, in which the Gaussian program records a completed calculation. It holds setup information, convergence progress, final energies, molecular orbital details, properties such as dipole moments and charges, and vibrational and thermochemical results when those were requested. A compact summary called the archive entry sits near the end. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000439 ! simulation log format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000885
name: GROMACS output format
def: "The GROMACS MD output typically refers to the primary text log file (.log) generated by the mdrun simulation engine. It contains summary information about the simulation setup, detailed performance data (like PME load balancing and timings), step-by-step progress updates (if configured in the .mdp file), and final run statistics including energy averages and runtime. This file is crucial for monitoring performance and verifying run completion." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000439 ! simulation log format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000886
name: Jaguar output format
def: "A text data format, written with the extension .out, in which the Jaguar program records a completed calculation. It holds the input parameters, convergence information for the SCF and geometry optimisation cycles, final energies, properties such as charges and dipole moments, and vibrational frequencies when requested. The final geometry is usually written to a separate structure file. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000439 ! simulation log format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000887
name: MOPAC output format
def: "An output file format holding the results of a calculation performed by the MOPAC semi-empirical program, written with the extension .out. It typically includes an echo of the input keywords, details of geometry optimization steps (if performed), the final optimized geometry, the calculated heat of formation (ΔH f), ionization potential, dipole moment, and atomic charges. A summary section usually highlights the key results and timings. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000439 ! simulation log format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000888
name: NWChem output format
def: "A text data format, written with the extension .out or .nwout, in which the NWChem program records the tasks its input file requested. It holds the calculation setup, convergence progress, energies from whichever quantum, molecular mechanics or combined method was used, properties and timings. Because the program accepts very varied inputs, the layout of the file varies with them. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000439 ! simulation log format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000889
name: Q-Chem output format
def: "A text data format, written with the extension .out or .qcout, in which the Q-Chem program records a completed calculation. It holds the method and basis set used, convergence information for the SCF and geometry optimisation, final electronic energies, molecular orbital information, and properties such as charges and dipole moments. A summary section usually collects the main computed values. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000439 ! simulation log format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000890
name: GAUSSIAN chk format
def: "A binary checkpoint file format that stores the state of a completed or running Gaussian calculation, including the molecular geometry, basis set details, molecular orbital coefficients, density matrix and forces. It is essential for restarting interrupted calculations (especially geometry optimizations or frequency calculations) and for post-processing tasks like generating cube files or performing wavefunction analysis. It can be converted to a formatted version (.fchk). (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000441 ! simulation state format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000891
name: GAUSSIAN restart format
def: "A binary data format, written with the extension .chk, in which Gaussian stores the state of a calculation so that a later job can continue from it. It holds the geometry, the wavefunction and Hessian information. A later job reads it when the input asks for it, for example with Geom=Checkpoint or Guess=Read. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000441 ! simulation state format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000892
name: GROMACS restart format
def: "A binary data format, written with the extension .cpt, in which GROMACS stores the complete state of a running simulation at intervals. It holds the step number, the time, the positions, the velocities, the box and the state of the thermostat and barostat. Resuming from it continues the run exactly, as though it had never stopped. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000441 ! simulation state format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000893
name: NWChem restart format
def: "Restarting an NWChem calculation involves using various files generated during a previous run, depending on the calculation type. This may include the run database (.db), molecular orbital vector files (.movecs), geometry files, or specific QM/MM restart files (.rst)." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000441 ! simulation state format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000894
name: mdfrc format
def: "A data format that stores the force on every atom of a system at each saved step of an AMBER simulation. It records forces where a trajectory format records positions. It is used for debugging a force field and for analyses that need the forces themselves. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "AMBER mdfrc format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001090 ! molecular trajectory format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000895
name: gro format
def: "The GROMACS .gro file is a simple, formatted text file used to store molecular coordinates, atom/residue names, and optionally velocities. It includes a title line, the total number of atoms, and then one line per atom specifying residue and atom information, coordinates (in nanometers), and optionally velocities. The file concludes with the periodic box vectors. It is typically used to store single structures." []
synonym: "GROMACS gro format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001088 ! molecular structure format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000896
name: TINKER xyz format
def: "A specialized text-based file format used by the TINKER software package. While it shares the '.xyz' extension with the standard Cartesian coordinate format, it is distinct in that it explicitly includes atom indices, force field atom types, and connectivity (bond) lists for every atom, serving as both a coordinate and topology file. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001088 ! molecular structure format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000897
name: TURBOMOLE coordinate format
def: "A data format used by TURBOMOLE to record atomic coordinates, written as a labelled section inside the program's control file rather than as a separate file. It lists Cartesian coordinates, in atomic units unless another unit is stated, followed by the element of each atom. Keeping it inside the control file is why a TURBOMOLE job is a directory rather than a single file. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001088 ! molecular structure format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000898
name: itp format
def: "A GROMACS include topology file (.itp) contains the topology definition for a specific type of molecule (like a protein, lipid, or solvent). It typically includes sections like [ moleculetype ], [ atoms ], [ bonds ], etc., and is designed to be reusable. These .itp files are incorporated into the main system topology (.top) file using the #include directive." []
synonym: "GROMACS include topology format" EXACT []
synonym: "GROMACS itp format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001091 ! molecular topology format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000899
name: top format
def: "A topology file format that describes an entire molecular system to be simulated with GROMACS, written with the extension .top. It typically starts by including force field parameter files and specific molecule topology files (.itp) using #include directives. Crucially, it concludes with a [ molecules ] section listing the names and counts of each type of molecule present in the simulation box. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: ".top" EXACT []
synonym: "GROMACS system topology format" EXACT []
synonym: "GROMACS top format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001091 ! molecular topology format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000900
name: NWChem topology format
def: "A data format specifying the topology of a system to NWChem, written as labelled sections inside the program's input file rather than as a separate file. It gives the atoms, their types and charges, and the force field to apply. Keeping it in the input file is why an NWChem calculation is described by 1 file rather than 2. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001091 ! molecular topology format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000901
name: PSF format
def: "A Protein Structure File (.psf) defines the atoms, connectivity (bonds, angles, dihedrals, impropers), and basic atomic properties (like type indices, charges, masses) for a molecular system. Importantly, it does not contain the actual force field parameters. PSF files are used by the simulation programs CHARMM and NAMD." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001091 ! molecular topology format
property_value: IAO:0000116 "The format originates with X-Plor. Recorded here rather than in the definition, which was verified on 2026-09-18 without it. Source: EDAM 1.25, class format_3882 PSF (http://edamontology.org/format_3882)." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393
property_value: skos:exactMatch format:3882

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000902
name: dcd format
def: "The DCD (.dcd) trajectory format is a widely used binary file format for storing atomic coordinates from molecular dynamics simulations, optionally including periodic box information. Originally developed for CHARMM, it is now supported by many simulation packages (like NAMD, LAMMPS) and analysis tools (like VMD) due to its efficiency and portability." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001090 ! molecular trajectory format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000903
name: GROMACS trajectory format
def: "A binary data format in which GROMACS records the positions of atoms through a simulation, in either a compressed form holding coordinates only or a full form holding velocities and forces as well. The compressed form discards low-order digits to save space, which is acceptable for analysis and not for restarting a run. Which was written determines what the trajectory can afterwards be used for. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001090 ! molecular trajectory format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000904
name: molecular structure
def: "A molecular structure is the information that specifies the three-dimensional arrangement of atoms in a molecule. It is typically represented by a list of atomic coordinates (X, Y, Z) for each atom in the system. This structural information is the fundamental input for visualization and is the starting point for any molecular simulation." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001073 ! molecular system specification
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000905
name: obsolete small molecule structure
def: "OBSOLETE. Small molecule structure formats are designed primarily for representing organic and drug-like molecules, often emphasizing chemical details like bond orders, formal charges, and stereochemistry. These formats are widely used in cheminformatics, drug discovery databases, and as input for various modeling tasks. Common examples include SDF, Mol2, and SMILES strings." []
comment: Retired in the file-format flattening. Classifying structure formats by molecule size was an artificial distinction: a small molecule can be stored in a PDB file and a macromolecule in a mol2 file. Its former children are now direct children of 'molecular structure format' (MOLSIM:001088). Reported in GitHub issue #20.
is_obsolete: true

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000906
name: Mol2 format
def: "The Mol2 format (.mol2) is a text-based file format originating from Sybyl software, commonly used to represent small molecules, especially in docking and cheminformatics applications. It stores atomic coordinates, atom names, connectivity (including bond orders), partial charges, and often uses specific Sybyl atom types. A single Mol2 file can contain multiple molecular structures." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001088 ! molecular structure format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000907 ! SDF format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393
property_value: skos:exactMatch format:3816

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000907
name: SDF format
def: "The Structure-Data File (SDF, .sdf) format is widely used in cheminformatics for storing libraries of small molecules along with associated data. It essentially consists of multiple blocks defining atomic coordinates and connectivity for each molecule concatenated together, where each block can be followed by data fields like IDs or calculated properties." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001088 ! molecular structure format
property_value: IAO:0000116 "The format was developed by MDL Information Systems. Recorded here rather than in the definition, which was verified on 2026-09-18 without it. Source: EDAM 1.25, class format_3814 SDF (http://edamontology.org/format_3814)." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393
property_value: skos:exactMatch format:3814

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000908
name: sequence data format
def: "Sequence formats are standardized ways to represent the primary structure of biological macromolecules, such as the order of amino acids in a protein or nucleotides in DNA/RNA, using strings of characters. These formats usually include a header line providing an identifier and description, followed by the sequence itself using standard codes (e.g., one-letter codes). They are fundamental in bioinformatics for storing and exchanging sequence data." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000436 ! data format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000909
name: volumetric data format
def: "A data format that stores a property varying continuously through 3-dimensional space, such as electron density or electrostatic potential, as values on a regular grid of points. A file in one of these formats states the grid's origin, its dimensions and its spacing, then lists a value for each point. They are used to visualize and analyse spatial distributions from simulation or from experiment. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000436 ! data format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000910
name: general data format
def: "General data formats are versatile, often standardized ways to structure and exchange data that are not tied to a specific application domain like molecular simulation. Formats like XML or JSON use tags or key-value pairs to create hierarchical and self-describing data structures. They are sometimes employed in simulation contexts for storing metadata, configuration, or for facilitating data exchange between different tools." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000436 ! data format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000911
name: analysis script
def: "A script holding the sequence of commands that an analysis program or library carries out on simulation data. It records exactly what was computed and in what order, so an analysis can be repeated. It is often the only surviving record of how a published number was obtained. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001074 ! process specification

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000912
name: FASTA format
def: "The Fasta format is a simple and widely used text-based format for storing biological sequence data (nucleotides or amino acids). Each sequence entry begins with a single-line description header, marked by a greater-than symbol ('>'), followed by the sequence data on one or more subsequent lines. Its simplicity makes it easily readable by humans and parsable by many bioinformatics tools." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000908 ! sequence data format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393
property_value: skos:closeMatch format:1929

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000913
name: cube format
def: "A text data format storing a property sampled on a regular 3-dimensional grid, together with the positions of the atoms it surrounds. It states the grid's origin, its axes and its spacing, then lists one value per point. Electron density, electrostatic potential and molecular orbitals are all distributed in it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "GAUSSIAN cube format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000909 ! volumetric data format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000914
name: XML format
def: "XML (Extensible Markup Language) is a flexible, text-based markup language used to encode data in a format that is both human-readable and machine-readable. It uses user-defined tags to structure data hierarchically with elements and attributes. XML is widely used for data exchange on the web and in various scientific domains, including bioinformatics." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000910 ! general data format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393
property_value: skos:exactMatch format:2332

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000915
name: CML format
def: "A data format, built on XML, that records chemical information as structured, labelled text. It defines tags for molecular structures, reactions, spectra and calculation results, so that a file states what each number is rather than relying on position. Its purpose is exchange between programs that would otherwise each need a reader for the others' formats. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000914 ! XML format
property_value: skos:exactMatch format:4023

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000916
name: Ptraj script format
def: "A text data format holding a sequence of commands for the ptraj or cpptraj trajectory analysis programs of AmberTools. A file in this format names the input trajectories with trajin, may name a reference structure, and then lists analysis commands such as rms, distance, hbond, radgyr or cluster. It is the record of how a trajectory was post-processed. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000438 ! script format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000917
name: structural analysis
def: "A category of analysis methods focused on examining the three-dimensional arrangement of atoms (geometry and conformation) and the overall shape and topology of molecules based on simulation data or optimized structures. This includes measuring geometric parameters (distances, angles, dihedrals), identifying characteristic local and global structural features, comparing structures, and quantifying structural fluctuations. It helps understand molecular architecture, flexibility, stability, and structure-function relationships." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000026 ! analysis method
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000918
name: obsolete global structure analysis
def: "OBSOLETE. A structural analysis focusing on the overall architecture, shape, fold, and packing of a macromolecule or molecular complex, rather than fine details. This is often characterized by metrics like the radius of gyration, principal moments of inertia, overall dimensions, secondary structure content (for proteins), or tertiary arrangement of domains. It provides a macroscopic view of the molecule's conformation and large-scale structural changes." []
comment: Retired because it grouped nothing: the analyses its definition named (radius of gyration, principal moments of inertia, secondary structure) are siblings under MOLSIM:000917 structural analysis, not subclasses of this term. Raised in the August 2026 definition review.
is_obsolete: true

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000921
name: crd format
def: "A generic name for a text-based file format that stores the Cartesian (x, y, z) coordinates of atoms in a molecular system. The specific layout can vary, as multiple simulation packages like CHARMM and Amber have their own distinct versions of a \".crd\" file. Due to its ambiguity, it is often necessary to specify which software's CRD format is being used." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001088 ! molecular structure format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000923
name: local structure analysis
def: "A structural analysis focusing on the detailed geometric arrangement of small groups of atoms within a molecule. This includes analyzing specific bond lengths, bond angles, dihedral angles, ring conformations (like sugar pucker), hydrogen bonding patterns, or the conformation of amino acid side chains. It provides fine-grained insights into specific interactions, conformational preferences, and flexibility at the atomic or residue level." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000917 ! structural analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000924
name: atom triplet angle calculation analysis
def: "A fundamental local structure analysis that calculates the angle formed by three specified atoms (A-B-C), centered on atom B. These bond angles are essential parameters defining the geometry and shape of molecules. Monitoring their values and distributions during simulations reveals information about molecular flexibility and conformational preferences around specific centers. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000923 ! local structure analysis
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000925 ! dihedral calculation analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000925
name: dihedral calculation analysis
def: "A local structure analysis technique that calculates the torsion angle defined by four sequentially bonded atoms (A-B-C-D), representing the rotation around the central bond (B-C). Dihedral angles are critical for determining the three-dimensional conformation of flexible molecules, including protein backbones, side chains, and polymer chains. Analyzing their values and distributions reveals accessible rotational states and conformational dynamics." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000923 ! local structure analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000926
name: distance calculation analysis
def: "A basic local structure analysis technique that measures the distance between any two specified atoms (bonded or non-bonded) in a molecular system. Monitoring distances is essential for tracking bond lengths, identifying close contacts, analyzing non-covalent interactions (like hydrogen bonds, salt bridges, van der Waals contacts), and assessing overall conformational changes or molecular dimensions." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000923 ! local structure analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000927
name: pucker analysis
def: "A specialized local structure analysis used to describe and quantify the non-planar conformation (puckering) of cyclic molecular fragments, particularly five-membered (e.g., furanose rings in DNA/RNA, proline) or six-membered rings (e.g., pyranose rings, cyclohexane). It employs parameters like pseudorotation angles and amplitudes to precisely define the ring's shape (e.g., envelope, twist, chair, boat conformations). This analysis is vital for understanding the structure and function of nucleic acids and carbohydrates. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000923 ! local structure analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000928
name: atomic properties analysis
def: "A type of structural analysis focusing on quantifying properties associated with individual atoms within the molecular structure, often reflecting their local environment or dynamics. Examples include atomic fluctuations (Root Mean Square Fluctuation, RMSF, or B-factors) indicating mobility, solvent accessibility surface area (SASA) quantifying exposure to solvent, or coordination numbers describing the local packing density. Analyzing these properties provides atom-specific insights into dynamics, interactions, and structural roles. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000917 ! structural analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000936
name: AMBER OL24
def: "A refined set of force field parameters specifically developed to improve the accuracy of DNA simulations using the AMBER force field. It provides an updated description of the sugar-pucker torsional potential, which is critical for correctly capturing the conformational equilibrium between A-form and B-form DNA. These parameters are intended as an update to be used in conjunction with a parent protein-DNA force field like ff14SB. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000010 ! DNA force field
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001444 ! AMBER OL15

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000937
name: structure clustering analysis
def: "An analysis method that groups the structures in a trajectory by how similar they are, usually measured by the distance between them after superposition. It reduces thousands of frames to a handful of representative shapes. Those representatives are what a trajectory is usually described and pictured by. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000123 ! clustering analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000938
name: structure clustering with dihedral binning
def: "A specialized structure clustering approach where conformations are grouped primarily based on the values of selected dihedral angles, rather than overall coordinate RMSD. Structures are assigned to bins based on which ranges their key dihedral angles fall into, and clusters are formed by grouping structures within the same or similar bins. This method is particularly useful for analyzing conformational changes driven by specific torsions, like backbone transitions or sidechain rotations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000937 ! structure clustering analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000939
name: dynamics analysis
def: "Dynamics analysis involves processing the time-series data generated from molecular dynamics simulations, primarily the trajectory files, to extract quantitative information and insights about the system's behavior. This encompasses a wide range of techniques aimed at understanding molecular motions, conformational changes, interactions, and kinetic or thermodynamic properties. The goal is to translate raw simulation output into meaningful physical or biological understanding." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000004 ! simulation analysis
is_a: MOLSIM:000026 ! analysis method
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000940
name: AMBER force field parameter format
def: "A text-based file format used by the AMBER software suite to store standard force field parameters. These files (historically using the .dat extension) contain the equilibrium values and force constants for bonds, angles, dihedrals, and non-bonded interactions for specific atom types. They serve as the central parameter database loaded by system-building tools like LEaP. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "AMBER dat format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:002066 ! force field parameter format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001079 ! frcmod format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000941
name: coordinate rotation modeling
def: "A coordinate rotation method is a structure modification method that applies a mathematical rotation to the coordinates of a molecule or a group of atoms. This procedure changes the orientation of the selected atoms in three-dimensional space without altering their internal structure." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000305 ! modeling method
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000942
name: time cross correlation analysis
def: "A dynamics analysis method that measures how the fluctuations of 2 different properties relate to each other over time, including at a time delay. A positive value means they rise and fall together, a negative value means one rises as the other falls, and near zero means they are independent. The delay at which the relationship is strongest shows which motion leads and which follows. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000342 ! correlation analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000943
name: RMSD correlation analysis
def: "A dynamics analysis method that measures how the displacement of each atom or residue from its average position relates to that of every other, over the course of a simulation. A strongly positive value means 2 sites move in the same direction, a negative value means they move in opposite directions. The result is usually drawn as a dynamic cross-correlation map, which shows which parts of a molecule move as one. (UNVERIFIED)" []
comment: is it synonymous as "atomic correlation analysis"?
is_a: MOLSIM:000342 ! correlation analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000944
name: motion analysis
def: "Motion analysis encompasses techniques used to characterize the types, directions, and magnitudes of movements occurring within a molecular system during a simulation. These methods aim to simplify the complex, high-dimensional atomic motions into understandable patterns or dominant modes. This helps identify functionally relevant conformational changes, flexibility, and collective dynamics." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000939 ! dynamics analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000945
name: principal axis alignment analysis
def: "A structural analysis method that superposes structures by matching their principal axes of inertia rather than by minimising the distance between corresponding atoms. It aligns on overall mass distribution and shape, so it is unaffected by local differences that would dominate a least-squares fit. It suits comparisons of rotational motion and of overall shape. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000944 ! motion analysis
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000946 ! coordinate projection analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000946
name: coordinate projection analysis
def: "A dynamics analysis method that maps the many-dimensional motion in a trajectory onto 1 or a few chosen directions. The chosen direction may be a simple geometric measure such as a distance or an angle, or a vector taken from principal component analysis. Projecting this way reduces a trajectory to a small number of curves that can be read directly. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000944 ! motion analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000947
name: eigenmode analysis
def: "A dynamics analysis method that decomposes the motion of a molecular system into a set of independent collective modes, each with a characteristic amplitude or frequency. Principal component analysis applied to a trajectory and normal mode analysis applied to a single structure are the 2 standard ways of obtaining them. The modes show the principal directions in which a molecule moves. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000944 ! motion analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000948
name: diffusion analysis
def: "A type of dynamics analysis focused on quantifying the random translational and rotational movement of molecules or particles within the simulation environment due to thermal energy. It primarily involves calculating diffusion coefficients, which measure the rate at which particles spread out over time. This analysis provides insights into transport properties, viscosity, and mobility in fluids, membranes, or crowded cellular environments. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000939 ! dynamics analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000949
name: diffusion calculation analysis
def: "An analysis method that extracts a diffusion coefficient from a trajectory, most often by tracking how the mean squared displacement of the molecules grows with time. Over long enough times that growth is linear, and its slope gives the coefficient. Reading a slope from too short a stretch of trajectory is the usual way this measurement goes wrong. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000948 ! diffusion analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000950
name: energy analysis
def: "A type of structural analysis focused on calculating and interpreting the potential energy associated with specific molecular structures or conformations obtained from simulations or modeling. This includes calculating single point energies, comparing energies of different conformers, or decomposing the total energy into contributing components. It helps assess the stability and likelihood of different structures." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000026 ! analysis method
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000951
name: binding energy analysis
def: "An energy analysis quantity representing the net energy change associated with the formation of a molecular complex from its individual, separated components in a specific reference state (e.g., gas phase or solution). It typically refers to the difference in potential energy or free energy between the bound complex and the unbound molecules, indicating the strength of the association (a more negative value implies stronger binding). Various computational methods (QM, MM-PBSA/GBSA) can estimate binding energies, sometimes including entropic and solvation effects (binding free energy). (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000950 ! energy analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000952
name: MM-PBSA analysis
def: "A widely used computational method for estimating the binding free energy of a molecular complex, particularly for large biomolecules like protein-ligand systems. It combines molecular mechanics (MM) energies calculated from simulation snapshots with continuum solvation models, specifically using the Poisson-Boltzmann (PB) equation to calculate electrostatic solvation energy and a surface area (SA) term for nonpolar solvation energy. It averages results over multiple simulation snapshots to implicitly include entropic effects related to conformation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:010025 ! effective energy analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000953
name: MM-GBSA analysis
def: "A computational method for estimating binding free energies, similar to MM-PBSA, that also combines molecular mechanics (MM) energies with continuum solvation and surface area (SA) terms. However, it uses the Generalized Born (GB) model, an approximation to the Poisson-Boltzmann equation, to calculate the electrostatic solvation energy. The GB model is generally computationally faster than PB, making MM-GBSA efficient for large-scale calculations like virtual screening, though potentially less accurate in some cases. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:010025 ! effective energy analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000954
name: interaction energy analysis
def: "An energy analysis term usually referring to the direct potential energy change when two or more molecules or fragments are brought together from infinite separation to their geometry within the complex, calculated using a specific theoretical level (MM or QM). It typically represents the sum of direct electrostatic and van der Waals (or quantum mechanical equivalents like electrostatics, exchange-repulsion, induction, dispersion) interactions between the components in the fixed complex geometry. It often excludes contributions from the energy required to distort the fragments upon binding and solvation effects, representing a key component of the total binding energy. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000951 ! binding energy analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000955
name: hydrogen bond interaction energies analysis
def: "A specific type of interaction energy analysis focused on quantifying the energetic contribution of individual or collective hydrogen bonds within or between molecules. This can be estimated using specialized energy decomposition schemes, analysis of electrostatic and van der Waals terms between donor-hydrogen-acceptor atoms from a force field, or derived from quantum mechanical calculations. Quantifying H-bond energies helps understand their role in stabilizing structures and mediating molecular recognition. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000954 ! interaction energy analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000956
name: base pair stacking energies analysis
def: "A specific interaction energy analysis quantifying the stabilizing energetic contribution from the non-covalent interactions (primarily van der Waals/dispersions and electrostatics) between adjacent nucleobases (DNA, RNA). These interactions occur between the aromatic base rings and are essential for the stability, geometry, and mechanical properties of nucleic acid structures. Stacking interaction energies are commonly estimated using quantum mechanical methods or specially parameterized molecular mechanics force fields." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000954 ! interaction energy analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-7544-0938

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000963
name: AMBER crd format
def: "This refers to one of the file formats used by Amber to store atomic coordinates. Its extension is commonly .inpcrd, .crd or .mdcrd. It contains a list of coordinates in ASCII, usually read alongside a topology file, and may optionally include periodic box information." []
comment: Amber's standard ASCII coordinate trajectory file format. The "Coordinates Data Set" or "COORDS" in Amber is not a file format, but rather a specialized, in-memory data structure used by the cpptraj analysis program. It is designed to efficiently hold and manipulate sets of coordinate frames (i.e., structures) loaded from trajectory files during an analysis session. Since the COORDS data set is an internal, in-memory representation, it does not have a file extension. Users can interact with it using file-based commands: Loading: users populate a COORDS data set by loading data from standard Amber file formats, such as restart files (.rst7), PDB files, or trajectory files (.nc, .mdcrd), using the loadcrd command. Saving: users write the contents of a COORDS data set to a file using the crdout command. The output will be in a standard coordinate or trajectory format (e.g., Amber restart, PDB, etc.), not a special "COORDS format."
synonym: "AMBER inpcrd format" EXACT []
synonym: "AMBER prmcrd format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000921 ! crd format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001038 ! MPDyn crd format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000974
name: solvent analysis
def: "A category of analysis methods focused specifically on characterizing the structure, dynamics, and properties of the solvent molecules (most commonly water) surrounding a solute molecule within a simulation. This includes examining solvent density and distribution around the solute, analyzing hydrogen bonding networks within the solvent and between solvent and solute, calculating residence times of solvent molecules near the solute, and assessing the overall impact of the solvent on solute behavior. It provides crucial insights into solvation phenomena. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000026 ! analysis method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000975
name: water shell analysis
def: "A concept within hydration analysis referring to concentric layers of water molecules surrounding a solute, typically defined based on distance thresholds from the solute atoms or surface. Analysis focuses on characterizing the properties of water within specific shells (e.g., first, second hydration shell), including the number of water molecules (coordination number), their average density, preferred orientations, hydrogen bonding patterns, and residence times compared to bulk water. This provides a structured way to describe the local solvent environment. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000983 ! hydration analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000976
name: radial distribution analysis
def: "A fundamental distribution analysis method that calculates the probability of finding a particle (e.g., a solvent atom like oxygen) at a given distance 'r' from a central reference point (e.g., a solute atom or the solute's center of mass), relative to the probability expected for a uniform distribution at that distance. The resulting function, the radial distribution function or RDF, often denoted g(r), typically shows peaks corresponding to ordered solvation shells and decays to 1 at large distances (bulk solvent). Integration of the first peak gives the average coordination number in the first solvation shell. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000984 ! distribution analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000978
name: conformation validation analysis
def: "A specific type of validation technique focused on assessing the quality of the three-dimensional arrangement of atoms (the conformation) in simulated biomolecules. It evaluates whether the molecular geometry, including bond lengths, angles, and steric arrangements, is plausible according to known chemical and physical rules. This ensures the structural models generated or sampled during a simulation are stereochemically sound. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000353 ! validation analysis
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000981 ! secondary structure assignment analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000979
name: ramachandran analysis
def: "A widely used graphical tool for conformation validation specifically applied to proteins. It plots the distribution of backbone dihedral angles (phi and psi) for each amino acid residue, allowing visualization of whether these angles fall into sterically allowed or disallowed regions. This provides a crucial check for the quality and realism of the protein backbone structure. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000917 ! structural analysis
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000980 ! structural check analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000980
name: structural check analysis
def: "A form of conformation validation that involves examining various geometric features of a biomolecular structure beyond just backbone torsion angles. This may include verifying appropriate bond lengths, bond angles, checking for unrealistic close contacts between atoms (clashes), or assessing other stereochemical parameters against standard values. It serves as a general quality control measure for the overall molecular model." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000978 ! conformation validation analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000981
name: secondary structure assignment analysis
def: "Refers to the regular, local folding patterns occurring within the backbone of polymers like proteins or nucleic acids, such as alpha-helices and beta-sheets in proteins. These structures are defined by specific patterns of hydrogen bonds between backbone atoms and represent key building blocks of the molecule's overall three-dimensional architecture. While not a technique itself, analyzing secondary structure content and stability is often part of simulation validation and analysis." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000917 ! structural analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000982
name: secondary structure changes analysis
def: "Refers to the dynamic transformations or fluctuations observed in the secondary structure elements of a biomolecule during a simulation or over time. Monitoring these changes, such as the formation or dissolution of helices or sheets, provides insights into molecular flexibility, folding pathways, or responses to interactions. Analyzing these dynamics helps understand how molecular function relates to structural transitions." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000981 ! secondary structure assignment analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000983
name: hydration analysis
def: "A specific type of solvent analysis focusing on the direct interaction of water molecules with a solute molecule. It involves characterizing the arrangement, orientation, dynamics, and energetics of water molecules in the immediate vicinity of the solute, often referred to as the hydration shell(s). Understanding hydration patterns is critical as these interfacial water molecules strongly influence the solute's structure, stability, dynamics, and interactions with other molecules. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000974 ! solvent analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000984
name: distribution analysis
def: "A solvent analysis technique focused on determining the average spatial arrangement or probability density of solvent molecules relative to the solute molecule, averaged over a simulation trajectory. This often involves calculating various distribution functions (e.g., radial, spatial, or angular) that quantify how the likelihood of finding a solvent molecule varies with position and/or orientation around the solute. It reveals preferred solvation sites and the overall structure of the solvent environment. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000974 ! solvent analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000985
name: matrix diagonalization analysis
def: "A core mathematical technique from linear algebra used to simplify a square matrix by finding its characteristic values (eigenvalues) and directions (eigenvectors), effectively transforming it into a diagonal matrix. In biomolecular simulations, this is heavily used in methods like Principal Component Analysis (PCA) to identify dominant modes of collective atomic motion from covariance matrices, or in Normal Mode Analysis (NMA) to find vibrational frequencies from Hessian matrices. Diagonalization reveals the fundamental components or modes underlying complex data or system dynamics. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000383 ! mathematical analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000986
name: coarse-grained elastic mesoscopic model
def: "A coarse-grained model in which groups of atoms, or whole residues, are represented as beads joined by simple springs. The springs are chosen to reproduce the overall shape and flexibility of the assembly rather than any chemistry, so the model can cover structures far too large to simulate atom by atom. What it can show is how the parts move relative to each other; what it cannot show is anything that depends on a specific chemical group. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000475 ! coarse-grained molecular dynamics

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000987
name: coarse-grained worm-like chain
def: "A coarse-grained model that treats a polymer as a bendable filament described by 2 numbers: its total length, and the distance over which it stays pointing the same way. In a simulation it is built as a chain of beads whose bond and angle terms reproduce those 2 numbers. It is how DNA is modelled when what matters is how it coils and loops rather than which base is where. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000475 ! coarse-grained molecular dynamics

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000988
name: complementary techniques for MD
def: "Experimental or computational methods used alongside Molecular Dynamics (MD) simulations to provide synergistic information, validate simulation accuracy, or compute properties challenging for standard MD alone. These techniques bridge simulation results with real-world measurements or provide deeper thermodynamic or structural insights. They help build a more comprehensive understanding of the molecular system under study." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000304 ! experimental method
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000989
name: nuclear overhauser effect (NOE)
def: "An experimental Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (NMR) phenomenon that arises from the through-space dipolar coupling between nearby nuclear spins (commonly protons), used as a complementary technique to MD. Detecting NOEs allows measurement of short inter-proton distances (typically < 6 Å), providing crucial experimental restraints for determining or validating biomolecular structures and conformational ensembles in solution. MD simulations can be used to predict NOEs for comparison with experiments or refined using experimental NOE data." []
synonym: "NOE" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000988 ! complementary techniques for MD
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:000990 ! small-angle scattering
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:000990
name: small-angle scattering
def: "An experimental technique, either using X-rays (SAXS) or neutrons (SANS), where radiation is scattered by molecules in solution at low angles, providing information complementary to MD simulations. The resulting scattering profile is sensitive to the overall size, shape, and quaternary structure (oligomerization) of the molecules, averaged over the entire ensemble present in the sample. SAS data provides valuable low-resolution structural information that can be used to validate conformational ensembles generated by MD or to guide modeling of large-scale structures. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "SAS" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000988 ! complementary techniques for MD

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001008
name: spectroscopy
def: "Spectroscopy is the study of how matter interacts with energy, particularly electromagnetic radiation like light. By analyzing how energy is absorbed, emitted, or scattered by a substance, we can learn about its atomic and molecular structure, composition, and dynamics. It serves as a fundamental set of tools for observing the properties of molecules." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000304 ! experimental method
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986
property_value: skos:closeMatch CHMO:0000228

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001009
name: vibrational spectroscopy
def: "A spectroscopic technique that probes how the bonds in a molecule stretch, bend and twist, by measuring absorption in the infrared or scattering of visible light. Each vibration has a frequency set by the masses involved and the stiffness of the bond, so the spectrum reports on chemical structure. It is one of the few measurements a simulation can be compared against directly, because a force field predicts exactly those frequencies. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001008 ! spectroscopy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001010
name: infrared spectra
def: "A spectrum recording how strongly a sample absorbs infrared light across a range of frequencies. Absorption occurs where the frequency matches a molecular vibration that changes the molecule's dipole, so the positions of the bands identify chemical groups. It is directly comparable with frequencies computed from a force field or a quantum calculation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001009 ! vibrational spectroscopy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001011
name: raman spectra
def: "A spectrum recording the small shift in frequency of light scattered by a sample, which reveals the vibrations that took or gave energy to the photons. It responds to vibrations that change the molecule's polarizability, which are largely different from those infrared absorption sees. The 2 techniques are therefore complementary rather than alternatives. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001009 ! vibrational spectroscopy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001012
name: pre-resonance raman spectra
def: "A spectrum recorded with the illuminating light tuned close to, but not at, a frequency the sample absorbs. Approaching an absorption greatly enhances the scattering from vibrations connected with it, so a chosen part of a large molecule dominates the spectrum. Staying short of the absorption avoids the sample being heated or damaged. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001009 ! vibrational spectroscopy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001013
name: vibrational circular dichroism
def: "A spectroscopic technique measuring the difference in infrared absorption between left and right circularly polarized light. Only molecules that are not superimposable on their mirror images show such a difference, and the sign of each band reveals which form is present. It reports on 3-dimensional structure in solution, where ordinary infrared absorption reports only on which groups are there. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001009 ! vibrational spectroscopy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001014
name: electronic spectroscopy
def: "A spectroscopic technique that probes transitions of electrons between energy levels, usually driven by ultraviolet or visible light. The energy absorbed or emitted reports on the spacing of those levels, which depends on bonding and conjugation. It is how colour, fluorescence and photochemical behaviour are studied. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001008 ! spectroscopy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001015
name: UV/visible spectra
def: "A spectrum recording how strongly a sample absorbs light across the ultraviolet and visible range, as a function of wavelength. Absorption occurs where the photon energy matches a gap between electronic levels, so the positions of the bands report on bonding and conjugation. It is the measurement a computed electronic transition is compared against. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "UV/Vis" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001014 ! electronic spectroscopy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001016
name: electronic transition band shape
def: "A property giving the full profile of an absorption or emission band in an electronic spectrum, including its width and any structure within it, rather than only where its peak lies. The width reports how much the molecule's geometry changes when it absorbs light, and the structure within it reveals individual vibrations. A calculation matching only the peak position can still be wrong about both. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001014 ! electronic spectroscopy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001017
name: magnetic spectroscopy
def: "A spectroscopic technique that probes the magnetic behaviour of nuclei or unpaired electrons, by observing how they respond in an applied magnetic field. The response depends on the local environment of each spin, which is what makes it report on structure. Nuclear magnetic resonance and electron paramagnetic resonance belong here. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001008 ! spectroscopy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001018
name: antiferromagnetic coupling
def: "An interaction between nearby unpaired electron spins that favours their pointing in opposite directions. The paired arrangement has lower energy than the aligned one, so the system has little or no net magnetism. It occurs between metal centres in many metalloproteins and determines their magnetic signature. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001017 ! magnetic spectroscopy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001019
name: hyperfine coupling tensor
def: "A 3-by-3 array describing how strongly an electron spin interacts with a nearby nuclear spin, and how that strength depends on direction. Its directional part reports where the unpaired electron sits relative to the nucleus. It is what electron paramagnetic resonance spectra are interpreted through. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "hyperfine spectra tensors" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001017 ! magnetic spectroscopy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001020
name: rotational spectroscopy
def: "A spectroscopic technique that probes transitions between a molecule's rotational energy levels, almost always in the gas phase where molecules turn freely. The spacing of the levels depends on how the molecule's mass is distributed, so the spectrum gives bond lengths and angles very precisely. It is among the most accurate structural measurements available and works only for small molecules. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001008 ! spectroscopy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001021
name: vibration-rotation coupling
def: "An interaction between a molecule's vibration and its rotation, arising because a vibrating molecule changes shape and so changes how easily it turns. It means the 2 motions cannot be treated as independent. It shows in a spectrum as a shift in rotational line spacing that depends on which vibrational state the molecule is in. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001020 ! rotational spectroscopy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001022
name: chiroptical spectroscopy
def: "A spectroscopic technique that measures how a sample responds differently to left and right circularly polarized light. Only molecules that are not superimposable on their mirror images give such a difference, so these techniques report on handedness. Optical rotation, circular dichroism and Raman optical activity belong here. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "specialized techniques" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001008 ! spectroscopy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001023
name: raman optical activity
def: "A spectroscopic technique that measures the small difference in scattered light intensity when a chiral sample is illuminated with left and right circularly polarized light. The difference is roughly one part in a thousand, so the measurement is difficult. It is sensitive to the 3-dimensional arrangement of a molecule in solution, which few other techniques report on directly. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001022 ! chiroptical spectroscopy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001024
name: optical rotation
def: "The turning of the plane of polarized light as it passes through a sample of molecules that are not superimposable on their mirror images. The direction and size of the turn depend on which mirror form is present and in what excess. It is how the handedness of a sample is measured, and computing it correctly is a demanding test of a quantum method. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "optical rotations" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001022 ! chiroptical spectroscopy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001032
name: running average calculation analysis
def: "A running average calculation is a statistical analysis technique used to smooth out short-term fluctuations in time-series data and highlight longer-term trends. It is calculated by averaging a property over a sliding time window as the simulation progresses. For simulation experts, monitoring the running average of properties like the total energy or temperature is a standard method for assessing whether a simulation has reached a stable equilibrium. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000400 ! statistical analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001037
name: GROMOS configuration format
def: "A text-based file format used by the GROMOS simulation software to store the complete configuration of a molecular system. It is organized into data blocks (e.g., POSITION, VELOCITY, BOX) and contains atomic coordinates, periodic box dimensions, and optionally velocities. This format typically uses the .cnf file extension and is the primary input for coordinates in GROMOS simulations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "cnf format" EXACT []
synonym: "g96 format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001088 ! molecular structure format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001038
name: MPDyn crd format
def: "A file format for the MPDyn simulation program that stores the atomic coordinates of a molecular system. This format contains the x, y, and z positions for each atom, structured for use with the MPDyn software package. It provides the essential structural input for running simulations with MPDyn. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000921 ! crd format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001039
name: trj format
def: "The .trj format is an ASCII (text-based) trajectory file format used by the Amber molecular dynamics software suite and other analysis programs. Its fundamental purpose is to store a time-series of atomic coordinates, capturing the dynamic motion of a system during a simulation. The file contains sequential \"frames\" where each frame is a complete set of X, Y, and Z coordinates for every atom in the system at a specific point in time. It can also store periodic box dimensions, although this capability is sometimes limited." []
comment: The .trj format belongs to a family of older Amber text-based trajectory formats. Its role is best understood in comparison to its relatives: vs. .mdcrd: The .trj and .mdcrd formats are functionally identical. Both are safe, relatively unambiguous choices for storing Amber ASCII trajectories. A file with one extension can often be renamed to the other without causing issues in analysis software. vs. .crd: The .crd extension is highly ambiguous and problematic. It is the native format for the CHARMM simulation package and is interpreted as such by default in many tools. Using .trj avoids this critical format conflict. vs. .nc (NetCDF): The NetCDF format is the modern, binary, and recommended format for Amber trajectories. Compared to .trj, NetCDF (.nc) files are smaller, faster to read/write, and store data with higher precision. The .trj format is considered a legacy option.
synonym: "AMBER trj format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001090 ! molecular trajectory format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001040
name: distance matrix format
def: "A distance matrix in molecular simulation is a 2D data set that stores the pairwise distances between a selection of particles, such as atoms or residues, calculated from a simulation trajectory. It is a common form of analysis used to study conformational changes, structural stability, and the relative movement of different parts of a molecule." []
comment: Common examples include: - General Text Formats: Often saved as plain text (.txt), comma-separated values (.csv), or a generic data (.dat) file for easy parsing and use in other programs. - Program-Specific Formats: Some simulation packages output the matrix in their own specific formats. For example, GROMACS can generate a distance matrix as an .xpm file, which is a portable pixmap image format. - Binary Formats: For efficiency, especially with large matrices, they may be saved in binary formats like NumPy's .npy format, which is common in Python-based analysis workflows.
is_a: MOLSIM:010020 ! molecular trajectory analysis format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001041
name: XPM format
def: "A text data format that stores a 2-dimensional matrix, such as a distance matrix, an RMSD matrix or a hydrogen bond pattern, by encoding each value as a character standing for a colour. It is a specialised use of the general XPixMap image format, so an ordinary image viewer can open it. GROMACS writes it and converts it to PostScript with gmx xpm2ps. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: ".xpm" EXACT []
synonym: "GROMACS xpm format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001040 ! distance matrix format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001042
name: prmtop format
def: "A text data format that holds the complete static description of a molecular system for an AMBER simulation: its atoms, the bonds between them, the force field parameters that govern their interactions, and their partial charges. It carries everything the simulation engine needs except the coordinates, which come from a separate file. It is read once at the start of a run and does not change during it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "AMBER PARM7 format" EXACT []
synonym: "AMBER parm7 format" EXACT []
synonym: "AMBER parmtop format" EXACT []
synonym: "AMBER prmtop format" EXACT []
synonym: "parm7 format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000472 ! AMBER topology format
property_value: skos:exactMatch format:3881

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001043
name: obsolete parm7 format
def: "OBSOLETE. A file format from the Amber simulation software that describes the structure and force field parameters of a molecule. This is the traditional, ASCII-based version of the Amber parameter/topology file, containing all information needed to calculate forces on the system. It is often used interchangeably with the prmtop format." []
comment: Retired 2026-08-07 as an internal duplicate of MOLSIM:001042 prmtop format. ParmEd writes one Amber topology format under two extensions, .prmtop and .parm7, so these were never two formats. Both terms also carried skos:exactMatch to the same EDAM term, EDAM:format_3881 AMBER top, which is what surfaced the duplication. prmtop survives because it is the name that actually occurs in practice: 19 occurrences against 0 for parm7 in the AMBER keyword corpus this ontology was extracted from. Its names are kept as exact synonyms on MOLSIM:001042.
synonym: "AMBER PARM7 format" EXACT []
synonym: "AMBER parm7 format" EXACT []
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: MOLSIM:001042

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001044
name: CIF format
def: "The Crystallographic Information File (cif) format is a standard text-based file format used to store information about molecular structures, especially those determined by experiments. It uses a flexible tag-based structure with key-value pairs, making it more robust and extensible for handling the large, complex structures and extensive metadata common in modern structural biology. As the official format of the Protein Data Bank (PDB), the macromolecular CIF (mmCIF) variant has superseded the older PDB format for archiving and distributing 3D coordinates of proteins and nucleic acids." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001088 ! molecular structure format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393
property_value: skos:exactMatch format:4024

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001045
name: arc format
def: "A file format used by the TINKER simulation package to store the trajectory of a molecular system. It archives the atomic coordinates from different snapshots of a simulation in a single file for later analysis. This is the standard trajectory output for TINKER simulations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
comment: This can also be a coordinate format from Tinker package as well.
synonym: ".arc" EXACT []
synonym: "TINKER arc format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001090 ! molecular trajectory format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001046
name: original residue number
def: "The original residue number is the number assigned to an amino acid in the original experimental data file. As a type of identifier, it represents the residue number as it appeared in the source file, typically a PDB file, before any renumbering may have occurred during simulation setup. This is crucial for mapping simulation results back to the standard numbering used in publications and other databases, especially when multiple chains or insertions are present." []
comment: The residue number as it appeared in the original input (e.g., PDB) file
synonym: "oresnums" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000447 ! identifier
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001047
name: chain ID
def: "A chain ID is a letter used to label different polymer molecules, like different protein chains, in a structure file. The chain ID usually has a limited number of characters like in the PDB format (1) or in mmCIF and PSF formats (4). It is an essential part of the atom selection syntax in analysis tools, allowing for targeting of specific molecules in a system." []
comment: An identifier used in PDB files to distinguish different polymer chains.
synonym: "chainid" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000447 ! identifier
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393
property_value: skos:closeMatch data:1008

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001048
name: insertion code
def: "An insertion code is a letter used in PDB and mmCIF structure files when extra amino acids have been inserted into a sequence without renumbering every residue after the insertion, thus allowing multiple residues to share the same residue number. This code is critical for unambiguously identifying specific residues in atom selections (e.g. residue \"10A\" is distinct from \"10B\"). This is referred to in PDB files as \"icode\"." []
comment: A character used in PDB files to handle insertions in a sequence.
synonym: "icodes" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000447 ! identifier
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001049
name: rst format
def: "A file format from the Amber software that saves the state of a simulation in plain text, allowing the run to be continued later. It contains the atomic coordinates, velocities, and periodic box dimensions at a specific point in time, in a human-readable form. The same ASCII format is written under several extensions, including .rst, .rst7 and .restrt. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "restrt format" EXACT []
synonym: "rst7 format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000471 ! AMBER restart format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001051 ! ncrst format
property_value: skos:closeMatch format:3886

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001050
name: obsolete rst7 format
def: "OBSOLETE. A text-based file format from the Amber software that saves the state of a simulation. It is the ASCII version of the Amber restart file, containing coordinates, velocities, and box information in a human-readable format. This format is often used for its portability and ease of inspection." []
comment: Retired 2026-08-07 as an internal duplicate of MOLSIM:001049 rst format. ParmEd writes one Amber ASCII coordinate format under several extensions, .rst7, .restrt and .inpcrd, so .rst and .rst7 were never two formats; the real division in this family is ASCII against the binary NetCDF MOLSIM:001051 ncrst format. Both terms also carried skos:closeMatch to the same EDAM term, EDAM:format_3886 RST, which is the pattern that surfaced the duplication. The curator chose rst as the surviving label; note that ParmEd itself does not write a .rst extension, so rst7 format and restrt format are kept as exact synonyms on MOLSIM:001049.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: MOLSIM:001049

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001051
name: ncrst format
def: "A binary file format from the Amber software that saves the complete state of a simulation. It is a NetCDF-based version of the Amber restart file, storing coordinates, velocities, and box vectors with high precision. This is the modern, preferred format for restarting Amber simulations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
comment: A NetCDF-based restart file for Amber simulations.
is_a: MOLSIM:000471 ! AMBER restart format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001052
name: CHARMM crd format
def: "CHARMM commonly uses coordinate files in its own CARD format (.crd), which is a formatted ASCII file including atom coordinates along with atom numbers, residue names/numbers, atom types, and possibly weighting factors. It often starts with a title section describing the system." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000921 ! crd format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001053
name: CHARMM cor format
def: "A file format from the CHARMM simulation software that stores the atomic coordinates of a molecule. It is a binary, unformatted version of the CHARMM coordinate file, making it more compact and faster to read than its text-based counterpart. This format is often used for saving and reading structures within CHARMM workflows. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000921 ! crd format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001054
name: trr trajectory format
def: "A binary file format from the GROMACS software that stores the full-precision trajectory of a simulation. It saves the atomic coordinates, velocities, and forces at each time step without any loss of precision. This format is used instead of XTC format when high accuracy is needed for analysis." []
synonym: "GROMACS trr format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000903 ! GROMACS trajectory format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001055 ! XTC trajectory format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001055
name: XTC trajectory format
def: "A compressed, binary file format from the GROMACS software for storing the trajectory of a molecular simulation. It uses a lossy compression algorithm to store atomic coordinates with reduced precision, resulting in much smaller file sizes. This is the most common trajectory format for GROMACS users when only atomic positions are needed for analysis. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "GROMACS xtc format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000903 ! GROMACS trajectory format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001056
name: TNG trajectory format
def: "A modern, binary file format from the GROMACS software used to store the results of a molecular simulation. It supports various compression algorithms and can store not only coordinates but also velocities, forces, and other trajectory data. This format is designed for high efficiency and flexibility in storing large simulation datasets. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "GROMACS tng format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000903 ! GROMACS trajectory format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001057
name: SQM input format
def: "An input file format for the SQM program, which performs a type of quantum mechanical calculation. It contains keywords and molecular geometry specifications that control the semi-empirical quantum mechanics calculation within the AmberTools suite. This format is typically used for generating atomic charges for new molecules. (UNVERIFIED)" []
comment: An input file format for the semi-empirical QM program SQM.
synonym: ".sqm" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000437 ! simulation input format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001058
name: dtr format
def: "A binary file format used by the Desmond simulation software to store the trajectory of a molecular system. It efficiently stores atomic coordinates, velocities, and other data in a block-based structure. This is the native trajectory output format for simulations run with Desmond. (UNVERIFIED)" []
comment: A trajectory file format used by the Desmond simulation software.
synonym: ".dtr" EXACT []
synonym: "Desmond dtr format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001090 ! molecular trajectory format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001059
name: conflib format
def: "A data format holding the set of conformations found by a low-mode conformational search, each with its energy. It is written as the search proceeds, so the accumulated results survive an interrupted run. It is read back to continue a search or to analyse the conformations found. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: ".conflib" EXACT []
synonym: "LMOD conflib format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001088 ! molecular structure format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001060
name: MDTraj h5 format
def: "A binary data format built on HDF5 in which the MDTraj library stores trajectories together with the topology they belong to. Keeping both in one file removes the usual need to supply a separate topology when reading a trajectory. It is the native format of that library rather than a community standard. (UNVERIFIED)" []
comment: An HDF5-based trajectory file format used by the MDTraj library.
synonym: ".h5" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001090 ! molecular trajectory format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001061
name: H5MD format
def: "A data format for molecular simulation data, defined as a community standard on top of the general-purpose HDF5 container. It specifies where positions, velocities, forces and metadata are placed, so any program following it can read another's output. It belongs to no single simulation program, which is what distinguishes it from the engine-specific formats. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: ".h5md" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001090 ! molecular trajectory format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001062
name: PQR format
def: "The PQR format is a modification of the standard Protein Data Bank (PDB) format used in computational biology to store atomic coordinate data along with atomic partial charges (Q) and radii (R). The name itself is a mnemonic, representing PDB + Q (charge) + R (radius). Its primary advantage is that it bundles the necessary structural and electrostatic parameters into a single, PDB-like file that is easily parsed by both analysis software and molecular visualization programs. These files are most commonly generated by the PDB2PQR software, which processes a standard PDB file, adds missing hydrogen atoms, and assigns atomic charges and radii based on a chosen force field." []
synonym: ".pqr" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001088 ! molecular structure format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071
property_value: skos:exactMatch format:4035

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001063
name: MOE
def: "The Molecular Operating Environment (MOE) is a comprehensive, commercial software system for drug discovery, molecular modeling, and computational chemistry developed by the Chemical Computing Group. It integrates visualization with a vast array of tools for structure preparation, docking, pharmacophore modeling, and molecular dynamics setup within a single unified interface." []
synonym: "Molecular Operating Environment" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000490 ! structure preparation tool
is_a: MOLSIM:002041 ! molecular structure visualization tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001064
name: TIP3PFW
def: "A water model with 3 sites whose bonds and angle can stretch and bend rather than being held rigid. Flexibility is needed when vibrational spectra are being computed, or when the model is combined with a method that cannot handle constraints. It forces a shorter timestep, because bond vibrations are the fastest motion in the system. (UNVERIFIED)" []
comment: A flexible three-site water model.
is_a: MOLSIM:000014 ! water model force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001065
name: SPCFW
def: "A water model with 3 sites, derived from the SPC geometry, whose bonds and angle can stretch and bend. Its bonded parameters were refitted alongside the flexibility so that the liquid's density and diffusion stay correct. Making a rigid model flexible without refitting changes both. (UNVERIFIED)" []
comment: A flexible three-site water model.
is_a: MOLSIM:000014 ! water model force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001066
name: ptraj format
def: "An output option of the secstruct command in cpptraj that writes secondary structure data as plain text laid out the way the older ptraj program wrote it. It is a formatting choice rather than a file type, so it fixes no file extension; the output goes to whatever filename the out directive gives. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "CPPTRAJ ptraj format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:010020 ! molecular trajectory analysis format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001067
name: xmgrace
def: "Xmgrace is a computer program used to make scientific graphs and plots from data. As a type of visualization tool, Xmgrace is a 2D plotting program for X Window Systems. Some simulation analysis tools, like GROMACS and cpptraj, can directly generate output files in a compatible format for easy plotting of time-series data like RMSD or energy. This tool is associated with file formats like .agr and .xvg." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002042 ! data plotting tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001068 ! gnuplot
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001068
name: gnuplot
def: "A visualization tool that draws 2-dimensional and 3-dimensional graphs from data files, driven from the command line or from a script. Because it is scriptable it can be called from an analysis pipeline to produce figures without a person present. It is one of the standard ways simulation output is plotted. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002042 ! data plotting tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001069
name: visual molecular dynamics
def: "A visualization program for displaying and animating molecular structures and trajectories in 3 dimensions. It handles systems of millions of atoms and includes a scripting language, so analyses can be run on what is being shown. It is the program most molecular dynamics trajectories are looked at in. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "VMD" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:002041 ! molecular structure visualization tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001070
name: NMWiz
def: "A visualization plugin for VMD that draws and animates collective modes of motion from normal mode analysis or principal component analysis. It shows a mode as arrows on the structure, or as a trajectory moving along it. It turns an eigenvector into something that can be looked at. (UNVERIFIED)" []
comment: A VMD plugin for visualizing and analyzing normal modes.
is_a: MOLSIM:002041 ! molecular structure visualization tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001071
name: traj3d format
def: "A data format that records a 3-dimensional histogram as though it were the path of a single particle, writing the 3 histogram dimensions as the x, y and z coordinates of 1 atom over successive frames. That trick lets a volumetric distribution, such as where water sits around a solute, be opened in a molecular viewer as a point cloud. It is produced by the hist command of cpptraj. (UNVERIFIED)" []
comment: The traj3d "pseudo-trajectory" is not a standard, independent file format but rather a specialized output option available within the hist command in Amber's cpptraj analysis program. It is created by taking the three data dimensions of a 3D histogram and writing them out as the X, Y, and Z coordinates of a single "atom" over time. This reformatting creates a trajectory-like file that can be loaded into molecular visualization software. The purpose is to allow researchers to visually inspect the 3D distribution of data from the histogram in a more intuitive, interactive 3D space, rather than as a static 2D plot. There is no mandatory file extension for the output file itself.
synonym: "CPPTRAJ traj3d format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001090 ! molecular trajectory format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001072
name: obsolete information content entity
def: "OBSOLETE. An information content entity is an abstract concept representing any piece of data, information, or knowledge that can be identified and described. In the context of simulations, it refers to the abstract data itself, such as the concept of a molecular structure or a simulation parameter set, separate from the specific file format used to store it. This distinction helps in organizing and standardizing the description of simulation data and metadata." []
comment: Retired 2026-08-12 when MOLSIM adopted COB as its upper level. IAO:0000030 information content entity is one of COB's five roots and says the same thing, so keeping a MOLSIM class beside it was a duplicate. Its 8 direct children were re-parented onto IAO:0000030 in the same change; the 46 terms below them moved with their parents.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: IAO:0000030

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001073
name: molecular system specification
def: "A molecular system specification defines the physical and chemical properties of a molecule required for computational chemistry and quantum mechanical simulations. This specification is the complete informational blueprint of the system before any simulation is performed." []
is_a: IAO:0000030 ! information content entity
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001074 ! process specification
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001074
name: process specification
def: "A process specification is the abstract set of instructions and parameters that define how a computational task, like a simulation or an analysis, should be performed. It represents the complete plan for the process, including the choice of algorithms, control settings, and input files. This specification must be recorded to ensure a computational experiment is reproducible." []
is_a: IAO:0000030 ! information content entity
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001075
name: process output
def: "An output file is generated by a computational program and contains the results of the calculation or simulation, along with logs, progress information, and any error messages. These files are crucial for analyzing the outcome of computational jobs." []
is_a: IAO:0000030 ! information content entity
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001076
name: molecular topology
def: "The description of what a molecular system is made of: its atoms, their types and charges, the bonds between them, and the force field parameters that apply. It does not change during a simulation, which is why it is kept separately from the coordinates. Without it, a set of coordinates is just a list of numbers. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001073 ! molecular system specification

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001077
name: CHARMM topology format
def: "A category of data formats used by the CHARMM simulation package to describe the molecular topology of a system. These formats define the atoms, connectivity, and the chemical nature of residues. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001091 ! molecular topology format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001078
name: rtf format
def: "A data format used by CHARMM that defines a reusable template for one chemical building block, such as an amino acid or a nucleotide. It gives the atoms in that block, their types and charges, the bonds between them, and their standard geometry. A topology for a whole molecule is assembled by joining these templates in sequence. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "residue topology file (RTF) format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001091 ! molecular topology format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001079
name: frcmod format
def: "A text data format used by AMBER to supply force field parameters that are missing from the main parameter files, or to override ones that are present. It lets a user add parameters for a non-standard molecule without editing the distributed force field. It is read in addition to the main files rather than in place of them. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "AMBER frcmod format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:002066 ! force field parameter format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001080
name: simulation parameter set
def: "The complete collection of settings that tells a program how to run one simulation, including the temperature and pressure to hold, how long to run, how often to save, and which physical approximations to use. It is normally kept as a single input file. Together with the starting structure it is what would be needed to repeat the run exactly. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001074 ! process specification

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001081
name: simulation trajectory
def: "A simulation trajectory is the record of a molecule's motion over time, captured during a simulation. It consists of a time-ordered sequence of snapshots or \"frames\" where each frame contains the 3D coordinates of all atoms at a specific instant. This trajectory is the primary output of a molecular dynamics simulation and is the raw data used for all subsequent analysis of the system's dynamic behavior." []
synonym: "trajectory" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001075 ! process output
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001082 ! simulation log
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001082
name: simulation log
def: "A simulation log is a text file that records everything that happened during a computer simulation. As a type of process output, the simulation log is a human-readable file that contains a time-ordered record of a simulation run, including an echo of input parameters, performance data, and periodic updates of thermodynamic properties. This file is the primary source for monitoring the progress and stability of a simulation and for diagnosing errors." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001075 ! process output
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001083
name: simulation state
def: "The complete set of information needed to resume a simulation exactly where it stopped. It includes the atomic positions and velocities, the box dimensions, and the internal variables of any thermostat or barostat. Restarting from positions alone gives a different trajectory, because the missing quantities are re-initialised. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001075 ! process output

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001084
name: analysis data
def: "Analysis data is the information content that is the result of analyzing simulation data. This includes any derived quantities calculated from a trajectory, such as RMSD values over time, a potential of mean force profile, or a list of identified hydrogen bonds. This processed data represents the scientific findings extracted from the simulation." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001075 ! process output
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001085
name: molecular data format
def: "A category for file formats designed to store information about molecules, such as their structure, movement, or the forces governing them. These formats provide standardized ways to represent molecular systems for use in computational chemistry and biology software. This class includes formats for atomic coordinates, trajectories, and force field parameters." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000436 ! data format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001086
name: prep (internal) format
def: "A prep format in which the geometry of the new building block is given as internal coordinates, being bond lengths, angles and rotations relative to atoms already placed. It is otherwise identical to the variant that uses Cartesian coordinates. Writing the geometry this way makes the connection tree explicit, which is what the residue linking rules are read from. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "AMBER prep (internal) format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001091 ! molecular topology format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001087
name: obsolete macromolecular structure format
def: "OBSOLETE. A file format specifically designed to describe the complex, three-dimensional structures of large biological molecules like proteins and DNA. These formats accommodate hierarchical descriptions, such as chains and residues, in addition to atomic coordinates. Examples include the widely used PDB and mmCIF formats." []
comment: Retired in the file-format flattening. Classifying structure formats by molecule size was an artificial distinction: a small molecule can be stored in a PDB file and a macromolecule in a mol2 file. Its former children are now direct children of 'molecular structure format' (MOLSIM:001088). Reported in GitHub issue #20.
is_obsolete: true

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001088
name: molecular structure format
def: "A type of file format that describes the three-dimensional arrangement of atoms in a molecule. These formats store atomic coordinates and often include information about chemical bonds and residue identity. They are essential for visualizing molecules and providing the starting point for simulations." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001085 ! molecular data format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001089
name: obsolete software-specific coordinate format
def: "OBSOLETE. A coordinate file primarily stores the three-dimensional positions (X, Y, Z coordinates) of atoms in a molecular system. It may also contain atom names, residue information, and potentially periodic box dimensions, but typically lacks detailed bonding (topology) or force field parameter information. Common examples include PDB, GRO, and XYZ formats, used for initial structures or snapshots from simulations." []
comment: Retired in the same file-format flattening. Grouping coordinate formats by the software that writes them proved unhelpful, since formats are not owned by one program. Its former children are now direct children of 'molecular structure format' (MOLSIM:001088). Related discussion in GitHub issue #20.
is_obsolete: true

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001090
name: molecular trajectory format
def: "A trajectory file stores the history of atomic positions (and sometimes velocities, forces, energies or the simulation box size) recorded at regular intervals during a molecular dynamics simulation. It contains a series of snapshots (or frames) representing the system's movement over time. Analyzing trajectories allows researchers to study dynamic processes, conformational changes, and calculate time-averaged properties." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001085 ! molecular data format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001091
name: molecular topology format
def: "A file format that defines the atoms of a molecular system, how they are bonded together, and the force field parameters that apply to them. This includes atom types, partial charges, and parameters for bonds, angles, dihedral angles, and non-bonded interactions (like Lennard-Jones parameters). It essentially provides the 'rules' for how atoms interact in a molecular mechanics simulation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001085 ! molecular data format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001092
name: prep (cartesian) format
def: "A prep format in which the geometry of the new building block is given as Cartesian coordinates, being 3 numbers per atom. It is otherwise identical to the variant that uses internal coordinates. Writing the geometry this way is easier to generate from an existing structure. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "AMBER prep (cartesian) format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001091 ! molecular topology format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001093
name: CHARMM par format
def: "A text data format used by CHARMM that holds the numerical force field parameters: force constants, preferred bond lengths and angles, rotation terms and van der Waals values. It is paired with a separate file defining the residues those parameters apply to. The 2 together are what a CHARMM topology is built from. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "CHARMM parameter format" EXACT []
synonym: "par format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:002066 ! force field parameter format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001094
name: GAUSSIAN coordinate format
def: "A data format that specifies the 3-dimensional arrangement of atoms inside a Gaussian input file, either as Cartesian x, y and z coordinates or as a Z-matrix of bond lengths, angles and dihedral angles. The Z-matrix form is chosen when internal coordinates or molecular symmetry need to be held fixed; the Cartesian form is simpler and more common. Both appear in the same place in the input file. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001088 ! molecular structure format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001095
name: GAUSSIAN z-matrix format
def: "A data format specifying a molecule's geometry inside a Gaussian input file as bond lengths, angles and rotations relative to atoms already placed. It is chosen when a geometry must be scanned or constrained, because one number can be varied or frozen directly. It is harder to write than plain coordinates and is not used unless that control is wanted. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001088 ! molecular structure format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001096
name: GAUSSIAN cartesian format
def: "A data format specifying a molecule's geometry inside a Gaussian input file as an element symbol and 3 coordinates per atom. It is the simpler of the 2 ways Gaussian accepts a geometry and the one nearly always used. Coordinates in this form are easy to generate and carry no information about which internal degrees of freedom matter. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001088 ! molecular structure format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001097
name: job control format
def: "A text data format holding the settings for a parameter fitting run: which parameters are to be fitted, which reference data to fit against, and how the fit is to be carried out. It is the file the fitting program reads to know what job it is doing. It is specific to that program. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000437 ! simulation input format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001098
name: ReaxFF force field format
def: "A text data format holding the parameters for a reactive force field, which are far more numerous than a conventional force field needs because bonding is computed rather than fixed. A single file covers every element combination the parameter set supports. Parameters for different element sets are not interchangeable, so the file identifies what can be simulated. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002066 ! force field parameter format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001099
name: DFTB parameter format
def: "A data format, held in files known as Slater-Koster files, that stores the pre-calculated electronic and repulsive properties between pairs of atom types for a density functional tight binding calculation. The values are derived once from more expensive quantum mechanical calculations and then reused. That reuse is what makes the method fast while keeping a quantum mechanical description of the system. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "skf format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:002066 ! force field parameter format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001100
name: cuttable bond list format
def: "A text data format listing which bonds a setup program may break when dividing a molecule into smaller pieces. Such a division is needed when parameters are derived fragment by fragment, and the cuts must fall where the chemistry allows. Listing them explicitly stops the program cutting through a group whose parameters must stay whole. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000437 ! simulation input format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001101
name: reservoir cluster info file format
def: "A file format that provides settings for a specialized type of simulation designed to enhance the sampling of molecular motions. It specifies dihedral angle definitions that are used for applying a non-Boltzmann reservoir weighting in enhanced sampling simulations. This format is used as input for advanced simulation techniques that target specific conformational changes. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000437 ! simulation input format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001102
name: EMIL input format
def: "A simulation parameter format that holds the control settings for an EMIL absolute free energy calculation in AMBER, conventionally in a file named emilParameters.in. It records the reference model parameters and the integration settings that the calculation needs. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "emilParameters.in format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:002065 ! simulation parameter format
property_value: IAO:0000119 "Berryman J.T. Absolute free energies for biomolecules in implicit or explicit solvent. Physics Procedia, 2014. States that the AMBER implementation of this method is called EMIL." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000119 "Berryman J.T. and Schilling T. Free energies by thermodynamic integration relative to an exact solution, used to find the handedness-switching salt concentration for DNA. J. Chem. Theory Comput. 9(1):679-686, 2013." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001103
name: cein format
def: "The cein format is a specialized input file used in constant redox-potential MD simulations. It defines the properties of residues that can exist in different oxidation states, such as a cysteine that can be oxidized or reduced. This file provides the necessary parameters for a constant redox potential simulation, allowing the system to dynamically change its electronic state in response to a defined electrochemical potential." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002065 ! simulation parameter format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001104
name: cpein format
def: "The cpein format is a complex input file for constant pH and electrochemical potential (CpH/E) MD simulations that simultaneously model changes in both protonation and electron-transfer states. It defines the properties of residues that can be affected by both the surrounding pH and the electrochemical potential. This format is required when studying complex bioenergetic processes where proton and electron transfers are coupled." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002065 ! simulation parameter format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001105
name: component cif
def: "A data file, in Crystallographic Information File format, that defines 1 chemical building block found in larger structures, giving its atom names, element types, bonds, charges and ideal geometry. It acts as a dictionary entry that deposited structures refer to rather than repeat. It is how a ligand or a modified residue is described once and reused. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001088 ! molecular structure format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001106
name: solvent analysis data format
def: "A data format that stores the results of analysing how solvent molecules are arranged and behave around a solute. Files in these formats typically hold values on a 3-dimensional grid, such as the chance of finding a solvent atom at a point or the average interaction energy there. Examples include solvent density maps and the correlation functions produced by 3D-RISM theory. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:010021 ! solvent analysis format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001107 ! solvent pair distribution format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001107
name: solvent pair distribution format
def: "A data format that stores a 3-dimensional grid giving the chance of finding a solvent molecule at each position around a solute, relative to a random distribution. The value at each point is the pair distribution function g(r): above 1 means the solvent gathers there, below 1 means it is pushed away. Peaks in the grid mark solvation shells and hydrogen bonding sites. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:010021 ! solvent analysis format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001108
name: solvent direct correlation format
def: "A data format that stores a 3-dimensional grid of the direct correlation function c(r) between a solute and the surrounding solvent. It isolates the solute's direct influence on a solvent molecule at each position, leaving out effects passed along through other solvent molecules. It is a basic quantity in liquid-state theories such as 3D-RISM and is used to derive thermodynamic properties of solvation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:010021 ! solvent analysis format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001109
name: solvent total correlation format
def: "A data format that stores a 3-dimensional grid of the total correlation function h(r) between a solute and the surrounding solvent. It gives the whole departure from a random solvent distribution caused by the solute, counting both direct and indirect effects, and it relates to the pair distribution function as h(r) = g(r) − 1. It is used in liquid-state theories to calculate solvation properties. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:010021 ! solvent analysis format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001110
name: solvent potential file format
def: "This file format stores a 3D map of the potential energy experienced by the solvent molecules in the space surrounding a central solute. The value at each grid point represents the average potential energy of the solvent at that location, reflecting the combined interactions with the solute and other solvent molecules. This format provides a view of the energetic landscape of the solvent, which can be used to identify energetically favorable or unfavorable regions for solvation." []
is_a: MOLSIM:010021 ! solvent analysis format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001111
name: solvent charge density distribution format
def: "A data format that stores a 3-dimensional grid of the average electric charge density contributed by solvent molecules around a solute. Unlike a map of where solvent atoms sit, it gives the net positive or negative charge at each point, averaged over the simulation. It shows how the solvent screens and responds to the solute's own charges. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:010021 ! solvent analysis format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001112
name: solvent charge distribution format
def: "A data format that stores a 3-dimensional grid giving, separately for each kind of partial charge a solvent molecule carries, the chance of finding that charge at each position around a solute. It differs from a charge density map by keeping the positive and negative sites apart rather than summing them. That separation is what reveals preferred hydrogen bonding geometries and ion solvation sites. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:010021 ! solvent analysis format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001113
name: solute-solvent potential energy format
def: "A data format that stores a 3-dimensional grid of the interaction energy a solvent molecule would feel at each position around a solute. Negative values mark positions the solvent is drawn to and positive values mark positions it is pushed away from. The grid shows the energetic landscape that determines how solvent arranges itself. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:010021 ! solvent analysis format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001114
name: site-site functionals format
def: "A data file format used in advanced solvent analysis to describe how the interaction between different types of atoms changes with distance. It stores the mathematical functions, known as pair functionals, that are the core components of integral equation theories like the 3D Reference Interaction Site Model (3D-RISM). These files contain the pre-calculated correlation functions for a pure solvent, which are then used by the 3D-RISM method to determine the solvent structure around a solute molecule. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:010022 ! quantum chemistry format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001115
name: total excess coordination number format
def: "A data format that stores the average number of extra solvent molecules gathered around a solvent molecule, above what the bulk liquid would give. It measures how strongly the solvent structures itself in the solution. It is produced by 1-dimensional RISM calculations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:010021 ! solvent analysis format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001116
name: total excess charge format
def: "A data format that stores how much extra electric charge from the solvent gathers around each type of solvent atom. It measures the net charge separation the solute induces in the solvent. It is produced by 3-dimensional RISM calculations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:010021 ! solvent analysis format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001117
name: GAUSSIAN electrostatic potential format
def: "A data format in which Gaussian writes the electrostatic potential it computed at a set of points around a molecule, together with those points' coordinates. It is the input a charge fitting program reads. The choice of where the points lie affects the charges obtained, so it is part of the fitting protocol rather than an incidental detail. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:010022 ! quantum chemistry format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001118
name: mdinfo format
def: "The mdinfo format is a text file generated by the Amber simulation software that provides a concise, real-time summary of a running simulation. It contains the most recently calculated energy terms and thermodynamic properties, such as temperature and pressure, formatted for easy monitoring. This file is continuously updated during a run, making it useful for checking the immediate status and stability of a simulation without having to parse the much larger main output file." []
synonym: "AMBER mdinfo format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000439 ! simulation log format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001119
name: database web server
def: "A database web server is an online application that provides a graphical interface for searching, visualizing, and retrieving data from a structured repository. It acts as an accessible gateway, allowing researchers to query complex datasets and download specific entries without needing direct interaction with the underlying database management system." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001671 ! web server
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001120
name: NEF format
def: "A standard text-based file format designed for exchanging NMR-derived information, particularly structural restraints like distances and angles. It provides a standardized way to represent experimental data used for structure calculation and simulation refinement. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "NMR exchange format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000440 ! NMR data format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001163
name: parameter
def: "An input variable or algorithmic setting defined prior to execution that governs the behavior, conditions, or numerical rules of a computational process (encompassing both simulation generation and post-run analysis). (UNVERIFIED)" []

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001164
name: simulation parameter
def: "An input setting that determines the physical interactions, boundary conditions or integration rules used to generate a trajectory. Examples are the target temperature a thermostat holds, the size of the timestep, and the distance beyond which interactions are ignored. These settings are part of what a result means, so a simulation cannot be reproduced or judged without them. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001163 ! parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001165
name: integration parameter
def: "A simulation parameter controlling how the equations of motion are advanced in time, including the timestep, the integration algorithm and how long the run lasts. The timestep is the most consequential: too large and the simulation becomes unstable, too small and it wastes time. Most of what makes a run stable or unstable is set here. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001164 ! simulation parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001166
name: simulation time step
def: "A type of integration parameter that specifies the discrete interval of time between successive steps in a molecular dynamics simulation. The choice of simulation time step is a critical balance between computational efficiency and numerical stability, as it must be short enough to capture the fastest atomic motions. This is commonly specified in input files with the keyword dt. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001165 ! integration parameter
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000003 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label time unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001167
name: simulation duration
def: "A type of integration parameter that specifies the total length of time the simulation is run. This determines how much conformational space can be explored and the timescale of the phenomena that can be observed. The simulation duration is typically set by specifying the total number of steps, nsteps, in the input file. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001165 ! integration parameter
property_value: skos:exactMatch SBO:0000585

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001168
name: simulation time per stage
def: "A specific type of simulation duration that defines the length of a single stage within a multi-stage simulation protocol. This is used in methods like steered MD or umbrella sampling but also during density adaptation and equilibration workflows, where the overall process is broken down into smaller, sequential runs. The simulation time per stage ensures that each part of the protocol is run for a defined period. This is often specified as nsteps within a block for a specific stage." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001167 ! simulation duration
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001169
name: minimization convergence criteria
def: "An integration parameter giving the conditions under which an energy minimization stops. The usual conditions are that the largest force on any atom has fallen below a threshold, or that the energy has stopped changing between steps. A minimization that stops too early leaves strain in the structure that the first simulation steps then release violently. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001165 ! integration parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001170
name: minimization drms criterion
def: "A specific minimization convergence criteria based on the root-mean-square of the gradient, which represents the forces on the atoms. The minimization will stop when the RMS of the forces falls below this specified threshold. This is a common way to define convergence and is often set with the keyword drms. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001169 ! minimization convergence criteria
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 434, entry drms." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001171
name: minimization gradient tolerance
def: "A specific minimization convergence criteria that sets the root-mean-square gradient threshold for terminating an energy minimization run. The minimization is considered converged when the RMS of the forces on the atoms is less than this gradient tolerance. This is a key parameter for controlling the strictness of the geometry optimization, often set with grms_tol. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001169 ! minimization convergence criteria

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001172
name: thermodynamic ensemble parameter
def: "A simulation parameter that fixes which quantities are held constant during a run, and so which statistical ensemble is sampled. Holding particle number, volume and temperature gives one ensemble; holding pressure instead of volume gives another. The choice determines which averages taken from the trajectory are meaningful. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001164 ! simulation parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001173
name: temperature control parameter
def: "A thermodynamic ensemble parameter specifying how the temperature is held at its target, covering the thermostat algorithm, the target value and the coupling strength. A thermostat both holds the temperature and changes the dynamics, so these settings affect more than the average temperature. They must be reported with any result that depends on rates. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001172 ! thermodynamic ensemble parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001174
name: thermostat algorithm parameter
def: "A temperature control parameter naming which algorithm holds the temperature, such as Berendsen, Nosé-Hoover or stochastic velocity rescaling. They differ in whether they produce the correct spread of energies or only the correct average. The Berendsen scheme does not, which is why it is used to bring a system to temperature and then replaced. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001173 ! temperature control parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001175
name: target temperature
def: "A temperature control parameter that specifies the desired temperature for the simulation. The thermostat algorithm will adjust the kinetic energy of the atoms to keep the average temperature fluctuating around this target temperature. This is a fundamental parameter for any simulation and is often set with the keyword temp0. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001173 ! temperature control parameter
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000005 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label temperature unit
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 436, entry temp0." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001176
name: thermostat coupling parameter
def: "A temperature control parameter setting how strongly the system is coupled to the simulated heat bath. Strong coupling holds the temperature close to target and interferes with the natural motion; weak coupling leaves the dynamics alone and lets the temperature wander. Any quantity involving rates depends on this choice. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001173 ! temperature control parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001177
name: thermostat coupling constant
def: "A thermostat coupling parameter giving the time over which a temperature difference is corrected. A short value corrects aggressively and damps the real motion of the system; a long value is gentle and slow to reach the target. It is the form the coupling strength takes in the Berendsen and Nosé-Hoover thermostats. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001176 ! thermostat coupling parameter
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 436, entry tautp." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001178
name: thermostat collision frequency
def: "A thermostat coupling parameter giving how often, on average, a particle receives a random kick from the simulated bath in a stochastic thermostat. A high frequency reaches the target temperature quickly and turns the motion into a random walk; a low one preserves the real dynamics and controls temperature weakly. It is the stochastic counterpart of a coupling time constant. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001176 ! thermostat coupling parameter
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 216, entry gamma_ln." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001179
name: pressure control parameter
def: "A thermodynamic ensemble parameter specifying how the pressure is held at its target, covering the barostat algorithm, the target value, the coupling strength and the compressibility. Pressure fluctuates so strongly in a small system that these settings determine how the volume behaves more than the target does. They apply only to constant-pressure runs. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001172 ! thermodynamic ensemble parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001180
name: barostat algorithm parameter
def: "A pressure control parameter naming which algorithm holds the pressure at its target, such as Berendsen, Parrinello-Rahman or a Monte Carlo scheme. They differ in whether they generate the correct distribution of volumes or merely the correct average. The Berendsen scheme equilibrates quickly and does not give the correct distribution, which is why it is used to settle a system and then replaced. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001179 ! pressure control parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001181
name: target pressure
def: "A pressure control parameter that specifies the desired pressure for the simulation. The barostat algorithm will adjust the volume of the simulation box to keep the average pressure fluctuating around this target pressure. This is a fundamental parameter for any constant pressure simulation and is often set with the keyword pres0. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001179 ! pressure control parameter
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 438, entry pres0." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001182
name: barostat coupling constant
def: "A pressure control parameter giving how quickly the box volume responds to a difference between the current and target pressure. A small value corrects pressure aggressively and makes the volume oscillate; a large one is gentle and slow to settle. Pressure in a small system fluctuates enormously, so this must be slow enough to average over those fluctuations rather than chase them. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001179 ! pressure control parameter
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 438, entry taup." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001183
name: compressibility
def: "A pressure control parameter giving how much the system's volume changes for a given change in pressure. Some barostats need it to work out how far to scale the box when correcting pressure. The value used is that of the solvent, because the solvent is nearly all of the volume. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001179 ! pressure control parameter
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 438, entry comp." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001184
name: interaction parameter
def: "A simulation parameter controlling how interactions between atoms are computed, covering the cutoff distances, the long-range electrostatic method and the treatment at the cutoff. These settings determine how much of each interaction is actually included. They affect both cost and correctness, which is why they are reported with any published simulation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001164 ! simulation parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001185
name: non-bonded interaction parameter
def: "An interaction parameter controlling how van der Waals and short-range electrostatic interactions are computed, covering the cutoff distance, the treatment at that cutoff, and the neighbour list settings. These settings decide how much of the interaction is included and what happens at the boundary. They are among the few settings that affect both speed and correctness directly. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001184 ! interaction parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001186
name: non-bonded method parameter
def: "A non-bonded interaction parameter naming how interactions are handled at the cutoff distance, such as truncating them sharply or smoothly switching them to zero over a range. A sharp truncation makes the force jump at the cutoff, which adds energy to the system every time a pair crosses it. The choice therefore affects whether energy is conserved. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001185 ! non-bonded interaction parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001187
name: non-bonded cutoff distance
def: "A non-bonded interaction parameter that specifies the single distance beyond which both van der Waals and electrostatic interactions are no longer calculated directly. Using one distance for both is the common case, and it is the main way to reduce the cost of a simulation. Programs that allow the two to be set separately use a more specific parameter for each. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001185 ! non-bonded interaction parameter
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000001 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label length unit
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 456, entry cut." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 467, card CUT, which names this quantity the non-bonded cutoff distance." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000119 "NAMD 3.x User's Guide, p. 55, section 5.2.3, entry cutoff. States that the cutoff is the local interaction distance common to both electrostatic and van der Waals calculations." xsd:string
property_value: MOLSIM:002254 "cut" xsd:string {dcterms:source="MOLSIM:000217"}

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001188
name: switching distance
def: "A non-bonded interaction parameter giving the distance at which a smoothing function starts bringing the interaction energy down to zero at the cutoff. Without it the energy jumps as a pair crosses the cutoff, which adds energy to the system each time. The gap between this distance and the cutoff sets how gentle that transition is. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001185 ! non-bonded interaction parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001189
name: pairlist update frequency
def: "A non-bonded interaction parameter giving how many steps pass between rebuilds of the neighbour list. Rebuilding often is safe and costly; rebuilding rarely is cheap and risks missing a pair that has moved into range. It is chosen together with the pairlist skin, since a thicker skin allows a longer interval. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001185 ! non-bonded interaction parameter
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 456, entry nsnb." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001190
name: pairlist skin
def: "A non-bonded interaction parameter giving the extra distance beyond the cutoff within which pairs of atoms are recorded in the neighbour list. Including pairs that are not yet interacting means the list stays valid for several steps as atoms move, so it need not be rebuilt every step. Too small a value lets a pair reach interaction range unnoticed, which silently loses interactions. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001185 ! non-bonded interaction parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001191
name: electrostatic parameter
def: "An interaction parameter controlling how electrostatic interactions are computed. Its members cover which long-range method is used and the settings that method needs, such as grid spacing and real-space cutoff. These settings determine accuracy and cost together, so they are chosen as a set rather than individually. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001184 ! interaction parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001192
name: long-range electrostatic method parameter
def: "An electrostatic parameter naming which algorithm computes the long-range electrostatic interactions, such as particle mesh Ewald, plain Ewald summation, or a reaction field. Electrostatic forces fall off slowly enough that simply ignoring them past a cutoff introduces visible artefacts. The choice of method is therefore part of what a published simulation must state. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001191 ! electrostatic parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001193
name: PME grid spacing
def: "An electrostatic parameter giving how far apart the points of the reciprocal-space grid lie in a particle mesh Ewald calculation. A finer grid is more accurate and costs more, and the cost rises with the cube of the refinement. It trades off against the real-space cutoff, so the 2 should be chosen together rather than separately. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001191 ! electrostatic parameter
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 500, entry fft_grids_per_ang." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001194
name: PME grid dimensions
def: "An electrostatic parameter used by the Particle Mesh Ewald (PME) method that specifies the number of grid points in each dimension for the reciprocal space calculation. Larger PME grid dimensions result in a more accurate calculation but are computationally more expensive. These are often set automatically based on the grid spacing, but can be specified directly with keywords like nfft1, nfft2, and nfft3. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001191 ! electrostatic parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001195
name: dielectric constant
def: "An electrostatic parameter giving how strongly a medium screens the electrostatic interaction between charges within it. It is 1 in vacuum and in explicit solvent simulations, where the water molecules do the screening themselves, and is raised in implicit solvent models to stand in for solvent that is not present. It scales every Coulomb interaction in the calculation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001191 ! electrostatic parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001196
name: internal dielectric constant
def: "A dielectric constant that describes the interior of the solute in a continuum solvation calculation. It is set low, usually between 1 and 4, because the packed interior of a molecule screens charge poorly. Its value is one of the largest sources of variation between published binding free energy estimates. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001195 ! dielectric constant
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 82, entry epsin." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 952, entry indi." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001197
name: external dielectric constant
def: "A dielectric constant that describes the bulk solvent surrounding a solute in a continuum solvation calculation. It is set high, near 80 for water, so that the solvent screens electrostatic interactions strongly. Together with the internal value it fixes the dielectric boundary at the molecular surface. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001195 ! dielectric constant
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 82, entry epsout." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 952, entry exdi." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001198
name: direct sum cutoff
def: "An electrostatic parameter giving the distance at which the directly summed part of an Ewald calculation stops. Raising it moves work out of the reciprocal-space part and into the real-space part, and lowering it does the reverse. The total accuracy depends on this and the grid spacing together, which is why changing one alone usually makes results worse. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001191 ! electrostatic parameter
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 499, entry es_cutoff." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001199
name: external field parameter
def: "An interaction parameter giving the strength, direction and time dependence of a field applied to the system from outside. It is what specifies an applied electric field in a simulation of ion transport or of a membrane under voltage. Without it the field has no defined magnitude. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001184 ! interaction parameter
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 457, entry efx." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001200
name: external electric field component
def: "A specific external field parameter that defines the magnitude of an applied external electric field along a particular axis. This is used to simulate the effect of a uniform electric field on the molecular system. The external electric field component is often specified for each axis, such as efx, efy, and efz. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001199 ! external field parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001201
name: constraint and restraint parameter
def: "A type of simulation parameter that controls the application of geometric constraints or restraints to the system. Constraints are used to fix certain degrees of freedom, while restraints are used to guide the system towards a particular conformation. These constraint and restraint parameter settings are used to control the flexibility of the system or to apply experimental data." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001164 ! simulation parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001202
name: constraint parameter
def: "A parameter controlling how geometric constraints are applied, most often to hold bonds involving hydrogen at a fixed length. Fixing those bonds removes the fastest motion in the system, which is what permits a timestep 2 to 4 times longer. Its members say which bonds are held, by which algorithm, and how exactly. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001201 ! constraint and restraint parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001203
name: constraint algorithm parameter
def: "A constraint parameter naming which algorithm enforces the geometric constraints, such as SHAKE, RATTLE, LINCS or SETTLE. The choice affects speed and how well the constraints are held, not what is being constrained. SETTLE is used for water specifically, because water's constraints have an exact solution that needs no iteration. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001202 ! constraint parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001204
name: constrained bond
def: "A constraint parameter naming which bonds are held at a fixed length, usually as a choice between all bonds, only those involving hydrogen, or none. Constraining hydrogen bonds is near universal, because it costs almost nothing in accuracy and permits a longer timestep. Constraining all bonds permits a longer step still and does begin to affect the results. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "constrained bonds" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001202 ! constraint parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001205
name: SHAKE tolerance
def: "A constraint parameter giving how close to its target length a constrained bond must be before the algorithm stops adjusting it. A tighter value holds the geometry more exactly and takes more iterations each step. Too loose a value lets energy drift over a long run, which is the usual sign it was set badly. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001202 ! constraint parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001206
name: restraint parameter
def: "A type of constraint and restraint parameter that specifies how artificial restraining potentials are applied to the system. These are used to guide the simulation towards a specific conformation. The restraint parameter settings are essential for biased simulations and structure refinement. These are often set with keywords like restraint_wt and restraintmask." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001201 ! constraint and restraint parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001207
name: restraint energy constant
def: "A restraint parameter that specifies the force constant for a harmonic or other restraining potential. A larger restraint energy constant results in a stronger force pulling the restrained atoms towards their target values. This is a key parameter for controlling the strength of the applied restraints. This is often set with the keyword restraint_wt." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001206 ! restraint parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 433, entry restraint_wt." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001208
name: restraint mask
def: "A restraint parameter that names which atoms a restraining force applies to, written as a selection expression rather than a list. It is what lets part of a system be held in place while the rest moves freely, such as holding a protein still while water settles around it. A mask that selects the wrong atoms produces a simulation that runs normally and means something else. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001206 ! restraint parameter
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 433, entry restraintmask." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001209
name: water cap force constant
def: "A specific restraint energy constant used to apply a restraining potential to a spherical cap of water molecules around a solute. This is used in some simulation setups to prevent the solute from becoming exposed to the vacuum. The water cap force constant controls the strength of this spherical boundary potential. This is often set with the keyword fcap." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001206 ! restraint parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 454, entry fcap." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001210
name: system setup parameter
def: "A simulation parameter that fixes what the system is made of and what state it is in, rather than how it is advanced in time. Examples are the size and shape of the box, the water model, and the number of ions added. These are chosen once while the system is built and do not change while it runs. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001164 ! simulation parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001211
name: pH
def: "A system setup parameter giving the acidity of the simulated solution. It determines which acidic and basic groups carry a proton, and so the charge on the molecule. In an ordinary simulation it is used once to assign fixed protonation states; in a constant pH simulation it is held during the run and the states respond to it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001210 ! system setup parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001212
name: ionic strength
def: "A system setup parameter that specifies the molar concentration of salt in the simulation solvent. The ionic strength affects the screening of electrostatic interactions and is crucial for mimicking experimental buffer conditions. This is a key parameter for accurately modeling the electrostatic environment of the system. This is often set with the keyword ion_concentration or saltcon." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001210 ! system setup parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 73, entry saltcon." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 984, entry ion_concentration." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001213
name: periodic box dimensions
def: "A system setup parameter that specifies the size and shape of the periodic box used to create a periodic system. The periodic box dimensions are essential for any simulation using periodic boundary conditions. They determine the overall density of the system." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001210 ! system setup parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001214
name: molecular termini state
def: "A system setup parameter giving the chemical state of each end of a polymer chain: charged, neutral, or capped with a group that mimics the continuation of the chain. Capping is used when the simulated fragment is part of a longer chain in reality, so that an artificial charge is not introduced. A wrong choice adds or removes charge at exactly the place a fragment is most exposed. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001210 ! system setup parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001215
name: alchemical transformation state
def: "A system setup parameter that specifies whether the simulation involves an alchemical transformation for a free energy calculation. This parameter indicates that some atoms/residues in the system have their properties changed over the course of the simulation. The alchemical transformation state is a key descriptor for identifying free energy calculations. This is often controlled by a perturbation flag (lambda, λ)." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001210 ! system setup parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001216
name: number of replicates
def: "A simulation process parameter that specifies the number of independent simulation runs performed from the same or similar initial conditions. Running number of replicates helps to assess the statistical robustness and convergence of simulation results. This is a key parameter of the overall simulation experimental design." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001210 ! system setup parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001217
name: surface tension
def: "A system setup parameter giving the target surface tension for a constant-pressure simulation containing an interface. It is used for membranes and liquid surfaces, where holding pressure alone leaves the area of the interface undetermined. Setting it to zero lets a membrane find its own area, which is usually what is wanted. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001210 ! system setup parameter
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 439, entry gamma_ten." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001218
name: number of QM/MM partitions
def: "A system setup parameter giving how many separate quantum regions an adaptive calculation maintains. Several are used when reacting groups sit far apart and would otherwise force one very large quantum region. Each brings its own boundary, so adding one adds another place the 2 descriptions must be joined. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001210 ! system setup parameter
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 211, entry n_partition." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001219
name: enhanced sampling parameter
def: "A type of simulation parameter that controls the application of a specific enhanced sampling method designed to accelerate the exploration of the system's conformational space. These parameters define the nature and strength of the biasing potential or other modifications to the standard simulation protocol." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001164 ! simulation parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001220
name: steered molecular dynamics parameter
def: "A type of enhanced sampling parameter that controls a steered molecular dynamics (sMD) simulation, where an external force is applied to pull the system along a specific coordinate. These parameters define the pulling speed, force constant, and direction of the steering. The steered molecular dynamics parameter settings are essential for setting up non-equilibrium pulling simulations. These are often set with keywords like smd." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001219 ! enhanced sampling parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001221
name: atom pulling velocity
def: "A steered molecular dynamics parameter that specifies the constant speed at which the steered coordinate is changed during a constant-velocity sMD simulation. The atom pulling velocity determines the rate at which the system is pulled in agreement with the selected reaction coordinate. This is often set with the keyword v." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001220 ! steered molecular dynamics parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001222
name: steered MD restraint energy constant
def: "A steered molecular dynamics parameter that specifies the stiffness of the harmonic potential used to pull the system along the reaction coordinate. A larger steered MD restraint energy constant results in a stiffer spring and less deviation from the target path. This is a key parameter for controlling the strength of the steering. This is often set with the keyword harm." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001220 ! steered molecular dynamics parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 610, entry harm." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001223
name: number of sMD stages
def: "A steered molecular dynamics parameter that specifies the total number of distinct stages or windows used in a staged sMD simulation protocol. This allows for the pulling to occur incrementally or for parameters to be changed between stages. The number of sMD stages is a key parameter for setting up complex pulling protocols. This is often set with the keyword nstage." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001220 ! steered molecular dynamics parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001224
name: umbrella sampling parameter
def: "A type of enhanced sampling parameter that controls an umbrella sampling simulation, where a biasing potential is used to confine the system to specific windows along a reaction coordinate. These parameters define the location and strength of the biasing potential in each window. The umbrella sampling parameter settings are essential for setting up simulations to calculate a potential of mean force. These are often set in the input file for each window." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001219 ! enhanced sampling parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001225
name: umbrella sampling restraint energy constant
def: "An umbrella sampling parameter that specifies the strength of the harmonic biasing potential applied in each umbrella sampling window. This force constant determines how strongly the system is restrained around the target value of the reaction coordinate for that window. The umbrella sampling restraint energy constant is a key parameter for ensuring sufficient sampling within each window. This is often set with the keyword anchor_strength." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001224 ! umbrella sampling parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001226
name: number of umbrella sampling windows
def: "An umbrella sampling parameter that specifies the total number of individual simulations (windows) performed in an umbrella sampling workflow. Each window is typically centered at a different value along the reaction coordinate. The number of umbrella sampling windows is a key parameter for ensuring adequate coverage of the entire reaction coordinate." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001224 ! umbrella sampling parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001227
name: umbrella anchor position
def: "An umbrella sampling parameter that determines the center or boundaries of the harmonic potential for a specific umbrella sampling window. This parameter defines the region of the reaction coordinate that will be sampled in that window. The umbrella anchor position is a key parameter that is varied between different windows. This is often set with the keyword anchor_position." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001224 ! umbrella sampling parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001228
name: accelerated MD parameter
def: "A type of enhanced sampling parameter that controls an accelerated molecular dynamics (aMD) simulation. These parameters define the energy threshold and strength of the boost potential that is applied to flatten the energy landscape. The accelerated MD parameter settings are crucial for controlling the degree of enhanced sampling. These are often set in a specific amd section of the input file." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001219 ! enhanced sampling parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001229
name: aMD dihedral energy threshold
def: "An accelerated MD parameter that specifies the energy threshold for the dihedral energy, below which the biased potential is applied. This parameter controls when the dihedral energy term is biased. The aMD dihedral energy threshold is a key parameter for tuning the aMD simulation. This is often set with the keyword EthreshD." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001228 ! accelerated MD parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001230
name: aMD dihedral alpha factor
def: "A scaling parameter used to flatten high potential energy barriers, allowing the simulation to explore conformational space much faster. It dictates the magnitude of the bias applied to the system's dihedral degrees of freedom. A smaller aMD dihedral alpha factor results in a larger boost. This is a key parameter for tuning the aMD simulation. This is often set with the keyword alphaD." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001228 ! accelerated MD parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001231
name: aMD potential energy threshold
def: "An accelerated MD parameter that specifies the energy threshold for the total potential energy, below which the biased potential is applied. This parameter controls when the total potential energy is biased. The aMD potential energy threshold is a key parameter for tuning the aMD simulation. This is often set with the keyword EthreshP." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001228 ! accelerated MD parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001232
name: aMD potential alpha factor
def: "An accelerated MD parameter that determines the strength of the biased potential applied to the total potential energy term. A smaller aMD potential alpha factor results in a larger boost. This is a key parameter for tuning the aMD simulation. This is often set with the keyword alphaP." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001228 ! accelerated MD parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001233
name: Gaussian accelerated MD parameter
def: "A type of enhanced sampling parameter that controls a Gaussian accelerated molecular dynamics (GaMD) simulation. These parameters define the upper limit of the standard deviation for the potential energy boost. The Gaussian accelerated MD parameter settings are crucial for controlling the balance between accuracy and enhanced sampling. These are often set in a specific gamd section of the input file." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001219 ! enhanced sampling parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001234
name: GaMD potential boost stddev limit
def: "A Gaussian accelerated MD parameter that specifies the upper limit of the standard deviation for the potential energy boost. This parameter controls the maximum strength of the applied bias. This is often set with keywords like sigma0P or sigma0D." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001233 ! Gaussian accelerated MD parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 526, entry sigma0D." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 526, entry sigma0P." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001235
name: random acceleration MD parameter
def: "A type of enhanced sampling parameter that controls a random acceleration molecular dynamics (RAMD) simulation. These parameters define the strength of the randomly applied acceleration force. The random acceleration MD parameter settings are crucial for enhancing the exploration of conformational space. These are often set in a specific ramd section of the input file." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001219 ! enhanced sampling parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001236
name: RAMD boost strength
def: "A random acceleration MD parameter that specifies the strength of the acceleration boost applied in a Random Acceleration Molecular Dynamics (RAMD) simulation. This parameter controls the magnitude of the random forces used to accelerate the system's exploration. The RAMD boost strength is a key parameter for tuning the RAMD simulation. This is often set with the keyword ramdboost." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001235 ! random acceleration MD parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 458, entry ramdboost." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001237
name: targeted MD parameter
def: "A type of enhanced sampling parameter that controls a targeted molecular dynamics (TMD) simulation. These parameters define the target structure and the strength of the biasing potential used to guide the simulation towards it. The targeted MD parameter settings are essential for simulating large-scale conformational transitions between known start and end states. These are often set in a specific tmd section of the input file." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001219 ! enhanced sampling parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001238
name: targeted MD force constant
def: "A targeted MD parameter that specifies the force constant for the RMSD restraint potential used to guide the simulation towards the target structure. A larger targeted MD force constant results in a stronger biasing force. This is a key parameter for controlling the strength of the targeted MD simulation. This is often set with the keyword tgtmdfrc." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001237 ! targeted MD parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 532, entry tgtmdfrc." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001239
name: targeted MD RMSD target
def: "A targeted MD parameter that specifies the target root-mean-square deviation (RMSD) value for the restraint. The simulation is guided to reduce the RMSD of the current structure relative to a reference structure to this targeted MD RMSD target value. This is a key parameter for defining the endpoint of the TMD simulation. This is often set with the keyword tgtrmsd." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001237 ! targeted MD parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 532, entry tgtrmsd." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001240
name: nudged elastic band parameter
def: "A type of enhanced sampling parameter that controls a nudged elastic band (NEB) simulation, which is used to find the minimum energy path between two conformations. These parameters define the number of intermediate structures (images) and the spring constants connecting them. The nudged elastic band parameter settings are essential for accurately mapping reaction pathways. These are often set in a specific neb section of the input file." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001219 ! enhanced sampling parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001241
name: NEB spring constant
def: "A nudged elastic band parameter that specifies the spring force constant connecting adjacent images along the reaction path. This parameter ensures that the images are evenly spaced and do not drift off the path. The NEB spring constant is a key parameter for the stability and convergence of the NEB calculation. This is often set with the keyword nebk." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001240 ! nudged elastic band parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 550, entry nebk." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001242
name: NEB number of images
def: "A nudged elastic band parameter that specifies the number of intermediate structures (images) to optimize along the reaction path. A larger NEB number of images provides a more detailed representation of the path but is computationally more expensive. This is a key parameter for controlling the resolution of the NEB calculation. This is often set with the keyword neb_nimage." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001240 ! nudged elastic band parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 550, entry neb_nimage." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001243
name: well-tempered metadynamics parameter
def: "A type of enhanced sampling parameter that controls a well-tempered metadynamics simulation. These parameters define how the height of the added Gaussian hills is rescaled over time, ensuring that the simulation eventually converges. The well-tempered metadynamics parameter settings are crucial for obtaining converged free energy surfaces. These are often set in a specific metadynamics section of the input file." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001219 ! enhanced sampling parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001244
name: well-tempered pseudo-temperature
def: "A well-tempered metadynamics parameter that controls the rate at which the height of the added Gaussian hills decreases. A higher well-tempered pseudo-temperature results in a faster convergence but a less detailed exploration of the energy landscape. This is a key parameter for tuning the well-tempered metadynamics simulation. This is often set with the keyword wt_temperature." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001243 ! well-tempered metadynamics parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 613, entry wt_temperature." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001245
name: QM/MM parameter
def: "A simulation parameter that controls a calculation in which part of the system is treated with quantum mechanics and the rest with a force field. Its members set which atoms are in the quantum region, which quantum method is used, and how bonds crossing the boundary are handled. The boundary treatment is the setting most likely to make a result wrong rather than merely imprecise. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001164 ! simulation parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001246
name: QM charge
def: "A QM/MM parameter giving the total charge of the quantum region as a whole number. The quantum calculation needs a definite number of electrons, so this cannot be left to be worked out. Setting it wrong gives a calculation that runs to completion and describes a different chemical species. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001245 ! QM/MM parameter
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 159, entry qmcharge." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001247
name: QM/MM link atom distance
def: "A QM/MM parameter giving how far the completing atom is placed from the quantum atom it is attached to. It is set so the resulting bond has a realistic length for the pair of elements involved. Too short or too long a value distorts the electronic structure right at the boundary, which is usually where the chemistry of interest is. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001245 ! QM/MM parameter
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 175, entry lnk_dis." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001248
name: QM/MM non-bonded cutoff
def: "A QM/MM parameter giving the distance beyond which interactions between the quantum region and the classical region are not evaluated. Every classical atom inside it enters the quantum calculation as a charge, so the value controls both cost and accuracy directly. It is usually set larger than the ordinary non-bonded cutoff. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001245 ! QM/MM parameter
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 172, entry qmcut." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001249
name: DFTB parameter
def: "A QM/MM parameter controlling a density functional tight binding calculation, covering which parameter files are used, how many charge iterations are allowed and how tightly they must converge. The parameter files are specific to each pair of elements, so a system containing an unparameterised pair cannot be run. Checking that first saves discovering it at run time. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001245 ! QM/MM parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001250
name: DFTB max iterations
def: "A parameter giving the greatest number of self-consistent charge iterations a tight binding calculation may take. It stops a calculation that will not converge from running indefinitely. Reaching the limit means the charges are not converged and the result must not be used. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001249 ! DFTB parameter
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 159, entry dftb_maxiter." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001251
name: DFTB electronic temperature
def: "A parameter that spreads electrons smoothly across orbitals near the highest occupied level, as though the electrons were at a raised temperature. The smoothing stops the occupation jumping between iterations, which is what prevents convergence in systems with closely spaced levels. It is a numerical device, and too large a value distorts the result. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001249 ! DFTB parameter
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 159, entry dftb_telec." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001252
name: SCF parameter
def: "A parameter controlling the iterative procedure that solves for a molecule's electrons, covering how close successive iterations must agree, how many are allowed, and which acceleration scheme is applied. A calculation that does not converge produces no result at all, so these decide whether it finishes. They are adjusted when a difficult system fails rather than set routinely. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001245 ! QM/MM parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001253
name: max SCF iterations
def: "A parameter giving the greatest number of iterations a self-consistent field calculation may take before it stops. It exists so that a calculation which will never converge does not run indefinitely. Reaching the limit means the result is not converged and must not be used, however reasonable it looks. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001252 ! SCF parameter
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 161, entry itrmax." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001254
name: SCF convergence criteria
def: "A parameter giving how little the energy or the electron density must change between iterations for a self-consistent field calculation to be considered finished. A tighter value gives a more accurate result and takes more iterations. Forces need a tighter setting than energies, because they are more sensitive to a partly converged density. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001252 ! SCF parameter
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 160, entry scfconv." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001255
name: SCF damping factor
def: "A parameter giving how much of the previous iteration's electron density is mixed into the next one. Mixing slows the calculation down and stops it oscillating between 2 near-solutions. It is raised when a difficult system will not converge and lowered otherwise, because it costs iterations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001252 ! SCF parameter
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 479, entry damp." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001256
name: DIIS parameter
def: "A self-consistent field parameter that controls the direct inversion in the iterative subspace procedure, which speeds up convergence by extrapolating from previous iterations. The values set how many previous iterations are kept and how many extrapolation attempts are made. Poor settings make a calculation converge slowly or oscillate without settling. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001252 ! SCF parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001257
name: DIIS attempts
def: "A DIIS parameter giving how many extrapolation attempts the convergence accelerator makes. Raising it makes the accelerator act more aggressively, which usually converges faster and occasionally oscillates instead. It is one of the first settings changed when a calculation fails to converge. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001256 ! DIIS parameter
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 162, entry ndiis_attempts." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001258
name: number of DIIS matrices
def: "A DIIS parameter giving how many previous error vectors the convergence accelerator keeps and extrapolates from. It sets the size of the subspace used, so a larger value uses more history and more memory. Too few gives a poor extrapolation and too many can include iterations no longer relevant. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "DIIS matrices" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001256 ! DIIS parameter
property_value: MOLSIM:002254 "ndiis_matrices" xsd:string {dcterms:source="MOLSIM:000217"}

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001259
name: constant pH parameter
def: "A simulation parameter controlling a constant pH run, covering how often protonation changes are attempted, how long the system is allowed to relax after one, and at what pH the simulation is held. These settings determine whether the protonation states are sampled properly or barely move. They are specific to this kind of simulation and appear nowhere else. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001164 ! simulation parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001260
name: CpHMD state change attempt frequency
def: "A constant pH parameter giving how many simulation steps pass between attempts to change a residue's protonation state. Attempting more often samples the protonation states better and costs more, because each attempt requires extra calculation. Attempting too rarely leaves a residue stuck in one state for most of the run. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001259 ! constant pH parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001261
name: number of CpHMD solvent relaxation steps
def: "A constant pH parameter that specifies the number of solvent relaxation steps performed after a protonation state change. Those steps let the solvent reorient around the residue that has just been charged or neutralised. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "CpHMD solvent relaxation steps" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001259 ! constant pH parameter
property_value: MOLSIM:002254 "ntrelax" xsd:string {dcterms:source="MOLSIM:000217"}

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001262
name: polarizable force field parameter
def: "A simulation parameter controlling a run with a polarizable force field, covering how the induced dipoles are solved for and how tightly they must converge. A loose convergence makes the forces slightly inconsistent with the energy, which shows as energy drift. These settings do not arise at all with a fixed-charge force field. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001164 ! simulation parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001263
name: induced dipole convergence criterion
def: "A polarizable force field parameter giving how little the induced dipoles must change between iterations before they are accepted. A tighter value gives forces closer to the exact ones and costs more iterations each step. Too loose a value makes the forces slightly inconsistent with the energy, which shows up as energy drift. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001262 ! polarizable force field parameter
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 465, entry dipole_scf_tol." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001264
name: analysis parameter
def: "An input setting that determines the mathematical, statistical or filtering rules applied when existing simulation data is processed. Examples are the distance below which 2 structures count as similar, the size of a block in an error estimate, and the spacing of an analysis grid. The same trajectory analysed with different settings gives different numbers, so they are part of the result. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001163 ! parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001265
name: clustering parameter
def: "A type of analysis parameter that controls a clustering algorithm used to group similar molecular conformations from a trajectory. These parameters define the distance metric, the cutoff for cluster membership, and the number of clusters to be generated. The clustering parameter settings are crucial for identifying the dominant conformational states sampled in a simulation." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001264 ! analysis parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001266
name: clustering distance cutoff
def: "A clustering parameter that specifies the distance threshold for grouping conformations into the same cluster. Two structures with a distance (e.g., RMSD) less than the clustering distance cutoff are considered to be in the same cluster. This is a key parameter for defining the granularity of the clustering. This is often set with the keyword epsilon or cutoff." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001265 ! clustering parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001267
name: number of clusters to generate
def: "A clustering parameter giving how many groups the algorithm should produce. Algorithms such as k-means require it in advance, so it is chosen either from prior knowledge or by trying several values and comparing a quality measure. Choosing it badly either merges distinct conformations or splits one into several. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001265 ! clustering parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001268
name: volumetric analysis parameter
def: "An analysis parameter that controls how a 3-dimensional grid of values is produced, such as a density or an electrostatic potential map. Its members set where the grid sits, how far apart its points are and what is computed at each. Spacing chosen too coarsely hides features; chosen too finely it produces files too large to handle. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001264 ! analysis parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001269
name: grid spacing
def: "A volumetric analysis parameter giving the distance between neighbouring points of a 3-dimensional grid. A finer grid resolves smaller features and produces a file whose size grows with the cube of the refinement. Too coarse a grid hides exactly the ordered water sites such an analysis is usually looking for. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001268 ! volumetric analysis parameter
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 138, entry grdspc." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001270
name: grid function
def: "A volumetric analysis parameter naming which quantity is computed at each point of a 3-dimensional grid, such as a density, an interaction energy or a correlation function. The choice determines what the resulting map shows. The available choices depend on the analysis program. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001268 ! volumetric analysis parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001271
name: number of grid points
def: "A volumetric analysis parameter that specifies the number of points in each dimension of a three-dimensional grid. It controls the size and the resolution of the volumetric data. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "grid points" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001268 ! volumetric analysis parameter
property_value: MOLSIM:002254 "--ng" xsd:string {dcterms:source="MOLSIM:000217"}

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001272
name: statistical analysis parameter
def: "An analysis parameter controlling a statistical calculation, such as the confidence level, the number of resampling trials or the block size. These settings determine what an error bar means, so a value quoted without them cannot be interpreted. They are part of the result rather than an implementation detail. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001264 ! analysis parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001273
name: p-value threshold
def: "A statistical analysis parameter giving the value below which a result is called significant. It is the share of the time a real effect would be claimed when none exists, so setting it at 0.05 accepts being wrong 1 time in 20. It must be chosen before the data are examined, or it means nothing. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001272 ! statistical analysis parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001274
name: confidence level
def: "A statistical analysis parameter giving how often an interval computed this way would contain the true value, if the whole procedure were repeated many times. A level of 95% means 19 such intervals in 20 would contain it. It does not mean there is a 95% chance the true value lies in the particular interval computed. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001272 ! statistical analysis parameter
property_value: skos:closeMatch STATO:0000561

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001275
name: number of bootstrap replications
def: "A statistical analysis parameter giving how many times the data are resampled in a bootstrap estimate. More resamples make the estimate of the uncertainty itself more stable, at a cost that is simply proportional. It does not make the underlying data more informative, which is the mistake this setting invites. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001272 ! statistical analysis parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001276
name: kernel density bandwidth
def: "A statistical analysis parameter giving the width of the smooth bumps placed on each data point in a kernel density estimate. Too narrow a width shows every random fluctuation as a peak; too wide a one merges genuinely separate peaks into one. It is the single most consequential choice in such an estimate. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001272 ! statistical analysis parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001277
name: free energy analysis parameter
def: "An analysis parameter that controls how a free energy is calculated from simulation data. The group covers settings for end-point methods, for thermodynamic integration and for the analysis of umbrella sampling. Its members determine whether an estimate converges, so they must be recorded with the result. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001264 ! analysis parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001278
name: MM-PBSA/GBSA parameter
def: "A free energy analysis parameter that controls a molecular mechanics Poisson-Boltzmann or generalized Born surface area calculation. Its members set the continuum solvent model and the surface area treatment. They are the settings that make 2 published binding free energies for the same system disagree. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001277 ! free energy analysis parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001279
name: membrane dielectric constant
def: "A dielectric constant that describes an implicit membrane slab in a continuum solvation calculation. It is set low to represent the non-polar lipid core, which screens charge about as poorly as a protein interior. It is what makes burying a charge in the membrane region cost energy in the model. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001278 ! MM-PBSA/GBSA parameter
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 953, entry emem." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001280
name: probe radius
def: "A parameter giving the radius of the sphere rolled over a molecule's van der Waals surface to define its solvent-accessible surface area. It is normally set to 1.4 ångström, the effective radius of a water molecule. It controls how far into clefts the solvent is considered to reach, and so it changes the non-polar part of the solvation free energy. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001278 ! MM-PBSA/GBSA parameter
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 952, entry prbrad." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001281
name: cavity offset
def: "A parameter giving the constant term added to the surface-area estimate of the non-polar solvation free energy. It absorbs the part of that energy which does not scale with area. It is fitted together with the surface tension coefficient and the 2 should not be taken from different sources. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001278 ! MM-PBSA/GBSA parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001282
name: cavity surface tension
def: "A parameter giving the coefficient that converts solvent-accessible surface area into non-polar solvation free energy. It plays the part surface tension plays for a macroscopic interface, though it is fitted to small-molecule data rather than measured. It is fitted together with the cavity offset. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001278 ! MM-PBSA/GBSA parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001283
name: thermodynamic integration parameter
def: "A free energy analysis parameter that controls a thermodynamic integration calculation. Its members set how many intermediate coupling states are used and how they are spaced along the path. Too few or badly spaced states leave the integral under-sampled where the energy changes fastest. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001277 ! free energy analysis parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001284
name: number of lambda windows
def: "A thermodynamic integration parameter giving how many intermediate coupling states are simulated along the transformation path. More windows make the numerical integration more accurate and the calculation proportionally more expensive. Too few leaves the integrand under-sampled where it changes fastest, which is usually near the end points. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001283 ! thermodynamic integration parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001285
name: umbrella sampling analysis parameter
def: "A type of free energy analysis parameter that controls the analysis of umbrella sampling simulations to generate a potential of mean force. These parameters define the settings for the histogramming and reweighting procedure. The umbrella sampling analysis parameter settings are crucial for correctly combining the data from multiple windows. These are often set in the input file for a WHAM or MBAR analysis program." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001277 ! free energy analysis parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001286
name: potential of mean force convergence step size
def: "An umbrella sampling analysis parameter that specifies the increment or step size used when assessing the convergence of the calculated Potential of Mean Force (PMF). The PMF is calculated using progressively larger amounts of data to check for convergence. The potential of mean force convergence step size is a key parameter for ensuring that the calculated free energy profile is reliable. This is a key parameter for WHAM analysis." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001285 ! umbrella sampling analysis parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001287
name: 3D-RISM parameter
def: "A parameter controlling a 3D-RISM calculation, covering the grid on which the solvent distribution is computed, the closure relation used, and how tightly the solution must converge. The closure choice changes the answer, not merely its precision. These settings must be reported for a solvation free energy from this method to be interpretable. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001277 ! free energy analysis parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001288
name: 3D-RISM convergence tolerance
def: "A 3D-RISM parameter giving how little the solution must change between iterations before the calculation is declared finished. A tighter value gives a more accurate solvent distribution and needs more iterations. Too loose a value returns a result that looks complete and is still drifting. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001287 ! 3D-RISM parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001289
name: solute-solvent interaction cutoff
def: "A parameter giving the distance beyond which solute-solvent interactions are not evaluated in a 3D-RISM calculation. Raising it improves accuracy and raises cost, because the number of grid points grows with the cube of the distance. It is one of the main controls on how long such a calculation takes. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001287 ! 3D-RISM parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001290
name: NMR analysis parameter
def: "A type of analysis parameter that controls the analysis of simulation data to generate properties that can be compared with Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (NMR) experiments. These parameters define the settings for calculating NMR-related observables from a trajectory. The NMR analysis parameter settings are crucial for validating simulations against experimental data. These are often set in the input file for an NMR analysis program." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001264 ! analysis parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001291
name: R6 averaged distance
def: "An NMR analysis parameter that specifies a particular form of distance averaging used in NMR structure calculation and refinement. This method involves averaging the inverse sixth power of the distance between two atoms, which is directly related to the Nuclear Overhauser Effect (NOE) intensity. The <r⁻⁶>⁻¹/⁶ averaged distance is a key parameter for back-calculating NOEs from a simulation trajectory. This is often referred to as R6 averaging." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001290 ! NMR analysis parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001292
name: computed observable
def: "A quantitative or qualitative output data item generated by a simulation or analysis process. It represents the actual measured state, derived metric, or calculated result of the system (e.g., instantaneous potential energy, calculated RMSD, assigned cluster IDs). (UNVERIFIED)" []

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001293
name: thermodynamic property
def: "A property describing the macroscopic thermodynamic state of a system, whose value depends only on that state and not on how the system reached it. In simulation it is obtained as an average over sampled configurations rather than from a single one. Energy, entropy and free energy are its members. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001292 ! computed observable

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001294
name: energy
def: "A thermodynamic property giving the total energy of a system, computed from the positions and velocities of its atoms using the force field. It is reported at intervals through a run and is the first quantity checked when something is suspected to be wrong. Its components are reported separately, because a fault usually shows in one of them rather than in the total. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001293 ! thermodynamic property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001295
name: potential energy
def: "A component of a system's energy that depends only on where the atoms are, not on how fast they are moving. It is computed from the force field, summing the bonded terms with the electrostatic and van der Waals interactions. Its gradient is the force on each atom, which is what drives the simulation forward. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001294 ! energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001296
name: total potential energy
def: "A potential energy summing every bonded and non-bonded contribution for one configuration of the system. It is reported at intervals during a run and is the first thing checked when a simulation is suspected of going wrong. A steady drift in it means the integration is unstable or a setting is inconsistent. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001295 ! potential energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001297
name: electrostatic energy
def: "A component of the potential energy arising from the Coulomb interaction between the partial charges on the atoms. It falls off slowly with distance, so it reaches much further than the other non-bonded term and needs special treatment in a periodic system. It is what makes polarity, solvation and ionic binding come out right or wrong. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001294 ! energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001298
name: 1-4 electrostatic energy
def: "A component of the electrostatic energy covering only pairs of atoms separated by exactly 3 bonds. Such pairs are close enough that the plain Coulomb term would double-count what the torsion term already describes, so force fields scale it down by a fixed factor. The factor differs between force fields, which is one reason their parameters cannot be mixed. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001297 ! electrostatic energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001299
name: Van der Waals energy
def: "A component of the potential energy covering the short-range interaction between atoms not bonded to each other: a steep repulsion when they approach too closely and a weaker attraction at slightly greater distance. The repulsion is what gives atoms an effective size. The attraction is what makes non-polar molecules condense into liquids at all. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001294 ! energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001300
name: 1-4 Van der Waals energy
def: "A component of the van der Waals energy covering only pairs of atoms separated by exactly 3 bonds. Such pairs are close enough that the full interaction would double-count what the rotation term already describes, so force fields scale it down. The scaling factor differs between force fields, which is one reason their parameters cannot be mixed. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001299 ! Van der Waals energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001301
name: angle energy
def: "A component of the potential energy stored in the bending of the angle between 3 bonded atoms away from its preferred value. It is softer than the bond stretching term, so angles deform more readily than bond lengths. It is what keeps a carbon centre roughly tetrahedral without any explicit rule saying so. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001294 ! energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001302
name: Urey-Bradley energy
def: "A component of the angle energy that adds a spring directly between the 2 outer atoms of a bonded triple, in addition to the angle term itself. It corrects the coupling between bending an angle and stretching the bonds around it, which the angle term alone cannot represent. It is used by the CHARMM force fields and not by most others. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001301 ! angle energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001303
name: dihedral energy
def: "A component of the potential energy associated with rotation about a bond, defined by 4 atoms in sequence and repeating as the rotation goes round. It is what makes some rotational positions preferred over others, which sets the shapes a molecule can adopt. It is the term most often refitted when a force field is improved, because conformational preferences depend on it most. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001294 ! energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001304
name: improper torsion energy
def: "A component of the potential energy that holds a group of 4 atoms flat, or holds a centre in one of its 2 mirror forms. Unlike an ordinary torsion it is defined over atoms that are not in a chain, and it has a single preferred value rather than repeating. Without it a planar group such as an aromatic ring or an amide would slowly pucker. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001294 ! energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001305
name: dispersion energy
def: "A component of the potential energy arising from momentary fluctuations in an atom's electron cloud inducing matching fluctuations in its neighbours. It is always attractive and falls off rapidly with distance, so only near neighbours contribute. It is weak between any 2 atoms and dominant in large non-polar molecules simply because there are so many pairs. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001294 ! energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001306
name: polarization energy
def: "A component of the potential energy arising from a molecule's electron cloud being distorted by the electric field of its surroundings. A force field with fixed atomic charges cannot represent it and absorbs its average effect into those charges instead. Representing it explicitly is what distinguishes a polarizable force field and what makes it several times more expensive. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001294 ! energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001307
name: restraint energy
def: "A component of the reported energy arising from artificial forces added to hold atoms near chosen positions or values. It measures how hard the restraint is pulling, so it says how far the system is straining against what was imposed on it. It is not part of the system's physical energy and must be excluded from any thermodynamic quantity. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001294 ! energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001308
name: QM energy
def: "A component of the reported energy computed quantum mechanically for one region of a system. It appears only in calculations where part of the system is treated that way and the rest with a force field. It cannot be compared with a force field energy, because the 2 are measured from different zero points. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001294 ! energy
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000111 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label energy unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001309
name: SCF energy
def: "A quantum mechanical energy giving the electronic energy of a region once the iterative solution has converged. It is the energy of the best single-configuration description of the electrons, before any correlation correction is added. It is the baseline that post-Hartree-Fock methods improve on. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001308 ! QM energy
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000111 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label energy unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001310
name: boost energy
def: "A component of the system's energy that represents an artificial (non negative) energy term added to the potential to accelerate sampling in enhanced sampling simulations. This non-physical energy helps the system overcome high energy barriers more quickly. It is reported in the log files of methods like Accelerated MD as E_boost or amd_boost." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001294 ! energy
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001311
name: accelerated MD boost energy
def: "Accelerated Molecular Dynamics (aMD or GaMD) is a powerful enhanced sampling technique designed to speed up conformational transitions in biomolecular simulations. It works by applying a harmonic boost potential to the system's true potential energy surface whenever it drops below a predefined threshold. The accelerated MD boost energy is the key quantity used to reweight the biased trajectory to recover correct thermodynamic properties. It is often reported in log files as amd_boost." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001310 ! boost energy
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001312
name: 10-12 H-bond energy
def: "A special potential term used in some older force fields to explicitly model hydrogen bonds. It is calculated using a 10-12 Lennard-Jones-like function between donor and acceptor atoms. This term is not commonly used in modern force fields but may be found in older simulation outputs. It is often reported as HBOND in energy summaries when such a potential is used." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001294 ! energy
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001313
name: locally enhanced sampling energy
def: "A component of the reported energy contributed by the several non-interacting copies of a region that a locally enhanced sampling simulation contains. Because the copies do not see each other, their energies are summed rather than being the energy of a real system. The term exists only in this kind of simulation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001294 ! energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001314
name: free energy property
def: "A thermodynamic property combining energy and entropy into the quantity that determines which way a process goes at fixed temperature. It is the amount of work obtainable from the system under those conditions. Because it contains entropy it cannot be read off a single structure, only from an ensemble. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001293 ! thermodynamic property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001315
name: binding free energy
def: "A free energy giving the change on taking 2 molecules from separate, solvated states to a bound complex. It is the quantity that determines binding affinity, so it is what a docking or free energy calculation is usually trying to predict. It is negative when binding is favourable. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001314 ! free energy property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001316
name: relative binding free energy
def: "A free energy giving the difference in binding free energy between 2 ligands binding the same receptor. It is obtained by transforming 1 ligand into the other alchemically, which cancels the parts of the calculation the 2 have in common. That cancellation is why it can be computed far more accurately than either absolute value. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001314 ! free energy property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001317
name: solvation free energy
def: "A free energy giving the change on moving a molecule from vacuum into a solvent. It measures how favourable it is for the molecule to be surrounded by that solvent, and so it underlies solubility and partitioning. It appears as a leg in most thermodynamic cycles used to compute binding. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001314 ! free energy property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001318
name: hydration free energy
def: "A solvation free energy where the solvent is water. It gives the change on moving a molecule from the gas phase into aqueous solution. It is the most common benchmark for testing whether a force field treats solute-water interactions correctly, because accurate experimental values exist for many small molecules. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001317 ! solvation free energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001319
name: polar solvation energy
def: "A component of the solvation free energy arising from electrostatic interaction between the solute's charges and the solvent. It covers both the favourable interaction of polar groups with the solvent and the cost of forming a cavity in a polar medium. Continuum solvent models compute this term and the non-polar term separately. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001317 ! solvation free energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001320
name: nonpolar solvation energy
def: "A component of the solvation free energy arising from everything other than electrostatics, chiefly the cost of forming a cavity and the dispersion attraction between solute and solvent. It is usually estimated as proportional to the solvent-accessible surface area. That approximation is the weakest step in most end-point free energy calculations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001317 ! solvation free energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001321
name: surface area energy
def: "A non-polar solvation energy computed as a function of the solvent-accessible surface area of a molecule, usually a constant times the area plus an offset. It stands for the cost of opening a cavity in the solvent together with the dispersion attraction across its surface. It is the simplest of the non-polar treatments and the one used by default. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001317 ! solvation free energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001322
name: Poisson-Boltzmann energy
def: "A polar solvation energy obtained by solving the Poisson-Boltzmann equation for a solute of low dielectric constant embedded in a continuum of high dielectric constant. It treats the electrostatics of solvation without approximating the shape of the molecule. It is more expensive and more faithful than the generalized Born alternative. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001317 ! solvation free energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001323
name: Generalized Born energy
def: "A polar solvation energy obtained from the generalized Born model, which approximates the Poisson-Boltzmann result with a closed-form expression using an effective radius for each atom. It is far faster, which is what makes it usable inside a running simulation rather than only in post-processing. Its accuracy depends on how the effective radii are computed. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001317 ! solvation free energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001324
name: 3D-RISM solvation energy
def: "A specific type of solvation free energy calculated using the 3D Reference Interaction Site Model (3D-RISM). This method provides a detailed, atomistic picture of the solvent structure around the solute and its thermodynamics. The 3D-RISM solvation energy is a key output of 3D-RISM calculations. This value is often reported as the excess chemical potential." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001317 ! solvation free energy
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001325
name: excess chemical potential
def: "A type of thermodynamic property representing the free energy change of adding one particle to a system at constant volume and temperature. It is a direct measure of solvation free energy and is the primary output of methods like 3D-RISM. The calculated Excess Chemical Potential, often denoted µex or --exchem, is a key indicator of a molecule's solubility. This term is often found in the output of 3D-RISM calculations." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001314 ! free energy property
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001326
name: entropy
def: "A thermodynamic property measuring how many microscopic arrangements a system can adopt while looking the same macroscopically. It enters the free energy with a negative sign multiplied by temperature, so a state with more arrangements is favoured, more strongly at higher temperature. It is far harder to compute from a simulation than energy, because it depends on the extent of the sampled region rather than on its depth. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001293 ! thermodynamic property
property_value: skos:closeMatch SBO:0000576

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001327
name: solvation entropy
def: "An entropy component giving the change in disorder when a solute is placed in a solvent. It combines the conformational freedom the solute loses with the reorganisation forced on the solvent around it. For a non-polar solute in water the solvent term dominates, which is the origin of the hydrophobic effect. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001326 ! entropy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001328
name: reweighting entropy
def: "A diagnostic quantity measuring how evenly the statistical weights are spread when data from several biased simulations are combined. A low value means a few configurations carry most of the weight, so the effective sample is much smaller than the number of frames. It is checked before a reweighted average is trusted. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001326 ! entropy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001329
name: translational entropy
def: "An entropy component arising from the positions a molecule's centre of mass can occupy. It falls when a molecule is confined, which is why binding always carries a translational entropy cost. It depends on concentration, so the standard state must be stated with any value. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001326 ! entropy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001330
name: orientational entropy
def: "An entropy component arising from the orientations a molecule can adopt. Like the translational component it falls on binding, because a bound molecule is held in a fixed orientation. The 2 together are the rigid-body entropy cost of forming a complex. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001326 ! entropy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001331
name: conserved quantity
def: "A thermodynamic property that should not change during a simulation in a given ensemble, and is therefore watched to check that the integration is sound. With no thermostat or barostat it is the total energy; with them it is that energy plus terms accounting for what they have added or removed. A steady drift in it means the timestep is too large or a setting is inconsistent, whatever else looks normal. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001293 ! thermodynamic property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001332
name: nonequilibrium work
def: "A thermodynamic property giving the work done on a system while it is driven away from equilibrium, obtained by integrating the applied force along the path taken. It differs between repetitions of the same process, so it is a distribution rather than a single number. A fluctuation theorem relates that distribution to the equilibrium free energy difference. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001293 ! thermodynamic property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001333
name: structural property
def: "A type of output data descriptor that quantifies some aspect of the three-dimensional arrangement of atoms in a molecule or system. These descriptors are used to characterize the conformation, shape, size, and flexibility of molecules. They are the most common type of analysis performed on simulation trajectories." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001292 ! computed observable
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001334
name: root mean square deviation (RMSD)
def: "A type of structural property that measures the average distance between the atoms of two superimposed molecular structures. It is the most common metric for quantifying the difference between two conformations, often used to track a simulation's stability relative to a starting structure. Analysis outputs frequently report the RMSD value over time." []
synonym: "RMSD" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000001 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label length unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001335
name: root mean square fluctuation (RMSF)
def: "A type of structural property that measures the fluctuation of each individual atom around its average position over the course of a simulation. It is used to identify flexible or mobile regions within a molecule, such as loops or termini in a protein. Analysis outputs often report the per-residue RMSF or atomicfluct to highlight these regions." []
synonym: "RMSF" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000001 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label length unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001336
name: distance RMSD (dRMSD)
def: "A type of structural property that measures the difference between two structures based on their internal pairwise atomic distances, rather than their Cartesian coordinates. This metric does not require structural alignment and can be more sensitive to changes in internal conformation. It is a useful alternative to standard RMSD for comparing flexible molecules." []
synonym: "dRMSD" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000001 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label length unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001337
name: hydrogen mass repartitioning analysis
def: "Hydrogen mass repartitioning is a system setup method where a portion of the mass of a heavy atom is transferred to its bonded hydrogen atoms. This makes the hydrogens heavier, which slows down their bond vibrations and allows a larger time step to be used in a molecular dynamics simulation. For experts, this technique, often abbreviated HMR, is a common strategy to increase computational efficiency without significantly altering the system's dynamics." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000328 ! system setup modeling
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001338
name: ion-oxygen distance
def: "A distance giving the average separation between an ion and the oxygen atoms of the water molecules around it. It is the first thing measured when an ion's parameters are tested, because it can be compared directly with X-ray and neutron scattering data. Getting it wrong means the ion's whole interaction with its environment is wrong. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000080 ! distance
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000001 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label length unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001339
name: angle
def: "A structural property giving the angle formed at the middle atom of 3 specified atoms. Following one through a trajectory is the simplest way to watch a local geometry change, such as a hydrogen bond opening. It is measured between any 3 atoms, whether or not they are bonded. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000121 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label angle unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001340
name: dihedral angle
def: "A type of structural property representing the torsion angle defined by four sequentially bonded atoms, which describes the rotation around the central bond. The dihedral angle is the most important descriptor for characterizing the overall conformation of a flexible molecule. Its value is a primary output of many structural analysis tools. This value is commonly referred to as dihedral or torsion." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000121 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label angle unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001341
name: protein backbone torsion angle
def: "A dihedral angle describing the rotation about one of the bonds in a protein backbone. The pair of angles either side of each alpha carbon determines the local shape of the chain, and so which secondary structure that stretch forms. Plotting the 2 against each other gives the Ramachandran plot, whose crowded and empty regions show which shapes are possible at all. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001340 ! dihedral angle
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000121 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label angle unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001342
name: protein side-chain torsion angle
def: "A specific type of dihedral angle that describes the conformation of an amino acid's side chain. These angles determine the spatial arrangement of the side chain's functional groups. They are critical for understanding molecular interactions and protein packing. These angles are commonly referred to as chi angles, such as chi1 or chi2." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001340 ! dihedral angle
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000121 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label angle unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-7544-0938

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001343
name: nucleic acid torsion angle
def: "A specific nucleic acid backbone dihedral angle is a torsion angle describing rotation about a bond in the sugar-phosphate backbone of DNA or RNA. The six backbone torsion angles (α, β, γ, δ, ε, and ζ), together with the glycosidic torsion angle (χ) and the sugar pucker, define the local conformation, flexibility, and overall geometry of the nucleic acid helix." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001340 ! dihedral angle
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000121 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label angle unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-7544-0938

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001344
name: radius of gyration
def: "A type of structural property that measures the overall compactness of a molecule or a group of atoms. It is calculated as the root-mean-square distance of the atoms from their common center of mass. The radius of gyration is used to monitor large-scale conformational changes like protein folding or unfolding." []
synonym: "Rg" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000001 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label length unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001345
name: B-factor
def: "A structural property that quantifies the positional fluctuation or displacement of an atom, representing its mobility. It is calculated from the mean-square fluctuations of atomic positions in a simulation and is analogous to the crystallographic B-factor or temperature factor. High B-factor values indicate regions of high flexibility. This value is often referred to as bfactor or B-factor." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000047 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label area unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-7544-0938

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001346
name: TM-score
def: "A structural property rating how similar the overall folds of 2 proteins are, on a scale from 0 to 1, with the contribution of each residue pair weighted so that the result does not depend on protein length. Length independence is what it adds over a plain distance measure, where a longer protein always scores worse. A value above roughly 0.5 means the 2 share the same fold. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001347
name: native contact
def: "A structural property giving how many of the atom or residue contacts present in a reference folded structure are also present in the conformation being scored. It is usually reported as a fraction of the reference set rather than a raw count. It is the most common single-number reaction coordinate for folding. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "native contacts" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000189 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label count unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001348
name: coordination number
def: "A type of structural property that represents the average number of neighboring particles within a certain distance of a central particle. For an ion in water, the Coordination Number typically refers to the number of water molecules in its first solvation shell. It is a fundamental descriptor of local solvent structure and is used to validate force fields. This value is often abbreviated as CN." []
synonym: "CN" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000189 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label count unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001349
name: molecular surface area
def: "A type of structural property that measures the surface area of a molecule that is accessible to a solvent. This quantity is crucial for understanding solvation effects. It is a key component in implicit solvent models and is often used to characterize a molecule's exposure to its environment. This value is commonly known as Solvent Accessible Surface Area or SASA." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000047 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label area unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001350
name: sugar pucker
def: "A type of structural property that describes the specific three-dimensional conformation of a sugar ring, such as the ribose in DNA or RNA. The pucker is a critical determinant of the local and global structure of a nucleic acid helix. It is often described by a pseudorotation angle and can be analyzed to characterize A-form, B-form, or other helical types. This value is a standard output of nucleic acid analysis tools." []
synonym: "puckering" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-7544-0938

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001351
name: chirality
def: "A structural property recording which of its 2 mirror forms a centre in a molecule takes. The 2 forms cannot be superimposed and often behave completely differently in a biological system. A force field cannot change one into the other, so an error here persists through an entire simulation unnoticed. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001352
name: molecular orientation
def: "A type of structural property that describes the rotational position of a molecule or a group of atoms in three-dimensional space. It is often represented by a set of Euler angles, a rotation matrix, or a quaternion. Analyzing the orientation is essential for understanding the tumbling of molecules in solution or the alignment of components in a complex." []
synonym: "orientation" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001353
name: orientation angle
def: "A specific type of orientation descriptor that represents the angle of rotation between the current orientation and a reference orientation. This provides a simple, scalar measure of how much a molecule has rotated. This value is often reported as ORIENTATION_ANGLE." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001352 ! molecular orientation
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000121 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label angle unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001354
name: orientation projection
def: "A specific type of orientation descriptor that represents the cosine of the angle of rotation between the current and reference positions. This value is often used in analyses of rotational correlation. This value is often reported as ORIENTATION_PROJ." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001352 ! molecular orientation
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001355
name: tilt
def: "A base pair step parameter that describes the rotation of one base pair relative to the next around their short axes. A non-zero tilt causes the helix to bend. It is an important parameter for describing DNA curvature. This is a standard output of nucleic acid analysis programs." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001366 ! base pair step parameter
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000121 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label angle unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-7544-0938

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001356
name: spin angle
def: "A specific type of orientation descriptor that represents the angle of rotation of a molecule around a specific unit axis. The SPINANGLE is useful for analyzing spinning motions." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001352 ! molecular orientation
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000121 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label angle unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001357
name: orientation quaternion
def: "A specific type of orientation descriptor that uses a four-component mathematical object to represent the rotation of a molecule in 3D space. A quaternion avoids the singularities that can occur with Euler angles, making it a robust way to track molecular orientation. The components are often labeled QUATERNION0 through QUATERNION3. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001352 ! molecular orientation

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001358
name: nucleic acid parameter
def: "A type of structural property that provides a detailed, quantitative description of the geometry of a nucleic acid helix. These parameters are calculated by specialized analysis programs to characterize the structure of DNA and RNA. They are essential for comparing simulated structures to experimental data and for understanding sequence-dependent structural variations. These are the standard output of programs like do_x3dna or cpptraj." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-7544-0938

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001359
name: base pair parameter
def: "A type of nucleic acid parameter that describes the relative geometry and orientation of the two bases within a single base pair. These parameters quantify any non-ideal arrangements within the pair. They are used to characterize the internal conformation and planarity of base pairs. These parameters include shear, stretch, stagger, buckle, propeller twist, and opening. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001358 ! nucleic acid parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001360
name: shear
def: "A base pair parameter that quantifies the translational displacement of one base relative to the other along their short axis, within the plane of the base pair. A non-zero shear indicates a lateral displacement of the two bases from their ideal paired geometry, altering their relative alignment while maintaining the base-pair plane. This is a standard output of nucleic acid analysis programs." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001359 ! base pair parameter
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000001 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label length unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-7544-0938

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001361
name: stretch
def: "A base pair parameter that quantifies the translational displacement of one base relative to the other along the axis of the hydrogen bonds. A non-zero stretch measures how much the base pair is pulled apart or compressed. It reflects the strength and dynamics of the hydrogen bonds holding the pair together. This is a standard output of nucleic acid analysis programs." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001359 ! base pair parameter
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000001 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label length unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-7544-0938

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001362
name: stagger
def: "A base pair parameter that quantifies the translational displacement of one base relative to the other along the axis perpendicular to the base pair plane. A non-zero stagger indicates that the two bases are offset in the direction normal to the base-pair plane, resulting in a difference in their relative height and a deviation from an ideal coplanar geometry. This is a standard output of nucleic acid analysis programs." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001359 ! base pair parameter
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000001 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label length unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-7544-0938

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001363
name: buckle
def: "A base pair parameter that describes the rotation of the two bases relative to each other around their long axis, roughly parallel to the hydrogen bonds. A non-zero buckle angle indicates that the bases are tilted relative to each other, producing a bent base-pair geometry. It contributes to the overall shape of the helix. This is a standard output of nucleic acid analysis programs." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001359 ! base pair parameter
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000121 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label angle unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-7544-0938

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001364
name: propeller twist
def: "A base pair parameter that describes the rotation of the two bases relative to each other around an axis connecting their glycosidic bonds. This propeller twist optimizes stacking with adjacent base pairs but can strain hydrogen bonds. It is a key determinant of helix stability and groove dimensions. This is a standard output of nucleic acid analysis programs." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001359 ! base pair parameter
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000121 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label angle unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-7544-0938

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001365
name: opening
def: "An intra-base-pair parameter that describes the relative rotation of the two bases around the axis perpendicular to the base-pair plane. A non-zero opening angle indicates that the base pair deviates from its ideal planar geometry, altering the orientation of the hydrogen-bonding and increasing their exposure to the solvent. Large opening values are often associated with transient base-pair opening (\"breathing\") or fraying events. Opening is a standard structural parameter reported by nucleic acid analysis programs." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001359 ! base pair parameter
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000121 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label angle unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-7544-0938

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001366
name: base pair step parameter
def: "A type of nucleic acid parameter that describes the relative geometry and orientation between two successive base pairs in a helix. These parameters define the local helical structure. They are essential for characterizing the sequence-dependent variations in DNA and RNA structure. These parameters include shift, slide, rise, tilt, roll, and twist." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001358 ! nucleic acid parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001367
name: shift
def: "A base pair step parameter that describes the translational displacement of one base pair relative to the next along their short axes. A non-zero shift indicates a lateral sliding motion. It affects the alignment and stacking interactions between adjacent base pairs. This is a standard output of nucleic acid analysis programs." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001366 ! base pair step parameter
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000001 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label length unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-7544-0938

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001368
name: slide
def: "A base pair step parameter that describes the translational displacement of one base pair relative to the next along their long axes. A non-zero slide is a major determinant of the width of the major and minor grooves. It is a key parameter for describing B-form DNA. This is a standard output of nucleic acid analysis programs." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001366 ! base pair step parameter
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000001 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label length unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-7544-0938

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001369
name: rise
def: "A base pair step parameter that describes the translational distance between two adjacent base pairs along the central helical axis. The rise per step is a primary determinant of the overall length of the DNA or RNA helix. This is a standard output of nucleic acid analysis programs." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001366 ! base pair step parameter
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000001 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label length unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-7544-0938

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001370
name: roll
def: "A base pair step parameter that describes the rotation of one base pair relative to the next around their long axes. A non-zero roll angle causes the helix to bend into the major or minor groove. It is a crucial parameter for DNA bendability and protein recognition. This is a standard output of nucleic acid analysis programs." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001366 ! base pair step parameter
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000121 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label angle unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-7544-0938

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001371
name: twist
def: "A base pair step parameter that describes the rotation of one base pair relative to the next around the central helical axis. The helical twist is the primary determinant of the number of base pairs per turn in a DNA or RNA helix. This is a standard output of nucleic acid analysis programs." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001366 ! base pair step parameter
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000121 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label angle unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-7544-0938

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001372
name: displacement parameter
def: "A nucleic acid parameter that quantifies the position of a base pair's reference frame relative to the global or local helical axis. Displacement is the distance (in Å) between the center of the base pair and the global helical axis, measured perpendicular to the helix axis. They include x-displacement and y-displacement." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001358 ! nucleic acid parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-7544-0938

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001373
name: x-displacement
def: "A displacement parameter that measures the translation of a base pair away from the central helical axis towards the major or minor groove. The x-displacement is a key parameter for distinguishing between A-form and B-form DNA. This is a standard output of nucleic acid analysis programs." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001372 ! displacement parameter
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000001 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label length unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-7544-0938

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001374
name: y-displacement
def: "A displacement parameter that measures the translation of a base pair away from the central helical axis along the axis of the base pair's hydrogen bonds. The y-displacement is typically small in canonical DNA structures. This is a standard output of nucleic acid analysis programs." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001372 ! displacement parameter
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000001 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label length unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-7544-0938

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001375
name: electronic property
def: "A property describing where a molecule's electrons are and how they behave, obtained from a quantum mechanical calculation. These properties cannot be obtained from a classical simulation, because it has no electrons to describe. They are what determines chemical reactivity and how a molecule responds to light or to a field. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001292 ! computed observable

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001376
name: atomic charge
def: "An electronic property giving the partial electric charge assigned to a single atom in a molecule. No such quantity exists in the underlying physics, because electrons are not divided between atoms; it is a convention for splitting a continuous distribution. Different conventions give different values for the same molecule, so the method must always be stated. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001375 ! electronic property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001377
name: electrostatic potential (ESP) derived charge
def: "An atomic charge obtained by fitting point charges so that they reproduce the electrostatic potential computed around the molecule. It is the kind of charge most force fields use, because reproducing that potential is what a charge in a force field is for. Its weakness is that buried atoms are poorly determined, which is why restrained variants of the fit exist. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001376 ! atomic charge

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001378
name: dipole moment
def: "An electronic property giving how far and in which direction a molecule's positive and negative charge are separated. It is what makes a molecule polar, and it determines how it aligns in a field and how strongly it interacts with other polar molecules. It is one of the few charge-related quantities that is measurable and does not depend on any convention. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001375 ! electronic property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001379
name: multipole moment
def: "An electronic property describing a molecule's charge distribution in more detail than a dipole, through terms that capture progressively finer features of its shape. A molecule with no dipole can still interact strongly through these, as benzene does. Polarizable force fields use them on each atom in place of a single point charge. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001375 ! electronic property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001380
name: polarizability
def: "An electronic property giving how easily a molecule's electron cloud is distorted by an electric field. A larger, softer electron cloud distorts more, so polarizability rises with molecular size. It determines the strength of dispersion attraction, which is what holds non-polar molecules together. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001375 ! electronic property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001381
name: hyperpolarizability
def: "A polarizability describing how a molecule's electron cloud responds to a strong electric field, beyond the part that responds in proportion to the field. It is what makes a material double the frequency of light passing through it, or change its refractive index with intensity. It matters for optical materials and is negligible at ordinary field strengths. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001380 ! polarizability

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001382
name: time-dependent polarizability
def: "A polarizability describing how a molecule's response to an electric field changes with the frequency at which the field oscillates. The electron cloud cannot follow a very rapidly changing field, so the response falls off as frequency rises. It is what determines refractive index and optical rotation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001380 ! polarizability

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001383
name: ionization potential
def: "An electronic property giving the least energy needed to remove an electron from a molecule. A high value means the molecule holds its electrons tightly and is hard to oxidise. Together with the electron affinity it says how readily the molecule will give or take electrons in a reaction. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001375 ! electronic property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000111 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label energy unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001384
name: electron affinity
def: "An electronic property giving the energy released when an electron is added to a molecule. A large value means the molecule accepts electrons readily and is easily reduced. It is the counterpart of the ionization potential, which measures losing one instead. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001375 ! electronic property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000111 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label energy unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001385
name: wavefunction property
def: "An electronic property read directly from the mathematical function describing a molecule's electrons, rather than from an energy difference. Orbital energies, orbital shapes and the electron density itself belong here. They depend on the method and basis set used, so they are comparable only between calculations done the same way. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001375 ! electronic property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001386
name: wavefunction energy
def: "A wavefunction property giving the total electronic energy of a system at a fixed arrangement of its nuclei. It is the main output of a quantum chemistry calculation and the quantity whose derivatives give the forces. It is meaningful only as a difference, because its absolute value depends on the method and basis set. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001385 ! wavefunction property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000111 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label energy unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001387
name: wavefunction stability index
def: "A wavefunction property saying whether a converged solution is a true minimum or merely a point where the iteration stopped changing. A self-consistent field calculation can settle on a solution that a small change would lower, which looks converged and is not. Checking this is routine for open-shell and transition metal systems, where such false solutions are common. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001385 ! wavefunction property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001388
name: charge distribution descriptor
def: "An electronic property giving the total charge of a chosen group of atoms rather than of a single one. Grouping is more robust than per-atom charges, because the arbitrariness of dividing charge between neighbouring atoms partly cancels. It is used to state the charge of a quantum region or of a functional group. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001375 ! electronic property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001389
name: core region charge
def: "A charge distribution descriptor giving the total charge of the atoms treated at the highest level of theory in a layered calculation. It must usually be an integer, and a non-integer value signals that the region was drawn across a polar bond. Checking it is a standard step when setting up a hybrid calculation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001388 ! charge distribution descriptor

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001390
name: buffer region charge
def: "A charge distribution descriptor giving the total charge of the atoms between the high-level region and the rest of the system. That intermediate shell exists so the high-level region is not in direct contact with the crudest description. Its charge is recorded because it determines the field the inner region feels. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001388 ! charge distribution descriptor

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001391
name: kinetic property
def: "A property describing how a system moves and changes with time, rather than what shape it has at one instant. Diffusion coefficients, relaxation times and transition rates belong here. They can only be obtained from a trajectory, because a single structure carries no information about time. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001292 ! computed observable

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001392
name: diffusion coefficient
def: "A kinetic property giving how fast particles spread out through random thermal motion. It is obtained from the slope of the mean squared displacement against time, or from the integral of the velocity autocorrelation function. It is one of the few simulated quantities that can be compared directly with a straightforward experiment. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001391 ! kinetic property
property_value: skos:closeMatch PBPKO:00431

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001393
name: mean square displacement
def: "A kinetic property giving the average of the squared distance a particle has moved from where it started, as a function of elapsed time. In a liquid it grows in proportion to time once the motion has become random, and the constant of proportionality gives the diffusion coefficient. Departure from that straight line marks motion that is still constrained rather than free. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001391 ! kinetic property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000047 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label area unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001394
name: NMR relaxation time
def: "A type of kinetic property that characterizes the rate at which nuclear spins return to thermal equilibrium after being perturbed in a Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (NMR) experiment. These relaxation times are sensitive to molecular motions on different timescales. They are key experimental observables that can be compared with simulation results to validate molecular dynamics. These are known as T1 and T2 relaxation times." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001391 ! kinetic property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000003 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label time unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001395
name: T1 relaxation
def: "A specific type of NMR relaxation time, also known as the spin-lattice or longitudinal relaxation time. It characterizes the rate at which the nuclear spins exchange energy with their surrounding environment (the \"lattice\"). The T1 relaxation time is sensitive to fast molecular motions, on the order of the inverse of the Larmor frequency. This is a key parameter in NMR spectroscopy." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001394 ! NMR relaxation time
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000003 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label time unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001396
name: T2 relaxation
def: "A specific type of NMR relaxation time, also known as the spin-spin or transverse relaxation time. It characterizes the rate at which the nuclear spins lose phase coherence with each other. The T2 relaxation time is sensitive to both fast and slow molecular motions, making it a rich source of dynamical information. This is a key parameter in NMR spectroscopy." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001394 ! NMR relaxation time
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000003 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label time unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001397
name: correlation time
def: "A type of kinetic property that represents the time scale over which a system's properties, such as the orientation of a bond, remain correlated. It is a measure of the \"memory\" of the system's dynamics. The correlation time is a key parameter in the interpretation of NMR relaxation data. This is often denoted tcorr or tau_c." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001391 ! kinetic property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000003 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label time unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001398
name: spectroscopic property
def: "A physical quantity that can be measured by or is related to a spectroscopic experiment. These properties are often calculated from simulations and compared directly with experimental data to validate the accuracy of the simulation model. They provide a crucial link between computational models and the real world. These are the primary outputs of computational spectroscopy." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001292 ! computed observable
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001399
name: J-coupling
def: "A type of spectroscopic property that measures the through-bond interaction between two nuclear spins, which causes splitting of NMR signals. The J-coupling is highly sensitive to the dihedral angle between the coupled nuclei, as described by the Karplus relationship. It is a key piece of experimental data used to determine molecular conformation. This is a standard output of NMR analysis programs." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001398 ! spectroscopic property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000105 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label frequency unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001400
name: residual dipolar coupling
def: "A type of spectroscopic property that provides long-range structural information in NMR experiments by measuring the orientation of bond vectors in a weakly aligned molecule. Residual Dipolar Couplings (RDCs) are extremely valuable for determining the relative orientation of distant parts of a molecule. They provide powerful restraints for refining molecular structures." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001398 ! spectroscopic property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000105 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label frequency unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001401
name: deuterium order parameter
def: "The deuterium order parameter (SCD) measures the orientational order and dynamic disorder of lipid acyl chains in MD simulations. It allows for direct validation of membrane fluidity and structural phases against deuterium NMR experiments." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001398 ! spectroscopic property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001402
name: S2 order parameter
def: "A type of spectroscopic property that measures the motional restriction of a bond vector, typically an N-H bond in a protein, on fast timescales. The S2 order parameter ranges from 0 (completely isotropic motion) to 1 (completely rigid) and is measured by NMR relaxation experiments. It is a powerful tool for characterizing internal protein dynamics. This is a standard output of NMR relaxation analysis." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001398 ! spectroscopic property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001403
name: statistical property
def: "A property obtained by statistical analysis of a dataset, typically a trajectory. Because a simulation samples rather than solves, almost everything reported from one is of this kind. Each carries an uncertainty that depends on how much independent data went into it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001292 ! computed observable

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001404
name: obsolete Pearson product-moment correlation coefficient
def: "OBSOLETE. A specific type of correlation coefficient that measures the linear relationship between two continuous variables. It is the most common method for calculating correlation. This value is often reported in analysis as the Pearson correlation coefficient or simply 'r'. This is a standard output of statistical packages." []
comment: Obsoleted 2026-07-29: duplicated both MOLSIM:000112 and STATO:0000280 - 'Pearson product-moment correlation coefficient' is the full formal name of Pearson's correlation coefficient. Replaced by the reused STATO term.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: STATO:0000280

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001405
name: obsolete Spearman rank correlation coefficient
def: "OBSOLETE. A specific type of correlation coefficient that measures the monotonic relationship between two variables, based on their ranks rather than their raw values. It is less sensitive to outliers than the Pearson correlation. The Spearman rank correlation coefficient is a non-parametric measure of association. This is often reported as rho or Spearman's rho." []
comment: Obsoleted 2026-07-29: duplicated STATO:0000201. STATO is the canonical OBO home for statistics and its definition of this term is fuller than MOLSIM's (it covers the monotonic-function reading, the perfect +/-1 case, and when to prefer it over Pearson's). Note the symbol 'rho' named in the retired definition is not carried on the STATO term, which has no synonyms, because MOLSIM must not annotate a foreign IRI.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: STATO:0000201

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001406
name: Kendall tau correlation coefficient
def: "A correlation coefficient measuring how far 2 variables place items in the same order, computed by counting the pairs they agree and disagree about. It uses only the ordering, so it is unaffected by how the values are spaced and by extreme outliers. That makes it the right measure when the purpose is to rank rather than to predict a number. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: STATO:0000142 ! correlation coefficient
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit
property_value: skos:closeMatch STATO:0000240

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001407
name: root mean square error (RMSE)
def: "A statistical property giving the typical size of the difference between predicted and observed values, computed by squaring the differences, averaging them and taking the square root. Squaring first makes large errors count disproportionately, so a single bad prediction moves it noticeably. It is in the same units as the quantity itself, which makes it directly interpretable. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001403 ! statistical property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001408
name: mean absolute error (MAE)
def: "A statistical property giving the average size of the difference between predicted and observed values, ignoring sign. Because it does not square the differences, every error counts in proportion to its size and one large error does not dominate. It is the measure to prefer when outliers are expected and should not be allowed to control the score. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001403 ! statistical property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001409
name: obsolete standard error of the mean (SEM)
def: "OBSOLETE. A type of statistical property that estimates the standard deviation of the sample mean, quantifying how precisely the sample mean represents the true population mean. It is calculated by dividing the sample standard deviation by the square root of the sample size. The standard error of the mean is a key measure of the uncertainty of a calculated average value. This is often abbreviated as SEM." []
comment: Obsoleted 2026-07-29: duplicated STATO:0000037. STATO is the canonical OBO home for statistics; reused in place of this term. Note the '(SEM)' abbreviation carried by the retired label is not reproduced on the STATO term, because MOLSIM must not annotate a foreign IRI; STATO's own definition spells out the abbreviation.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: STATO:0000037

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001410
name: obsolete coefficient of determination
def: "OBSOLETE. A type of statistical property, also known as R-squared, that indicates the proportion of the variance in the dependent variable that is predictable from the independent variable(s). It provides a measure of how well the observed outcomes are replicated by the model. The coefficient of determination is a key metric for assessing the goodness of fit of a regression model. This is often reported as R^2 or R-squared." []
comment: Obsoleted 2026-07-29: duplicated STATO:0000564. STATO is the canonical OBO home for statistics; reused in place of this term.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: STATO:0000564

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001411
name: distribution overlap
def: "A type of statistical property that quantifies the degree to which two probability distributions share common regions. In umbrella sampling simulations, this is a critical diagnostic for ensuring that adjacent simulation windows have sampled sufficiently overlapping regions of phase space. The distribution overlap is a key metric for validating the results of umbrella sampling or replica exchange simulations. This is often reported as Phase space overlap (PSO)." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001403 ! statistical property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001412
name: phase space overlap
def: "A measure of how far the configurations sampled at 2 neighbouring alchemical states coincide. Free energy estimators need configurations typical of 1 state to be reachable from the other; where they are not, the estimate is biased whatever its apparent precision. It is checked per pair of neighbouring states, not once for the whole calculation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001411 ! distribution overlap
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001413
name: conditional probability
def: "A statistical property giving how likely something is, given that something else is already known to have happened. It is what the transition probabilities of a Markov model are: the chance of being in one state next, given the state now. Confusing it with the unconditional probability is among the commonest errors in reading such a model. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001403 ! statistical property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001414
name: obsolete standard deviation
def: "OBSOLETE. A type of statistical property that measures the amount of variation or dispersion of a set of values. A low standard deviation indicates that the values tend to be close to the mean, while a high value indicates that the values are spread out over a wider range. It is a fundamental measure of the variability of a calculated property. This is often abbreviated as sd or stdev." []
comment: Obsoleted 2026-07-29: duplicated STATO:0000237. STATO is the canonical OBO home for statistics; reused in place of this term.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: STATO:0000237

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001415
name: Hausdorff distance
def: "A statistical property giving how far apart 2 sets of points are, as the largest distance from any point of either set to the nearest point of the other. It is controlled by the worst-matched point rather than by the typical one. That makes it sensitive to a single outlier, which is sometimes the intention and sometimes a trap. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001403 ! statistical property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001416
name: clustering quality metric
def: "A statistical property rating how well a set of groups describes the data, typically by comparing how tight the groups are against how far apart they lie. Such measures are used to choose how many groups to make, since most algorithms will produce any number asked for. No measure settles the question; they narrow it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001403 ! statistical property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001417
name: Davies-Bouldin Index
def: "A clustering quality metric giving the average, over all groups, of how similar each group is to the one it most resembles. Similarity here combines how spread out the 2 groups are with how close their centres lie. A lower value means the groups are compact and well separated, so it is minimised rather than maximised. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001416 ! clustering quality metric
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001418
name: pseudo-F statistic
def: "A clustering quality metric giving the ratio of the variation between groups to the variation within them. A high value means the groups differ from each other far more than their members differ among themselves. It is computed for several possible numbers of groups, and the number giving the highest value is taken as the best. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001416 ! clustering quality metric
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001419
name: SSR/SST ratio
def: "A clustering quality metric giving the share of the total variation in the data that is accounted for by the differences between groups. A value near 1 means almost all the variation is captured by the grouping. It always rises as more groups are added, so it is read by looking for where it stops rising steeply rather than by taking its maximum. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001416 ! clustering quality metric
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001420
name: cluster silhouette
def: "A clustering quality metric giving, for each structure, how much closer it is to its own group than to the nearest other group, on a scale from −1 to 1. A value near 1 means it clearly belongs where it was put, near 0 that it sits on a boundary, and negative that it would fit another group better. Averaging it over all structures rates the whole grouping. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001416 ! clustering quality metric
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001421
name: correlation function
def: "A statistical property giving how strongly 2 quantities are related when separated by a given distance or a given interval of time. Its shape says both how strong the relationship is and over what range it persists. Almost every dynamic or structural quantity taken from a trajectory is one of these or derived from one. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001403 ! statistical property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001422
name: velocity autocorrelation function
def: "A correlation function giving how much a particle's velocity at one moment still resembles its velocity a given time later. It starts at its maximum and decays as collisions randomise the motion, so how fast it decays measures how crowded the environment is. Its integral over time gives the diffusion coefficient. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "VACF" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001421 ! correlation function

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001423
name: auto-covariance
def: "A specific type of correlation function that measures the covariance of a signal with itself at different time points. It is similar to the autocorrelation function but is not normalized." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001421 ! correlation function
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001424
name: total correlation function
def: "A correlation function giving the total departure from randomness in the positions of 2 particles in a liquid, counting both their direct influence on each other and influence passed through intervening particles. It is written h(r) and relates to the pair distribution function as h(r) = g(r) − 1. It is 1 of the 2 unknowns the RISM equations solve for. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001421 ! correlation function

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001425
name: direct correlation function
def: "A specific type of correlation function that describes the direct correlation between two particles in a liquid, excluding indirect effects mediated by other particles. It is a fundamental quantity in the statistical mechanics of liquids, related to the total correlation function by the Ornstein-Zernike equation. This is often denoted as c(r). (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001421 ! correlation function

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001426
name: pair-distribution function
def: "A correlation function giving how likely a particle is to be found at each distance from another particle, relative to a uniform distribution. Peaks mark the distances at which neighbours prefer to sit, so the first peak gives the size of the first solvation shell. It is the standard way the structure of a liquid is described. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001421 ! correlation function

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001427
name: miscellaneous descriptor
def: "A type of output data descriptor for calculated properties that do not fit into the other major categories like thermodynamic or structural properties. This includes mathematical quantities derived from the potential energy surface or other specific analysis metrics. These are often specialized outputs from analysis programs." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001292 ! computed observable
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001428
name: gradient
def: "A vector of the first derivatives of the potential energy with respect to each atomic coordinate. Its negative is the force on each atom, which is what a simulation uses to move them. A minimization has converged when it is close to zero everywhere. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001427 ! miscellaneous descriptor

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001429
name: hessian
def: "A matrix of the second derivatives of the potential energy with respect to every pair of atomic coordinates. It gives the curvature of the energy surface at a point, so it says whether that point is a minimum, a saddle or neither. Diagonalising it gives the vibrational normal modes and their frequencies. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001427 ! miscellaneous descriptor

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001430
name: atom interaction count
def: "A descriptor giving how many interactions of a chosen kind, such as hydrogen bonds or close contacts, involve a particular atom or group. It reduces a pattern of contacts to a single number that can be followed over time. What it counts depends entirely on the distance and angle criteria used, which must be stated with it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001427 ! miscellaneous descriptor
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000189 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label count unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001431
name: similarity score
def: "A type of miscellaneous descriptor that provides a metric for measuring the similarity between two entities, such as molecular structures or atom types. The similarity score is a quantitative measure used in various contexts, from virtual screening to parameter estimation. This is a key output of cheminformatics tools. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001427 ! miscellaneous descriptor
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001432
name: adaptive string method
def: "The Adaptive String Method (ASM) is a numerical technique used in computational chemistry and physics to find minimum free energy paths (MFEPs) or reaction pathways in complex, high-dimensional systems such as chemical reactions, conformational changes in biomolecules, or phase transitions. It is an improvement over the original string method because it adapts the distribution of points (\"images\") along the path to better capture regions of high curvature or complexity. For experts, this adaptive placement of images leads to a more efficient and accurate determination of the minimum free energy path." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000860 ! string method
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001433
name: ensemble trajectory analysis
def: "Ensemble trajectory analysis is a method that involves analyzing a large collection of independent simulation trajectories together, rather than just a single long one. This approach provides a more robust and statistically reliable picture of a molecule's behavior by sampling a wider range of starting conditions and potential pathways. It is particularly important for studying complex processes like protein folding or for achieving converged statistics on a system's properties." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000939 ! dynamics analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001434
name: ABCG2 charge model
def: "A method for assigning partial atomic charges to organic molecules for use in molecular simulations. This model aims to produce charges that accurately reproduce a molecule's interaction with water, a key factor in predicting properties like solvation free energy. When used with the General AMBER Force Field (GAFF2), it has demonstrated the ability to achieve \"chemical accuracy\" for a wide range of compounds. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000204 ! ligand charge model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001435
name: CM1 charge method
def: "A method that obtains atomic charges by taking the charges from a fast semi-empirical calculation and correcting them with terms fitted to reproduce measured dipole moments. The correction is what fixes the known bias of the underlying charges. It is fast enough to apply to large numbers of molecules. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000204 ! ligand charge model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001436
name: CM2 charge model
def: "A charge model refining the earlier CM1 scheme with corrections fitted against a larger set of measured dipole moments and covering more elements. The functional form is unchanged; the fitting set and the coverage are wider. It is used where semi-empirical charges are wanted quickly and reliably. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000204 ! ligand charge model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001437
name: Gasteiger charge model
def: "A charge model that assigns partial charges by passing charge between bonded atoms according to their electronegativity until the flow stops. It needs no quantum calculation at all, only the bond connectivity. It is fast enough for millions of molecules and crude enough that it is used for screening rather than for simulation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000204 ! ligand charge model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001438
name: iterative polarizable charge model
def: "A charge model in which atomic charges are recomputed in response to the surrounding electric field, and the calculation repeated until they stop changing. Each atom's charge affects the field its neighbours feel, so they cannot be solved one at a time. It is one of the ways a polarizable force field represents the response of the electron cloud. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000204 ! ligand charge model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001439
name: AMBER OL3
def: "A force field for RNA, built on the AMBER ff99 parameter set with the backbone and glycosidic dihedral terms refit by the Olomouc group. The refit corrected a drift into non-native backbone conformations that earlier RNA parameters suffered from over long simulations. It is the standard AMBER choice for RNA. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000011 ! RNA force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001440
name: AMBER ff15ipq
def: "This is a specialized force field for simulating proteins that pays extra attention to how proteins interact with water and charged ions. The AMBER ff15ipq force field was developed to improve the description of protein interactions with ions by using a novel charge model (Implicitly Polarized Charge, IPq) that better reproduces experimental hydration free energies. This force field is particularly recommended for simulations where the accurate modeling of protein-ion interactions or salt bridge dynamics is critical to the system's behavior." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001441
name: AMBER ff15ipq-m
def: "A force field specifically parameterized for the simulation of protein mimetics, which are synthetic molecules designed to mimic natural proteins. It extends the existing ff15ipq force field to include parameters for non-standard, artificial, heterogenous building blocks, such as D-amino acids and beta-amino acids. This enables researchers to accurately model the structure and dynamics of these non-natural biopolymers." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001442
name: AMBER ff03
def: "Amber ff03 is a modified version of the ff99 AMBER force field. The main changes are that charges are now derived from quantum calculations that use a continuum dielectric to mimic solvent polarization, and that the φ and ψ backbone torsions for proteins are modified, with the effect of decreasing the preference for helical configurations. The changes are just for proteins; nucleic acid parameters are the same as in ff99." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001443
name: AMBER ff03ua
def: "This is a simplified version of the AMBER ff03 force field where the aliphatic hydrogen atoms on all amino acid side-chains are united to their corresponding carbon atoms. The aliphatic hydrogen atoms on all alpha carbon atoms are still represented explicitly to minimize the impact of the united-atom approximation on protein backbone conformations. In addition, aromatic hydrogens are also explicitly represented. Nucleic acid parameters are still in all atom and kept the same as in ff99." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001444
name: AMBER OL15
def: "A force field for DNA, built on the AMBER parameter set with the backbone dihedral terms refit by the Olomouc group. It improves the description of the sugar-phosphate backbone and of helical twist over the preceding DNA parameters. It was the standard AMBER choice for DNA until the 2021 revision. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000010 ! DNA force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001445
name: nucleic acid force field
def: "A nucleic acid force field is a set of mathematical functions and parameters specifically designed to simulate the behavior of DNA and RNA molecules. These force fields contain parameters optimized to accurately reproduce the unique structural features of nucleic acids, such as the double helix, sugar puckering, and base stacking interactions. They are essential for any realistic simulation of genetic material or functional RNA molecules." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000772 ! chemical entity-based force field
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001446
name: AMBER bsc1
def: "The AMBER bsc1 force field is a specific and widely used refinement for the dihedral angle parameters of the DNA backbone, designed for use with AMBER force fields. Developed by the Barcelona Supercomputing Center (BSC), it significantly improves the description of DNA's structural dynamics compared to the uncorrected force fields. It is considered a standard addition for obtaining accurate DNA simulations." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001445 ! nucleic acid force field
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001447
name: tumuc1 DNA force field
def: "A force field for DNA whose bonded parameters and partial charges were derived from high-level quantum mechanical calculations rather than fitted to experimental data. The consistent derivation is what distinguishes it from force fields assembled from separately fitted terms. It targets DNA structure and dynamics specifically. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000010 ! DNA force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001448
name: AMBER OL21
def: "A force field for DNA from the Olomouc group, refit against new quantum mechanical calculations and experimental data. It is the most recent member of that series and supersedes the 2015 revision. It targets the same systems with a broader fitting set. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000010 ! DNA force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001449
name: lipid11
def: "A force field for phospholipids in the AMBER family, released in 2011, built on a modular scheme in which head groups and tails are parameterised separately and combined. The modularity allows lipids not in the original set to be assembled from existing pieces. It has been superseded by later revisions in the same series. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000008 ! lipid force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001450
name: GAFFLipid
def: "A force field for lipids built on the General Amber Force Field, deriving its parameters from that general scheme rather than fitting them to membrane properties. Being general, it covers lipid species that a purpose-built membrane force field does not. It reproduces bulk membrane properties less well than parameters fitted for that purpose. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000008 ! lipid force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001451
name: ParmAM1
def: "A parameter set in which the bonded terms of a force field are derived from calculations with the AM1 semi-empirical quantum method. Deriving parameters this way gives coverage for molecules no fitted force field includes, at the accuracy that method allows. It is used when a molecule falls outside every available parameter set. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000013 ! organic molecule force field
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001452 ! ParmPM3

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001452
name: ParmPM3
def: "A parameter set in which the bonded terms of a force field are derived from calculations with the PM3 semi-empirical quantum method. Deriving parameters this way gives coverage for molecules no fitted force field includes, at the accuracy that method allows. PM3 and AM1 were fitted differently, so the 2 parameter sets are alternatives rather than successive versions. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000013 ! organic molecule force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001453
name: material force field
def: "A force field parameterised for solid-state materials such as metals, oxides and semiconductors. It must represent bonding that has no fixed pairing, such as the shared electrons of a metal, which the bonded terms of a biomolecular force field cannot. It is not interchangeable with a biomolecular force field. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000007 ! force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001454
name: GAL17 force field
def: "A material force field for zeolites, which are porous crystalline aluminosilicates. It covers the framework atoms and their interaction with molecules held in the pores. It is a materials force field and shares no parameters with the biomolecular ones. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001453 ! material force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001455
name: AMBER-DYES force field
def: "A force field parameter set for the fluorescent dye molecules used to label biomolecules in experiments. It is built to be used alongside the standard AMBER protein and nucleic acid parameters without modification. It lets a labelled construct be simulated as it was actually measured, which matters when interpreting FRET distances. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000013 ! organic molecule force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001456
name: PDDG/PM3
def: "A semi-empirical quantum method applying pairwise distance-dependent corrections to the PM3 parameterisation. The corrections markedly improve heats of formation for organic molecules. It uses the same underlying approximation and differs in the correction terms and their fitted values. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000803 ! semi-empirical method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001457
name: MNDO/d
def: "A semi-empirical quantum method extending MNDO with d orbitals on the heavier main-group elements. Without them, elements from the third row onwards are described badly, because their bonding involves those orbitals. It extends the method's usable range rather than changing how it treats the elements it already covered. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000803 ! semi-empirical method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001458
name: external field model
def: "A model that adds the effect of a field imposed from outside the system, such as an electric or magnetic field. The field acts on the charges in the system but is not affected by them. It is how a simulation represents an applied voltage, or the environment of a membrane under a potential difference. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000006 ! model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001459
name: external point charge model
def: "An external field model in which the field comes from one or more fixed charges placed in or around the system. The charges do not move and feel no force themselves. It is a way of representing a nearby charged object without simulating it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001458 ! external field model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001460
name: local density approximation
def: "The simplest approximation used for the exchange-correlation term in density functional theory, which treats the electron density at each point as though it were part of a uniform gas of that density. It uses no information about how the density varies from place to place. It is reasonable for metals and poor for molecules, where the density changes sharply. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "LDA" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000627 ! density functional theory
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001461 ! generalized gradient approximation

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001461
name: generalized gradient approximation
def: "A class of approximations for the exchange-correlation term in density functional theory that uses how fast the electron density changes at each point as well as its value there. Including that rate of change corrects much of the error of the simpler treatment for molecules. It is the level most routine calculations use. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "GGA" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000627 ! density functional theory

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001462
name: hybrid GGA functional
def: "An exchange-correlation functional that mixes a fixed fraction of exactly computed exchange from Hartree-Fock theory with a density-based approximation. The mixture cancels part of the error each part makes alone, particularly the artificial repulsion of an electron from itself. It costs several times more than a purely density-based functional and is markedly more accurate for molecules. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000627 ! density functional theory

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001463
name: QM/MM model component
def: "A constituent part of a hybrid model in which a small region is treated with quantum mechanics and the rest with a force field. The parts are the quantum region, the classical region, and the treatment of the boundary between them. The boundary is the difficult part, because bonds crossing it must be handled without either description breaking down. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000006 ! model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001464
name: integration grid
def: "A set of points at which a function is evaluated so that an integral over space can be computed as a weighted sum. Density functional theory needs one because part of its energy cannot be integrated analytically. Its density controls both the accuracy of the result and a noticeable share of the cost. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001463 ! QM/MM model component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001465
name: SG1 integration grid
def: "A fixed, pre-defined integration grid for density functional theory calculations, chosen as a general-purpose default. Its point counts are set in advance rather than adapted to the molecule, so results are reproducible between programs that use it. It trades some accuracy for that predictability. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001464 ! integration grid

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001466
name: link atom
def: "An extra atom, usually a hydrogen, placed in a hybrid quantum and classical simulation to complete a bond cut by the boundary between the 2 regions. Without it the quantum region would have an unsatisfied valence and behave like a radical. It is not part of the real molecule and is invisible to the classical region. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001463 ! QM/MM model component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001467
name: bond stretching potential
def: "The part of a force field giving how the energy rises as a covalent bond departs from its preferred length. It is almost always a simple spring, chosen because it is cheap and accurate for the small departures thermal motion produces. A spring cannot break, which is the deliberate limitation of a classical force field. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000331 ! force field component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001468
name: angle bending potential
def: "The part of a force field giving how the energy rises as the angle between 3 bonded atoms departs from its preferred value. Like the bond term it is usually a spring, but a much softer one. That softness is why bending is the main way a molecule accommodates strain. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000331 ! force field component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001469
name: dihedral potential
def: "The part of a force field giving how the energy varies as a bond is rotated, written as a sum of cosine terms so that it repeats through a full turn. The number of minima per turn is set by which cosine terms are included. It carries most of what a force field knows about molecular shape. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000331 ! force field component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001470
name: 1-4 non-bonded interaction
def: "It is an electrostatic or van der Waals force between two atoms that are separated by at least three covalent bonds. It is typically composed of two parts: the van der Waals component, which models short-range repulsion and dispersion, and the electrostatic component, which models the Coulomb interaction between atomic partial charges." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000331 ! force field component
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001471
name: virtual site
def: "A point in a force field that carries charge or interaction parameters but no mass, held at a fixed position relative to real atoms. It lets charge be placed where no nucleus sits, such as on a lone pair or slightly off a nucleus. The 4-point water models and the extra points on halogens are the common examples. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "extra points" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000331 ! force field component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001472
name: bonded metal model
def: "A way of modelling a metal ion with explicit bonds to the atoms coordinating it, so the geometry of the site is held by the same terms that hold any other bond. It reproduces the fixed arrangement of a metal centre in a protein. The bonds cannot break, so the ion cannot exchange its coordinating atoms or leave. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000015 ! ion force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001473
name: non-bonded metal model
def: "A way of modelling a metal ion as a charged sphere interacting only through electrostatics and van der Waals terms, with no bonds to its neighbours. The ion can then exchange its surroundings freely, as a real ion in solution does. It cannot reproduce the fixed geometry of a metal held in a protein site. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000015 ! ion force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001474
name: 12-6-4 Lennard-Jones model
def: "A non-bonded potential that adds a term falling off with the fourth power of distance to the usual repulsion and attraction, representing the ion polarizing the molecules around it. That extra attraction is what a fixed-charge model otherwise omits entirely for a highly charged ion. It lets one parameter set reproduce both an ion's hydration energy and its ion-water distance, which the standard form cannot. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000015 ! ion force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001475
name: water cap
def: "A solvation model in which the solute is surrounded by a spherical droplet of explicit water rather than a fully periodic box. Using a droplet cuts the number of water molecules sharply, which is the whole purpose. It introduces a free surface, where water behaves unlike bulk, so results near the edge of the droplet are unreliable. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000065 ! solvation model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001476
name: molecule model
def: "A representation of a single molecule as a set of atoms together with the rules governing how they interact. It fixes what is represented explicitly and what is left out, such as whether hydrogens appear individually. It is the unit a simulated system is assembled from. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000006 ! model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001477
name: Einstein molecule model
def: "A model in which a molecule is represented as a set of independent harmonic oscillators, each vibrating about a fixed position. It is not meant to describe any real molecule; it serves as a reference state whose free energy is known exactly. That known value is what absolute free energies of solids and of bound states are measured against. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001476 ! molecule model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001478
name: generalized Born implicit solvent model
def: "An implicit solvent model that approximates the electrostatic part of the solvation free energy with a closed-form expression, using an effective radius for each atom that reflects how deeply it is buried. It avoids solving a partial differential equation, so it is fast enough to run inside a simulation rather than only afterwards. Its accuracy rests entirely on how those effective radii are computed. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000068 ! implicit solvent model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001479
name: GB-Neck2 implicit solvent model
def: "A generalized Born implicit solvent model that refines the neck correction to the effective Born radii with re-fitted parameters. It reproduces Poisson-Boltzmann solvation energies more closely than the earlier neck model. It is the version recommended for folding and for intrinsically disordered systems. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001478 ! generalized Born implicit solvent model
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001509 ! OBC implicit solvent model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001480
name: experimental refinement model
def: "An experimental refinement model is a computational model used to improve or interpret raw experimental data, particularly in structural biology. It combines a theoretical energy function, like a molecular mechanics force field, with terms that represent the experimental observations, such as X-ray diffraction patterns or NMR restraints." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000006 ! model
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001481
name: bulk solvent model
def: "A model of the disordered solvent in a crystal, used during experimental structure refinement to account for the scattering that ordered atoms do not explain. It treats that solvent as a uniform continuum of constant electron density rather than as individual water molecules. Without it, the low-resolution terms of a diffraction pattern cannot be fitted. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001480 ! experimental refinement model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001482
name: soft core potential
def: "A non-bonded potential energy function modified so that the energy stays finite when 2 atoms overlap completely. It removes the singularity in the Lennard-Jones and Coulomb terms that appears as an atom is created or annihilated in an alchemical calculation. Without it the calculation becomes numerically unstable near the end points of the coupling parameter. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000430 ! non-bonded potential

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001483
name: additive force field
def: "A force field in which the total energy is the sum of independent terms, each depending on a fixed set of atoms and unaffected by the rest of the system. Independence is what makes the energy cheap to compute and easy to parallelise. It also means the parameters cannot respond to their environment, which is what a polarizable force field adds. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000007 ! force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001484
name: statistical mechanics model
def: "A model that describes a system through the probabilities of its possible microscopic arrangements, rather than by following any one of them. It connects what individual particles do to the temperature, pressure and free energy that are actually measured. Every thermodynamic quantity taken from a simulation rests on one. (UNVERIFIED)" []
comment: Not to be confused with STATO:0000107 "statistical model", which is a statistics and inference concept: a formalization of relationships between random variables. This term is the statistical-MECHANICS sense - the theoretical framework connecting the microscopic motion of atoms to macroscopic thermodynamic properties, for example the canonical ensemble. Renamed 2026-07-29 to remove that ambiguity; "statistical model" is retained as an exact synonym.
synonym: "statistical model" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000006 ! model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001485
name: Maxwell-Boltzmann distribution
def: "A statistical model giving how the speeds of particles are spread at a given temperature, when the system is at thermal equilibrium. Most particles move near an average speed, with a long tail of fast ones and few very slow ones. Starting velocities in a simulation are drawn from it, and the observed distribution is checked against it to confirm the system has equilibrated. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001484 ! statistical mechanics model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001486
name: two-state transition model
def: "A two-state transition model is a simplified statistical mechanics model used to describe a system that can exist in two distinct states, such as a protein in a folded or unfolded state. The model characterizes the probability of switching from one state to the other, often used to analyze the kinetics of conformational changes." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001484 ! statistical mechanics model
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001487
name: Becke integration grid
def: "A scheme for building the grid of points on which a density functional theory calculation is integrated, by giving each atom its own spherical grid and blending them with weights that sum to 1 everywhere. The blending avoids double counting where atomic grids overlap. It is the standard construction such grids are built by. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001464 ! integration grid

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001488
name: Lebedev integration grid
def: "A set of points and weights on a sphere chosen so that a numerical integration over that sphere is exact for spherical harmonics up to a stated order. It reaches a given accuracy with far fewer points than an evenly spaced grid. It is the angular part of the grid a density functional theory calculation integrates on. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001464 ! integration grid

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001489
name: SPC/E-b
def: "A rigid 3-site water model refitted from its predecessor to reproduce measured properties of biomolecules in water rather than of bulk water alone. The refit adjusts how strongly water interacts with a solute. It exists because a model fitted to pure water does not necessarily solvate a protein correctly. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000014 ! water model force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001490
name: TIP3P-FB
def: "A rigid 3-site water model refitted from its predecessor against a wide set of measured properties simultaneously, rather than a few. Fitting to many targets at once gives better agreement across temperature and pressure than fitting to a handful. It keeps the 3-site form, so it costs no more than the model it replaces. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000014 ! water model force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001491
name: OPC3
def: "A rigid 3-site water model whose charges and geometry were chosen to reproduce the measured electrostatic moments of a water molecule in the liquid, rather than being fitted directly to bulk properties. Getting those moments right makes the bulk properties follow. It reproduces more measured quantities than other 3-site models at the same cost. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000014 ! water model force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001492
name: OPC3-pol
def: "A 3-site water model that adjusts its charge distribution in response to the electric field around it. Real water is markedly more polar in the liquid than as an isolated molecule, and a fixed-charge model must compromise between the 2. A polarizable model does not have to, at several times the cost. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000014 ! water model force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001493
name: WatFour (WT4) coarse-grained
def: "A coarse-grained water model in which 1 interaction bead stands for 4 real water molecules. Reducing the solvent particle count fourfold is where most of the speed of a coarse-grained simulation comes from, because solvent dominates the atom count. It is used with coarse-grained force fields such as MARTINI. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000014 ! water model force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001494
name: crystallographic model component
def: "A crystallographic model component is a fundamental concept used to describe the structure of a crystal. It represents one of the key pieces of information, such as the repeating unit or the symmetry rules, that define how molecules are arranged in a crystalline solid." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000006 ! model
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001495
name: asymmetric unit
def: "The smallest portion of a crystal from which the whole structure can be built by applying the symmetry operations of its space group. It may hold 1 molecule, several, or a fraction of 1, depending on where the molecules sit relative to the symmetry elements. It is what a deposited crystal structure file usually contains. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001494 ! crystallographic model component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001496
name: solvation shell
def: "A solvation shell refers to the layer of solvent molecules that are in direct contact with or in the immediate vicinity of a solute molecule. These solvent molecules are often more ordered and have different dynamic properties compared to the bulk solvent further away. Usually, analyzing the structure and dynamics of the first and second solvation shells is crucial for understanding the details of solute-solvent interactions." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000065 ! solvation model
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001497
name: molecular structure representation
def: "A way of describing the 3-dimensional arrangement of atoms in a molecule, either as Cartesian coordinates or as internal coordinates such as bond lengths, angles and dihedral angles. The 2 carry the same information but behave differently: internal coordinates make a constraint or a symmetry easy to impose, Cartesian ones make a translation or a rotation trivial. The choice is usually dictated by the program. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000006 ! model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001498
name: Z-matrix coordinate representation
def: "A way of describing a molecule's geometry by giving each atom's position relative to atoms already placed, as a bond length, an angle and a rotation. It expresses shape directly, so a symmetry or a constraint can be imposed by fixing one number. It becomes unstable when 3 atoms it refers to lie nearly in a straight line. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001497 ! molecular structure representation

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001499
name: force field parameter set
def: "The collection of fitted numbers that gives a force field its behaviour for a particular class of molecules, such as proteins, lipids or carbohydrates. The functional form stays the same across sets; the numbers change. A simulation states both the form and the set, because the form alone does not identify what was used. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000006 ! model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001500
name: phosaa10 parameter set
def: "A parameter set covering phosphorylated amino acids such as phosphoserine, phosphothreonine and phosphotyrosine, for use alongside the ff10 protein force field. Standard protein parameters do not include them, because phosphorylation is a modification rather than a standard residue. It is matched to that protein force field and should not be used with another. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001499 ! force field parameter set
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001501 ! phosaa14SB parameter set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001501
name: phosaa14SB parameter set
def: "A parameter set covering phosphorylated amino acids such as phosphoserine, phosphothreonine and phosphotyrosine, for use alongside the ff14SB protein force field. Standard protein parameters do not include them, because phosphorylation is a modification rather than a standard residue. It is matched to that protein force field and should not be used with another. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001499 ! force field parameter set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001502
name: phosaa19SB parameter set
def: "A parameter set covering phosphorylated amino acids such as phosphoserine, phosphothreonine and phosphotyrosine, for use alongside the ff19SB protein force field. Standard protein parameters do not include them, because phosphorylation is a modification rather than a standard residue. It is matched to that protein force field and should not be used with another. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001499 ! force field parameter set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001503
name: Joung/Cheatham ion parameter set
def: "A set of parameters for common single-atom ions, fitted separately for each of several water models. Fitting per water model is the point: parameters that behave correctly with one water model do not with another. Using them with a water model they were not fitted for gives wrong hydration and wrong ion pairing. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001499 ! force field parameter set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001504
name: basis set
def: "A collection of mathematical functions combined to represent the shape of each electron orbital in a quantum chemistry calculation. The true orbitals cannot be written down, so they are built up from a finite set of simpler functions instead. Everything a calculation can and cannot describe follows from which functions are in that set. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001463 ! QM/MM model component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001505
name: auxiliary basis set
def: "A set of mathematical functions used to approximate products of orbital basis functions, rather than the orbitals themselves, so that electron repulsion integrals can be computed more cheaply. It is what makes density fitting and resolution-of-identity methods fast. It must be matched to the orbital basis set it is paired with, or the speed-up costs accuracy. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001504 ! basis set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001506
name: Lipid_ext parameter set
def: "A parameter set extending the standard lipid parameters to cover lipid species they do not include. It is used when a membrane contains a lipid the main parameter set was never fitted for. Parameters obtained this way are less well tested than those in the main set. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001499 ! force field parameter set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001507
name: deep potential range corrected potential
def: "A type of machine learning force field that combines a deep neural network for short-range atomic interactions with a classical physics-based function for long-range interactions. The neural network is trained on high-accuracy quantum mechanics data to learn the complex, many-body interactions at short distances. This hybrid approach leverages the power of machine learning for the most difficult part of the calculation while retaining an efficient and physically correct description of the long-range forces, such as electrostatics. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001463 ! QM/MM model component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001508
name: space group
def: "A description of the full symmetry of a crystal, listing the rotations, reflections, translations and their combinations that leave the structure unchanged. There are 230 such groups in 3 dimensions, and every crystal belongs to exactly 1. Together with the asymmetric unit it determines the entire crystal. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001494 ! crystallographic model component
property_value: skos:closeMatch PROCO:0000110

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001509
name: OBC implicit solvent model
def: "A generalized Born implicit solvent model that computes effective Born radii with the scheme of Onufriev, Bashford and Case. Its radii agree closely with Poisson-Boltzmann results at a small fraction of the cost. It is the default implicit solvent in AMBER and the most widely used member of this family. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001478 ! generalized Born implicit solvent model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001510
name: GBn implicit solvent model
def: "A generalized Born implicit solvent model that corrects the effective Born radii for the narrow regions between overlapping atomic spheres, which earlier formulations treated as more solvent-exposed than they are. The correction matters most in crevices and buried pockets. The letter n in the name stands for those neck regions. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001478 ! generalized Born implicit solvent model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001511
name: SYBYL atom type
def: "A label classifying an atom by its element and its local bonding environment, in the scheme used by the SYBYL software and by the Mol2 file format. It distinguishes, for instance, an aromatic carbon from a carbon in a double bond. It is the classification most cheminformatics tools read from a structure file. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000331 ! force field component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001512
name: generalized distance coordinate restraint
def: "A generalized distance coordinate restraint is a type of restraint that is applied to a complex coordinate defined as a combination of multiple distances, angles, or dihedrals. This allows for the restraining of complex conformational changes, such as the movement of a whole domain, that cannot be described by a single distance." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000364 ! restrained simulation method
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001513
name: magnetic susceptibility tensor
def: "An electronic property giving how a molecule's electrons respond to a magnetic field, as a 3-by-3 array because the response depends on the field's direction relative to the molecule. A molecule with circulating electrons, such as an aromatic ring, responds much more strongly along one axis than the others. It is what underlies the ring current shifts seen in NMR spectra. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001375 ! electronic property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001514
name: alignment tensor
def: "An alignment tensor is a mathematical object that describes the degree and direction of the average orientation of molecules in a sample that is not perfectly random. In an NMR experiment, molecules can be weakly aligned by a magnetic field, and the alignment tensor quantifies this small but measurable preference in orientation. This tensor is crucial for interpreting experimental data like residual dipolar couplings (RDCs), which provide powerful long-range structural information." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001375 ! electronic property
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001515
name: Lennard-Jones parameter
def: "A pair of numbers defining the van der Waals interaction of an atom type: one giving how strongly it is attracted and one giving its effective size. Parameters for 2 different atom types are combined by a rule specific to each force field. Those combining rules differ between force fields, which is one reason their parameters cannot be mixed. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "Lennard-Jones parameters" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000331 ! force field component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001516
name: Poisson-Boltzmann model
def: "An implicit solvent model that represents a solute as a low-dielectric cavity in a high-dielectric continuum and solves for the electrostatic potential, including the screening by mobile salt ions. It makes no analytical approximation to the molecule's shape, so it is the reference the faster models are judged against. Solving it numerically is expensive, which is why it is usually applied to snapshots rather than during a simulation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000068 ! implicit solvent model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001517
name: analytical linearized Poisson-Boltzmann model
def: "A Poisson-Boltzmann model in which the equation is linearized and solved in closed form under simplifying assumptions about geometry. It is far faster than solving the full non-linear equation numerically. It holds only where electrostatic potentials are small, so it is unreliable for highly charged systems. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001516 ! Poisson-Boltzmann model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001518
name: CHAGB implicit solvent model
def: "A generalized Born implicit solvent model that accounts for charge hydration asymmetry, the fact that a negative ion and a positive ion of the same size are not solvated equally by water. It adjusts the solvation term according to the sign of the charge, which a standard generalized Born model cannot do. It was built to improve solvation free energies for ions. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001478 ! generalized Born implicit solvent model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001519
name: GBION implicit solvent model
def: "A generalized Born implicit solvent model whose effective Born radii for ions were re-fitted to reproduce measured hydration free energies. It targets the ions specifically, leaving the treatment of the solute unchanged. It is used where ion solvation must be right but explicit water is too expensive. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001478 ! generalized Born implicit solvent model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001520
name: GBNSR6 implicit solvent model
def: "A generalized Born implicit solvent model that computes each atom's effective radius from an analytical integral over the molecular surface rather than over atomic volumes. Integrating over the surface reproduces Poisson-Boltzmann results more closely, particularly for buried atoms. It is built for accuracy at a cost still far below solving the Poisson-Boltzmann equation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001478 ! generalized Born implicit solvent model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001521
name: group transfer free energy model
def: "A model that estimates the free energy of a process by adding up tabulated free energies for moving each chemical group between environments, such as from water into a protein interior. The group values are measured once on small molecules and then reused. It is fast and additive, which also means it cannot capture effects that depend on how groups are arranged relative to one another. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000006 ! model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001522
name: small molecule structural database
def: "A database holding the 2-dimensional and 3-dimensional structures of small organic compounds. Such collections supply the starting geometries and the reference conformations that force field parameters are fitted and tested against. They differ from protein structure archives in holding many small entries rather than few large ones. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000691 ! structural database

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001523
name: 3D-RISM model
def: "A RISM model that solves the integral equations on a 3-dimensional grid around a solute, giving the spatial distribution of each solvent site. It shows where solvent molecules are likely to sit, including individual ordered water positions, without running a simulation. It needs the bulk solvent correlation functions from a 1-dimensional calculation as input. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001535 ! RISM model
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001524 ! closure relation

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001524
name: closure relation
def: "An approximate equation relating the 2 unknown correlation functions in an integral equation theory of liquids, so that the system can be solved. Without it there are 2 unknowns and 1 equation. Different choices, such as hypernetted-chain or Kovalenko-Hirata, give measurably different solvation free energies from otherwise identical input. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001535 ! RISM model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001525
name: Kovalenko-Hirata closure
def: "The Kovalenko-Hirata (KH) closure is a mathematical approximation used in the statistical mechanical Ornstein-Zernike (OZ) integral equation theory (commonly utilized in 3D-RISM theory) to calculate solvent structure and solvation free energy." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001524 ! closure relation
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001526
name: machine-learned solvent excluded surface model
def: "An implicit solvent model that predicts solvation free energy with a model trained on more expensive calculations, using the shape of the surface the solvent cannot enter. It replaces the analytical approximation that a generalized Born model makes with a fitted one. It is faster than solving the Poisson-Boltzmann equation and more accurate than the analytical approximations, within the range it was trained on. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000068 ! implicit solvent model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001527
name: delta machine learning potential
def: "A machine-learned potential that predicts only the difference between a cheap approximate calculation and an accurate one, rather than the full energy. The difference is smaller and smoother than the energy itself, so far less training data is needed to learn it well. The cheap calculation still has to be run, which is the cost of the approach. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001463 ! QM/MM model component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001528
name: RESP induced dipole charge model
def: "A charge model that fits permanent point charges to the electrostatic potential and adds an induced dipole on each atom to represent the response to a field. The permanent part describes the isolated molecule and the induced part its response to the environment. It is how a polarizable force field is parameterised from quantum calculations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000204 ! ligand charge model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001529
name: RESP permanent multipole charge model
def: "A charge model that fits a dipole and higher terms on each atom, not only a point charge, to reproduce the electrostatic potential around a molecule. The extra terms capture features a point charge cannot, such as the anisotropy of a lone pair or the positive region on a halogen. It is more accurate and more expensive to use. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000204 ! ligand charge model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001530
name: AMBER fb15
def: "The AMBER FB15 (force-balanced 15) protein force field is a refinement of the AMBER94 ff with a systematic and thorough optimization of the intramolecular terms. The key difference in the optimized result is a significant lowering of the potential in regions away from the energy minima, which is expected to yield greater flexibility in finite temperature simulations. This force field is particularly useful for simulations of proteins, particularly when fluctuations away from equilibrium, conformational changes, and/or temperature dependence are expected to play important roles." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001531
name: united-atom force field
def: "A force field in which non-polar hydrogens are merged into the heavy atom they are bonded to, so that a methyl group is one interaction site. It roughly halves the atom count of an organic system at little cost in accuracy, because those hydrogens carry almost no charge. Polar hydrogens are kept, because they form hydrogen bonds. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000007 ! force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001533
name: drude oscillator
def: "A light charged particle attached by a spring to an atom, used to represent how that atom's electron cloud shifts in an electric field. The particle moves with the field while the atom stays put, which reproduces polarization without any electrons being modelled. Treating polarization as an extra particle lets an ordinary integrator handle it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001262 ! polarizable force field parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001534
name: 1D-RISM model
def: "A RISM model that solves the integral equations for a homogeneous fluid, giving site-to-site correlation functions that depend only on distance. It describes the structure of the bulk solvent itself, with no solute present. Its output is the required input for a 3-dimensional calculation around a solute. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001535 ! RISM model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001535
name: RISM model
def: "A statistical mechanical model of molecular liquids that predicts how solvent molecules arrange themselves around a solute by solving integral equations for site-to-site correlation functions. It gives an atomistic picture of solvation without simulating individual solvent molecules moving. It sits between an implicit solvent model and explicit solvent in both cost and detail. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "reference interaction site model" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000065 ! solvation model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001536
name: dielectrically consistent RISM model
def: "A RISM model corrected so that its results reproduce the known dielectric constant of the solvent. Standard RISM does not, which distorts long-range electrostatics. The correction matters most for solvation free energies of charged solutes. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001535 ! RISM model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001537
name: temperature
def: "A thermodynamic property giving the average kinetic energy of the particles in a system, expressed on a conventional scale. In a simulation it is computed from the velocities and fluctuates strongly, because the system is small. A value quoted from a short stretch of trajectory can differ from the target by several degrees for that reason alone. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001293 ! thermodynamic property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000005 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label temperature unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001538
name: charge-dependent van der Waals correction
def: "A force field feature in which an atom's effective size changes with the partial charge it currently carries. A real atom shrinks as it loses electron density and expands as it gains it, which a fixed radius cannot represent. It matters most for atoms whose charge varies widely between environments. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001463 ! QM/MM model component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001539
name: GFN1-xTB
def: "A semi-empirical tight binding method parameterised to give good geometries, vibrational frequencies and non-covalent interactions across most of the periodic table. It was fitted against those 3 targets rather than against energies, which is what its name records. It is used to optimise structures and screen conformations quickly. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000803 ! semi-empirical method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001540
name: GFN2-xTB
def: "A semi-empirical tight binding method that adds atom-centred multipoles and a density-dependent dispersion treatment to the earlier method in its family. Those additions improve non-covalent interactions and the description of charged systems. It is the member of the family in general use. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000803 ! semi-empirical method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001541
name: PIF correction
def: "A correction applied to free energy calculations in which the electronic description changes between the 2 states, adjusting for the mismatch between them. Without it the computed difference contains a contribution from the change of method rather than from the chemistry. It is applied after the calculation rather than changing how it runs. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001463 ! QM/MM model component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001542
name: MAIS correction
def: "A correction applied to free energy calculations run with a particular polarizable force field, adjusting for the way that force field attenuates interactions at short range. Without it the computed free energies carry a systematic offset. It is applied after the calculation rather than changing how it runs. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001463 ! QM/MM model component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001543
name: reactive force field
def: "A force field that allows bonds to form and break during a simulation, by making the bonding terms depend on how many neighbours each atom currently has rather than on a fixed list. That removes the fixed topology an ordinary force field relies on. It reaches system sizes no quantum method can while still describing reactions, at a cost far above a conventional force field. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000007 ! force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001544
name: ReaxFF
def: "A reactive force field in which the strength of every bond is recomputed from interatomic distances at each step, so bonds can form and break. Charges are also recomputed, since they change as bonds do. It reaches system sizes no quantum method can while still describing reactions, at perhaps 100 times the cost of a conventional force field. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001543 ! reactive force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001545
name: NBFIX correction
def: "An adjustment that replaces the van der Waals parameters for one particular pair of atom types, overriding whatever the combining rule would give. It exists because the combining rule is a convenience rather than physics, and fails badly for some pairs, ions with carboxylate oxygens in particular. It is applied pair by pair rather than by changing the atom types themselves. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000331 ! force field component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001546
name: polarization algorithm
def: "An algorithm that computes the induced dipole on each atom in a polarizable force field. Each induced dipole changes the field felt by the others, so they must be solved together rather than one at a time. That coupling is what makes a polarizable simulation several times more expensive than a fixed-charge one. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000382 ! simulation control algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001547
name: Applequist scheme
def: "A classical model that computes induced dipoles in a set of polarizable atoms by giving each a point polarizability and solving the resulting linear equations self-consistently. It captures how the dipole induced on one atom polarizes its neighbours in turn. It diverges when atoms are too close together, which later schemes damp. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001546 ! polarization algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001726 ! QM/MM region selection algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001548
name: RESP permanent virtual site charge model
def: "A charge model that fits point charges to the electrostatic potential while allowing some of them to sit at fixed positions away from any nucleus. Placing charge off-nucleus reproduces directional features, such as a lone pair, without the cost of higher multipole terms. It is the cheaper alternative to a multipole description. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000204 ! ligand charge model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001549
name: linear mixing potential
def: "A potential energy function formed as a straight-line interpolation between the functions of an initial and a final state, controlled by a coupling parameter running from 0 to 1. It is what makes a continuous path between 2 chemically different states possible in an alchemical calculation. It behaves badly when atoms appear or disappear, which is why the soft-core variant exists. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000331 ! force field component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001550
name: CpHMD library format
def: "A data format defining, for each residue that can gain or lose a proton, the topology and charges of every protonation state it can take and the reference energy of each. A constant pH simulation reads it to know what states are available and what switching between them costs. A residue absent from the library cannot titrate. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001091 ! molecular topology format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001551
name: correction map
def: "A force field component that adds an energy correction read from a 2-dimensional grid indexed by a pair of neighbouring backbone rotation angles. The pair of angles is treated together rather than as 2 independent terms, which is what lets the correction fix their coupling. It was introduced to bring simulated backbone conformational populations into line with experiment. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "CMAP" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000331 ! force field component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001552
name: restraint potential
def: "A restraint potential is an artificial energy function that is added to the force field to guide a simulation. This potential adds an energy penalty when the system deviates from a user-defined geometric target, such as a specific distance, angle, or RMSD value." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000331 ! force field component
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001553
name: inhomogeneous fluid solvation theory
def: "A statistical mechanical theory that describes solvent around a solute by treating the solvent as a fluid whose density and orientation vary with position. It assigns energy and entropy to each region rather than to the system as a whole. That local assignment is what lets individual water sites be scored for displacement by a ligand. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000141 ! theoretical approach

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001554
name: periodic boundary conditions
def: "A simulation technique in which the box is treated as one cell of an infinite lattice of identical copies, so a particle leaving one side re-enters the opposite side. It removes the surface that a finite box would otherwise have, where molecules would behave unlike those in bulk. The box must be large enough that a molecule does not interact with its own image. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000006 ! model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001555
name: expanded ensemble simulation
def: "An expanded ensemble simulation is an enhanced sampling method where the simulation samples not only the coordinates of the system but also an additional thermodynamic variable, such as temperature or an alchemical coupling parameter. The system can move dynamically between different temperatures or states, which helps it to overcome energy barriers and sample a wider range of conformations. For experts, this method is a powerful framework that generalizes techniques like replica-exchange and lambda-dynamics for calculating free energies." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001556
name: system setup tool
def: "A software program that assembles the parts of a simulation into a system that is ready to run. It places the molecule in a box, fills the box with solvent, adds ions to reach the intended charge and concentration, and writes the topology and coordinate files. It is the step at which a structure becomes a simulatable system. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001850 ! modeling and setup tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001557
name: AddToBox
def: "A system preparation program that inserts a stated number of molecules, such as solvent or ions, into a simulation box that already contains other molecules. It places them without creating overlaps. It is used at the end of system preparation to reach a target composition or density. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001956 ! system packing and solvation tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001603 ! Packmol

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001558
name: electrostatics analysis tool
def: "An electrostatics analysis tool is a type of software designed to calculate and visualize the electrostatic properties of a molecule. These tools typically take a molecular structure with assigned atomic charges and compute quantities like the electrostatic potential on the molecule's surface or the total electrostatic energy of solvation. They are essential for understanding how a molecule will interact with other charged molecules and its polar solvent environment." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000164 ! analysis tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001559
name: adaptive Poisson-Boltzmann solver
def: "A numerical solver that computes the electrostatic potential around a molecule in solvent by solving the Poisson-Boltzmann equation on a grid that is refined where the potential changes fastest. Refining only where needed gives the accuracy of a fine grid at much lower cost. It is the usual way continuum electrostatics is computed for a large biomolecule. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001558 ! electrostatics analysis tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001560
name: mbondi3
def: "A set of van der Waals radii in the modified-Bondi series, with further adjustments to the radii of specific atoms including carboxylate oxygens and the hydrogens bonded to nitrogen. It was fitted for use with a particular generalized Born model and improves salt-bridge and nucleic acid behaviour. It is the third revision in that series. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000272 ! radii set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001561
name: cphstats
def: "An analysis program that processes the output of a constant pH molecular dynamics run and reports pKa values and titration curves for the titratable residues. It reads the record of protonation state changes rather than the trajectory. It is what turns a constant pH simulation into a number that can be compared with experiment. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001962 ! titration analysis tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001657 ! calcpka

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001562
name: application programming interface
def: "A defined set of functions and rules through which one piece of software uses another. It fixes what can be asked for and what comes back, so the 2 sides can change independently as long as the agreement holds. It is how a simulation engine is driven from a script rather than from a command line. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000170 ! software component
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001566 ! software library
property_value: skos:closeMatch SWO:9000054

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001563
name: CUDA
def: "A programming platform and interface for running general computation on NVIDIA graphics processors. A graphics processor performs thousands of simple operations at once, which suits computing forces on many atoms simultaneously. Most simulation engines run several times faster through it than on processors alone, at the cost of working only on one manufacturer's hardware. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001562 ! application programming interface
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001676 ! MPI

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001564
name: free energy analysis tool
def: "A software program that computes free energy differences from the data produced by enhanced sampling simulations. It implements estimators such as the weighted histogram analysis method or the multi-state Bennett acceptance ratio, which combine data across simulation windows. It is the last step of a free energy workflow, turning many biased runs into 1 number. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000164 ! analysis tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001565
name: edgembar
def: "An analysis program that computes free energy differences across the edges of an alchemical network using the multi-state Bennett acceptance ratio estimator. Treating the calculation as a network lets inconsistencies around closed cycles be detected and corrected. It is built for campaigns of many ligands rather than single pairs. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001968 ! alchemical analysis tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001566
name: software library
def: "A software library is a collection of pre-written code and subroutines that provide specific functionalities to be used by other programs. Libraries are not executed directly by end-users but are imported or linked by developers to perform specialized tasks, such as mathematical computations or file parsing." []
synonym: "library" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000170 ! software component
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001567
name: FFTW
def: "A software library for computing discrete Fourier transforms, which convert data between a description in space or time and one in frequency. Particle mesh Ewald performs one at every step, so its speed sets a large part of a simulation's cost. The library measures the machine it is running on and chooses its method accordingly. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001566 ! software library

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001568
name: mdgx
def: "A simulation engine, distributed with AmberTools, used for force field parameter fitting, free energy calculations and testing new algorithms as well as for ordinary molecular dynamics. It exposes parts of the calculation that the production engines keep fixed. It is a development and method-testing tool rather than a production engine. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000160 ! molecular dynamics engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001569
name: utility script
def: "A small script that performs one well-defined supporting task inside a larger workflow, such as converting between file formats or pulling one value out of an output file. It does no science itself; it makes the pieces that do fit together. A published workflow usually depends on several, which is why they are recorded here. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001802 ! script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001570
name: metalpdb2mol2.py
def: "A utility script that converts a structure file containing a metal ion into a format carrying explicit bonds and charges. A structure file records positions and leaves bonding implicit, which is not enough to build a metal site. It is the first step of parameterising a metal centre. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001571
name: Onufriev-Bashford-Case radii set
def: "A set of atomic radii fitted for use with the generalized Born model of the same authors. Radii and generalized Born model are fitted together, so using 1 with a different model degrades both. It is the default radii set for that model in AMBER. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000272 ! radii set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001572
name: ndfes
def: "The ndfes software, included in the FE-ToolKit package, is used to analyze biased umbrella sampling to estimate free energy surfaces in an arbitrary number of reaction coordinate dimensions using either the variational free energy profile (vFEP), multistate Bennett acceptance ratio method (MBAR), or the highly-related weighted thermodynamic perturbation and generalized weighted thermodynamic perturbation methods." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001969 ! free energy surface analysis tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001573
name: ParmEd
def: "ParmEd is a software package and Python library designed for manipulating and converting molecular topology and parameter files from various simulation packages, with a primary focus on the AMBER force field format. It allows users to programmatically modify force field parameters, change molecular connectivity, and convert between different file formats." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001566 ! software library
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001574
name: pdb4amber
def: "A system preparation program that cleans a Protein Data Bank structure file so the AMBER tools can read it. It renumbers residues, corrects atom naming, and reports problems such as missing atoms, alternate locations and unusual residues. It is run before force field parameters are assigned, because those steps fail on an unprepared file. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001957 ! structure cleaning and manipulation tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001601 ! gwh

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001575
name: PropPDB
def: "A system setup program that builds a larger box by repeating a small crystallographic unit cell along chosen directions. It is needed when the original cell is smaller than the distance at which interactions are cut off, which would let a molecule interact with its own image. Repeating the cell makes the box big enough for that not to happen. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001955 ! crystallographic build tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001583 ! UnitCell
property_value: dcterms:source https://ambermd.org/doc12/Amber25.pdf

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001576
name: ProScrs.py
def: "A utility script in AmberTools that scores protein structures or docked poses using a choice of scoring functions. It ranks candidate structures rather than producing one. It is used to sift the output of a docking run before any of it is simulated. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001577
name: py_resp.py
def: "A utility script that fits atomic charges to a computed electrostatic potential, with a restraint pulling charges on buried atoms towards zero. The restraint exists because the potential outside a molecule barely constrains its interior, so an unrestrained fit gives buried charges that are large and arbitrary. It is the Python implementation of that fitting procedure. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001578
name: pyresp_gen.py
def: "A utility script that writes the input file for the charge fitting program, recording which charges are constrained to be equal and how strongly buried atoms are restrained. Setting those constraints by hand is the part of the procedure most easily got wrong. It performs no fitting itself. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001579
name: pytraj
def: "Pytraj is a Python library that provides a programmable interface to the powerful trajectory analysis capabilities of the cpptraj engine from the AmberTools suite. It allows users to write Python scripts to perform a wide range of analyses, such as calculating RMSD, distances, and hydrogen bonds, directly on simulation trajectories. Pytraj enables the creation of complex, automated, and reproducible analysis workflows that integrate seamlessly with other Python data science tools." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000251 ! trajectory processing tool
is_a: MOLSIM:001566 ! software library
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001580
name: SQM
def: "A quantum chemistry program in AmberTools that performs semi-empirical calculations, used both on its own and as the quantum part of a hybrid simulation. It implements the NDDO-based methods and the tight binding ones. It is the engine the AmberTools charge assignment tools call. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000161 ! quantum chemistry engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001581
name: TeraChem
def: "A quantum chemistry engine written from the outset to run on graphics processors rather than adapted to them. Being designed for that hardware rather than ported to it gives it a substantial speed advantage on the calculations it supports. It supports fewer methods than a general-purpose package in exchange. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000161 ! quantum chemistry engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001582
name: torch PBSA runtime
def: "A software library that performs Poisson-Boltzmann surface area calculations using the PyTorch framework. Running the calculation that way gives it graphics processor acceleration and automatic derivatives without either being written by hand. The derivatives are what let the solvation term contribute forces during a simulation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001566 ! software library

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001583
name: UnitCell
def: "A system setup program that rebuilds a complete crystallographic repeating unit from a structure file by applying the symmetry operations recorded in it. A deposited file usually contains only the smallest unique part, leaving the rest to be generated. The program performs that generation so the full contents of the cell can be simulated. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001955 ! crystallographic build tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001584
name: xleap
def: "A graphical system preparation program that builds a molecular system for AMBER interactively: loading a structure, applying a force field, adding solvent and ions, and writing the topology and coordinate files. It is the graphical front end to the same engine the command-line tool uses. The 2 produce identical output from identical commands. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000259 ! topology and coordinate generation tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001585
name: build system tool
def: "A program that turns source code into a working executable, working out what must be compiled and in what order. It also finds the libraries the program depends on and links them in. Which options it was given affects how fast the resulting program runs, and sometimes what it can do. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000171 ! software development and management tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001588 ! package manager

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001586
name: CMake
def: "A build system tool that reads a single description of how a program is assembled and generates the build files each platform's compiler expects. It lets one set of instructions serve Linux, macOS and Windows. Most simulation software is built with it, so which version was used is part of reproducing an installation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001585 ! build system tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001587
name: Intel oneAPI Math Kernel Library
def: "The Intel oneAPI Math Kernel Library (oneMKL) is a collection of highly optimized mathematical functions for science, engineering, and financial applications, specifically tuned for Intel processors. It provides high-performance implementations of routines for linear algebra (BLAS, LAPACK, ScaLAPACK), Fast Fourier Transforms (FFT), and other core mathematical operations. For biomolecular simulation software, linking against oneMKL can significantly boost performance by accelerating the fundamental mathematical computations underlying the simulation algorithms." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001566 ! software library
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001588
name: package manager
def: "A package manager is a tool that automates the process of installing, upgrading, configuring, and removing software packages and their dependencies. It simplifies the management of the complex web of software required for scientific computing by handling the details of where to find packages and which versions are compatible. For simulation scientists, package managers like Conda are crucial for creating stable and reproducible software environments." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000171 ! software development and management tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001589
name: Miniconda
def: "Miniconda is a minimal, bootstrap installer for the Conda package manager, which is widely used in the scientific computing community. It includes only the Conda package manager and Python, allowing users to create customized software environments by installing only the packages they need. For researchers, Miniconda provides a lightweight way to set up isolated and reproducible environments for their simulation and analysis software." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001588 ! package manager
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001590
name: update_amber
def: "A utility script distributed with AmberTools that fetches and applies official updates and fixes to an existing installation. It contacts the update server, downloads what applies to the installed version, and patches the source. Which updates have been applied is part of what identifies the version a result came from. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001591
name: rism1d
def: "An analysis program that solves the 1-dimensional RISM equations for a pure solvent, giving its structural and thermodynamic properties. Its output describes the bulk liquid with no solute present. It must be run before any 3-dimensional RISM calculation, which takes those results as input. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001963 ! solvation analysis tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001592
name: QUICK
def: "A quantum chemistry engine for density functional theory written to run on graphics processors. Its integral evaluation is the part moved onto that hardware, which is where most of the time in such a calculation goes. It is used as the quantum part of hybrid simulations, where the same calculation must be repeated at every step. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000161 ! quantum chemistry engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001593
name: MRCC
def: "A quantum chemistry program for very high accuracy electronic structure calculations, implementing coupled cluster methods to arbitrary excitation level and their multi-reference forms. Those methods are the benchmark other methods are measured against. Its cost restricts it to small systems. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000161 ! quantum chemistry engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001594
name: Fireball
def: "A quantum chemistry engine that performs density functional calculations using orbitals confined to a fixed radius around each atom, with the resulting integrals tabulated in advance. Confining the orbitals is what makes the tabulation possible and the calculation fast. It is used for large systems where full density functional theory would be too slow. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000161 ! quantum chemistry engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001595
name: DFTB+
def: "A quantum chemistry engine implementing density functional tight binding, an approximation that replaces most of the electronic integrals with values tabulated in advance. It is 2 to 3 orders of magnitude faster than full density functional theory while remaining quantum mechanical. Its accuracy depends on parameters fitted for each pair of elements, so it works only for element combinations that have been parameterised. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000161 ! quantum chemistry engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001596
name: xTB
def: "A quantum chemistry program implementing the extended tight binding family of semi-empirical methods. It is fast enough to optimise geometries and search conformations for molecules of a few hundred atoms in seconds. It is widely used as a preliminary step before a more expensive calculation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000161 ! quantum chemistry engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001597
name: PUPIL
def: "A software framework that connects separate simulation programs so that each can compute the part of a system it is best suited to. It passes coordinates, energies and forces between them and keeps them in step. It is what allows a quantum chemistry program and a molecular dynamics program to run 1 simulation together. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000157 ! simulation framework
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001685 ! WAMM

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001598
name: TCPB-cpp
def: "A software library that lets a classical simulation program request energies and forces from the TeraChem quantum chemistry program over a network connection. The 2 programs run separately and exchange data at each step. It is what allows a quantum and a classical engine to run one hybrid simulation together. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001566 ! software library

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001599
name: PuReMD
def: "A simulation engine built to run reactive force field simulations, where bonding is recomputed at every step rather than fixed. Recomputing the bond network is what makes such a simulation expensive, and the engine is written around doing it in parallel. It is used for reactions in materials and at surfaces. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000160 ! molecular dynamics engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001600
name: reduce
def: "A structure preparation program that adds hydrogen atoms to a macromolecular structure and chooses their positions. It also decides how to orient groups whose 2 possible arrangements X-ray data cannot distinguish, such as the ends of asparagine and glutamine side chains. Crystallography rarely sees hydrogens, so a structure file usually arrives without them and a simulation cannot start until they are there. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000223 ! generic protonation tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001601
name: gwh
def: "A system setup utility that places the hydrogen atoms of water molecules taken from an experimental structure. Crystallography sees the oxygen of an ordered water and not its hydrogens, so their orientation must be worked out. It chooses orientations that make sensible hydrogen bonds with the surroundings. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "guess water hydrogens" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001957 ! structure cleaning and manipulation tool
property_value: dcterms:source https://ambermd.org/doc12/Amber25.pdf

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001602
name: pdbremix
def: "Pdbremix is a utility designed for advanced manipulation and modification of Protein Data Bank (PDB) files. It allows users to perform a wide range of tasks such as renumbering residues, changing atom or residue names, and translating or rotating parts of a molecule. Experts use this tool for complex system-building tasks that require precise, custom modifications to a standard PDB file before simulation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001957 ! structure cleaning and manipulation tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001603
name: Packmol
def: "A system preparation program that builds an initial arrangement of molecules inside a defined region by packing them to satisfy stated counts and spatial constraints while keeping them from overlapping. It solves a constrained optimisation rather than placing molecules at random. It is how a mixed or layered starting system is built when a regular lattice will not do. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001956 ! system packing and solvation tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001604
name: AMBAT
def: "AMBAT is a software tool used to construct three-dimensional models of cell membranes for use in AMBER molecular simulations. Consisting of a set of scripts, it automates the complex process of arranging lipid molecules to form a proper bilayer and can then embed a protein structure within that prepared membrane. As part of the AmberTools suite, AMBAT (Amber Membrane Builder and Analysis Tool) provides a script-based workflow for both the initial construction of lipid bilayer systems and for subsequent analysis of membrane properties, serving as a specialized tool for preparing membrane protein simulations." []
synonym: "Amber Membrane Builder and Analysis Tool" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000225 ! membrane packing tool
property_value: dcterms:source https://ambermd.org/doc12/Amber25.pdf
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001605
name: parameter fitting tool
def: "A software program that derives force field parameters by adjusting them until the force field reproduces reference data, usually quantum calculations. It is used when no existing parameter covers a molecule and assignment by analogy is not good enough. Its output is a parameter set, not a prepared system. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000172 ! topology and parameterization tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001970 ! parameter assignment tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001606
name: Parmscan
def: "A utility program that searches automatically for force field parameters giving the best agreement with reference data, by trying many combinations rather than fitting one term at a time. Searching the whole space at once can find a combination that fitting terms separately misses. It is used for parameter development rather than for preparing a single system. (UNVERIFIED)" []
comment: described in https://doi.org/10.1002/jcc.1079
is_a: MOLSIM:001605 ! parameter fitting tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001609 ! paramfit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001607
name: parmchk2
def: "A utility program in AmberTools that checks whether every parameter a molecule needs is present in the chosen force field, and writes an additional parameter file supplying the missing ones by analogy. Missing parameters otherwise stop system preparation with an error. Parameters it supplies by analogy are guesses and are flagged as such in its output. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001970 ! parameter assignment tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001608 ! parmcal

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001608
name: parmcal
def: "An interactive utility included in the AmberTools software package for deriving force field parameters. It assists users in calculating new parameters for bond lengths and angles based on a set of built-in empirical rules. This tool is particularly useful when parameterizing a new molecule for which no existing force field parameters are available. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001970 ! parameter assignment tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001609
name: paramfit
def: "A utility program in AmberTools that fits rotation parameters by adjusting them until the force field reproduces energies computed quantum mechanically along a rotation. Rotation terms are the ones most often wrong for a new molecule, because they depend on the whole local environment. It is used when the parameters supplied by analogy are not good enough. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001605 ! parameter fitting tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001610
name: MCPB.py
def: "A utility program in AmberTools that builds force field parameters for a metal centre in a protein, from quantum calculations on the metal and the groups around it. A metal site has no standard parameters, because its geometry and charge depend on which groups coordinate it. It automates a procedure that is otherwise long and easy to get wrong. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001605 ! parameter fitting tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001611
name: pyMSMT
def: "A Python toolkit for parameterising metal sites in biomolecules, providing the components that the metal centre parameter builder is assembled from. It handles the quantum calculations, the charge fitting and the assembly of the resulting parameters. It is a toolkit rather than a single program. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001605 ! parameter fitting tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001612
name: atomtype
def: "A utility program in AmberTools that assigns a force field atom type to every atom of a molecule, from its element and its bonding environment. Every parameter a molecule receives follows from those assignments. It is run before parameters are looked up, and its output is worth inspecting for unusual chemistry. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001970 ! parameter assignment tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001613
name: am1bcc
def: "A utility program in AmberTools that assigns partial charges to an organic molecule by running a fast semi-empirical calculation and then applying tabulated corrections based on each bond's type. The corrections are fitted so the result approximates a far more expensive fitted charge set. It is how charges are produced for a ligand in seconds rather than hours. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001971 ! charge derivation tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001615 ! respgen

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001614
name: bondtype
def: "A utility program in AmberTools that works out the bond order of each bond in a molecule, distinguishing single, double and aromatic bonds. Structure files often record coordinates without bond orders, which must then be inferred from geometry. The result determines which parameters the bond receives. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001970 ! parameter assignment tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001615
name: respgen
def: "A utility program in AmberTools that writes the input files for a restrained fit of atomic charges to a computed electrostatic potential. It sets up which charges are constrained to be equal and how strongly buried atoms are restrained, which is the part that is easy to get wrong by hand. The fit itself is performed by a separate program. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001971 ! charge derivation tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001616
name: prepgen
def: "A utility program in AmberTools that builds a residue template file for a new molecule from its structure and charges. It works out the connection tree and which atoms serve as the head and tail. It is run once per new building block, and its output is reused thereafter. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001972 ! residue template tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001617 ! residuegen

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001617
name: residuegen
def: "A utility program in AmberTools that produces a complete residue template for a new molecule, running charge assignment and atom typing and then building the template. It automates the sequence of steps that the individual tools would otherwise be run through by hand. It is the usual route for adding a modified residue. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001972 ! residue template tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001618
name: divcon
def: "A quantum chemistry engine that divides a large molecule into overlapping regions, solves each separately, and assembles the result. Doing so makes the cost grow in proportion to the system size rather than far faster, which is what puts whole proteins within reach. The overlap between regions is what keeps the joins from introducing errors. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000161 ! quantum chemistry engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001619
name: acdoctor
def: "A validation script that inspects a small molecule structure file for the faults that stop force field parameters being assigned, such as wrong atom types, bad connectivity and inconsistent valences. It reports each fault and in some cases corrects it. It is run before antechamber rather than after a failure. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001620
name: IPMach.py
def: "A utility script in AmberTools that helps fit parameters for ion models, by running simulations at trial parameter values and comparing the resulting hydration free energies and ion-water distances against measurements. Ion parameters must be fitted against such properties rather than derived, because no calculation gives them directly. It automates the repeated trials that fitting requires. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001621
name: PdbSearcher.py
def: "This is a utility script designed to search for and retrieve specific molecular structure files from the Protein Data Bank (PDB). It allows a user to programmatically find structures based on criteria such as the PDB ID, the name of the molecule, or the experimental method used. This automates the process of gathering the necessary input structures for a large-scale simulation or analysis project. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001622
name: genremdinputs.py
def: "A system preparation script that writes 1 input file per replica for a replica exchange molecular dynamics run, from a template and a list of temperatures. A replica exchange run needs as many input files as it has replicas, which is too many to write by hand. It is what makes the number of replicas a parameter rather than a chore. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001623
name: nfe-umbrella-slice
def: "The nfe-umbrella-slice script is a utility used in the analysis of umbrella sampling simulations, likely as part of a larger free energy calculation workflow. Its purpose is to extract a specific portion or \"slice\" of the simulation data from the collective output of all umbrella windows. Experts use this for tasks such as assessing the convergence of the free energy profile by analyzing how it changes as more data is included." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001624
name: cpinutil.py
def: "A system preparation script, part of AmberTools, that writes the input file a constant pH molecular dynamics run needs. It records which residues may change protonation state and the parameters the titration algorithm uses. Without it the simulation has no list of titratable sites. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001625
name: ceinutil.py
def: "The ceinutil.py script is a utility used to prepare the input files for constant redox-potential MD simulations in AMBER. It allows the user to specify which residues can change their redox state and defines the parameters for the simulation. This script is essential for setting up simulations that model the behavior of molecules in a specific electrochemical environment." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001626
name: cpeinutil.py
def: "A system preparation script that writes the input file for a simulation holding both pH and redox potential constant. It records which residues may change protonation state and which may change oxidation state. It is the constant pH preparation script extended to redox-active sites. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001627
name: cyana_rest_to_amberRST
def: "The cyana_rest_to_amberRST script iscript converts CYANA .upl upper distance limit files into AMBER .RST format, allowing for the inclusion of restraints in molecular dynamics simulations. This conversion tool is commonly used to prepare input data for AMBER's sander or pmemd applications." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001628
name: makeDIP_RST
def: "This script is a utility for creating a restraint file (RST) for a simulation that uses direct dipolar coupling (DIP) data from NMR experiments. It likely reads experimental dipolar coupling values and generates the corresponding energy restraint terms in a format that can be read by a simulation program like AMBER. This automates the process of incorporating this specific type of experimental data into a simulation." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001629
name: placeAV.py
def: "placeAV.py is a utility script used to convert the predicted solvent binding sites from a Placevent analysis into explicit atomic coordinates. It reads the centers of high-density solvent regions determined by the analysis and places dummy atoms or water molecules at those specific locations within a structure file. This tool allows researchers to visualize potential hydration sites or use them as defined starting positions for explicit solvent molecules in subsequent simulations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001630
name: FRETrest.py
def: "The FRETrest.py script is a utility used to generate distance restraints for a molecular dynamics simulation based on experimental data from Förster Resonance Energy Transfer (FRET) experiments. It translates the efficiency of energy transfer between two fluorescent labels into a distance distribution that can be used to bias the simulation." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001631
name: ambpdb
def: "The ambpdb utility is a command-line tool in the AmberTools suite that converts AMBER's native topology (.prmtop) and coordinate (.inpcrd or .rst7) files into the standard Protein Data Bank (PDB) format." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001632
name: ante-MMPBSA.py
def: "A system preparation script that derives the separate receptor and ligand topology files needed for an end-point binding free energy calculation by stripping atoms from the topology of the complex. Deriving them this way guarantees the 3 topologies are consistent. Building them independently is the common source of mismatched-topology errors. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001633
name: extract_WAMMenergies.pl
def: "A Perl script used as part of the FEW (Free Energy Workflow) software to post-process simulation data. Its primary function is to parse output files and calculate a summary of effective binding energies from a free energy calculation. This script automates the data extraction step, making the analysis of complex binding energy simulations more efficient. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001634
name: extract_LIEenergies.pl
def: "The extract_LIEenergies.pl script is a utility designed to parse simulation output files and extract the specific energy components required for a Linear Interaction Energy (LIE) calculation. It typically reads the log files to find the average van der Waals and electrostatic interaction energies of a ligand with its environment. For researchers using the LIE method, this script automates the data extraction step needed to calculate the binding free energy. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001635
name: identify_transformations.pl
def: "This script is a utility used in the setup of alchemical free energy calculations to automatically identify the atoms that change between two different ligand structures. It likely compares two molecule files and generates a list of the atoms that are unique to each, which is necessary for defining the alchemical transformation. This automates a key and often error-prone step in preparing relative binding free energy calculations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001636
name: bar_pbsa.py
def: "The bar_pbsa.py script is a utility that likely combines results from Bennett Acceptance Ratio (BAR) free energy calculations with endpoint MM/PBSA calculations. This hybrid approach may be used to refine free energy estimates or to decompose a rigorously calculated free energy into physically intuitive components. For experts in free energy methods, this script represents a tool for advanced, multi-step analysis workflows. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001637
name: edgembar-amber2dats.py
def: "A utility script that converts output files from AMBER simulations into the specific data format required by the edgembar free energy analysis program. It processes AMBER's energy or log files to extract the necessary potential energy values for each frame of the simulation. This script is an essential data preparation step for using the edgembar tool to analyze free energy calculations that were performed with the AMBER software. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001638
name: edgembar-WriteGraphHtml.py
def: "A utility script from the edgembar software package that visualizes the results of a large-scale free energy calculation. It takes the calculated free energy differences between many different molecules and generates an interactive HTML file that displays the results as a network graph. This allows researchers to easily explore the relationships and predicted binding affinities for a whole series of compounds in a web browser. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001639
name: edgembar-bookend2dats.py
def: "This is a utility script from the edgembar software package used to process the output from a specific type of free energy calculation. It likely extracts the necessary energy data from simulations of the \"bookend\" or reference states in a large alchemical network. This data preparation is a required step before the main edgembar program can combine all the results to calculate the final relative free energies. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001640
name: fetkutils-tischedule.py
def: "A utility script that generates the list of coupling parameter values a thermodynamic integration calculation will simulate, choosing their number and spacing. Even spacing is wasteful, because the integrand changes much faster near the end points than in the middle. It produces the schedule before the simulations are run rather than adjusting it during them. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001641
name: ndfes-PrepareAmberData.py
def: "This script is a utility designed to convert simulation output files from the AMBER software package into a format that can be used by the ndfes free energy analysis toolkit. It reads AMBER trajectory and output files and extracts the necessary data, such as the values of collective variables over time. This is an essential interoperability step for analyzing AMBER simulations with the ndfes suite of tools. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001642
name: ndfes-CheckEquil.py
def: "This script is a utility used to check if a simulation has reached a stable equilibrium. It analyzes a time-series of a specific property, such as a collective variable, from a simulation output file to determine if its average value has stopped fluctuating systematically. This is a crucial step in free energy calculations to ensure that the data used for analysis is from a well-equilibrated system. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001643
name: ndfes-CombineMetafiles.py
def: "This script is a utility for combining multiple metadata files generated during a free energy calculation, particularly from metadynamics simulations. It merges the information about the biasing potential that was added at different times or from different parallel runs into a single, unified file. This is a necessary data processing step before the final free energy surface can be reconstructed from the combined simulation data. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001644
name: ndfes-PrintFES.py
def: "This script is a utility that takes the final, processed data from a free energy calculation and writes it out as a human-readable file representing the free energy surface (FES). The output is typically a data grid where each point has a coordinate and a corresponding free energy value. This file is the final result of the calculation and is used directly for plotting and visualizing the energetic landscape of the molecular process. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001645
name: ndfes-AvgFESs.py
def: "This script is a utility from a specific software package (ndfes) used to average multiple free energy surfaces (FESs). It likely takes several free energy profiles, for example from replicate simulations, and calculates their average and standard deviation. This is a standard final step in free energy analysis to obtain a statistically robust result and estimate its uncertainty. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001646
name: ndfes-path
def: "This is a computational tool used to find the most likely transition pathway between two stable molecular shapes on a free energy surface. It takes a pre-calculated free energy landscape and uses an algorithm to identify the minimum free energy path connecting two specified states. This analysis is used to understand the mechanism and sequence of events during a conformational change or a chemical reaction. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001647
name: ndfes-path-prepguess.py
def: "This script is a utility used to create a plausible starting guess for the transition pathway between two molecular conformations. It typically generates a series of intermediate structures by linearly interpolating between the known start and end states. This initial guess provides a starting point for more sophisticated path-finding algorithms that then refine the path to find the minimum free energy route. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001648
name: ndfes-path-analyzesims.py
def: "This script is a utility for analyzing the set of simulations that were run to determine a transition pathway. It processes the trajectories from simulations performed along a path to refine its position or to calculate properties, such as the average force, along that path. This analysis is a key part of iterative path-finding methods that use simulation data to converge on the minimum free energy path. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001649
name: finddgref.py
def: "A utility script that selects a reference free energy value from a set of calculations, so that every result in the set can be quoted relative to the same zero point. A relative free energy calculation gives differences, not absolute values, so a common reference has to be chosen before results can be compared. It reads the calculation outputs and reports which value it chose. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001650
name: espgen.py
def: "A utility script that extracts the electrostatic potential and the points it was computed at from quantum chemistry output, and writes them in the form a charge fitting program expects. It is a format conversion between 2 steps of charge derivation. It performs no fitting itself. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001651
name: pype-resp.py
def: "A utility script that runs the whole charge derivation procedure end to end: the quantum calculation, the extraction of the potential, the construction of the fitting input and the fit itself. Doing it in one step removes the several file conversions the separate tools require. Those conversions are where the procedure is usually got wrong. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001652
name: chamber
def: "The chamber script is a utility within the AmberTools suite that facilitates the conversion of CHARMM-formatted force field files into a format that can be used by AMBER. It processes CHARMM topology (PSF) and parameter (PAR) files, allowing users to run simulations with CHARMM force fields using the AMBER simulation engines." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001653
name: match_atomname
def: "match_atomname is a utility program within the AmberTools suite that takes an input file and a reference file in pdb, ac, prepi, prepc and mol2 format and it automatically detects the corresponding atom name in the reference for each atom name in the input. An output file in the same format as that of the input is generated using the matched atom names. Designed to recover atom-name information lost after running Gaussian calculations." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001569 ! utility script
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001654
name: MPI library
def: "A software library implementing the message passing standard, providing the functions a parallel program calls to send and receive data between machines. The standard says what the functions do; a library is a working version of them. Which one is installed affects performance but not results. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001566 ! software library

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001655
name: MVAPICH2-GDR
def: "An implementation of the message passing standard that moves data directly between graphics processors on different machines, without routing it through their central processors. Avoiding that detour removes a large part of the delay in a simulation running across several machines with accelerators. It requires network hardware that supports direct access. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001654 ! MPI library

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001656
name: ARPACK
def: "A software library for finding a few eigenvalues and eigenvectors of a very large matrix without forming the whole matrix. Normal mode analysis of a large structure needs exactly that, since only the slowest modes are of interest. Computing every mode would be impossible for a system of that size. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001566 ! software library

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001657
name: calcpka
def: "A computational tool used to predict the acidity constant, or pKa, of ionizable groups in a protein or other molecule. It takes a 3D structure as input and uses a model, often based on continuum electrostatics, to calculate how the local chemical environment shifts the pKa of each titratable residue. This is a critical preparation step for any simulation, as it allows for the assignment of the correct protonation states for all residues at a given experimental pH. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001962 ! titration analysis tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001658
name: addles
def: "A system preparation program that rewrites a topology file to contain several non-interacting copies of a chosen region of a molecule, as locally enhanced sampling requires. The copies feel the rest of the system but not each other. It is run before the simulation, because the method cannot be switched on afterwards. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000259 ! topology and coordinate generation tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001659
name: programming language
def: "A formal system of instructions and syntax rules in which computer programs are written. Which one a tool is written in affects how fast it runs and how easily it can be changed or extended. It is recorded because reproducing a computational result may require the same language version. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000001 ! software

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001660
name: NAB
def: "NAB, or Nucleic Acid Builder, is a specialized programming language designed specifically for the purpose of constructing and manipulating three-dimensional models of nucleic acids and proteins. For experts, NAB provides a powerful and scriptable way to build complex or non-standard biomolecular structures that would be difficult to create with standard graphical tools. Originally distributed with the AmberTools software suite, it is now only available from an independent GitHub repository." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001659 ! programming language
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001661
name: FE-ToolKit
def: "The FE-ToolKit is a collection of tools designed to facilitate the setup, execution, and analysis of alchemical free energy simulations and umbrella sampling." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001566 ! software library
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001662
name: saxs_rism
def: "An analysis program that computes a theoretical small-angle X-ray scattering profile from a structure together with a solvent distribution from 3D-RISM theory. Including the ordered solvent layer matters because that layer scatters measurably. It differs from the trajectory-based tool in obtaining the solvent from theory rather than from sampling. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001961 ! scattering analysis tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001663 ! saxs_md

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001663
name: saxs_md
def: "An analysis program that computes a theoretical small-angle X-ray scattering profile from a molecular dynamics trajectory, by averaging the scattering of the sampled conformations. Averaging over an ensemble is what makes the result comparable with a measurement on a solution. It uses the trajectory alone, with no explicit solvent model. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001961 ! scattering analysis tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001664
name: software suite
def: "A collection of separate programs distributed and installed together, sharing file formats and conventions so that the output of one is directly usable by the next. AmberTools and GROMACS are examples. The distinction from a single program matters, because a suite's name is often used loosely for the one program in it that a study actually ran. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000001 ! software

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001665
name: MoFT
def: "A software suite for developing, fitting and checking force field parameters. It covers the whole process from quantum calculations through fitting to validation against reference data. It is used to build a parameter set rather than to prepare a single system. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001664 ! software suite

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001666
name: metatwist
def: "Metatwist is an analysis tool for studying the twisting motions of helical molecules, such as DNA, using data from a metadynamics simulation. It is probably designed to analyze a free energy surface calculated as a function of a helical twist collective variable. This would allow a researcher to quantify the energetic cost and identify the pathways associated with the twisting and untwisting of a molecular helix. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001960 ! nucleic acid analysis tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001682 ! 3DNA

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001667
name: ptraj
def: "A trajectory analysis program, formerly part of the AMBER suite, that read a script of commands and computed properties such as RMSD, distances and angles from a coordinate file. It has been superseded by cpptraj, which is faster and handles more formats. It is retained because older published workflows refer to it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000251 ! trajectory processing tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001668
name: placevent analysis
def: "An analysis method that converts a continuous solvent density map into a list of discrete water positions, by repeatedly taking the highest remaining peak and removing the density around it. A simulation needs individual water molecules, and a theory-derived map gives only a density. It is the step that turns one into the other. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000328 ! system setup modeling

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001669
name: PMEMD
def: "A simulation engine, distributed with the commercial AMBER package, optimised for speed on large systems and on graphics processing units. It supports fewer methods than the general-purpose engine but runs the common ones far faster. It is the engine most production molecular dynamics in AMBER is run with. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000160 ! molecular dynamics engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001670
name: sander
def: "A simulation engine, distributed with AmberTools, that performs energy minimisation, molecular dynamics and some free energy calculations. It is the general-purpose engine of the suite and supports the widest range of methods. It is slower than the optimised engine in the commercial package, which is the trade for that breadth. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000160 ! molecular dynamics engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001671
name: web server
def: "A software service reached through a web browser that runs a computational tool on the user's behalf and returns the result. Nothing is installed locally, which puts methods within reach of people who could not otherwise run them. The trade is that the input leaves the user's machine and the version that ran it cannot be pinned down later. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000001 ! software

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001672
name: GLYCAM-Web
def: "GLYCAM-Web is a collection of online tools and web servers that assist researchers in building three-dimensional models of carbohydrates and glycoproteins. It uses the GLYCAM force field to generate realistic structures and provides tools for tasks like predicting the conformation of glycosidic linkages." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000714 ! tool web server
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001673
name: Glycoprotein Builder
def: "The Glycoprotein Builder is a web-based tool that automates the process of constructing three-dimensional models of glycoproteins. It allows users to start with a protein structure and graphically attach various glycan (sugar chain) structures to specific amino acid residues. For researchers, this tool greatly simplifies the otherwise complex and tedious task of building a complete, simulation-ready model of a glycosylated protein." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001119 ! database web server
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001674
name: RDKit
def: "An open-source software library for working with chemical structures, covering reading and writing file formats, computing molecular descriptors, generating 3-dimensional conformations and comparing molecules. It is the foundation most cheminformatics workflows in Python are built on. It handles the chemistry around a simulation rather than the simulation itself. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001566 ! software library

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001675
name: OpenMM
def: "A software library for running molecular dynamics, designed to be called from a program rather than run as a command. It is built around graphics processors and is among the fastest engines available on them. Being a library rather than an application is what makes it the usual foundation for new methods. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000160 ! molecular dynamics engine
is_a: MOLSIM:001566 ! software library

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001676
name: MPI
def: "A standard specifying how parts of a parallel program running on separate machines exchange data by sending messages to one another. Because the machines share no memory, every piece of shared information must be sent explicitly. It is how a single simulation is spread across the nodes of a cluster. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "Message Parsing Interface" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001562 ! application programming interface

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001677
name: OpenMP
def: "A programming interface that lets parts of a program run on several processor cores that share the same memory, by marking sections of the code rather than rewriting it. It is how most simulation engines use the cores of a single machine. It does not spread work across separate machines, which needs a different mechanism. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001562 ! application programming interface

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001678
name: BLAS
def: "A specification of low-level linear algebra routines, such as multiplying a matrix by a vector or by another matrix. Hardware vendors supply versions tuned for their own processors, so the same program runs at very different speeds depending on which is installed. Almost every numerical library is built on top of it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001566 ! software library

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001679
name: LAPACK
def: "A software library providing routines for linear algebra problems such as solving systems of equations, finding eigenvalues and eigenvectors, and least-squares fitting. Normal mode analysis, principal component analysis and many other analyses reduce to calls into it. Its speed determines how large a matrix those analyses can handle. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001566 ! software library

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001680
name: DL-Find
def: "DL-Find is a software library that provides a collection of robust algorithms for geometry optimization tasks. It contains routines for efficiently finding energy minima (stable structures) and first-order saddle points (transition states) on a potential energy surface. This library acts as an optimization engine that can be incorporated into other simulation or quantum chemistry programs to perform complex structural searches and reaction path calculations." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001566 ! software library
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001681
name: sff
def: "A software library that reads force field definition files and makes their parameters available to a program. It handles the file formats the parameters are distributed in, so that each simulation program does not need its own reader. It is a component used inside other software rather than a program a user runs. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001566 ! software library

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001682
name: 3DNA
def: "x3DNA is a comprehensive software package for the analysis, rebuilding, and visualization of three-dimensional nucleic acid structures. It takes a DNA or RNA structure file as input and calculates a wide range of standard helical and base pair parameters that are used to describe the detailed geometry of the helix. It is a cornerstone tool in the field of nucleic acid structural biology for characterizing and comparing experimental or simulated structures." []
synonym: "x3DNA" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001960 ! nucleic acid analysis tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-7544-0938

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001683
name: MBX
def: "A simulation engine that computes intermolecular interactions by summing separately fitted contributions from pairs, triples and larger groups of molecules. Building up the interaction this way reaches near quantum accuracy for water and small molecules. Its cost rises steeply with the size of the groups included. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000160 ! molecular dynamics engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001684
name: match analysis tool
def: "A match analysis tool is a program that compares two or more molecular structures or datasets to find and quantify their similarities. This can involve superimposing two protein structures to calculate their RMSD or searching a database of small molecules to find ones that have a similar shape or chemical features to a query compound." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000164 ! analysis tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001685
name: WAMM
def: "An integration algorithm that advances a simulation using a weighted average of momenta from more than one point in the step. The averaging damps the numerical error that accumulates in a plain scheme. It is intended to permit a longer timestep than the standard integrators allow. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "Weighted Averaging Momentum Method" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000157 ! simulation framework
property_value: dcterms:source https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jcp.2013.06.039

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001686
name: LIEW
def: "A software framework that automates a binding free energy calculation by the linear interaction energy method, running the simulations of the bound and free ligand and combining their averaged interaction energies. It carries out in 1 step what would otherwise be a hand-assembled sequence of runs. The empirical coefficients it applies are what turn the energy differences into a free energy. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "Linear Interaction Energy Workflow" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000157 ! simulation framework

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001687
name: TIW
def: "A software framework that automates a relative binding free energy calculation by thermodynamic integration, preparing the system, running the series of coupling states and analysing the result. It removes the bookkeeping of managing many simultaneous runs. It is the thermodynamic integration counterpart to the linear interaction energy workflow. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "Thermodynamic Integration Workflow" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000157 ! simulation framework
property_value: dcterms:source https://doi.org/10.1002/jcc.23218

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001688
name: numerical solver algorithm
def: "A numerical solver is an algorithm that finds approximate solutions to complex mathematical equations that cannot be solved by hand. These algorithms are the computational engines that solve the underlying mathematical problems in many scientific simulations. For experts, this includes iterative algorithms like the conjugate gradient method used to solve the large systems of linear equations that arise in implicit solvent models or quantum mechanical calculations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000037 ! algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001689
name: biconjugate gradient solver algorithm
def: "An iterative algorithm for solving a large system of linear equations whose matrix is not symmetric. The ordinary conjugate gradient method requires symmetry and fails without it. It is used for the equations arising in continuum electrostatics, where the matrix is not symmetric. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001688 ! numerical solver algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001690 ! modified direct inversion in the iterative subspace solver algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001690
name: modified direct inversion in the iterative subspace solver algorithm
def: "An algorithm that speeds up an iterative calculation by combining several previous iterations into a better next guess, with the combination chosen to make the estimated error smallest. It is the standard way a self-consistent field calculation is brought to convergence. Without it many calculations oscillate indefinitely instead of settling. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001688 ! numerical solver algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001691
name: integration algorithm
def: "An algorithm that advances the positions and velocities of the atoms from one step to the next, using the forces computed at the current step. It approximates the continuous equations of motion by a sequence of small jumps. How well it conserves energy over a long run is the main thing that separates one from another. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000382 ! simulation control algorithm
property_value: skos:closeMatch KISAO_0000475

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001692
name: Beeman integrator
def: "An integration algorithm that advances positions and velocities using the forces at the current and 2 previous steps. It produces the same trajectory as the Verlet family but computes velocities more accurately at each point. That matters when a quantity depending on velocity, such as kinetic energy, is being reported. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001691 ! integration algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001693
name: modified incomplete Choleski conjugate gradient solver algorithm
def: "An iterative algorithm for solving a large system of linear equations that first computes a rough approximate factorisation of the matrix and uses it to make the problem easier to solve. The approximation is deliberately incomplete, because an exact one would cost as much as solving the system directly. It converges in far fewer iterations than the unaided method. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001688 ! numerical solver algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001694
name: numerical integration algorithm
def: "An algorithm that computes the approximate value of a definite integral from values sampled at discrete points. It is used wherever the function being integrated is known only at the points where it was measured or computed. The free energy of a thermodynamic integration calculation is obtained this way. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000037 ! algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001695
name: Lebedev quadrature algorithm
def: "A numerical integration algorithm for integrating a function over the surface of a sphere, using a fixed set of points and weights chosen to be exact for spherical harmonics up to a given order. It reaches a given accuracy with far fewer points than an evenly spaced arrangement. It supplies the angular part of the grid used in density functional theory. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001694 ! numerical integration algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001699 ! trapezoid integration algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001696
name: analysis algorithm
def: "An algorithm that computes a property or finds a pattern in raw simulation data. It is the concrete procedure an analysis method is carried out by, as distinct from the idea of the method itself. Two programs implementing the same method can use different algorithms and give slightly different numbers. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000037 ! algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001697
name: signal processing algorithm
def: "An analysis algorithm that examines or transforms data recorded as a sequence in time. A trajectory is such a sequence, so techniques built for signals apply to it directly. Smoothing, filtering and decomposing a series into its frequencies all belong here. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001696 ! analysis algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001715 ! surface area calculation algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001698
name: butterworth filter algorithm
def: "A signal processing algorithm that removes frequencies above or below a chosen point while leaving the remaining ones as flat as possible. Flatness in the kept range is what it optimises, at the cost of a gradual rather than sharp cut-off. It is used to separate slow collective motion in a trajectory from fast thermal noise. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001697 ! signal processing algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001706 ! fast fourier transform algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001699
name: trapezoid integration algorithm
def: "A numerical integration algorithm that approximates the area under a curve by joining neighbouring points with straight lines and summing the resulting trapezoids. It needs only the sampled points, with no assumption about the function between them. It is the usual way the thermodynamic integration curve is integrated over the coupling parameter. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001694 ! numerical integration algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001700
name: random number generator algorithm
def: "A random number generator is an algorithm designed to produce a sequence of numbers that lacks any discernible pattern, appearing to be random. In computational science, these are essential for introducing the element of chance required by certain simulation methods. For experts, these pseudo-random number generators are critical components of stochastic thermostats and Monte Carlo algorithms. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000037 ! algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001701
name: Marsaglia random number generator algorithm
def: "A pseudo-random number generator of the family developed by Marsaglia, built from simple shift and multiply operations on a small internal state. The simplicity makes them fast and easy to implement, which is why they appear inside simulation engines. They pass standard statistical tests while using far less state than a long-period generator. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001700 ! random number generator algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001702 ! Mersenne Twister random number generator algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001702
name: Mersenne Twister random number generator algorithm
def: "A pseudo-random number generator that produces a sequence repeating only after an extremely long period, with no detectable pattern in ordinary statistical tests. It is the default generator in many scientific libraries. It is not suitable where an adversary must not predict the sequence, which does not arise in simulation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001700 ! random number generator algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001703
name: permuted congruential random number generator algorithm
def: "A permuted congruential generator is a type of pseudo-random number generator that aims to improve the statistical properties of simpler linear congruential generators. It takes the output of a standard congruential generator and applies a permutation (shuffling) to its bits to break up correlations. For experts, this represents a class of generators that offers a good trade-off between computational simplicity and improved statistical quality. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001700 ! random number generator algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001704
name: Xoshiro128++ random number generator algorithm
def: "A pseudo-random number generator built from shift, rotate and add operations on 128 bits of state. It is fast and passes current statistical test suites, and its small state makes it cheap to keep one per thread. Giving each thread its own generator is what keeps a parallel simulation reproducible. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001700 ! random number generator algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001705
name: MDposit
def: "MDposit is a web-based platform and portal designed for the sharing, visualization, and analysis of molecular dynamics simulation data. It serves as a distributed database interface that allows users to browse, access, and interactively view trajectories from different research groups. This tool aims to facilitate the dissemination and reuse of large-scale simulation datasets within the scientific community." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001119 ! database web server
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001706
name: fast fourier transform algorithm
def: "An algorithm that converts data between a description in time or space and one in frequency, in a time that grows only slightly faster than the amount of data. Computing the same transform directly would cost far more, growing with the square of the data size. It is what makes particle mesh Ewald affordable, since one is performed at every step. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001697 ! signal processing algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001707
name: DBSCAN clustering algorithm
def: "A clustering algorithm that grows a group outward from any point with enough neighbours within a chosen distance, and leaves sparse points unassigned. It needs no target number of groups and can find groups of any shape. Structures left unassigned are treated as rare conformations rather than forced into a group, which suits a trajectory well. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000253 ! clustering algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001708
name: k-means clustering algorithm
def: "A clustering algorithm that divides structures into a fixed number of groups by repeatedly assigning each to the nearest group centre and then recomputing the centres. The number of groups must be chosen in advance, which is its main limitation. It also assumes groups are roughly round and of similar size, which conformations often are not. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000253 ! clustering algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001709
name: density peaks clustering algorithm
def: "A clustering algorithm that picks group centres as points which have many close neighbours and are also far from any point with still more neighbours. Those 2 conditions identify a peak in the crowding rather than an arbitrary starting point. Every other point then joins the nearest denser point, which assigns the whole set in one pass. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000253 ! clustering algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001710
name: Levenberg-Marquardt algorithm
def: "An optimization algorithm for fitting a non-linear model to data, which shifts between 2 strategies according to how well the fit is going: a cautious one far from the answer and a fast one near it. That shift is what makes it converge reliably from a poor starting guess. It is the standard method for fitting force field parameters to reference data. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000407 ! optimization algorithm
property_value: skos:exactMatch KISAO_0000515

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001711
name: residue library
def: "A data file holding the complete definition of a molecular building block, giving its atoms, their types and charges, the bonds between them and their standard geometry. It lets a topology be assembled from a sequence without every atom being specified. A residue absent from it cannot be built automatically. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000331 ! force field component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001712
name: downhill simplex minimizer algorithm
def: "An optimization algorithm that keeps a set of trial points forming a simple shape and repeatedly replaces its worst point by reflecting it through the others. It never needs a derivative, only the ability to evaluate the function. That makes it usable where derivatives are unavailable or unreliable, at the cost of converging slowly. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000408 ! energy minimization algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001713
name: Hawkins-Cramer-Truhlar radii set
def: "A set of effective atomic radii fitted for use with the SMx family of implicit solvent models. The radii absorb part of the error of the underlying model, which is why they are specific to it. Substituting a general-purpose set such as Bondi changes the computed solvation energies. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000272 ! radii set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001714
name: Gaussian quadrature algorithm
def: "A numerical integration algorithm that evaluates a function at specially chosen points, with matching weights, so the result is exact for polynomials up to a given degree. Choosing the positions as well as the weights doubles the degree that a given number of points can handle. It needs the function to be evaluable anywhere, not only at points already sampled. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001694 ! numerical integration algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001715
name: surface area calculation algorithm
def: "An algorithm that computes how much of a molecule's surface a solvent molecule can reach. It does so by rolling a sphere the size of a solvent molecule over the atoms and measuring the area traced out. The result is used to estimate how much it costs to make a hole in the solvent for the molecule to sit in. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001696 ! analysis algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001716
name: LCPO algorithm
def: "An algorithm that estimates solvent-accessible surface area from a sum over overlapping pairs of atoms, with fitted coefficients, rather than by placing test points. Having a closed form makes it fast enough to run at every step of a simulation, and to be differentiated so it contributes forces. Point-based methods are more accurate and cannot do either. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001715 ! surface area calculation algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001743 ! ICOSA algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001717
name: RMSD calculation algorithm
def: "An algorithm that measures how far 2 structures differ, by first superposing them to remove any overall shift or rotation and then taking the root mean square of the remaining distances between matched atoms. Without the superposition step, moving a molecule across the box would register as a large change in shape. The choice of which atoms to superpose on decides what the number means. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001696 ! analysis algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001718
name: quaternion RMSD algorithm
def: "An algorithm that finds the optimal superposing rotation by solving a 4-by-4 eigenvalue problem rather than by decomposing a matrix. Representing the rotation with 4 numbers avoids the numerical failure that matrix methods can suffer when the 2 structures are nearly mirror images. It gives the same answer as the matrix route and is more robust. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001717 ! RMSD calculation algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:010011 ! Kabsch RMSD algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001719
name: Broyden-Fletcher-Goldfarb-Shanno algorithm
def: "An optimization algorithm that builds an approximation to the curvature of a function from the slopes seen at successive steps, and uses it to choose each new step. Approximating the curvature rather than computing it converges in far fewer steps than using slope alone, without the cost of second derivatives. It stores a full matrix, which limits it to problems with a moderate number of variables. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "BFGS" EXACT []
synonym: "BFGS algorithm" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000407 ! optimization algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001720
name: conjugate gradient algorithm
def: "A minimization algorithm that chooses each step from the current downhill direction combined with the previous step's direction, so that it does not undo progress already made. That memory is what lets it follow a long narrow valley, where steepest descent zig-zags. It is the usual choice once the worst overlaps in a structure have been removed. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000408 ! energy minimization algorithm
property_value: skos:closeMatch KISAO_0000357

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001721
name: Powell's algorithm
def: "An optimization algorithm that finds a minimum by searching along one direction at a time and gradually replacing those directions with better ones built from the progress made. It never needs a derivative, only function values. It suits problems where derivatives are unavailable or too noisy to trust. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000407 ! optimization algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001722
name: multiple time-stepping algorithm
def: "An integration algorithm that updates different forces at different intervals, evaluating the fast-changing bonded forces every step and the slow-changing long-range forces only every few steps. Most of the cost of a simulation is in the long-range forces, so evaluating them less often is a large saving. Stretching the interval too far makes the simulation unstable. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001691 ! integration algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001723
name: r-RESPA integrator
def: "A multiple time-stepping algorithm that separates forces by how fast they change and nests their updates inside one another, in a way that can be run backwards to recover the starting state exactly. That reversibility is what keeps energy from drifting, which simpler multiple time-stepping schemes do not manage. It is the standard implementation of the idea. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001722 ! multiple time-stepping algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001725 ! force-coordinate extrapolation integrator

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001724
name: Treecode algorithm
def: "An algorithm that computes long-range forces quickly by grouping distant particles into a hierarchy of cells and treating each distant group as a single source. A group far enough away is indistinguishable from a point, so computing its members separately is wasted work. It reduces the cost from growing with the square of the particle count to growing close to linearly. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000384 ! force calculation algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001725
name: force-coordinate extrapolation integrator
def: "An advanced algorithm for updating atom positions in a molecular dynamics simulation that uses information from previous steps to predict the future motion. It works by extrapolating both the forces and the coordinates to the next time point, which can allow for a larger time step while maintaining numerical stability. This type of integrator is a specialized method aimed at improving the computational efficiency of a simulation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001722 ! multiple time-stepping algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001726
name: QM/MM region selection algorithm
def: "An algorithm that decides, during a simulation, which atoms belong in the quantum region at each moment. It is needed when molecules such as solvent move in and out of the region of interest, so a fixed list would either trap them or cut them in half. The difficulty is changing the assignment without a jump in energy. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001546 ! polarization algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001727
name: hysteretic region selection algorithm
def: "A region selection algorithm that uses 2 distance thresholds, a nearer one for entering the quantum region and a farther one for leaving it. The gap between them stops an atom sitting exactly at the boundary from switching back and forth every step. That repeated switching is what makes a single-threshold rule unusable. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001726 ! QM/MM region selection algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001728
name: quantum mechanics algorithm
def: "An algorithm that solves the equations of quantum mechanics for a molecular system, to obtain how its electrons are arranged and what energy that costs. All such algorithms are approximate, because the exact equations cannot be solved for more than one electron. They differ in which approximation they make and what it costs. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000037 ! algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001729
name: divide and conquer algorithm
def: "An algorithm that makes a quantum calculation on a large molecule possible by splitting it into overlapping pieces, solving each, and recombining them. A conventional calculation costs far more than proportionally more as the system grows, which is what this avoids. The pieces must overlap, or the joins between them introduce errors. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001728 ! quantum mechanics algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001730
name: I/r-RESPA integrator
def: "A multiple time-stepping algorithm of the RESPA family adapted for polarizable force fields, where the induced dipoles must be resolved at each evaluation of the long-range forces. Polarizable models make the long-range part far more expensive, so separating it out matters more than usual. It splits the forces by range as well as by how quickly they change. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001722 ! multiple time-stepping algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001731
name: Nose-Hoover chain thermostat
def: "A temperature control algorithm that couples the system to a bath variable, that variable to a second, and so on along a chain. The chain fixes a failure of the single-variable form, which cannot reach the correct distribution for a system with few degrees of freedom or one starting far from equilibrium. A chain of 3 to 5 is usual. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000038 ! thermostat algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001732
name: Bussi thermostat
def: "A temperature control algorithm that rescales the velocities towards the target temperature by a factor drawn partly at random, so that the energy follows the correct distribution rather than being driven to a single value. It reaches equilibrium as quickly as the simple rescaling schemes while sampling correctly, which they do not. stochastic velocity rescaling thermostat should be kept as an exact synonym. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000038 ! thermostat algorithm
property_value: MOLSIM:002254 "ntt=11" xsd:string {dcterms:source="MOLSIM:000217"}

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001733
name: velocity-Verlet middle integrator
def: "An integration algorithm of the velocity-Verlet family in which the thermostat acts halfway through each step rather than at its start or end. Placing it there keeps the sampled distribution closer to the correct one when the timestep is large. The difference shows up as an error in temperature that grows with timestep in the other arrangements. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001691 ! integration algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001734
name: Car-Parrinello induced dipole scheme
def: "A polarization algorithm that gives each induced dipole a small fictitious mass and lets it move under its own equation of motion, instead of solving for it exactly at every step. If the mass is small enough the dipoles stay close to the exact solution while never being solved for. It removes the iteration that otherwise dominates the cost. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001546 ! polarization algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001735
name: middle thermostat scheme
def: "A way of placing the thermostat's action halfway through each integration step rather than at its beginning or end. That placement keeps the sampled distribution correct at much larger timesteps than the alternatives allow. The difference appears as a temperature error that grows with timestep in the other arrangements. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000038 ! thermostat algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001736
name: Tan&Luo radii set
def: "A set of atomic radii fitted for use with the GB-Neck2 implicit solvent model. Fitting them alongside that model is what lets it reproduce Poisson-Boltzmann solvation energies closely. They are not interchangeable with radii fitted for other generalized Born models. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000272 ! radii set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001737
name: Polak-Ribiere conjugate gradient algorithm
def: "A minimization algorithm that chooses each search direction from the current downhill slope combined with the previous direction, using a particular formula for how much of the previous one to keep. That formula is what separates it from the other conjugate gradient variants. It recovers well when progress stalls, because its formula resets the direction automatically in that case. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001720 ! conjugate gradient algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001738
name: limited-memory BFGS algorithm
def: "An optimization algorithm that builds an approximate picture of the curvature of a function from the last few steps taken, rather than storing the full curvature matrix. Storing that matrix is impossible when there are hundreds of thousands of variables, as in a large molecular system. Keeping only recent history gives most of the benefit at a fraction of the memory. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "L-BFGS algorithm" EXACT []
synonym: "L-BGFS minimizer" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001719 ! Broyden-Fletcher-Goldfarb-Shanno algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001739
name: truncated Newton conjugate gradient algorithm
def: "A minimization algorithm that uses curvature information about the energy surface to choose each step, computing that information only approximately and stopping the approximation early. Using curvature converges in far fewer steps than using slope alone, and computing it exactly would be impossible for a large system. Stopping early is the compromise the name refers to. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000408 ! energy minimization algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001740
name: enhanced sampling algorithm
def: "An enhanced sampling algorithm is a computational procedure that modifies a standard simulation to accelerate the exploration of a molecule's possible states or to observe rare events. These algorithms are designed to overcome the high energy barriers that can trap a simulation in a single state for a long time." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000037 ! algorithm
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001741
name: multiple-walkers algorithm
def: "An enhanced sampling algorithm where multiple independent simulation replicas (walkers) simultaneously explore the conformational space and contribute to a single, shared biasing potential. This parallelization significantly accelerates the convergence of methods like metadynamics or adaptive biasing force." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001740 ! enhanced sampling algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001967 ! replica exchange algorithm
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001742
name: InChI code
def: "The IUPAC International Chemical Identifier (InChI) is a standardized text string that provides a unique, machine-readable signature for a specific chemical substance. It is algorithmically generated from a molecule's structural information and it is sensitive to its chirality, ensuring that a given compound will always produce the same identifier regardless of how it is drawn. This code serves as a universal label for linking chemical information across different databases and software." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000447 ! identifier
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001743
name: ICOSA algorithm
def: "The ICOSA algorithm is a computational method used to rapidly calculate the solvent-accessible surface area (SASA) of a molecule. It works by placing a sphere of dots, arranged in a pattern based on an icosahedron, around each atom and then counting how many of these dots are not covered by neighboring atoms. This numerical approach provides a fast and efficient way to estimate the molecular surface area, a property that is crucial for implicit solvent models and for analyzing a molecule's exposure to its environment." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001715 ! surface area calculation algorithm
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001744
name: steepest descent algorithm
def: "A minimization algorithm that moves the atoms at each step in the direction of the force on them, which is the steepest downhill direction from where they are. It is robust and almost never fails, because that direction always lowers the energy. It slows to a crawl in a long narrow valley, where the steepest direction points across the valley rather than along it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000408 ! energy minimization algorithm
property_value: skos:exactMatch KISAO_0000511

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001745
name: secondary structure assignment algorithm
def: "An algorithm that identifies which parts of a protein form regular repeating shapes, such as helices and sheets, from the coordinates of its backbone. It works by finding the pattern of hydrogen bonds between backbone groups, or by examining backbone angles. It is what turns a list of coordinates into the helix-and-arrow picture of a protein. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001696 ! analysis algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001746
name: DSSP algorithm
def: "The DSSP (Define Secondary Structure of Proteins) algorithm is the most widely used and standard algorithm for assigning secondary structure to the residues of a protein. It works by identifying the characteristic hydrogen-bonding patterns between the backbone amide and carbonyl groups that define alpha-helices and beta-sheets. The detailed, per-residue output of the DSSP algorithm is a standard tool for protein structure analysis and validation." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001745 ! secondary structure assignment algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:010012 ! STRIDE algorithm
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001747
name: obsolete trajectory analysis algorithm
def: "OBSOLETE. A trajectory analysis algorithm is a computational procedure that processes the time-series of atomic coordinates from a simulation to calculate a specific property. These algorithms are the engines of analysis tools, turning raw simulation output into interpretable scientific data. For experts, this includes the specific algorithms for tasks like imaging periodic trajectories, calculating correlation functions, or clustering conformations." []
comment: candidate for removal per https://github.com/CPCLab/molsim-ontology/issues/21
is_obsolete: true

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001748
name: toroidal-view-preserving algorithm
def: "A specialized algorithm for visualizing molecules in a periodic simulation box that ensures chemical bonds are always drawn correctly, even when they cross a boundary. It treats the periodic box as a torus (a donut shape), so that when a molecule is viewed, its connectivity is preserved without being artificially \"broken\" at the box edges. This scheme is important for creating clear and unambiguous visualizations of molecular structures and their interactions within a periodic environment. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001696 ! analysis algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001749
name: cubic spline interpolation algorithm
def: "An algorithm that draws a smooth curve through a set of points by fitting a cubic polynomial between each neighbouring pair and matching their slopes and curvatures where they join. The matching is what stops the curve having visible corners. It is how a free energy profile is drawn from values computed at discrete points. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001697 ! signal processing algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001750
name: continuous wavelet transform
def: "A method that decomposes a signal into contributions at each frequency and each moment at once, by matching it against a shape that is stretched and shifted across the data. A plain frequency analysis gives no information about when. That matters for a trajectory, where a motion may appear only during part of the run. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001697 ! signal processing algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001751
name: statistical algorithm
def: "An algorithm that applies the methods of statistics to summarise data, estimate a quantity, or judge how reliable a result is. Simulation output is a sample rather than an exact answer, so every number taken from it needs one. Reporting a value without an uncertainty is the most common failure this addresses. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001696 ! analysis algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001752
name: kernel density estimation algorithm
def: "A statistical algorithm that estimates the distribution behind a set of points by placing a small smooth bump on each and adding them together. It assumes no particular shape for the distribution, unlike fitting a named family. How wide the bumps are decides whether it reveals real structure or smooths it away. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001751 ! statistical algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:010013 ! Gaussian mixture model algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001753
name: residue name
def: "A residue name is a standardized short code, typically three or four letters, used in structure files to identify a specific type of molecular building block. For example, 'ALA' is the residue name for the amino acid alanine, and 'DG' can represent a deoxyguanosine nucleotide." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000447 ! identifier
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0003-4177-3619

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001754
name: GLYCAM residue name
def: "A short code identifying a particular sugar in the GLYCAM carbohydrate force field, encoding not only which sugar it is but which of its hydroxyl groups are linked onward. Sugars branch, so the same sugar appears in many linkage patterns and each needs its own template. That is why the naming carries linkage information where amino acid codes do not. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001753 ! residue name

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001755
name: atom name
def: "An atom name is a unique label given to an atom within a specific residue to distinguish it from other atoms of the same element. For example, in an amino acid, the names 'CA' and 'CB' are used to differentiate the alpha-carbon from the beta-carbon." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000447 ! identifier
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0003-4177-3619
property_value: skos:exactMatch data:1757

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001756
name: residue connection atom
def: "The atom of a residue designated to form the bond joining it to the neighbouring residue in a chain. Building a polymer from residue templates requires knowing which atom on each side makes that bond. Without it, templates could be listed in order and never joined. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001711 ! residue library

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001757
name: unit head atom
def: "The atom of a residue template that bonds to the preceding residue in a chain. In a protein it is the backbone nitrogen. Together with the tail atom it defines the direction in which templates are joined. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001711 ! residue library

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001758
name: unit tail atom
def: "The atom of a residue template that bonds to the following residue in a chain. In a protein it is the backbone carbonyl carbon. A template with no tail atom defined cannot be followed by another, which is how a chain terminus is expressed. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001711 ! residue library

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001759
name: obsolete Miller indices
def: "OBSOLETE. Miller indices are a set of three integers (h, k, l) that uniquely describe the orientation of a plane of atoms within a crystal lattice. These indices are determined from the positions of the spots in an X-ray diffraction pattern and are fundamental to crystallography. They are used to define the specific crystal faces and to calculate the theoretical diffraction pattern from a structural model." []
comment: Marked for removal. See: https://github.com/CPCLab/molsim-ontology/issues/26
is_obsolete: true

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001760
name: residue type
def: "A classification recorded in a topology stating what general kind of building block a residue is, such as protein, nucleic acid, water, ion or solvent. Analysis tools use it to select parts of a system without naming every residue. A mis-set value makes a selection quietly omit or include the wrong atoms. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001711 ! residue library

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001761
name: volumetric data component
def: "A constituent part of a 3-dimensional data map, being either a grid point or the value stored at it. The grid points fix where the map is sampled and the values say what was found there. The term exists so that the 2 can be referred to separately. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001762
name: voxel
def: "A single cell of a 3-dimensional grid, holding one value for the small volume of space it covers. It is to a volume what a pixel is to an image. Analyses that map a property through space, such as where water sits around a protein, report their results one of these at a time. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001761 ! volumetric data component
property_value: skos:closeMatch NCIT:C79424

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001763
name: atom type
def: "A classification assigned to an atom to describe its fundamental chemical identity or its specific physical and computational properties within a molecular model." []
comment: Previous definition: An atom type is a classification assigned to an atom in a force field that defines its interaction parameters based on its chemical environment. It encodes not just the chemical element but also its hybridization state and bonding pattern, so a carbonyl carbon will have a different atom type than an aromatic carbon.
is_a: MOLSIM:000447 ! identifier
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0003-4177-3619

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001764
name: neural network atom type
def: "A description of an atom's surroundings used by a machine-learned force field, computed from the positions of its neighbours rather than assigned from a table. A conventional atom type is a fixed label such as \"aromatic carbon\"; this instead varies continuously with the local geometry. That is what lets such a model describe environments it was never given a label for. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001763 ! atom type

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001765
name: modified amino acid residue name
def: "A code identifying an amino acid that has been chemically altered, such as by phosphorylation or methylation. The standard 3-letter codes cover only the 20 unmodified residues, so a modified one needs a code of its own. The code is what links the residue to the extra parameters its modification requires. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001753 ! residue name

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001766
name: path image
def: "A path image is a single, discrete snapshot or structure that represents one point along a continuous pathway between two molecular states. A collection of these images is used in methods like the Nudged Elastic Band (NEB) to map out a reaction path or conformational transition." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000006 ! model
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001767
name: trajectory post-processing
def: "Trajectory post-processing is the general process of cleaning and preparing raw simulation trajectory files before performing detailed scientific analysis. This typically involves essential steps like removing the overall rotation and translation of a target molecule to keep it centered, and fixing any molecules that appear \"broken\" by the periodic boundary conditions. These routine procedures are necessary to create a clean trajectory that is suitable for correct visualization and accurate calculation of structural properties." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000004 ! simulation analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001768
name: match list preparation
def: "A system preparation stage in which a correspondence is established between the atoms of 2 structures, saying which atom of one plays the part of which atom of the other. An alchemical transformation needs it to know which atoms change and which stay. A wrong correspondence produces a calculation that runs to completion and gives a wrong answer. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000002 ! simulation preparation

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001769
name: topology and coordinate file preparation
def: "A preparation process that produces the 2 files a simulation needs: a topology file saying what the system is made of, and a coordinate file saying where everything currently is. The topology lists the atoms, the bonds between them and the force field parameters, and it does not change during the run. The coordinates change at every step, which is why the 2 are kept apart. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000002 ! simulation preparation

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001770
name: rotational diffusion
def: "The random tumbling of a molecule in a liquid, caused by collisions with the solvent around it. How fast it tumbles depends on its size and shape and on how viscous the solvent is. It is what NMR relaxation measurements are sensitive to, which is how a simulated value can be checked. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001391 ! kinetic property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001771
name: backmapping modeling
def: "A modelling method that rebuilds an all-atom structure from a coarse-grained one, placing the atoms each grouped site stands for. Information was discarded when the coarse model was built, so the rebuilt atoms are a plausible arrangement rather than a recovered one. It is used to inspect a coarse-grained result in atomic detail, or to continue a simulation at finer resolution. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000305 ! modeling method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001772
name: NMR refinement
def: "NMR refinement is a computational process used to generate or improve a three-dimensional model of a molecule using experimental data from Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (NMR) spectroscopy. The method involves finding a structure, or an ensemble of structures, that is both stereochemically realistic and consistent with a set of experimental restraints, such as distances between atoms derived from the Nuclear Overhauser Effect. This process is essential for translating the raw data from an NMR experiment into a high-resolution atomic model." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000202 ! nuclear magnetic resonance
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001773
name: LEaP preparation
def: "A system preparation stage in which a molecular system is assembled and given force field parameters, producing the topology and coordinate files a simulation needs. It covers loading the structure, choosing the force field, adding solvent and counter-ions, and writing the output. It is the step at which a structure becomes a simulatable system. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000002 ! simulation preparation

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001774
name: momentum removal
def: "A procedure applied at intervals during a simulation that subtracts any overall translation, and sometimes rotation, of the whole system. Small numerical errors accumulate into a drift of the entire box, which would otherwise be counted as thermal motion and inflate the temperature. Removing it keeps the reported temperature meaning what it should. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000002 ! simulation preparation

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001775
name: post-translational modification
def: "A chemical change made to a protein after it has been built from its amino acid sequence, such as attaching a phosphate, a sugar or a lipid. It can switch the protein's activity on or off, mark it for destruction, or send it to a particular part of the cell. Standard force fields do not include the modified residues, so extra parameters are needed to simulate one. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000006 ! model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001776
name: N-linked glycosylation
def: "A post-translational modification in which a branched sugar chain is attached to the nitrogen of an asparagine side chain. It is among the most common modifications of proteins on the cell surface and of secreted proteins. The sugar chains are large, flexible and highly variable, which makes them among the hardest parts of a protein to simulate. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001775 ! post-translational modification

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001777
name: O-linked glycosylation
def: "A post-translational modification in which sugars are attached to the oxygen of a serine or threonine side chain, added one at a time rather than as a preassembled block. Because they are added singly, the resulting chains vary far more between copies of the same protein than the nitrogen-linked kind. That variability is what makes such proteins hard to define, let alone simulate. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001775 ! post-translational modification

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001778
name: wavefunction model
def: "A model specifying the mathematical form assumed for the many-electron wavefunction in a quantum chemistry calculation, such as a single determinant or a combination of several configurations. It fixes what electronic structure the calculation is able to represent before any basis set is chosen. A single determinant cannot describe bond breaking or a near-degenerate ground state. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001463 ! QM/MM model component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001779
name: restricted closed-shell wavefunction
def: "A wavefunction model in which every occupied molecular orbital holds exactly 2 electrons of opposite spin. It applies to molecules with no unpaired electrons, which is most stable organic molecules in their ground state. It is the default assumption of a quantum chemistry calculation unless an open-shell model is asked for. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001778 ! wavefunction model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001780
name: unrestricted open-shell wavefunction
def: "A type of wavefunction model specifically used for molecules that have unpaired electrons, such as radicals or certain metal complexes. In an unrestricted open-shell wavefunction, electrons with spin-up and spin-down are allowed to occupy different spatial orbitals, providing the necessary flexibility to describe the different distributions of the unpaired electrons. This model is the basis for Unrestricted Hartree-Fock (UHF) and open-shell DFT calculations and is essential for correctly modeling the electronic structure and properties of radical species. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001778 ! wavefunction model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001781
name: secondary structure
def: "A regular, repeating local shape that a stretch of a protein or nucleic acid chain folds into, held together by hydrogen bonds between nearby parts of the backbone. In proteins the common ones are the helix and the sheet; in nucleic acids they include the double helix and the hairpin. It is local, so one chain contains many such stretches with irregular regions between them. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: SO:0001078 ! polypeptide_secondary_structure

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001782
name: beta sheet
def: "A beta sheet is a common shape in proteins where parts of the amino acid chain line up side-by-side like ribbons in a flat, pleated sheet. It is a secondary structure motif formed by two or more extended polypeptide chains, called beta-strands, which are linked laterally by a regular pattern of hydrogen bonds between their backbone atoms. These sheet structures form the rigid core of many proteins and are critical for creating binding surfaces for other molecules. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001781 ! secondary structure
property_value: skos:closeMatch NCIT:C13802

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001783
name: parallel beta sheet
def: "A parallel beta sheet is a type of beta sheet where the adjacent protein chains all run in the same direction, like lanes on a one-way highway. In this arrangement, the neighboring beta-strands are all aligned in the same N-terminus to C-terminus direction, which results in a pattern of angled, evenly spaced hydrogen bonds between the strands. This arrangement is typically found buried in the core of a protein and often requires long loop connections between the strands." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001782 ! beta sheet
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001784
name: anti-parallel beta sheet
def: "An anti-parallel beta sheet is a type of beta sheet where the adjacent protein strands run in opposite directions, like traffic on a two-way street. In this arrangement, the neighboring beta-strands are aligned in opposite N-terminus to C-terminus directions, resulting in a pattern of straight, perpendicular hydrogen bonds between the strands. This arrangement is generally more stable than the parallel form and is a very common structural motif found in many proteins." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001782 ! beta sheet
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001785
name: obsolete helix
def: "OBSOLETE. A helix is a common shape in proteins and DNA where the molecular chain is twisted into a spiral or corkscrew. It is a secondary structure motif characterized by a repeating pattern of backbone dihedral angles that causes the polymer chain to follow a helical path, which is stabilized by a regular pattern of internal hydrogen bonds. The alpha-helix in proteins and the double helix of DNA are two of the most fundamental and recognizable structures in biology." []
comment: Retired 2026-08-05 in favour of the Sequence Ontology term, which covers the same concept in the ontology whose scope owns protein secondary structure. The MOLSIM hierarchy position is preserved: the SO class is asserted under MOLSIM:001781 secondary structure so the DSSP category set stays in one place.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: SO:0001114

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001786
name: obsolete 3-10 helix
def: "OBSOLETE. The 3-10 helix is a type of spiral shape found in proteins that is tighter and more narrow than the common alpha-helix. It is a secondary structure motif characterized by a repeating hydrogen bond between the backbone carbonyl of a residue and the backbone amide of the residue three positions down the chain (i → i+3). While less common than the alpha-helix, short segments of 3-10 helix are often found at the ends of alpha-helices, acting as a cap to the structure." []
comment: Retired 2026-08-05 in favour of the Sequence Ontology term, which covers the same concept in the ontology whose scope owns protein secondary structure. The MOLSIM hierarchy position is preserved: the SO class is asserted under MOLSIM:001781 secondary structure so the DSSP category set stays in one place.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: SO:0001119

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001787
name: obsolete alpha helix
def: "OBSOLETE. The alpha-helix is the most common spiral shape found in proteins, resembling a coiled ribbon. It is a right-handed secondary structure motif characterized by a repeating hydrogen bond between the backbone carbonyl of a residue and the backbone amide of the residue four positions down the chain (i → i+4). This highly stable and common structure forms a fundamental building block for the architecture of most proteins." []
comment: Retired 2026-08-05 in favour of the Sequence Ontology term, which covers the same concept in the ontology whose scope owns protein secondary structure. The MOLSIM hierarchy position is preserved: the SO class is asserted under MOLSIM:001781 secondary structure so the DSSP category set stays in one place.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: SO:0001117

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001788
name: obsolete pi helix
def: "OBSOLETE. The pi-helix is a wide spiral shape found in proteins that is less stable than the common alpha-helix. It is a secondary structure motif characterized by a repeating hydrogen bond between the backbone carbonyl of a residue and the backbone amide of the residue five positions down the chain (i → i+5). Because its internal packing is less favorable, the pi-helix is usually found only as a short, single-turn insertion within other helical structures. Once thought to be rare, short π-helices are found in 15% of known protein structures and are believed to be an evolutionary adaptation derived by the insertion of a single amino acid into an α-helix." []
comment: Retired 2026-08-05 in favour of the Sequence Ontology term, which covers the same concept in the ontology whose scope owns protein secondary structure. The MOLSIM hierarchy position is preserved: the SO class is asserted under MOLSIM:001781 secondary structure so the DSSP category set stays in one place.
is_obsolete: true
replaced_by: SO:0001118

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001789
name: turn
def: "A secondary structure element in which 3 to 5 residues reverse the direction of a protein chain over a short distance. It is what lets 2 stretches of chain run back alongside each other, so a compact fold is possible at all. Without turns a chain could only extend. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001781 ! secondary structure

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001790
name: bend
def: "A bend is a region in a protein chain that creates a sharp turn, changing the direction of the polypeptide. It is a short structural motif, typically involving a few amino acid residues, that is characterized by a specific pattern of backbone dihedral angles that reverses the direction of the chain." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001781 ! secondary structure
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001791
name: extended beta conformation
def: "A backbone conformation in which a polypeptide segment is stretched into a flat zig-zag, with backbone dihedral angles near the fully extended region of the Ramachandran plot. It is the conformation a strand takes inside a beta sheet, and the most extended a polypeptide reaches. The zig-zag is what places successive side chains on alternating faces. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001781 ! secondary structure

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001792
name: beta bridge
def: "A beta bridge is an isolated, localized hydrogen bond between two amino acid residues from different segments of a protein, mimicking the interactions found in β-sheets." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001781 ! secondary structure
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001793
name: conformational transition
def: "A conformational transition is the process where a molecule changes from one stable three-dimensional molecular arrangement to another. This can be a large-scale event, such as a protein switching between an active and an inactive state, or a more local change like the flipping of a sugar ring. Studying these transitions is fundamental to understanding how molecular function is controlled by changes in structure." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001391 ! kinetic property
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986
property_value: skos:closeMatch SBO:0000181

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001794
name: crankshaft motion
def: "A crankshaft motion refers to a specific, localized, correlated movement of a protein's backbone. Specifically, it is an oscillation or rotation of a rigid peptide plane along an axis defined by two adjacent Cα carbon atoms." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001793 ! conformational transition
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001795
name: MDL solvent model format
def: "The Solvent MoDeL (MDL) file is an explicit molecular model input used for 1D-RISM and 3D-RISM (Reference Interaction Site Model) calculations in software like Amber. It supplies atomic coordinates, partial charges, and Lennard-Jones parameters for solvent molecules or ions." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001091 ! molecular topology format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001796
name: mean solvation force
def: "In computational chemistry and molecular dynamics, the mean solvation force is the average net force exerted by solvent molecules on a solute molecule, with all solvent degrees of freedom thermally averaged out. It represents the derivative of the potential of mean force (PMF) and drives conformational changes and structural binding in liquids." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001391 ! kinetic property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000107 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label force unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001797
name: atom position
def: "The atom position is the precise location of an atom in three-dimensional space. It is described by a set of three Cartesian coordinates (X, Y, Z) that specify its location relative to a defined origin. The collection of all atom positions for a molecule at a given instant constitutes a single \"frame\" of a simulation trajectory, and the evolution of these positions over time is the fundamental output of a molecular dynamics simulation." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001798
name: charge transfer energy
def: "An interaction energy component arising when a small amount of electron density moves from one molecule to another at close range. It is a quantum mechanical effect that a force field with fixed atomic charges cannot represent, yet it contributes measurably to hydrogen bonds and to interactions with metal ions. Capturing it needs a polarizable force field or a quantum mechanical treatment. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001294 ! energy
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000111 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label energy unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001799
name: reference energy
def: "An energy chosen as the zero point against which other energies in a calculation are reported. In a free energy calculation it is usually a known or simplified state, and every other state is quoted as a difference from it. Comparisons between systems are meaningless unless the same choice was made for both. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001294 ! energy
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000111 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label energy unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001800
name: physical property
def: "A physical property is a measurable characteristic of a substance or system that describes its physical state, such as its temperature, pressure, or density. In molecular simulations, these properties are calculated as averages over the course of the trajectory to describe the macroscopic state of the simulated system. These calculated properties are the primary outputs used to validate a simulation against experimental data and to understand the material characteristics of the molecular model." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001292 ! computed observable
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001801
name: atomic scattering factor
def: "A quantity giving how strongly a single atom scatters a wave, as a function of scattering angle. It rises with the number of electrons the atom has and falls as the angle increases, because the electron cloud has finite size. It is the per-atom term that structure factors are built from. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001800 ! physical property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001802
name: script
def: "A program written in a language that is interpreted as it runs rather than compiled first, used to drive a sequence of steps automatically. Being interpreted makes it quick to change and slow to execute, which suits work that is mostly waiting on other programs. Most of the workflow around a simulation is scripts rather than compiled code. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000001 ! software

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001803
name: interaction energy
def: "An energy arising from the forces between 2 or more separate molecules, or between distinct parts of 1 molecule, computed as the energy of the whole minus the sum of the energies of the parts held at the same geometry. It gathers the electrostatic and van der Waals contributions into a single number. It measures how strongly the parts are held together, but it is not a free energy, because it contains no entropy. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001294 ! energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001804
name: solute-water interaction energy
def: "An interaction energy between a solute and all the water molecules around it. It sums the electrostatic and van der Waals contributions over every solute-water pair. Following it through a trajectory shows how the solute's contact with water changes as it moves. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001803 ! interaction energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001805
name: water-water interaction energy
def: "An interaction energy summing the interactions of every water molecule with every other water molecule in a system. It measures how strongly the solvent holds itself together, separately from anything the solute does. Changes in it are how the cost of opening a cavity for a solute is seen. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001803 ! interaction energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001806
name: REMD round-trip time
def: "The REMD round-trip time is a diagnostic metric that measures how long it takes for a single simulation copy to travel through the full range of temperatures in a Replica Exchange Molecular Dynamics simulation. In this method, multiple simulations are run at different temperatures, and this metric tracks the time for one replica to go from the lowest to the highest temperature and back again. A short round-trip time indicates that the simulation is sampling conformations efficiently, which is necessary to obtain reliable results." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001391 ! kinetic property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000003 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label time unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001807
name: lifetime curve data
def: "Lifetime curve data is a graph that shows how long a specific molecular interaction, such as a hydrogen bond, typically lasts in a simulation. The curve usually plots the probability that an interaction, once formed, will still exist after a certain amount of time has passed. This data is generated by calculating the autocorrelation function of an interaction's existence over a trajectory, and fitting the curve provides a characteristic lifetime for that interaction." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001391 ! kinetic property
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001808
name: running average
def: "An average taken over a window that moves along a series, giving one value for each position of the window. It removes short-term fluctuation so that a slower trend can be seen. The width of the window sets what counts as fluctuation and what counts as trend. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001403 ! statistical property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001809
name: root-mean-square inner product
def: "A measure of how far 2 sets of collective modes span the same motions, computed from the inner products between their eigenvectors. A value near 1 means the 2 sets describe the same motion, and a value near 0 means they do not. It is how the modes from 2 simulations, or from a simulation and an experiment, are compared. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001403 ! statistical property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001810
name: RMS average correlation
def: "A single number summarising how strongly the parts of a molecule move together, computed as the root mean square of all the pairwise correlation values. It reduces a whole correlation matrix to 1 figure, so 2 simulations can be compared directly. It says how much correlated motion there is but not where. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: STATO:0000142 ! correlation coefficient
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001811
name: solute-solvent interaction energy density
def: "A quantity giving the average interaction energy between a solute and the solvent at each point in the space around it, stored on a 3-dimensional grid. Negative regions mark positions where a solvent molecule is held, positive regions mark positions it avoids. It differs from a density map in reporting energy rather than how often solvent is found. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001803 ! interaction energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001812
name: solvent-solvent interaction energy density
def: "A quantity giving, at each point of a 3-dimensional grid, the average interaction energy between solvent molecules there. Comparing it with the bulk value shows where a solute has disturbed the solvent's own structure. Regions where solvent holds itself together less well than in the bulk are where a ligand can most easily displace it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001803 ! interaction energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001813
name: normalized PME solvent energy
def: "An energy giving the average electrostatic interaction of a single solvent molecule with all the other solvent molecules, obtained by dividing the total solvent-solvent energy by the number of solvent molecules. Normalising this way makes the value comparable between systems holding different amounts of solvent. Without it, a larger box simply reports a larger number. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001294 ! energy
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001814
name: PME solvent energy density
def: "A quantity giving the average electrostatic energy of the solvent at each point of a 3-dimensional grid, computed with particle mesh Ewald. It shows where the solvent is electrostatically stabilised and where it is strained. It differs from a solvent density map in reporting energy rather than how much solvent is present. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001294 ! energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001815
name: normalized water-water interaction energy
def: "An interaction energy giving the average interaction of a single water molecule with its neighbours, obtained by dividing the total water-water energy by the number of water molecules. Dividing this way makes systems containing different amounts of water comparable. A shift in it marks water that is more or less strongly bound than in the bulk. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001803 ! interaction energy
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001816
name: dipole moment density
def: "A quantity giving the average direction and size of molecular dipoles at each point of a 3-dimensional grid. It shows how solvent molecules orient themselves around a solute, which a plain density map cannot. Regions where the dipoles all point the same way mark strong local electric fields. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001375 ! electronic property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001817
name: neighbor density
def: "A measure of how crowded the surroundings of an atom or molecule are, given as the number of neighbours within a chosen distance. It is the simplest description of local packing. Comparing it with the bulk value shows where a structure is more or less tightly packed than usual. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001818
name: normalized neighbor count
def: "A measure of how many molecules sit near a chosen point, divided by how many would be expected there if they were spread evenly. A value above 1 means molecules gather at that point and below 1 means they avoid it. Dividing out the expected number is what makes values at different distances comparable. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001348 ! coordination number
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001819
name: tetrahedral order parameter
def: "A measure of how closely the 4 nearest neighbours of a water molecule sit at the corners of a regular tetrahedron around it. Water in its ordinary hydrogen-bonded network is close to tetrahedral, and disruption shows as a fall in the value. It is how water near a surface or an ion is shown to be structured differently from bulk water. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001820
name: normalized tetrahedral order parameter
def: "A tetrahedral order parameter rescaled to run from −1/3 to 1, where 1 is a perfect tetrahedron and 0 is a random arrangement. The rescaling puts the value of random water at 0, so a number can be read directly as how much more ordered than random the arrangement is. It is the form usually reported. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001819 ! tetrahedral order parameter
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001821
name: chemical shift restraint simulation
def: "A chemical shift restraint simulation is a method where experimental Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (NMR) chemical shifts are used to guide a molecular dynamics simulation. An additional energy term is added that penalizes the simulation if the back-calculated chemical shifts from the trajectory do not agree with the experimental values. For experts, this method is a powerful tool for refining the accuracy of a structural ensemble to be consistent with experimental NMR data." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000364 ! restrained simulation method
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001822
name: pseudocontact shift restraint simulation
def: "A pseudocontact shift restraint simulation is a technique that uses a specific type of NMR data, known as pseudocontact shifts (PCS), to guide a simulation. PCS provide long-range distance and angular information relative to a paramagnetic metal center in the molecule. For structural biologists, using PCS restraints is a powerful method for determining the structure and dynamics of proteins and their complexes." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000364 ! restrained simulation method
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001823
name: direct dipolar coupling restraint simulation
def: "A direct dipolar coupling restraint simulation is a method that incorporates experimental NMR data from residual dipolar couplings (RDCs) to guide a MD simulation. RDCs provide information about the orientation of chemical bonds relative to an external magnetic field." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000364 ! restrained simulation method
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001824
name: residual chemical shift anisotropy restraint simulation
def: "A residual chemical shift anisotropy (RCSA) restraint simulation is a technique that uses NMR RCSA data to guide a MD simulation. RCSA provides information about the orientation of the chemical shift tensor for specific atoms, which is sensitive to local structure and dynamics." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000364 ! restrained simulation method
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001825
name: book-keeping energy term
def: "A value printed in a simulation's energy output that tracks part of the algorithm rather than any physical interaction. Thermostats and barostats that add extra degrees of freedom to the system report these, so that a conserved total can still be checked. Adding such a value into a reported potential energy is a common and silent error. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001294 ! energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001826
name: solvent reaction field potential
def: "An electrostatic method that represents the solvent beyond a cutoff distance as a uniform medium that polarizes in response to the charges inside, rather than as individual molecules. The polarized medium pushes back with a field that is added to the direct interactions. It is much cheaper than Ewald summation and less accurate, particularly for a system carrying a net charge. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001294 ! energy

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001827
name: collective variable
def: "A collective variable is a simplified coordinate that helps describe a complex process in a simulation, such as the distance between two proteins as they bind. Instead of tracking thousands of atomic coordinates, a collective variable reduces the system's motion to one or a few key parameters that capture the essence of the event. These variables are frequently used in enhanced sampling methods to focus computational effort on exploring a specific conformational change or reaction pathway." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000006 ! model
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001828
name: distance collective variable
def: "A distance collective variable is a simple coordinate that measures the separation between two specific atoms or groups of atoms. It is one of the most common variables used in simulations to track processes like a drug molecule unbinding from its target protein. Monitoring this distance provides a straightforward way to follow the progress of an association or dissociation event." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001827 ! collective variable
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001829
name: center of mass distance collective variable
def: "A center of mass distance collective variable measures the separation between the centers of mass of two groups of atoms, such as two entire proteins or a protein and a ligand. This provides a robust measure of the distance between whole molecular entities, averaging out the fast motions of individual atoms." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001828 ! distance collective variable
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001830
name: difference of center of mass distances collective variable
def: "This is a complex coordinate that tracks the difference between two separate center-of-mass distance measurements. It defines a reaction coordinate by calculating the absolute difference between two distinct COM distance measurements." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001828 ! distance collective variable
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001831
name: linear combination of distances collective variable
def: "A linear combination of distances is a mathematical expression used in molecular simulations to define a collective variable (CV). It sums or subtracts multiple specific atomic distances, each multiplied by a defined weight, creating a single reaction coordinate to track conformational changes like folding or chemical reactions." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001828 ! distance collective variable
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001832
name: angle collective variable
def: "An angle collective variable is a low-dimensional geometric descriptor that measures the angle formed by three specific atoms or groups of atoms during a simulation. This variable is used to monitor hinge-like motions, such as the opening and closing of domains in a protein." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001827 ! collective variable
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001833
name: center of mass angle collective variable
def: "A center of mass angle collective variable measures the angle formed by the centers of mass of three distinct groups of atoms. This is useful for describing the large-scale orientation of entire protein domains or molecules relative to one another, smoothing out the rapid fluctuations of individual atoms." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001827 ! collective variable
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001834
name: torsion collective variable
def: "A torsion collective variable is a coordinate that tracks the value of a specific dihedral angle, which describes the rotation around a chemical bond. These variables are fundamental for describing the detailed three-dimensional shape of a flexible molecule. They are often used in enhanced sampling simulations to accelerate the rotation of protein side chains or to explore different backbone conformations." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001827 ! collective variable
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001835
name: center of mass torsion collective variable
def: "A center of mass torsion collective variable is a dihedral angle defined by the centers of mass of four distinct groups of atoms, rather than four single atoms. This allows for the description of torsional or twisting motions between large molecular domains or subunits." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001834 ! torsion collective variable
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001836
name: sum of cosines of dihedrals collective variable
def: "This is a collective variable created by summing the cosine values of several different dihedral angles within a molecule. This mathematical combination creates a smooth, continuous variable that describes the collective rotational state of multiple bonds at once. It is often used in enhanced sampling methods to create a simplified coordinate that captures a complex, multi-dimensional conformational change." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001834 ! torsion collective variable
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001837
name: sum of sines of dihedrals collective variable
def: "This is a collective variable created by summing the sine values of several different dihedral angles within a molecule. This mathematical combination creates a smooth, continuous variable that describes the collective rotational state of multiple bonds at once. It is often used in enhanced sampling methods to create a simplified coordinate that captures a complex, multi-dimensional conformational change." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001834 ! torsion collective variable
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001838
name: paired dihedral collective variable
def: "A paired dihedral collective variable is a coordinate that combines two different dihedral angles, often the phi and psi backbone angles of a protein, into a single analysis. This is most commonly used to generate a two-dimensional free energy map, known as a Ramachandran plot, which reveals the energetically allowed conformations of the protein backbone. This analysis is fundamental for understanding protein structure and flexibility." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001834 ! torsion collective variable
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001839
name: pattern dihedral collective variable
def: "A pattern dihedral is a specialized Collective Variable (CV) used in MD to track the conformational transitions of a molecular system, such as protein folding or crystal polymorphs. It measures a weighted linear combination of multiple specific dihedral angles to act as a low-dimensional structural parameter, often replacing a complex set of atomic coordinates." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001834 ! torsion collective variable
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001840
name: radius of gyration collective variable
def: "The radius of gyration is a collective variable that measures the overall compactness of a molecule or a group of atoms. It quantifies how spread out the atoms are from the molecule's center of mass, with a smaller value indicating a more compact shape. This variable is commonly used as a simple metric to monitor large-scale conformational changes, such as the process of a protein folding into its native structure or unfolding." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001827 ! collective variable
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001841
name: multi-RMSD collective variable
def: "A multi-RMSD collective variable is a coordinate that simultaneously measures a molecule's structural similarity to several different reference structures. This is useful for tracking a molecule's transitions between multiple known functional states, such as an active, inactive, and an intermediate conformation. By monitoring which reference structure the molecule is closest to, this variable can map out the complex conformational landscape connecting different states." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001827 ! collective variable
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001842
name: number of bonds collective variable
def: "A number of bonds collective variable is a coordinate that counts the number of specific chemical bonds that exist at any given moment in a simulation. This variable is only meaningful when using a reactive force field that allows chemical bonds to form and break. It serves as a simple and direct way to track the progress of a chemical reaction by monitoring the creation or destruction of key covalent bonds." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001827 ! collective variable
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001843
name: handedness collective variable
def: "A handedness collective variable is a mathematical measure that quantifies the chirality, or \"handedness,\" of a molecular structure, such as the left-handed versus right-handed twist of a helix. This variable provides a continuous value that can track a molecule's transition between different chiral states during a simulation." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001827 ! collective variable
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001844
name: structure factor
def: "A complex quantity describing how strongly and with what phase a crystal scatters a wave in a given direction, summed over the atoms in its repeating unit. Its magnitude is what a diffraction experiment measures; its phase is not, which is the central difficulty of crystallography. The electron density follows from both by Fourier transform. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001800 ! physical property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001845
name: hardware
def: "The physical components of a computer system on which software runs: processors, memory, storage and the networks between machines. It is recorded alongside a simulation because how long the work took, and sometimes whether it is bit-for-bit reproducible, depends on it. The scientific result should not depend on it, and a difference between machines is a sign of a problem. (UNVERIFIED)" []

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001846
name: van der Waals radius
def: "A parameter giving the effective size of an atom, as the distance at which another atom begins to be repelled strongly. It is the radius of the hard sphere that best represents where Pauli repulsion overtakes the weak attraction between 2 non-bonded atoms. These radii set the molecular surface used in solvation models and in most measures of packing. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000272 ! radii set

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001847
name: Larmor frequency
def: "The Larmor frequency is the specific rate at which a magnetic particle, like an atomic nucleus, wobbles or \"precesses\" when placed in a strong external magnetic field. This is analogous to the way a spinning top wobbles in the Earth's gravitational field. This frequency is the fundamental principle behind all Nuclear Magnetic Resonance (NMR) experiments, as it determines the exact frequency of energy the nucleus will absorb." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001800 ! physical property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000105 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label frequency unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001848
name: QM/MM switching function
def: "A function that varies smoothly between 0 and 1 across a shell of space, used to blend an atom's quantum and classical descriptions as it crosses the boundary. Blending removes the jump in energy that an abrupt reassignment would cause. The width of the shell trades smoothness against how many atoms are in a mixed state at once. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001463 ! QM/MM model component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001849
name: convergence analysis
def: "A data analysis method that tests whether a simulation has run long enough for the quantity of interest to stop drifting. It follows a chosen property, such as total energy or a structural measure, and checks whether its running average settles over the later part of the trajectory. Without it, a reported average may reflect only the part of the trajectory that happened to be sampled. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000004 ! simulation analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001850
name: modeling and setup tool
def: "A modeling and setup tool is a type of software used to construct and prepare a molecular system before a simulation is run. This involves tasks like building a molecule from scratch, repairing a structure from an experimental database, or surrounding a protein with water molecules to mimic its natural environment. For an expert, these tools are essential for creating a chemically correct and physically stable starting point, which is a prerequisite for any meaningful simulation." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000158 ! simulation and modeling software
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001851 ! simulation engine
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001851
name: simulation engine
def: "A software program that performs a simulation itself, computing the forces on every atom and advancing their positions step by step. It takes a prepared system and a set of parameters and produces a trajectory. Everything else in a simulation workflow either prepares its input or analyses its output. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000158 ! simulation and modeling software

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001852
name: essential dynamics analysis
def: "A dynamics analysis method that reduces the motion in a trajectory to the few collective movements that account for most of the total fluctuation, using principal component analysis. The largest components are usually functionally meaningful, such as hinge bending between domains, while the smallest are thermal noise. It lets a trajectory of thousands of coordinates be discussed in terms of 2 or 3 motions. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000939 ! dynamics analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001853
name: correlation matrix
def: "A matrix whose entry at row i and column j gives the correlation between the fluctuations of quantities i and j. In trajectory analysis the quantities are usually the displacements of atoms or residues, so the matrix says which parts of the molecule move together. It is the input from which correlated motion and network analyses are computed. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001403 ! statistical property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001854
name: flexibility analysis
def: "A structural analysis method that identifies which parts of a molecule are rigid and which move, usually by computing the root-mean-square fluctuation of each atom or residue about its average position. The result separates a stable core from mobile loops and termini. It is also what simulated values are compared against experimental B-factors with. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000917 ! structural analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001855
name: contact map
def: "A contact map is a simplified 2D picture that shows which parts of a molecule are touching other parts of itself or other molecules. Contact maps provide a representation of molecular interactions or a protein foldings." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001856
name: native contact map
def: "A contact map recording which pairs of atoms or residues are in contact in a reference folded structure. It is built once from an experimental structure and then used as the benchmark a simulated conformation is scored against. The fraction of its contacts that a conformation reproduces is the usual measure of how folded that conformation is. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001855 ! contact map

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001857
name: non native contact map
def: "A non-native contact map is a contact map that shows the atomic touches in a misfolded or unfolded protein structure that are not present in its correct, functional shape. It is used to identify incorrect or transient interactions that may form during a simulation, especially in the study of protein folding pathways or misfolded states. Analyzing non-native contacts is crucial for understanding the formation of misfolded intermediates and kinetic traps on the folding landscape. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001855 ! contact map

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001858
name: hydrophobic patch
def: "Hydrophobic patches are clusters of non-polar, \"water-fearing\" atoms or amino acid side-chains that are exposed on the surface of a larger molecule, such as a protein. Because water molecules are highly polar, they are repelled by these non-polar regions and instead cluster together to interact with themselves." []
synonym: "hydrophobic patches" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001859
name: network analysis
def: "A data analysis method that represents a molecule as a graph, with atoms or residues as nodes and interactions or correlations as edges, and then applies graph theory to it. It finds residues that act as hubs and traces paths of correlated motion between distant sites. It is the usual way to reason about allosteric communication and about the reach of a mutation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000004 ! simulation analysis
property_value: skos:closeMatch operation:3927

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001860
name: pocket analysis
def: "A structural analysis method that finds cavities on or inside a molecule and measures their size, shape and how they change over time. A cavity that appears only briefly cannot be seen in a single experimental structure. Finding such transient cavities is one of the things simulation adds to a static structure. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000917 ! structural analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001861
name: ligand analysis
def: "An analysis method that examines the behaviour of a small molecule bound to a larger one during a simulation. It covers how the ligand moves within its site, which contacts it makes and keeps, and whether it stays bound at all. It treats the ligand as the subject rather than as part of the system. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000004 ! simulation analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001862
name: computing system
def: "The complete set of hardware on which a simulation runs, from a single workstation to a large cluster. It is recorded because how long a simulation took, and sometimes whether it is exactly reproducible, depends on it. Results should not depend on it, and a difference between machines is a sign that something is wrong. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001845 ! hardware
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001939 ! processing unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001863
name: ligand cavity analysis
def: "An analysis method that characterises the pocket a ligand occupies, measuring its volume, shape and how that changes as the simulation proceeds. A pocket that opens and closes during a run cannot be judged from the single structure a crystal gives. It is how a binding site is shown to be druggable or transient. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000984 ! distribution analysis
is_a: MOLSIM:001860 ! pocket analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001864
name: residence time
def: "Residence time is the average amount of time that a molecule, such as a water molecule or a ligand, spends in a specific, defined location, like a protein's binding site. It is calculated from a simulation by monitoring when a molecule enters a region and when it leaves, and then averaging this duration over many such events." []
synonym: "residence times" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001391 ! kinetic property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000003 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label time unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001865
name: pLDDT
def: "A confidence score produced by a structure prediction model for each residue, estimating how accurately that residue's position has been placed, on a scale from 0 to 100. It reports the model's confidence, not the accuracy of the structure, so a confident prediction can still be wrong. Regions scoring low are often genuinely disordered rather than badly predicted. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001403 ! statistical property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001866
name: backbone DH fluctuation
def: "Backbone DH fluctuations are a measure of how much the backbone of a protein wiggles and changes shape during a simulation. It specifically quantifies the fluctuations in the dihedral angles (DH) of the protein's backbone, which describe the rotations around the chemical bonds that connect the amino acids. Analyzing these fluctuations provides a detailed picture of the protein's flexibility and dynamics that is independent of its overall tumbling motion." []
synonym: "backbone DH fluctuations" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001867
name: membrane analysis
def: "Membrane analysis is a category of analysis methods specifically focused on characterizing the properties of lipid bilayer simulations. These methods are used to quantify the structural and dynamic behavior of the membrane itself and its interactions with other molecules, like embedded proteins. This includes calculating key properties such as the area per lipid, membrane thickness, and lipid order parameters to validate the simulation and understand membrane function." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000004 ! simulation analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001868
name: area per lipid
def: "The area per lipid is a fundamental biophysical metric representing the average cross-sectional surface area occupied by a single lipid molecule within a lipid bilayer. It is calculated by dividing the total area of the simulation box in the membrane plane by the number of lipids in one leaflet." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000004 ! simulation analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001869
name: lipid contact analysis
def: "Lipid contact analysis is an analysis method used to identify and quantify the interactions between lipid molecules and a protein embedded in the membrane. The analysis tracks which specific lipid molecules are in close contact with the protein over the course of a simulation. This method may be used for identifying potential \"hotspot\" lipid binding sites on a membrane protein and understanding the composition of the annular lipid shell." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001867 ! membrane analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001870
name: lipid density
def: "Lipid density is a measure of how tightly packed the lipid molecules are in a simulated cell membrane. It is typically calculated as a one-dimensional profile along the axis perpendicular to the membrane plane, showing the mass or electron density of different lipid components like headgroups and tails. Analyzing the lipid density profile is a fundamental check to ensure the simulated membrane has the correct structure and thickness, and it reveals how an embedded protein might locally perturb the lipid packing." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000052 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label mass density unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001871
name: lipid distribution analysis
def: "Lipid distribution refers to the spatial arrangement and composition of different types of lipid molecules within a simulated membrane. In a mixed bilayer, lipids are often not randomly distributed but can form distinct domains or clusters, and some lipids may preferentially accumulate around an embedded protein. Analyzing this distribution is crucial for understanding membrane organization and the specific lipid environment required for a membrane protein's function." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000984 ! distribution analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001872
name: lipid order parameter
def: "Lipid order parameters are a set of values that measure how well-aligned and ordered the flexible tails of lipid molecules are within a simulated cell membrane. A value of 1 means the lipid tail is perfectly straight and aligned perpendicular to the membrane surface, while a value of 0 means it is completely disordered. These parameters, specifically the deuterium order parameter (SCD), can be directly compared with experimental results from NMR spectroscopy, making them one of the most important metrics for validating the physical accuracy of a membrane simulation." []
synonym: "lipid order parameters" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001398 ! spectroscopic property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000186 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label dimensionless unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001873
name: membrane geometry
def: "Membrane geometry describes the overall three-dimensional shape and dimensions of a simulated cell membrane. This includes properties like the membrane's thickness, its lateral dimensions in the simulation box, and its overall shape, which can be planar, curved, or even vesicular. Characterizing the membrane geometry is a fundamental part of analyzing membrane simulations, ensuring the system is stable and providing the context for the behavior of embedded proteins." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001874
name: membrane curvature
def: "Membrane curvature is a measure of how much a simulated cell membrane is bent or curved. This property is calculated by fitting the positions of the lipid headgroups to a mathematical surface and then determining the local or average curvature of that surface. Analyzing membrane curvature is essential for studying processes like vesicle formation, membrane fusion, and the influence of proteins that induce or sense bending in the lipid bilayer." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001875
name: membrane width
def: "The membrane width is the thickness of a simulated cell membrane, measured from one side to the other, along the z-axis. It is typically defined as the distance between the peaks in the density profile of the lipid headgroups or phosphate atoms on opposite sides of the bilayer. The membrane width is a key structural parameter that is monitored to confirm a simulation is properly equilibrated and is used to understand how membrane proteins match their hydrophobic length to the surrounding lipid environment." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000001 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label length unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001876
name: pore dimension
def: "The pore dimension refers to the size and shape of a channel or tunnel that passes through a protein. This property is calculated by finding the radius of the narrowest point (the constriction site) and the overall profile of the channel's radius along its length. Analyzing the pore dimensions is critical for understanding how ion channels and transporters function, as it determines which molecules are small enough to pass through the membrane." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000001 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label length unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001877
name: DNA-bendability
def: "DNA bendability is the intrinsic mechanical property that describes how easily a DNA double helix can deviate from its ideal straight conformation by adopting a bent or curved structure. This property depends on the nucleotide sequence, with some sequences being inherently more flexible than others. Sequence-dependent bendability plays a key role in DNA packaging, nucleosome formation, and protein-DNA recognition, as many proteins induce or stabilize DNA bending upon binding." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001391 ! kinetic property
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-7544-0938

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001878
name: base breathing
def: "Base breathing refers to a specific and transient opening of one or more base pairs in a DNA or RNA double helix due to the temporary disruption of hydrogen bonds. During these events, the bases become transiently exposed to the surrounding solvent and more accessible without necessarily becoming fully unstacked from the helix. When this opening occurs at the ends of the duplex, it is commonly referred to as terminal fraying. These spontaneous opening events are a natural part of the helix's dynamics and are thought to be important for allowing proteins to access the genetic information encoded in the bases. Analyzing the frequency and duration of these motions provides insight into the local stability and accessibility of the DNA or RNA structure." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001793 ! conformational transition
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-7544-0938

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001879
name: helical parameter
def: "A helical parameter is one of a set of measurements that describe the detailed 3D shape of a DNA or RNA double helix. These parameters quantify the relative position and orientation of adjacent base pairs, including values for twist, roll, slide, and rise, which define the local helical geometry. Calculating these parameters from a simulation trajectory is the standard method for characterizing the sequence-dependent structure of nucleic acids and for distinguishing between different helical forms like A-DNA and B-DNA." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001358 ! nucleic acid parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001880
name: inter-BP correlation analysis
def: "Inter-base pair (Inter-BP) correlation analysis refers to the statistical coupling between the structural parameters of neighboring DNA base pairs or base-pair steps. It quantifies how variations in one helical parameter (e.g., roll, twist, or slide) are associated with changes in the same or different parameters at adjacent base pairs. These correlations reveal sequence-dependent structural coupling and cooperative conformational behavior within the DNA double helix, providing insight into its flexibility, mechanics, and recognition by DNA-bining proteins." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000342 ! correlation analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-7544-0938

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001881
name: nucleic acid backbone flexibility
def: "Nucleic acid backbone flexibility is a measure of the ability of the sugar-phosphate backbone of DNA or RNA to adopt different conformations through rotations about its backbone torsion angles. It is commonly characterized by analyzing the distributions and fluctuations during a simulation of the backbone dihedral angles (α, β, γ, δ, ε, ζ), the glycosidic angle (χ), and the sugar pucker. Backbone flexibility plays a fundamental role in determining the structural dynamics, mechanical properties, and biological functions of nucleic acids, influencing DNA bending and packaging as well as RNA folding and molecular recognition." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-7544-0938

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001882
name: nucleosome wrapping
def: "Nucleosome wrapping describes the way a long DNA molecule is spooled around a histone protein octamer, forming the fundamental repeating unit of chromatin. Studying nucleosome wrapping is essential for understanding how DNA is compacted and how access to the genetic code is regulated for gene expression." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001883
name: stiffness
def: "A property giving how strongly a structure resists being deformed by an applied force. For a single bond or angle it is set by the force constant in the force field; for a whole molecule or assembly it emerges from the network of interactions. It is the inverse of flexibility and is measured in force per unit displacement. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001800 ! physical property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001884
name: concerted motions analysis
def: "A dynamics analysis method that identifies groups of atoms whose movements are correlated, so that they travel together as a unit rather than fluctuating independently. It picks out large-scale events such as a protein domain shifting or twisting as a whole. Those events are usually the ones that matter for function, such as an active site opening and closing. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000342 ! correlation analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001885
name: trajectory meta analysis
def: "Trajectory meta-analysis refers to a higher level of analysis that involves comparing, contrasting, or combining the results from multiple, independent simulation trajectories. This can be used to improve statistical certainty, assess the convergence of a simulation, or identify the differences in dynamics between a wild-type protein and a mutant. This approach is essential for drawing robust conclusions that are not dependent on a single simulation run." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000004 ! simulation analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001886
name: trajectory comparison
def: "Trajectory comparison is a specific type of meta-analysis where two or more simulation trajectories are quantitatively compared to identify similarities and differences in their conformational sampling. This is often done by calculating metrics that measure the overlap of the conformational ensembles or by projecting the trajectories onto a common free energy landscape. This method is used to rigorously assess the impact of a mutation or ligand binding on a protein's dynamics." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001885 ! trajectory meta analysis
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001887
name: molecular simulation system
def: "A molecular simulation system is the complete collection of all the molecules included in a computational model for a simulation. This includes the main molecule of interest, such as a protein, as well as all the surrounding solvent molecules, ions, and any other components." []
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001888
name: carbohydrate system
def: "A carbohydrate system is a type of molecular simulation system where the primary molecules being studied are carbohydrates. This can range from a single sugar molecule in water to a complex polysaccharide or the glycan portion of a glycoprotein. These systems require specialized force fields and analysis techniques to accurately model the unique stereochemistry and flexibility of glycosidic linkages." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001887 ! molecular simulation system
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001889
name: complex system
def: "A complex system in this context refers to a molecular simulation system that contains two or more interacting macromolecules, or a macromolecule interacting with a smaller molecule like a drug. The primary focus of simulating such a system is to study the interactions, binding, and functional consequences of the molecules coming together." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001887 ! molecular simulation system
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001890
name: ligand complex system
def: "A ligand complex system is a type of complex system where the focus is on the interaction between a large macromolecule, such as a protein or DNA, and a smaller molecule, known as a ligand. These simulations are central to the field of drug discovery, where the goal is to understand how a potential drug molecule binds to its biological target." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001889 ! complex system
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001891
name: DNA-ligand system
def: "A DNA-ligand system is a type of molecular simulation system where the primary molecules being studied are DNA molecules interacting with small molecule ligands. These simulations are used to study how drugs or other small molecules bind to DNA, which can be a mechanism for anti-cancer or anti-viral therapies. These systems are important for understanding intercalation, groove binding, and the structural changes induced in DNA upon ligand binding." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001890 ! ligand complex system
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001892
name: RNA-ligand system
def: "An RNA-ligand system is a type of molecular simulation system where the primary molecules being studied are RNA molecules interacting with small molecule ligands. With the growing recognition of RNA as a major drug target, these simulations are becoming increasingly important for discovering and designing new therapeutics. These systems are challenging due to the high flexibility of RNA and the often subtle nature of the binding interactions." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001890 ! ligand complex system
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001893
name: protein-ligand system
def: "A molecular system consisting of a protein bound to a small molecule. It is the most commonly simulated kind of complex, because it is what drug binding is. What is usually studied is how tightly the 2 bind and which contacts hold them together. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001890 ! ligand complex system

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001894
name: hybrid complex system
def: "A hybrid complex system is a type of complex system composed of macromolecules from different biological classes. This most commonly refers to a complex formed between a protein and a nucleic acid, such as a transcription factor bound to DNA. Simulating these systems is essential for understanding many fundamental biological processes like gene regulation and DNA repair." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001889 ! complex system
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001895
name: nucleic acid complex system
def: "A nucleic acid complex system is a type of molecular simulation system where the primary molecules being studied are two or more nucleic acid molecules. This can include a standard DNA double helix, an RNA duplex, or more complex structures like DNA-RNA hybrids or multi-stranded RNA junctions. These simulations are crucial for understanding the structure and stability of the genetic material and functional RNA molecules." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001889 ! complex system
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001896
name: DNA-DNA system
def: "A DNA-DNA system is a type of molecular simulation system where the primary molecules being studied are two or more interacting strands of DNA. The most common example is the simulation of a DNA double helix to study its sequence-dependent structure and dynamics. These systems are also used to study more complex assemblies like DNA quadruplexes or Holliday junctions." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001895 ! nucleic acid complex system
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001897
name: DNA-RNA system
def: "A DNA-RNA system is a type of molecular simulation system where the primary molecules being studied are one ore more DNA strands interacting with one or more RNA strands. Such hybrid helices are important biological intermediates that occur during processes like transcription and reverse transcription. Simulating these systems is important for understanding the structural basis of these fundamental genetic processes." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001895 ! nucleic acid complex system
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001898
name: RNA-RNA system
def: "An RNA-RNA system is a type of molecular simulation system where the primary molecules being studied are two or more interacting RNA strands. This includes RNA duplexes, which are common in viral genomes and regulatory RNAs, as well as the vast and complex RNA assemblies that form the ribosome. Simulating these systems is critical for understanding the structural basis of RNA function and catalysis." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001895 ! nucleic acid complex system
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001899
name: protein complex system
def: "A molecular system in which a protein is bound to another macromolecule, either a second protein or a nucleic acid. Such a system is simulated to study how the 2 recognise each other and what holds them together. The interface between them is usually what the study is about. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001889 ! complex system

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001900
name: protein-DNA system
def: "A protein-DNA system is a type of molecular simulation system where the primary molecules being studied are proteins interacting with DNA molecules. These systems are fundamental to nearly all aspects of genetics, including DNA replication, repair, and the regulation of gene expression by transcription factors. Simulating these complexes is crucial for understanding the molecular basis of how proteins read and manipulate the genetic code." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001899 ! protein complex system
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001901
name: protein-RNA system
def: "A protein-RNA system is a type of molecular simulation system where the primary molecules being studied are proteins interacting with RNA molecules. These complexes, known as ribonucleoproteins, are central to a vast range of cellular processes, including protein synthesis by the ribosome and RNA splicing. Simulating these systems is essential for understanding the intricate interplay between proteins and RNA that governs much of cell biology." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001899 ! protein complex system
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001902
name: protein-protein system
def: "A protein complex system made up of 2 or more proteins bound to each other. Such pairings carry most cellular signalling and hold most large cellular structures together. What is usually studied is the interface: which residues touch, and how tightly. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001899 ! protein complex system

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001903
name: ion system
def: "A molecular system whose subject is the behaviour of ions, usually dissolved in water. Such systems are simulated to test how well a force field reproduces measured hydration free energies, activity coefficients and ion pairing. Getting ions right is a precondition for trusting any simulation of a charged biomolecule. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001887 ! molecular simulation system

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001904
name: lipid system
def: "A lipid system is a type of molecular simulation system where the primary molecule being studied are lipids, usually arranged as a bilayer in water. These simulations are used to study the fundamental physical properties of biological membranes, such as their phase behavior, fluidity, and permeability." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001887 ! molecular simulation system
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001905
name: nucleic acid system
def: "A nucleic acid system is a type of molecular simulation system where the primary molecules being studied are nucleic acids, such as a DNA duplex or a folded RNA. These simulations are typically performed to study the intrinsic structure, flexibility, and conformational dynamics of the nucleic acid." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001887 ! molecular simulation system
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001906
name: DNA system
def: "A DNA system is a type of molecular simulation system where the primary molecules being studied are DNA. This most often involves the simulation of a DNA double helix to investigate its sequence-dependent structure, flexibility, and dynamics. These simulations are used to understand properties like DNA bending and the transitions between different helical forms like A- and B-DNA." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001905 ! nucleic acid system
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001907
name: RNA system
def: "An RNA system is a type of molecular simulation system where the primary molecules being studied are RNA. Unlike DNA, RNA molecules often fold into complex and specific three-dimensional structures to perform their biological functions. Simulating these systems is crucial for understanding the principles of RNA folding and the structural basis of RNA catalysis." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001905 ! nucleic acid system
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001908
name: protein system
def: "A protein system is a type of molecular simulation system where the primary molecules being studied are proteins. These simulations are typically run to study its structural stability, intrinsic flexibility, and conformational changes. This is the most common type of simulation, fundamental to understanding how a protein's structure relates to its function." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001887 ! molecular simulation system
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001909
name: intrinsically disordered protein system
def: "An Intrinsically Disordered Protein (IDP) system refers to proteins or regions of proteins that lack a fixed, stable three-dimensional structure under physiological conditions. Instead of adopting a single rigid shape, they exist as dynamic ensembles of interconverting structures that drive vital cellular functions." []
synonym: "IDP system" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001908 ! protein system
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001910
name: membrane protein system
def: "A membrane protein system is a specific type of protein system where the protein is embedded within a lipid bilayer, mimicking its native environment in a cell membrane. These are among the most complex and computationally demanding types of simulations to set up and run. For experts, these simulations are essential for understanding the function of proteins that act as channels, transporters, and receptors in the cell." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001908 ! protein system
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001911
name: small molecule system
def: "A molecular system whose subject is one or more small organic molecules rather than a macromolecule. Such systems are simulated to obtain properties like solubility or partitioning, and to test force field parameters before they are used on anything larger. They are small enough that long simulations and many repeats are affordable. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001887 ! molecular simulation system

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001912
name: water system
def: "A molecular system containing water and nothing else. It is simulated to test how well a water model reproduces measured properties such as density, diffusion coefficient, dielectric constant and the temperature of maximum density. No water model reproduces all of them at once, so the choice depends on which matter for the intended study. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001887 ! molecular simulation system

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001913
name: simulation model resolution
def: "A property of a simulation model giving how much detail is kept when the real system is represented, from every atom down to whole domains as single sites. It is the first choice made when a model is built, because it fixes both what the model can show and what it costs. The levels below it are the named steps on that scale. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000006 ! model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001914
name: all atom
def: "All-atom is a simulation model resolution where every atom in the system, including all hydrogen atoms, is represented as an individual particle with its own parameters. This provides the highest level of structural detail and is the standard for most high-resolution biomolecular simulations." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001913 ! simulation model resolution
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001915 ! coarse grained
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001915
name: coarse grained
def: "A simulation model resolution in which several atoms are represented by 1 interaction site. Cutting the particle count and smoothing the energy landscape allows both larger systems and a longer timestep, so far longer times become reachable. Nothing smaller than a site can be observed in such a model. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001913 ! simulation model resolution

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001916
name: mesoscopic
def: "A simulation model resolution in which whole proteins, or long segments of a polymer, are each represented by a single site. It is the coarsest level at which particles are still tracked individually, above which a continuum description is used instead. It is used for assembly and phase behaviour, where molecular detail does not affect the result. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001913 ! simulation model resolution

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001917
name: united-atom
def: "A simulation model resolution in which non-polar hydrogens are merged into the heavy atom they are bonded to, while all other atoms are kept. It removes roughly half the particles in an organic system at almost no cost in accuracy, because those hydrogens carry little charge. It sits between all-atom and coarse-grained resolution. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001913 ! simulation model resolution

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001918
name: MDAnalysis
def: "MDAnalysis is an open-source Python library used for the analysis of molecular dynamics simulation trajectories. It provides a flexible and object-oriented framework that allows users to read, write, and manipulate atomic coordinate data from a wide variety of simulation packages. MDAnalysis is a powerful tool for writing custom, complex, and reproducible analysis scripts in a familiar Python environment." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000251 ! trajectory processing tool
is_a: MOLSIM:001566 ! software library
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001919
name: MDTraj
def: "MDTraj is a modern, open-source Python library designed for the fast and efficient analysis of molecular dynamics trajectories. It excels at reading and writing a very broad range of trajectory and topology file formats, making it highly interoperable. MDTraj provides a fast and powerful toolkit for performing common structural and time-series analyses on simulation data." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000251 ! trajectory processing tool
is_a: MOLSIM:001566 ! software library
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001920
name: ProDy
def: "A Python library for analysing protein structural dynamics, covering structure file parsing, conformational ensemble analysis and the calculation of collective modes. It brings normal mode analysis and elastic network models into a scripting environment. It is used to compare simulated motion with motion inferred from experimental structures. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001566 ! software library

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001921
name: BioBB
def: "BioBB, or BioExcel Building Blocks, is a library of Python wrappers that create a standardized interface for many common biomolecular simulation programs like GROMACS and AmberTools. Each building block performs a specific task, such as running an energy minimization or calculating an RMSD, using a consistent input and output format. For computational biologists, BioBB provides an interoperable toolkit for constructing complex, reproducible, and portable simulation workflows." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001566 ! software library
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001922
name: 3DMol.js
def: "3Dmol.js is a JavaScript library used for creating interactive, 3D visualizations of molecular structures directly within a web browser. It allows web developers to embed high-quality molecular viewers into websites and web applications without requiring any plugins. For creators of online scientific resources, 3Dmol.js provides a lightweight and versatile tool for displaying and interacting with molecular data on the web." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001566 ! software library
is_a: MOLSIM:002041 ! molecular structure visualization tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001923
name: NGL
def: "NGL Viewer is a WebGL-based JavaScript library for the fast and high-quality visualization of large molecular complexes and trajectories in the web browser. It is designed for high-performance rendering, enabling smooth, interactive exploration of even very large structures like ribosomes or viral capsids." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001566 ! software library
is_a: MOLSIM:002041 ! molecular structure visualization tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001924
name: Open Babel
def: "Open Babel is a versatile software program and library, often called a \"chemical toolbox,\" for reading, writing, and converting between over 100 different chemical file formats. It allows users to easily interconvert between the various file types used by different simulation, modeling, and visualization programs. Its powerful interoperability makes it an essential utility in many simulation and modeling workflows for preparing and manipulating molecular structure files." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000166 ! file conversion tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001925
name: editconf
def: "A system preparation program in the GROMACS suite that manipulates a structure file: converting between formats, setting the size and shape of the box, centring the molecule and rotating or translating it. It changes how a system is placed rather than what it contains. It is normally run before the box is filled with solvent. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001956 ! system packing and solvation tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001926
name: gmx
def: "A command-line program that provides access to every tool in the GROMACS suite through a single entry point, with the tool named as its first argument. It is not itself a simulation engine; it dispatches to the preparation, simulation and analysis programs. Almost every GROMACS command in a published protocol begins with it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000251 ! trajectory processing tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001927
name: CHARMM-GUI
def: "CHARMM-GUI is a powerful and widely used web server that provides a graphical interface for generating input files for a wide variety of complex biomolecular simulations. It automates many difficult and error-prone setup tasks, such as building lipid membranes, solvating proteins, and preparing systems for free energy calculations." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000225 ! membrane packing tool
is_a: MOLSIM:000714 ! tool web server
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001928
name: Modeller
def: "Modeller is a widely used computer program for generating three-dimensional models of proteins through homology or comparative modeling. It predicts a protein's structure by using the known structure of a related protein as a template and satisfying spatial restraints. For researchers, Modeller is a powerful tool to create high-quality structural hypotheses for proteins whose experimental structures have not yet been determined, providing a starting point for further simulation." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001958 ! homology modeling tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001929
name: ACEMD
def: "A molecular dynamics program written to run on NVIDIA graphics processors. It was among the first engines to reach microsecond simulations on a single desktop machine. Its speed comes from targeting one kind of hardware rather than supporting many. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000160 ! molecular dynamics engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001930
name: SAMSON
def: "A software platform for building, viewing and simulating molecular systems at the nanometre scale. Its functions are supplied by separate modules, so users and developers can add capabilities without changing the platform itself. That modular design is what distinguishes it from a fixed-feature suite. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001664 ! software suite

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001931
name: Blender
def: "Blender is a free and open-source 3D computer graphics software suite used for creating animated films, visual effects, art, and 3D printed models. While not a dedicated molecular viewer, it is often used by computational biologists to import molecular structures and create high-quality, cinematic renderings and scientific animations. Blender provides a professional-level tool for producing visually stunning figures and movies for publications and presentations." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002041 ! molecular structure visualization tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001932
name: Jmol
def: "Jmol is a free, open-source molecular viewer for 3D chemical structures, written in the Java programming language. Because it is Java-based, it can run on a wide variety of operating systems and was often used as a tool for displaying molecules on websites. For researchers and educators, Jmol provided a versatile and accessible tool for basic molecular visualization and analysis. Nowadays replaced by JavaScript and openGL tools such as JSMol, NGL or Mol*." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002041 ! molecular structure visualization tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001933
name: MolStar
def: "MolStar (Mol*) is a modern, web-based toolkit for visualizing and analyzing large-scale molecular data. It is designed for high-performance rendering of extremely large structures, such as those from cryo-electron microscopy, directly in a web browser. For the structural biology community, Mol* is the state-of-the-art viewer integrated into databases like the PDB for exploring complex biological assemblies." []
synonym: "Mol*" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:002041 ! molecular structure visualization tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001934
name: UCSF Chimera
def: "A visualization and analysis program for molecular structures and related data, extensible through user-written modules. It produces publication-quality images and handles structures together with density maps and sequence data. It has been superseded for large data by its successor, but remains in use because many published workflows depend on it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000490 ! structure preparation tool
is_a: MOLSIM:002041 ! molecular structure visualization tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001935
name: YASARA
def: "A molecular modelling and simulation software suite covering structure prediction, structure cleaning, simulation and analysis in one program. Its steps are heavily automated, so a full workflow can be run without assembling separate tools. That automation is what distinguishes it from suites that expose each step separately. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000160 ! molecular dynamics engine
is_a: MOLSIM:001664 ! software suite

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001936
name: high-performance computing cluster system
def: "A computing system consisting of a group of individual computers (nodes) linked together by a high-speed network to function as a single, coordinated system for parallel processing. This encompasses a wide range of scales, from small laboratory clusters to massive institutional systems. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "HPC system" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001862 ! computing system
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001938 ! cloud computing platform system

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001937
name: supercomputer system
def: "A high-performance computing cluster system that operates at or near the maximum performance rate for computers at the time of its deployment. Supercomputers are typically characterized by massive scale, specialized high-speed interconnects, and act as national or global resources for the most demanding computational tasks (e.g., Summit, Frontier, or specialized MD machines like Anton). (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001936 ! high-performance computing cluster system

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001938
name: cloud computing platform system
def: "A cloud computing platform is a service that provides on-demand access to powerful computing resources over the internet. This allows researchers to run large-scale simulations on virtual clusters hosted by commercial providers like Amazon Web Services (AWS) or Google Cloud. This approach offers flexible access to the latest hardware, such as high-end GPUs, without the cost and maintenance of owning a physical supercomputer. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001862 ! computing system

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001939
name: processing unit
def: "The hardware component that performs the arithmetic and logic of a computation. A general-purpose one handles varied work a few operations at a time, while a graphics processor performs thousands of similar operations at once. Which kind a simulation runs on changes its speed by a large factor. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001845 ! hardware

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001940
name: central processing unit
def: "The general-purpose processor of a computer, which handles varied instructions a few at a time with a large amount of fast local memory. It runs the parts of a simulation that are not easily done many at once, such as file handling and control logic. It is much slower than a graphics processor at the force calculation and much faster at everything irregular. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001939 ! processing unit
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001941 ! graphics processing unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001941
name: graphics processing unit
def: "A processor holding thousands of small cores that carry out the same operation on many pieces of data at once. Computing the force on every atom is exactly that kind of work, which is why simulations run several times faster on one. It performs badly on work that branches differently for each item. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001939 ! processing unit
property_value: skos:closeMatch NCIT:C64196

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001942
name: application-specific integrated circuit
def: "A chip built to perform one particular computation, with its circuitry fixed at manufacture. Giving up all flexibility buys a very large gain in speed and energy efficiency for that one task. The Anton machines, built solely for molecular dynamics, are the example in this field. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "ASIC" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001939 ! processing unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001943
name: network interconnect
def: "The high-speed communication hardware linking the machines of a cluster to one another. A simulation spread across many machines exchanges data every step, so the delay in that link can matter more than the speed of the processors. It is what limits how far one simulation can usefully be spread. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001845 ! hardware

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001944
name: pressure
def: "A thermodynamic property giving the force per unit area the particles exert on the boundaries of the simulation box. It is computed from the virial, which combines the positions of the atoms with the forces between them. It fluctuates far more violently than temperature, often by hundreds of atmospheres, so only a long average is meaningful. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001293 ! thermodynamic property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000109 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label pressure unit
property_value: skos:closeMatch SBO:0000279

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001946
name: volume
def: "A thermodynamic property giving the size of the periodic simulation box. It is fixed in a constant-volume simulation and varies in a constant-pressure one, where it is the quantity the barostat adjusts. Its average, divided into the mass in the box, gives the density that is compared with experiment. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001293 ! thermodynamic property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000095 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label volume unit
property_value: skos:closeMatch SBO:0000468

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001947
name: ethernet
def: "A networking technology used to connect computers in most ordinary local networks. It is cheap and universal, and its delay in delivering a message is higher than a specialised cluster network's. A simulation spread across machines connected this way spends much of its time waiting. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001943 ! network interconnect
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001948 ! infiniband

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001948
name: infiniband
def: "A networking technology built for computing clusters, with very low delay and the ability to move data straight between machines' memory without involving their processors. That directness is what makes it suitable for a simulation whose parts must exchange data at every step. It is the most common cluster network. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001943 ! network interconnect

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001949
name: omni-path
def: "A networking technology built by Intel for connecting the nodes of a supercomputer, competing with InfiniBand on delay and bandwidth. It appeared in several large machines and is no longer developed by its originator. It is recorded because published simulations ran on machines using it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001943 ! network interconnect

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001950
name: MDrepo
def: "MDRepo is a public repository dedicated to the archival and sharing of molecular dynamics simulation data generated by the research community. It provides a standardized infrastructure for scientists to upload, store, and retrieve simulation trajectories and associated metadata. By centralizing access to these datasets, MDRepo promotes the reproducibility and secondary analysis of biomolecular simulations." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001119 ! database web server
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001951
name: ATLAS
def: "ATLAS is a specialized database that stores a comprehensive collection of standardized all-atom molecular dynamics simulations of proteins. It combines simulation trajectories with analyses of protein flexibility and dynamics, linked to experimental structural data. This resource allows researchers to explore the dynamic properties of a wide range of protein families in a consistent and comparative manner." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001119 ! database web server
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001952
name: GPCRmd
def: "GPCRmd is a community-driven database and web platform specifically focused on molecular dynamics simulations of G-protein-coupled receptors (GPCRs). It provides a repository for storing simulation trajectories of this important protein family, along with tools for interactive visualization and analysis. This resource aids researchers in understanding the complex signaling mechanisms and conformational landscapes of GPCRs." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001119 ! database web server
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001953
name: InflateGro
def: "InflateGRO is a utility script used to construct lipid membrane systems by packing lipids around a membrane protein. It works by initially expanding the distance between lipid molecules and then iteratively shrinking the system back to a realistic density while removing lipids that overlap with the protein. This method automates the challenging process of embedding a protein structure into a tight, pre-equilibrated lipid bilayer." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000225 ! membrane packing tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001954
name: MemProtMD
def: "MemProtMD is a database that provides a collection of coarse-grained molecular dynamics simulations for membrane proteins found in the Protein Data Bank. It uses an automated pipeline to insert protein structures into lipid bilayers and simulate their equilibrium dynamics. This resource offers insights into the membrane orientation, lipid interactions, and stability of a vast number of membrane proteins." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000225 ! membrane packing tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001955
name: crystallographic build tool
def: "A crystallographic build tool is a software utility used to reconstruct a full crystal lattice or supercell from the asymmetric unit provided in a structure file. It applies the specific symmetry operations defined by the space group to generate the complete crystallographic packing environment." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001556 ! system setup tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001956
name: system packing and solvation tool
def: "A software program that defines the shape and size of a simulation box and fills it with solvent molecules and ions at a target density and concentration. It places the molecules so that none overlap, which a random arrangement would not achieve. It is the step that turns a lone molecule into a system with an environment. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001556 ! system setup tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001957
name: structure cleaning and manipulation tool
def: "A software program that standardises and repairs the formatting of a molecular structure file, by renumbering residues, correcting atom names, removing unwanted records and splitting or joining chains. The work is clerical rather than scientific, but nothing downstream runs until it is done. Most structure files from experimental sources need it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000490 ! structure preparation tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001958
name: homology modeling tool
def: "A homology modeling tool is a software program designed to predict the three-dimensional structure of a protein based on its amino acid sequence and experimentally determined template structures. It constructs a model by mapping the target sequence onto the backbone of a homologous protein and computationally refining the loops and side chains to resolve steric conflicts. For experts, these tools are a solution for generating starting structural models when high-resolution crystallography or NMR data for the specific target is unavailable." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001850 ! modeling and setup tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001959
name: AutoDock Vina
def: "AutoDock Vina is an open-source software tool for molecular docking that predicts the preferred orientation and binding affinity of a small molecule to a protein receptor. It utilizes a sophisticated iterated local search global optimizer combined with an empirical scoring function to efficiently explore the conformational space of the ligand." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000162 ! docking tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:002049 ! AutoDock
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001960
name: nucleic acid analysis tool
def: "A nucleic acid analysis tool is a specialized software program designed to characterize the geometry and topology of DNA and RNA structures. It calculates parameters such as base-pair step geometry (roll, tilt, twist), groove dimensions, and sugar pucker to describe the helical conformation." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000164 ! analysis tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001961
name: scattering analysis tool
def: "A software program that computes the scattering pattern a structure or trajectory would produce in an experiment. Comparing that computed pattern with a measured one is how a simulated ensemble is tested against solution data. It turns coordinates into something directly comparable with a measurement. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000164 ! analysis tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001962
name: titration analysis tool
def: "A software program that works out which acidic and basic groups in a molecule carry a proton, and at what acidity they gain or lose one. It either predicts those values from the structure or measures them from a simulation that allowed protons to move. Which groups are charged changes a molecule's behaviour, so this must be settled before a simulation is set up. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000164 ! analysis tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001963
name: solvation analysis tool
def: "A software program that characterises the structure and thermodynamics of the solvent around a solute. It computes quantities such as radial distribution functions, solvent density maps, and the solvation free energies given by integral equation theories. It is how a hydration shell is described quantitatively rather than by eye. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000164 ! analysis tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001964
name: TM-align
def: "An algorithm and program that superposes 2 protein structures and scores how similar their folds are, on a scale that does not depend on how long the proteins are. Length independence is what lets a short and a long protein be compared meaningfully. It finds the correspondence between residues itself, so no alignment need be supplied. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001684 ! match analysis tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001965 ! DALI

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001965
name: DALI
def: "DALI (Distance Alignment) is a software method that compares protein structures by analyzing their internal distance matrices rather than their rigid-body superposition. This approach allows to detect distant evolutionary relationships and structural similarities even when the proteins have undergone significant conformational changes or distortions." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001684 ! match analysis tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001966
name: LS-align
def: "LS-align is an algorithm designed for atom-level structural comparison of ligand molecules. The target function of LS-align is a combination of inter-atom distance, atom mass, and chemical bond connections; while the final atom-to-atom alignment is generated by maximizing such target function through an enhanced-greedy based, iterative heuristic search algorithm." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001684 ! match analysis tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001967
name: replica exchange algorithm
def: "An enhanced sampling algorithm that manages multiple parallel simulation replicas running at different thermodynamic states (e.g., temperatures or Hamiltonians). It evaluates and periodically attempts to swap the states of these replicas based on a Metropolis-style acceptance criterion to facilitate barrier crossing and improve conformational sampling." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001740 ! enhanced sampling algorithm
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001968
name: alchemical analysis tool
def: "A software program that computes a free energy difference from simulations run along a path of non-physical intermediate states. It implements estimators such as the multi-state Bennett acceptance ratio or thermodynamic integration. It is separate from the simulation engine that generated the states. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001564 ! free energy analysis tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001969
name: free energy surface analysis tool
def: "A free energy surface analysis tool is a software utility used to reconstruct the multidimensional free energy landscape of a system from enhanced sampling simulation data. It processes the history of visited states or applied biases, such as those from metadynamics or umbrella sampling, to generate a potential of mean force (PMF) map. Enable the visualization of low-energy basins and transition barriers along specific collective variables or reaction coordinates." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001564 ! free energy analysis tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001970
name: parameter assignment tool
def: "A software program that inspects a molecule, works out which atom type each atom belongs to, and looks up the parameters that follow. The assignment is made from element and bonding environment. It is where a general force field becomes a specific set of numbers for one molecule. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000172 ! topology and parameterization tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001971
name: charge derivation tool
def: "A software program that computes partial atomic charges for a molecule so it can be simulated with a force field. The method used must match the one the force field's own charges were derived with, or the molecule will interact too strongly or too weakly with everything else. It is run once per new molecule. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000172 ! topology and parameterization tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001972
name: residue template tool
def: "A software program that produces the library file defining a new building block: its atoms, their types and charges, the bonds between them and the atoms that join it to its neighbours. Once written, that template lets the block be used anywhere in a chain. It is what makes a non-standard residue reusable rather than a one-off. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000172 ! topology and parameterization tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001973
name: AMBERGS
def: "A force field of the AMBER family with its backbone rotation terms refitted to correct a bias towards helical structure in the parameters it was derived from. The bias mattered because a simulation would form helices whatever the sequence. It targets peptides and small proteins where secondary structure is the property under study. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000009 ! protein force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001974
name: GROMOS 53a6
def: "A GROMOS parameter set whose non-bonded parameters were refitted to reproduce free energies of transfer between water and cyclohexane for amino acid analogues. That refit corrected a known bias towards over-stabilising folded structures. It became the standard choice for protein simulation in that family. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001531 ! united-atom force field
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:001975 ! GROMOS 53a5

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001975
name: GROMOS 53a5
def: "A GROMOS parameter set fitted to reproduce properties of biomolecules in non-polar surroundings, such as the interior of a membrane. It shares its bonded parameters with the aqueous-fitted set of the same generation and differs in the non-bonded ones. The 2 are alternatives chosen by environment, not successive versions. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001531 ! united-atom force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001976
name: GROMOS 43a1p
def: "A GROMOS parameter set extending an earlier one with parameters for phosphorylated amino acids. Standard parameter sets do not include them, because phosphorylation is a modification rather than a standard residue. It covers phosphoserine, phosphothreonine and phosphotyrosine. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001531 ! united-atom force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001977
name: GROMOS-87
def: "A force field of the GROMOS family, released in the late 1980s, in which non-polar hydrogens are merged into the heavy atoms they are bonded to. It set the parameter conventions the later GROMOS revisions were built on. It is of historical interest rather than in current use. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001531 ! united-atom force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001978
name: PLUMED
def: "PLUMED is an open-source software library designed to analyze molecular dynamics simulations and perform enhanced sampling of free energy landscapes. It functions as middleware that interfaces with various simulation engines to calculate collective variables and apply biasing potentials in real-time." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001566 ! software library
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001979
name: domain decomposition algorithm
def: "A parallel computing method that divides the simulation box into regions and gives each to a different processor, which handles the atoms currently inside it. Because interactions are short-ranged, a processor mostly needs data from its own region and its immediate neighbours. It is what allows a single simulation to use hundreds of processors at once. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000382 ! simulation control algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001980
name: GROMOS force field
def: "A family of force fields in which non-polar hydrogens are merged into the heavy atoms they are bonded to, with parameters fitted to reproduce measured free energies of transfer between water and a non-polar liquid. Fitting to transfer free energies is what distinguishes it, since that quantity governs how a molecule partitions between environments. The family is identified by a number naming each parameter set. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001531 ! united-atom force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001981
name: GROMOS96
def: "The GROMOS96 force field is a family of united-atom molecular mechanics parameter sets developed in conjunction with the GROMOS96 simulation software. It treats non-polar hydrogen atoms as part of the heavy atoms they are bonded to (e.g., CH, CH2, CH3) to reduce computational complexity while maintaining accuracy for biomolecular simulations." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001531 ! united-atom force field
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001982
name: MARTINI force field
def: "A coarse-grained force field that maps roughly 4 heavy atoms and their hydrogens onto 1 interaction bead, with beads classified by polarity, charge and hydrophobicity. The small number of bead types makes it transferable across lipids, proteins and carbohydrates. It is the most widely used coarse-grained model for membrane simulation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000736 ! coarse-grained force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001983
name: OPLS-AA/M
def: "A force field of the OPLS all-atom family with its protein parameters refitted again, against both quantum calculations and measured properties of peptides in solution. Fitting to solution data as well as to isolated molecules is what distinguishes it from the earlier revision. It is the current OPLS choice for proteins. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000759 ! OPLS-AA

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001984
name: OPLS-AA/L
def: "A force field of the OPLS all-atom family with its protein backbone and side-chain rotation terms refitted against high-level quantum calculations. The refit corrected secondary structure preferences that the original parameters got wrong. It was the standard OPLS choice for proteins before the later revision. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000759 ! OPLS-AA

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001985
name: polarizable water
def: "A computer model of water that allows the electric charge distribution within each molecule to shift in response to its surroundings. Unlike fixed-charge models, it explicitly includes terms for electronic polarization, often via induced dipoles, Drude oscillators, or fluctuating charges. For experts, these models (e.g., TIP4P-FQ, AMOEBA water) capture non-additive many-body effects and are essential for accurately simulating interfaces, ion solvation, and spectroscopic properties. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000014 ! water model force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001986
name: minimum image convention
def: "A rule used in computer simulations to calculate forces in a repeating, infinite system. It states that a particle should interact only with the nearest instance of another particle, whether that instance is in the same simulation box or a neighboring periodic copy. For experts, this approximation is valid when the cutoff radius is less than half the shortest box vector, ensuring particles do not interact with their own periodic images (except in small systems where this artifact is intentional). (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000037 ! algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001987
name: minimum distance
def: "A measurement of the closest separation between two distinct groups of atoms in a structure. It is calculated by evaluating the Euclidean distance between all possible atom pairs from the two groups and selecting the smallest value. This metric is frequently used in trajectory analysis to define contact maps, monitor collision avoidance, or serve as a collective variable for pathway sampling." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000001 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label length unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001988
name: helmholtz free energy
def: "A measure of the useful energy available to do work in a system held at constant temperature and volume. It is a thermodynamic potential defined as the internal energy minus the product of temperature and entropy (A=U−TS). For experts, this quantity is the natural free energy ensemble for NVT (canonical) simulations and is often calculated using methods like thermodynamic integration or Bennett acceptance ratio. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001314 ! free energy property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001989
name: gibbs free energy
def: "A measure of the maximum reversible work a system can perform at constant temperature and pressure. Defined as the enthalpy minus the product of temperature and entropy (G=H−TS), it determines the direction of spontaneous change and chemical equilibrium. For experts, this is the primary thermodynamic potential of interest in NPT simulations and is used to calculate binding affinities, solvation energies, and phase equilibria. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001314 ! free energy property
property_value: skos:closeMatch SBO:0000580

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001990
name: virial
def: "A mathematical quantity used to calculate the pressure of a system based on the positions and forces of its atoms. It is derived from the virial theorem and involves summing the dot products of atomic coordinates and the forces acting upon them. For experts, in molecular dynamics, the instantaneous virial is essential for the pressure tensor calculation and the function of barostat algorithms in NPT simulations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001293 ! thermodynamic property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001991
name: autocorrelation function
def: "A statistical tool that measures how much a property's value at one time resembles its value at a later time. It quantifies the \"memory\" of a system by calculating the correlation between a time-series signal and a time-shifted version of itself. For experts, calculated as C(t)=⟨A(0)A(t)⟩, it is fundamental for computing transport coefficients (like diffusion via Green-Kubo relations) and relaxation times. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001421 ! correlation function

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001992
name: cromer's method
def: "A mathematical approach used to estimate how strongly atoms scatter X-rays. It approximates the atomic scattering factor using a sum of Gaussian functions based on quantum mechanical calculations of electron density. For experts, this parametrization (often the Cromer-Mann coefficients) is standard in crystallography and simulation analysis for calculating theoretical structure factors and comparing simulation trajectories with experimental X-ray scattering data (SAXS/WAXS). (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001696 ! analysis algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001993
name: accelerated weight histogram
def: "An enhanced sampling method that applies a bias which is updated as the simulation runs, driven by how evenly the chosen coordinate has been visited so far. The bias grows where the system has spent time and shrinks where it has not, which pushes it into unvisited regions. The free energy profile is recovered from the bias that was needed. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001994
name: reaction coordinate
def: "A simplified variable used to track the progress of a chemical reaction or a complex structural change. It reduces the motion of thousands of atoms into a single parameter that describes the transition from a starting state to a final state." []
comment: Distinct from the object property MOLSIM_001036. Modeled here as a Class (the variable itself).
is_a: MOLSIM:001827 ! collective variable
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001995
name: position restraints
def: "A computational technique used to anchor atoms to specific locations in 3D space during a simulation. It applies an artificial harmonic energy penalty proportional to the square of the displacement of an atom from a reference coordinate. For experts, these are heavily used during system equilibration (to relax solvent around a fixed solute) or in free energy calculations to prevent ligand drift, typically defined with a force constant k in units of kJ/(mol*nm^2) or kcal/mol." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001552 ! restraint potential
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001996
name: Urey-Bradley potential
def: "A specific interaction term used in molecular mechanics force fields to refine the vibrational behavior of bond angles. It introduces a harmonic potential acting on the distance between the two atoms at the ends of a bond angle (the 1-3 interaction), effectively placing a spring across the angle. For experts, this term is a hallmark of the CHARMM force field family, used to couple bond stretching and angle bending modes to better reproduce vibrational frequencies obtained from spectroscopy. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000331 ! force field component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001997
name: exclusions
def: "A configuration setting or list within a molecular topology that identifies pairs of atoms whose non-bonded interactions (electrostatic and van der Waals) should be ignored during force calculation. These exclusions typically apply to atoms connected by one or two covalent bonds (1-2 and 1-3 pairs) to prevent conflicts with bonded energy terms. For experts, exclusion rules vary by force field (e.g., AMBER scales 1-4 interactions, while CHARMM or GROMOS may exclude them entirely), making this a critical factor in topology conversion. (UNVERIFIED)" []
comment: Defines the concept of the exclusion list/rule.
is_a: MOLSIM:001185 ! non-bonded interaction parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001998
name: holonomic constraint
def: "A mathematical restriction applied to a molecular system that depends only on the coordinates of the particles and time, reducing the system's degrees of freedom. In molecular dynamics, these typically manifest as fixed bond lengths or rigid water geometries (f(r1,r2,…)=0). For experts, integrating these constraints requires specialized algorithms like SHAKE, RATTLE, or LINCS to solve for the Lagrange multipliers that maintain the geometric requirements. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001201 ! constraint and restraint parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:001999
name: smooth particle mesh Ewald
def: "An enhanced version of the Particle Mesh Ewald method that uses Euler exponential splines (B-splines) to interpolate charge density onto a grid. Unlike standard PME which uses Lagrangian interpolation, SPME allows the potential to be differentiated analytically to obtain forces, improving energy conservation and accuracy. For experts, this is the standard implementation in packages like AMBER and GROMACS (Essmann et al., 1995), offering N log N scaling. (UNVERIFIED)" []
comment: SPME
is_a: MOLSIM:000054 ! particle mesh Ewald

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002000
name: dispersion interaction parameter
def: "A numerical coefficient in a force field that quantifies the strength of the long-range attractive forces between two atoms due to induced dipole fluctuations. In the standard Lennard-Jones potential, this is the C6 term, proportional to the product of the interaction energy well depth and the sixth power of the collision diameter (4ϵσ^6). For experts, this parameter governs the asymptotic decay of the van der Waals potential and is often derived from atomic polarizabilities. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001515 ! Lennard-Jones parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002001
name: repulsion interaction parameter
def: "A numerical coefficient in a force field that defines the stiffness of the short-range repulsive barrier between two atoms. In the Lennard-Jones potential, this is the C12 term (4ϵσ^12), approximating the Pauli exclusion principle that prevents atomic overlap. For experts, while physically approximating an exponential repulsion, the 1/r ^12 form is chosen primarily for computational efficiency as the square of the dispersion term. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001515 ! Lennard-Jones parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002002
name: atom freezing
def: "A simulation technique where the positions of a selected group of atoms are kept strictly fixed throughout the integration. This is achieved by zeroing the forces and velocities (or setting masses to infinity) for those atoms, effectively removing them from the equations of motion. For experts, this is distinct from position restraints (where atoms vibrate around a point) and is used to model rigid walls, surface adsorption, or to equilibrate solvent around a static protein structure. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001201 ! constraint and restraint parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002003
name: coarse-graining
def: "A modelling method that reduces a system's degrees of freedom by grouping atoms into single interaction sites according to chemical or structural rules. It is the act of building the model, as distinct from the resolution the resulting model has. The rule chosen for grouping determines what the model can still represent. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000305 ! modeling method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002004
name: stochastic dynamics
def: "A simulation method that adds a random force and a matching frictional drag to the equations of motion, imitating collisions with a surrounding fluid that is not itself simulated. The 2 additions are tied together so the system settles at the intended temperature. It also serves as a thermostat, which is why it is often used even when the solvent is present. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000843 ! molecular dynamics

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002005
name: non-equilibrium molecular dynamics
def: "A simulation method in which the system is deliberately driven away from equilibrium by an applied force, flow or gradient. Measuring how it responds gives transport properties such as viscosity and thermal conductivity directly, which an equilibrium simulation can only obtain indirectly from fluctuations. The driving must be gentle enough that the response stays proportional to it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "NEMD" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000843 ! molecular dynamics

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002006
name: flooding potential
def: "A computational technique used to force a protein out of its stable resting shape so it can explore new structures. It works by adding a localized repulsive energy hill, based on the system's principal components, to the energy minimum the molecule currently occupies." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001552 ! restraint potential
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002007
name: simulated tempering
def: "Simulated tempering is an enhanced sampling technique that helps a system explore different configurations by allowing its temperature to fluctuate dynamically up and down during a single simulation. Unlike replica exchange, which uses parallel copies, this method uses a single trajectory that jumps between discrete temperature levels based on a probabilistic acceptance rule. It requires the pre-calculation or iterative determination of weighting factors for each temperature to ensuring uniform sampling and efficient barrier crossing." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001555 ! expanded ensemble simulation
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002008
name: bonded type
def: "A classification code in a force field topology that selects which parameters apply to a bond, angle or rotation, based on the kinds of atoms involved. Assigning it is how a general parameter set is applied to a particular molecule. A wrong assignment gives a molecule the wrong stiffness or the wrong preferred shape, and nothing reports it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000447 ! identifier

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002009
name: salt bridge
def: "A salt bridge is a strong non-covalent interaction formed between a positively charged amino acid side chain and a negatively charged one. It combines two physical forces: an electrostatic attraction between the opposing charges and a hydrogen bond between specific atoms in the residues. For experts, these interactions (typically between Arg/Lys and Asp/Glu) contribute significantly to protein thermostability but have a complex energetic dependence on the local dielectric environment and pH." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000187 ! electrostatic interaction
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002010
name: solvation
def: "A preparation process in which a solute is placed inside a box of solvent molecules, usually water, and any solvent that overlaps the solute is removed. The solvent box is normally pre-equilibrated, so the liquid already has the right density and structure before the solute enters it. Without this step a simulation would have the molecule sitting in a vacuum, which changes its behaviour completely. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000002 ! simulation preparation

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002011
name: termini
def: "The 2 ends of a biological polymer chain, which differ chemically from each other and from everything between them. In a protein one end carries a free amino group and the other a free carboxyl group, each charged at ordinary acidity. They must be assigned a chemical state before a simulation, because a standard residue template does not cover them. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002012
name: continuation state
def: "A configuration setting that instructs a molecular dynamics engine to resume a simulation exactly from where a previous run finished. It requires reading the full state of the system—including atomic positions, velocities, and sometimes forces—from a checkpoint or restart file to ensure a seamless trajectory." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001164 ! simulation parameter
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002013
name: test particle insertion
def: "A sampling method that computes the chemical potential of a species by repeatedly placing a non-interacting trial particle at random positions in a simulation and recording the energy it would have. Averaging the Boltzmann factor of those energies gives the excess chemical potential directly. It fails for dense systems, where almost every insertion overlaps an existing particle. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000610 ! thermodynamics analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002014
name: Gibbs sampling replica exchange
def: "Gibbs sampling replica exchange is an advanced simulation method used to efficiently explore the different shapes and energy states of a molecule. Unlike standard replica exchange which attempts to swap temperatures between neighboring simulations, this method attempts to swap configurations among all running simulations simultaneously based on a global probability criterion. It is an advanced Markov chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) algorithm. It overcomes the problem of simulations getting trapped in low-energy \"metastable\" states by running multiple copies (replicas) of a system at different conditions." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000858 ! replica-exchange molecular dynamics
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002015
name: shell molecular dynamics
def: "A simulation method for polarizable force fields in which each polarizable atom is given a light charged particle attached to it by a spring. The particle shifts in response to the local electric field, which reproduces how an atom's electron cloud distorts. Treating polarization as an extra particle lets an ordinary integrator handle it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000843 ! molecular dynamics

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002016
name: enforced rotation simulation
def: "A simulation method that forces a specific part of a molecular system, such as a protein subunit, to spin around a defined axis. An external potential is applied to a group of atoms to induce rotation at a constant angular velocity or under a constant torque while the rest of the system responds dynamically." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000859 ! steered dynamics
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002017
name: MTTK pressure coupling
def: "A mathematical method used to keep the pressure constant in a computer simulation of a molecular system. The Martyna-Tobias-Klein (MTTK) algorithm controls pressure by dynamically adjusting the size of the simulation box using equations of motion that rigorously sample the correct statistical ensemble. For experts, while theoretically rigorous for generating the NPT ensemble without the artifacts of stochastic collisions, it involves coupling the cell vectors to a thermostat chain and has been largely superseded or modified in some software versions due to implementation complexities or equipartition issues. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000039 ! barostat algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002018
name: buckingham potential
def: "A mathematical formula used to calculate the forces between atoms that are not chemically bonded to each other. Unlike the standard Lennard-Jones model, it replaces the steep r ^−12 repulsion term with an exponential function to better describe the softness of atomic electron clouds at short distances. For experts, the potential usually takes the form V(r)=Aexp(−Br)−Cr^−6, and while physically more accurate for repulsion, requires computational safeguards to prevent atomic fusion at very short distances where the exponential term turns over. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000430 ! non-bonded potential

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002019
name: neural network potential
def: "A computational model that uses machine learning algorithms to predict the potential energy and forces of a molecular system. It approximates the complex quantum mechanical energy landscape by training a neural network on a large dataset of reference atomic configurations and energies. For experts, these potentials (like ANI or DeepMD) offer ab initio accuracy at a computational cost closer to classical force fields, provided the simulation remains within the chemical space represented in the training data. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000007 ! force field

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002020
name: hybrid NNP/MM simulation
def: "A multiscale simulation technique that couples a region described by a Neural Network Potential (NNP) with a larger environment described by a classical molecular mechanics (MM) force field. It allows for the accurate modeling of reactive centers or complex electronic effects using machine learning, while efficiently capturing long-range environmental effects with standard physics-based models. For experts, this method typically employs electrostatic or mechanical embedding schemes similar to QM/MM to handle the boundary interactions between the NNP-active region and the classical surroundings. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "hybrid NNP/MM simulations" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000336 ! multiscale simulation method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002021
name: interactive molecular dynamics
def: "A simulation technique that allows a user to visualize and physically manipulate a running molecular simulation in real-time. Through a specialized interface or haptic device, the user applies external forces to specific atoms while the simulation engine calculates the system's response on the fly. For experts, IMD uses a client-server architecture where the visualization client sends force vectors to the simulation server, which integrates these as time-dependent external potentials, useful for guiding docking or unfolding pathways. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000843 ! molecular dynamics

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002022
name: leapfrog integrator
def: "A numerical method used to solve the equations of motion in a simulation by updating positions and velocities at offset time intervals. It calculates velocities at half-integer time steps and positions at integer time steps, ensuring that the integration is time-reversible and symplectic (energy-conserving). For experts, while computationally efficient and stable (O(Δt ^2)), it does not provide velocities and positions at the same instant, requiring interpolation for calculating kinetic energy or pressure at step t. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001691 ! integration algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002023
name: velocity verlet integrator
def: "A numerical algorithm for integrating Newton's equations of motion that updates atomic positions and velocities at the same time step. It improves upon the leap-frog method by providing synchronized coordinates and velocities, which is essential for accurate calculation of kinetic energy and instantaneous pressure. For experts, this symplectic, time-reversible integrator is the standard in many MD codes because it facilitates the implementation of velocity-dependent algorithms like thermostats and barostats with high numerical stability. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001691 ! integration algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002024
name: brownian dynamics integrator
def: "A numerical algorithm used to simulate the motion of particles in a fluid where friction dominates over inertia. It integrates the overdamped Langevin equation, assuming that the momenta relax instantaneously, so particle positions are updated based on forces and a random displacement derived from the diffusion coefficient. For experts, this integrator allows for much larger time steps than standard MD by ignoring fast inertial motions, making it ideal for simulating diffusion-controlled processes or coarse-grained systems. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001691 ! integration algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002025
name: brownian dynamics
def: "A simulation method that models the movement of molecules as a random walk driven by thermal collisions and damped by solvent viscosity. Unlike standard molecular dynamics, it ignores the mass and inertia of the particles, assuming that friction brings them to a terminal velocity instantly in response to forces. For experts, this is the limit of Langevin dynamics where the friction coefficient is very large (overdamped regime), often used for simulating large biomolecules or coarse-grained models where solvent is treated implicitly. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000843 ! molecular dynamics
property_value: skos:closeMatch NCIT:C70775

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002026
name: stochastic dynamics integrator
def: "A numerical algorithm that incorporates random noise and frictional drag directly into the equations of motion to mimic the effect of a solvent. It integrates the Langevin equation (or similar stochastic differential equations) to simultaneously propagate the system and control its temperature. For experts, this integrator (often GROMACS' sd integrator) acts as a local thermostat, ensuring correct canonical ensemble sampling without the synchronization artifacts sometimes seen with global thermostats like Berendsen or Nosé-Hoover. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001691 ! integration algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002027
name: triclinic box
def: "A triclinic box is a geometric shape for a periodic simulation cell defined by three vectors of arbitrary length and mutual angles. This flexibility allows it to represent any crystal lattice system or to optimize the solvent volume around a solute by fitting the box shape more closely than a standard cube." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000032 ! box type
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002028
name: stochastic cell rescaling barostat
def: "A pressure control algorithm that changes the box size according to an equation combining a steady restoring term with a random one. The random term is what makes it produce the correct distribution of volumes rather than merely the correct average. It reaches equilibrium quickly like the simple rescaling schemes while being correct like the deterministic ones. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000039 ! barostat algorithm
property_value: MOLSIM:002254 "baro_stochastic=1" xsd:string {dcterms:source="MOLSIM:000217"}
property_value: MOLSIM:002254 "pcoupl=C-rescale" xsd:string {dcterms:source="MOLSIM:000247"}

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002029
name: integrator type
def: "A configuration parameter that specifies the numerical algorithm used to propagate the system's coordinates and velocities through time. It determines whether the simulation performs energy minimization (e.g., steepest descent), classical dynamics (e.g., leap-frog, velocity Verlet), or stochastic dynamics (e.g., Langevin). For experts, this setting (e.g., integrator in GROMACS, imin in AMBER) fundamentally defines the physics engine and the ensemble generated by the simulation executable. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001165 ! integration parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002030
name: trajectory output interval
def: "A simulation control parameter that dictates how frequently the system's atomic coordinates are written to the trajectory file during a run. It is defined as an integer representing the number of integration time steps between save events. For experts, variables like nstxout (GROMACS) or ntwx (AMBER) must be chosen to balance the need for high temporal resolution in analysis against data storage limits and I/O performance overhead. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002108 ! output control parameter
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:002109 ! energy output interval

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002031
name: temperature coupling groups
def: "A simulation setting that divides the molecular system into distinct subsets, such as \"Protein\" and \"Solvent,\" each regulated by its own independent thermostat. This separation ensures that energy is distributed evenly across components with different heating rates or degrees of freedom, preventing the \"hot solvent, cold solute\" artifact. For experts, correct assignment (e.g., tc-grps in GROMACS) is critical in non-periodic or vacuum simulations to prevent the accumulation of translational kinetic energy, known as the \"flying ice cube\" effect. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001173 ! temperature control parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002032
name: cutoff scheme
def: "A configuration parameter that selects the algorithmic strategy used to generate neighbor lists and truncate non-bonded interactions. It dictates whether the neighbor search is performed based on individual atoms or charge-neutral groups, and how the buffer zone is managed to permit infrequent list updates. For experts, modern engines favor the \"Verlet\" scheme (buffered neighbor lists) over the legacy \"Group\" scheme, as the former supports efficient parallelization on GPUs and ensures better energy conservation with PME. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001185 ! non-bonded interaction parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002033
name: neighbor list cutoff
def: "A distance parameter that defines the radius of the sphere around an atom within which neighboring atoms are tracked for potential interactions. Atoms found within this distance are stored in a neighbor list, which allows the simulation to avoid calculating distances between distant atom pairs at every time step. For experts, this value (rlist) must be strictly larger than the interaction cutoff (rvdw + rlist_skin) to ensure that atoms diffusing into interaction range are accounted for between list updates. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001185 ! non-bonded interaction parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002034
name: velocity generation
def: "A preparation step that assigns starting velocities to the atoms, drawn at random from the distribution appropriate to a chosen temperature. A structure alone carries no velocities, so they must come from somewhere before dynamics can begin. Drawing them from that distribution rather than setting them to zero is what lets the system reach the intended temperature quickly. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001210 ! system setup parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002035
name: spatial distribution function
def: "A function giving the density of a chosen atom or molecule at each point in the space around a reference molecule, relative to its average density in the bulk. Unlike a radial distribution function, which averages over all directions and returns a curve, it keeps the direction and returns a 3-dimensional map. That is what lets specific sites be seen, such as a water molecule that sits in the same pocket throughout a simulation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "SDF" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001421 ! correlation function

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002036
name: GROMACS portable energy format
def: "A binary file format used by the GROMACS simulation package to store time-series data of system energies and thermodynamic properties. It records values such as potential energy components, temperature, pressure, and box dimensions at specified intervals in a portable, machine-independent format. For experts, this file (extension .edr) is accessed via the gmx energy tool to extract statistics or plotting data, and its binary nature ensures no loss of precision compared to text logs. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000439 ! simulation log format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002037
name: GROMACS index format
def: "A text-based file format used by GROMACS to define specific subsets or groups of atoms within a molecular system. It lists atom indices assigned to named groups, allowing users to apply specific actions (like thermostatting, restraining, or analyzing) to just those selected parts. For experts, this file (extension .ndx) is generated by gmx make_ndx and is essential for setting up non-standard simulation protocols where default groups like \"Protein\" or \"Solvent\" are insufficient. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000437 ! simulation input format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002038
name: GROMACS portable input format
def: "A binary file format used by GROMACS that creates a self-contained description of a simulation ready to be executed. It combines the atomic coordinates, velocities, molecular topology, and all simulation control parameters into a single, portable machine-readable file. For experts, this file (extension .tpr) is generated by the gmx grompp preprocessor and ensures consistency by validating that the structure matches the topology and parameters before the simulation engine is launched. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000441 ! simulation state format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002039
name: atom ID
def: "An atom ID is usually a number, that uniquely defines a given atom in a molecular structure. It is typically used in molecular topology descriptions to uniquely identify an atom from the set of atoms defining the system." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000447 ! identifier
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0003-4177-3619
property_value: skos:exactMatch data:0983

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002040
name: JSmol
def: "JSmol is an open-source, HTML5/JavaScript-based molecular viewer that allows for the interactive 3D visualization of chemical structures within web browsers without requiring Java or other plugins. It is the modern, JavaScript implementation of the popular Jmol applet, widely used in chemical education, databases, and web-based cheminformatics tools." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002041 ! molecular structure visualization tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002041
name: molecular structure visualization tool
def: "A visualization tool designed specifically to render and interactively display three-dimensional models of molecular structures, complexes, and dynamic simulation trajectories. These tools are used to visually inspect atomic coordinates, molecular surfaces, and spatial relationships." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000163 ! visualization tool
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:002042 ! data plotting tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002042
name: data plotting tool
def: "A visualization tool designed to generate 2D or 3D graphs, charts, and plots from numerical data files." []
synonym: "data visualization tool" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000163 ! visualization tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002043
name: CAMPARI
def: "A simulation program that performs both molecular dynamics and Monte Carlo sampling of biological macromolecules. It is used particularly for intrinsically disordered proteins, where no single structure exists and broad sampling matters more than speed. Its Monte Carlo moves can change a chain's shape in ways dynamics would take far longer to reach. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000160 ! molecular dynamics engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002044
name: HIP
def: "A programming interface, developed by AMD, that lets the same source code run on graphics processors from more than one manufacturer. It closely mirrors the interface used for NVIDIA hardware, so existing code can be converted with little change. It exists so that a simulation engine need not be maintained twice. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001562 ! application programming interface

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002045
name: SYCL
def: "A standard C++ layer that lets code for processors of different kinds be written as ordinary single-source C++, with the device parts compiled out of the same file. It removes the separate device language that earlier portable interfaces required. It is the route several simulation engines have taken to support more than one manufacturer's accelerators. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001562 ! application programming interface

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002046
name: OpenCL
def: "An open standard for writing programs that run across processors of different kinds, including central processors, graphics processors and specialised accelerators. One program can then use whatever hardware is present. Its portability comes at some cost in speed against an interface written for one manufacturer. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "open computing language" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001562 ! application programming interface

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002047
name: OpenMPI
def: "An open-source implementation of the message passing standard, assembled from several earlier projects and designed to support many kinds of network hardware. It is the other of the 2 implementations in general use. Which one a simulation was built against is part of reproducing its performance, though not its results. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001566 ! software library

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002048
name: MPICH
def: "An open-source implementation of the message passing standard, used directly and also as the basis several hardware vendors build their own versions on. It is one of the 2 implementations nearly all clusters use. Its performance depends heavily on the network hardware it is configured for. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001566 ! software library

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002049
name: AutoDock
def: "AutoDock is a suite of automated docking tools designed to predict how small molecules bind to a receptor of known 3D structure. AutoDock (e.g., AutoDock 4) utilizes a Lamarckian genetic algorithm and a grid-based empirical scoring function." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000162 ! docking tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002050
name: GOLD
def: "GOLD (Genetic Optimisation for Ligand Docking) is a highly regarded commercial docking program developed by the Cambridge Crystallographic Data Centre (CCDC). It uses a genetic algorithm to explore ligand conformational space and offers multiple scoring functions. It is frequently used in pharmaceutical pipelines to generate highly accurate protein-ligand complex structures for subsequent MD refinement." []
synonym: "Genetic Optimisation for Ligand Docking" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000162 ! docking tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002051
name: Glide
def: "Glide (Grid-based Ligand Docking with Energetics) is a commercial molecular docking program within the Schrödinger software suite. It uses a systematic, hierarchical search of positional, orientational, and conformational space followed by evaluation with an empirical scoring function. It is heavily utilized in industry for virtual screening and preparing complexes for Desmond MD simulations." []
synonym: "Grid-based Ligand Docking with Energetics" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000162 ! docking tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002052
name: rDock
def: "A molecular docking program that predicts how a small molecule will bind to a protein or a nucleic acid, and scores how well it fits. It searches for good positions using a mix of random and directed steps, which lets it cover many possibilities without testing them all. It was one of the first docking programs built to handle nucleic acid targets as well as proteins. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000162 ! docking tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002053
name: adaptive biasing force algorithm
def: "An enhanced sampling algorithm used in molecular dynamics to calculate free energy profiles and accelerate the sampling of complex molecular systems. By continuously applying an on-the-fly biasing force, ABF allows systems to escape kinetic traps and evenly explore reaction pathways." []
synonym: "ABF algorithm" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001740 ! enhanced sampling algorithm
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002054
name: Wang-Landau algorithm
def: "Wang-Landau algorithm simulations are a class of flat-histogram Monte Carlo methods designed to directly estimate the density of states (DOS) of a physical or mathematical system. Unlike traditional methods dependent on temperature, it generates a random walk in energy space that allows you to calculate thermodynamic properties across all temperatures." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001740 ! enhanced sampling algorithm
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002055
name: well-tempered metadynamics algorithm
def: "A specific algorithmic extension of metadynamics where the height of the added Gaussian biasing potentials is gradually decreased over time based on the amount of bias already accumulated at that location. This ensures that the biasing potential converges smoothly to the true free energy surface, avoiding the over-filling of energy basins." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001740 ! enhanced sampling algorithm
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002056
name: steered molecular dynamics algorithm
def: "An algorithm that applies a time-dependent, usually harmonic, guiding potential to specific atoms or collective variables. It calculates the necessary biasing forces to force the system to evolve along a predefined reaction coordinate, simulating non-equilibrium processes like ligand unbinding or protein unfolding." []
synonym: "SMD algorithm" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001740 ! enhanced sampling algorithm
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002057
name: multiple-walkers metadynamics
def: "An enhanced sampling simulation method and a specific variant of metadynamics where multiple independent simulations (walkers) are run in parallel. All walkers simultaneously explore the conformational space and deposit Gaussian bias potentials into a single, shared history-dependent bias grid. This approach significantly accelerates the reconstruction of complex free energy surfaces while maintaining the exact theoretical accuracy of standard metadynamics." []
synonym: "MWMD" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000852 ! metadynamics
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002058
name: PDBQT format
def: "The PDBQT format is an extension of the standard PDB format specifically designed for use with the AutoDock and AutoDock Vina molecular docking suites. In addition to atomic coordinates, it stores calculated partial charges ('Q') and AutoDock-specific atom types ('T'), making it a structural format that intrinsically carries the predictive interaction parameters required for, and generated by, docking algorithms." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000715 ! prediction data format
is_a: MOLSIM:001088 ! molecular structure format
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:002059 ! PROPKA output format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071
property_value: skos:exactMatch format:4036

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002059
name: PROPKA output format
def: "A text data format recording the predicted acidity of each titratable group in a protein, together with the structural reasons for each prediction. It lists the contributions separately, such as burial from solvent and nearby charges, so a prediction can be checked rather than taken on trust. It is normally written with the extension .pka. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "pka format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000715 ! prediction data format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002060
name: docking log format
def: "A docking log format is a text-based or tabular file generated by molecular docking software (such as AutoDock Vina, Glide, or GOLD) to record the numerical results of a virtual screening or pose prediction run. It typically contains ranked lists of predicted binding poses, estimated binding affinities or docking scores, and clustering metrics like RMSD, serving as the primary predictive output for analyzing binding without needing to parse the 3D structure files." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000715 ! prediction data format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002061
name: PAE matrix format
def: "A data format, usually written as JSON, that stores the predicted aligned error matrix from a deep learning protein structure prediction. Entry X,Y gives the expected error in the position of residue X when the predicted and true structures are superposed on residue Y. It is how the confidence in relative domain orientation and in predicted interfaces is judged, which a per-residue confidence score cannot show. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "Predicted Aligned Error matrix format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000715 ! prediction data format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002062
name: Maestro format
def: "The Maestro format (typically .mae or .maegz) is the native, proprietary text-based format developed by Schrödinger software suite, used to store molecular structures along with associated properties." []
synonym: "mae format" EXACT []
synonym: "maegz format" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000715 ! prediction data format
is_a: MOLSIM:001088 ! molecular structure format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-8291-8071

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002063
name: metropolis Monte Carlo
def: "A sampling algorithm that proposes a random change to a system and accepts it always if the energy falls, and with a probability depending on the energy rise if it does not. Repeating this generates configurations in the right proportions for the temperature, without ever computing a force. It samples equilibrium properties correctly but says nothing about how fast anything happens. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001740 ! enhanced sampling algorithm
property_value: skos:exactMatch KISAO_0000278

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002064
name: mdrun
def: "A simulation engine, the program in the GROMACS suite that performs the simulation itself. It reads a single pre-compiled input file holding the system, the parameters and the starting state, and writes the trajectory. Every other GROMACS program prepares its input or analyses its output. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000160 ! molecular dynamics engine

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002065
name: simulation parameter format
def: "A data format that specifies the control variables, algorithmic settings, and thermodynamic conditions required to execute a computational simulation run. It dictates exactly how the simulation engine will propagate the system over time, defining parameters such as the integration algorithm, time step, total duration, non-bonded cutoff distances, and the specific thermostat and barostat algorithms used for temperature and pressure coupling. For experts, files in this format (such as GROMACS .mdp or AMBER mdin) define the physical ensemble and numerical methods of the computational experiment, acting as the primary instruction set for the core molecular dynamics engine. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000437 ! simulation input format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002066
name: force field parameter format
def: "A data format that stores the numerical coefficients and empirical rules defining the potential energy function of a molecular mechanics force field. It contains the specific values needed to calculate interactions between atom types, including equilibrium lengths and force constants for bonded terms (bonds, angles, dihedrals), as well as Lennard-Jones parameters and partial charges for non-bonded terms. For experts, these files (such as AMBER .dat/.frcmod or CHARMM .par) supply the fundamental physical constants required by the simulation engine to compute interatomic forces, and are kept strictly distinct from the molecular coordinates or run control settings. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000437 ! simulation input format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002067
name: simulation environment
def: "A simulation environment represents the overall physical medium or surrounding context in which the primary molecular system is embedded during a computational study. It defines the macroscopic nature of the system's surroundings, such as whether the molecule is in a vacuum, dissolved in a liquid, or embedded in a lipid bilayer." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000006 ! model
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002068
name: vacuum environment
def: "An environment in which a molecule is simulated entirely on its own, with nothing around it. Without solvent a molecule collapses on itself, because the non-polar groups that would avoid water have nothing to avoid. It is used for parameterisation and for comparison with gas-phase measurements, not to represent biological conditions. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002067 ! simulation environment

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002069
name: solvated environment
def: "A solvated environment is a simulation context in which the primary solute molecule is completely surrounded by a liquid medium composed of solvent molecules. This environment is characterized by bulk liquid properties such as density, viscosity, and a specific dielectric constant. Simulating molecules in a solvated environment is essential for capturing the thermodynamic and structural effects of solvent interactions, which heavily dictate biomolecular folding and binding." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002067 ! simulation environment
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002070
name: aqueous environment
def: "A solvated environment in which the liquid is water, alone or nearly so. It is the setting almost all biological molecules exist in, so it is the default choice for a biomolecular simulation. The behaviour of water near a surface differs enough from bulk water that the amount included matters. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002069 ! solvated environment

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002071
name: non-aqueous environment
def: "A solvated environment in which the liquid is something other than water, such as methanol, chloroform or octanol. These solvents differ from water in polarity and in their ability to form hydrogen bonds, so a molecule adopts different shapes in them. Simulations in octanol are used to predict how a drug will partition between water and fat. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002069 ! solvated environment

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002072
name: membrane environment
def: "A membrane environment is a highly anisotropic, heterogeneous simulation context representing a cellular membrane, typically composed of a self-assembled lipid bilayer separating two aqueous compartments. It features a hydrophobic core and polar interfacial regions. Modeling a membrane environment is essential for simulating the structure, dynamics, and transport mechanisms of transmembrane proteins, ion channels, and membrane-active peptides or drugs." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002067 ! simulation environment
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002073
name: crystal lattice environment
def: "An environment in which molecules are packed in a regular repeating arrangement fixed by a crystallographic space group, as in a solid. Neighbouring molecules constrain each other, so shapes seen here may not be those the molecule takes in solution. Simulating it is how a crystal structure is checked against the conditions it was measured in. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002067 ! simulation environment

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002074
name: interfacial environment
def: "An interfacial environment is a simulation context characterized by the boundary or interface between two distinct physical phases, such as a liquid-vapor (water-air) interface or a liquid-solid interface. The physical properties of the system change drastically across this boundary." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002067 ! simulation environment
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002075
name: conformational ensemble
def: "A dataset consisting of a collection of distinct molecular structures or conformations. Unlike a simulation trajectory, it does not inherently possess a chronological order, but rather represents a sampling of the structurally accessible states of a molecule (e.g., an NMR structural ensemble, or representative frames extracted via clustering). (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "structural ensemble" EXACT []
is_a: IAO:0000030 ! information content entity

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002076
name: molecular mechanics
def: "A computational method that models molecules using classical physics, treating atoms as particles and bonds as springs, with the energy given by a fitted set of functions called a force field. Electrons never appear, so the method cannot describe a bond being made or broken. What it buys by that omission is speed: systems of hundreds of thousands of atoms become affordable. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "MM" EXACT []
synonym: "molecular mechanics method" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000841 ! empirical method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002077
name: empirical scoring method
def: "A method that estimates binding strength by adding up contributions from countable features of a complex, such as hydrogen bonds, buried surface and rotatable bonds, with weights fitted to measured affinities. It computes no physics, which is what makes it fast enough to rank millions of candidates. It ranks far better than it predicts, so its numbers should not be read as energies. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "empirical scoring function" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000841 ! empirical method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002078
name: implicit solvent method
def: "A modelling method that represents the effect of a surrounding liquid as a continuous medium instead of as individual molecules. It computes solvation free energy from the shape and charges of the solute using parameters such as atomic radii and a surface tension coefficient. It removes most of the atoms from a simulation, which makes it far faster but blind to any effect that depends on a specific solvent molecule. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "continuum solvation model" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000841 ! empirical method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002079
name: elastic network modeling
def: "A modelling method that represents a macromolecule as nodes, usually 1 per residue, joined by simple springs between neighbours within a cutoff distance. It discards chemistry entirely and keeps only shape and connectivity, which is enough to reproduce large-scale collective motion. It is cheap enough to apply to assemblies far too large to simulate. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "ENM" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000841 ! empirical method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002080
name: quantitative structure-activity relationship modeling
def: "A modelling method that predicts a molecule's biological effect from numbers computed about its chemical structure. It fits a statistical relationship on compounds whose activity is known, then applies it to compounds whose activity is not. It predicts well only for molecules resembling the training set, which is why the range it was fitted over must be reported with it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "QSAR" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000841 ! empirical method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002081
name: machine-learned potential method
def: "A computational method that predicts the energy and forces of a system using a model trained on quantum mechanical calculations, instead of a fitted analytical force field. It aims for quantum accuracy at a cost close to a force field's. It is reliable only for systems resembling those it was trained on, which is its central limitation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000841 ! empirical method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002082
name: secondary structure change
def: "A local change in which a stretch of a protein or nucleic acid chain switches from one regular repeating shape to another, or to no regular shape at all. It happens by breaking and remaking the hydrogen bonds between nearby parts of the backbone, for example when a helix unwinds into a loop. It is local, so the rest of the molecule can stay as it was. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001793 ! conformational transition

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002083
name: folding
def: "The process by which a linear chain of amino acids or nucleotides collapses into the compact 3-dimensional shape it needs to work. It is driven by non-polar groups avoiding water, by hydrogen bonds forming, and by charges attracting or repelling. Simulating it is hard because the process is slow on the scale a simulation can reach, yet the chain must find 1 shape among an enormous number. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001793 ! conformational transition

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002084
name: unfolding
def: "The process by which a structured molecule loses its working 3-dimensional shape and becomes a disordered chain. It happens when the many weak interactions holding the structure together are disrupted at once, by heat, pressure, a change in acidity, or a chemical that competes for them. It is often simulated instead of folding, because it can be driven to happen fast enough to watch. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001793 ! conformational transition

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002085
name: domain motion
def: "A collective motion in which a whole folded region of a protein shifts or rotates relative to the rest. It usually happens by bending or twisting at a hinge joining 2 more rigid regions. It is the kind of motion that opens and closes a binding site. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001793 ! conformational transition

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002086
name: allosteric transition
def: "A structural change in which something happening at one site on a molecule alters how a distant site behaves. The effect travels through the molecule along connected, coupled motions rather than through direct contact. It is how a molecule binding at one place can switch activity on or off somewhere else entirely. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001793 ! conformational transition

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002087
name: ligand-induced allosteric transition
def: "An allosteric transition set off by a small molecule binding at one site, which changes behaviour at a distant one. The effect travels through connected motions in the structure rather than through direct contact. It is how a drug can switch a protein's activity without touching its active site. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002086 ! allosteric transition

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002088
name: entropy-driven allosteric transition
def: "An allosteric transition in which the signal is carried by a change in flexibility rather than by a change in average shape. A perturbation at one site alters how much a distant site fluctuates, which changes its affinity without moving it. Because the average structure barely changes, crystallography alone cannot detect it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002086 ! allosteric transition

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002089
name: sugar ring pucker transition
def: "A conformational rearrangement in which the five-membered sugar ring of a nucleotide shifts between different non-planar shapes. In nucleic acids, this commonly involves transitions between North (C3′-endo-like) and South (C2′-endo-like) conformations, affecting local backbone geometry. Correctly reproducing these populations is an important test of nucleic-acid force fields and helps distinguish A- and B-form helices." []
synonym: "sugar ring flip" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001793 ! conformational transition
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002090
name: molecular structural component
def: "A physical constituent of a simulated molecular system that is treated as a distinct unit with its own properties and spatial coordinates. It covers atoms, ions, residues, polymer chains and whole molecules. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "molecular entity" EXACT []
property_value: IAO:0000116 "Top-level parent for the structural components of a simulated system. Kept as a MOLSIM class rather than reusing CHEBI:23367 molecular entity, because this branch spans 2 ChEBI branches that do not meet: atom and molecule are molecular entities in ChEBI, while residue and chain sit under CHEBI:24433 group, a sibling of molecular entity. Grouping all 4 suits the description of a coordinate file, where they are 4 levels of one containment hierarchy. Renamed from 'molecular entity' on 2026-08-21 so that the primary label is unique across the ontologies MOLSIM is released alongside; the former name is kept as an exact synonym." xsd:string

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002091
name: residue
def: "A single building block within a polymer chain, such as one amino acid in a protein or one nucleotide in a nucleic acid. It is a group of atoms that share an identifier and are handled together, so a structure file can refer to \"residue 45\" rather than to each of its atoms. Most analyses work at this level, because it matches how biologists talk about a structure. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002090 ! molecular structural component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002092
name: atom
def: "The smallest unit of a chemical element, and the smallest particle a classical molecular simulation tracks. In such a simulation it is represented as a point carrying a mass, a partial electric charge and a radius, all taken from the force field rather than computed. Everything else in a simulated system is built from these points and the bonds between them. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002090 ! molecular structural component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002093
name: chain
def: "A continuous run of residues joined by covalent bonds and labelled with a single identifier in a structure file, such as one strand of DNA or one polypeptide. The identifier is what separates the subunits of a complex from one another. Getting it wrong joins 2 separate molecules into 1 in the eyes of every tool that reads the file. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002090 ! molecular structural component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002094
name: molecular unit
def: "A chemical unit composed of two or more atoms bonded together, or a single monoatomic ion counted as one. In computational chemistry, it represents a complete, covalently continuous structure—ranging from a single solvent molecule to a massive protein—that does not share covalent bonds with other entities in the system. For simulation experts, defining individual molecules is necessary for applying periodic boundary imaging, managing solvent dynamics, and computing macroscopic thermodynamic properties like diffusion. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "molecule" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:002090 ! molecular structural component

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002095
name: pocket detection tool
def: "A pocket detection tool a computational algorithm that identifies and characterizes transient or persistent cavities on the surface of a biomolecular structure from a trajectory or static coordinate set, typically by analyzing atomic coordinates, solvent accessibility, or geometric properties, to predict potential ligand-binding sites and assess their dynamic accessibility and druggability." []
synonym: "cavity detection tool" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000164 ! analysis tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002096
name: fpocket
def: "fpocket is a fast, open-source algorithm designed to predict and analyze potential binding pockets (cavities) on proteins and other biomolecules. It is used in structural bioinformatics for applications like drug discovery, protein function annotation, and the analysis of molecular dynamics trajectories." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002095 ! pocket detection tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002097
name: Curves+
def: "Curves+ is a software program for the structural analysis of DNA and RNA three-dimensional structures. It calculates a comprehensive set of geometric parameters describing nucleic acid conformation, including base-pair, base-pair step, backbone, groove, and helical axis parameters, using a reference frame attached to each base. These descriptors provide a detailed characterization of nucleic acid structure and flexibility." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001960 ! nucleic acid analysis tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-7544-0938

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002098
name: restart simulation process
def: "An execution that resumes a previously interrupted or completed molecular dynamics run by reading saved coordinates, velocities, and simulation state from a restart file. It allows a long simulation to be continued across multiple sessions without loss of continuity. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000003 ! simulation execution

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002099
name: metadata extraction tool
def: "A data processing tool that reads simulation input, output, or trajectory files and extracts descriptive metadata such as system composition, run settings, and provenance information. It supports cataloguing and FAIR annotation of simulation datasets. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000165 ! data processing tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002100
name: PMEMD.cuda
def: "A build of the AMBER simulation engine that runs on NVIDIA graphics processors. It performs the whole simulation on the graphics card, so data need not be moved back and forth each step, which is where the speed comes from. It supports fewer methods than the processor build, so which was used should be recorded. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001669 ! PMEMD

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002101
name: metadata validation process
def: "A validation analysis that checks recorded or extracted metadata for completeness, correctness, and internal consistency against expected schemas or physical constraints. It helps ensure that a simulation dataset is reliably described before it is shared or archived. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000353 ! validation analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002102
name: coordinate wrapping process
def: "A trajectory post-processing that translates atomic coordinates back into the primary periodic unit cell." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001767 ! trajectory post-processing
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002103
name: NMR restrained simulation
def: "A restrained simulation method that biases the dynamics using experimental nuclear magnetic resonance observables, such as interatomic distance restraints from nuclear Overhauser effects or torsion-angle restraints from scalar couplings. It guides the simulated structure toward conformations consistent with the measurements. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000364 ! restrained simulation method

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002104
name: belly dynamics
def: "A restrained subset dynamics in which only a selected group of atoms is allowed to move while the remaining atoms are held fixed throughout the run. It reduces computational cost and focuses sampling on a region of interest, taking its name from the Amber convention of designating a mobile region. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000335 ! restrained subset dynamics

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002105
name: replica exchange attempt frequency
def: "An enhanced sampling parameter that specifies how often exchanges between neighboring replicas are attempted during a replica exchange simulation. It controls the rate at which configurations are swapped between conditions such as different temperatures. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001219 ! enhanced sampling parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002106
name: center of mass removal interval
def: "An integration parameter that specifies how frequently the net translational motion of the system's center of mass is removed during a run. Periodic removal prevents the gradual accumulation of spurious overall drift of the simulated system. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001165 ! integration parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002107
name: multi-timestep inner loop count
def: "An integration parameter that specifies how many short inner integration steps are taken per long outer step in a multiple-timestep integration scheme. It sets how often fast-varying forces are evaluated relative to slow-varying forces to improve computational efficiency. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001165 ! integration parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002108
name: output control parameter
def: "A simulation parameter that governs how frequently and in what form simulation data are written to output files during a run. It determines the temporal resolution and volume of the recorded energies, coordinates, and diagnostic information. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001164 ! simulation parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002109
name: energy output interval
def: "An output control parameter that specifies how often energy and related thermodynamic quantities are written to the output or log during a run. Smaller intervals give finer-grained monitoring at the cost of larger output files. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002108 ! output control parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002110
name: restart output interval
def: "An output control parameter that specifies how often a restart file containing the current coordinates, velocities, and state is written during a run. It determines how much progress can be recovered if the run is interrupted. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002108 ! output control parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002111
name: log output interval
def: "An output control parameter that specifies how often diagnostic and status information is written to the simulation log during a run. It controls the verbosity and temporal resolution of the recorded run history. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002108 ! output control parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002112
name: simulation state time
def: "A simulation state that represents the elapsed model time reached by the system at a given point in a molecular dynamics run. It records how far the simulation has advanced along the physical time coordinate." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001083 ! simulation state
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000003 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label time unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002113
name: final density
def: "A thermodynamic property that represents the mass density of the simulated system at the end of a run or equilibration stage. It is commonly compared against experimental density to assess whether the system has equilibrated correctly. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001293 ! thermodynamic property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000052 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label mass density unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002114
name: computational performance metric
def: "A computed observable that quantifies the computational cost or efficiency of a simulation run rather than a physical property of the system. Examples include elapsed real time and the amount of simulated time produced per unit of computing time. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001292 ! computed observable

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002115
name: total wallclock time
def: "A computational performance metric that measures the total real-world elapsed time taken to complete a run from start to finish. It reflects the actual time a user waits, including all computation and input or output. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002114 ! computational performance metric
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:002116 ! total cpu time
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000003 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label time unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002116
name: total cpu time
def: "A computational performance metric that measures the cumulative processor time consumed by a run, summed across all active compute cores. It reflects total computational effort rather than elapsed real time. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002114 ! computational performance metric
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000003 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label time unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002117
name: setup wallclock time
def: "A computational performance metric that measures the real-world elapsed time spent preparing a run before the production phase begins, such as reading inputs and building data structures. It isolates initialization overhead from the main computation." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002114 ! computational performance metric
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000003 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label time unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002118
name: production wallclock time
def: "A computational performance metric that measures the real-world elapsed time spent in the production phase of a simulation run, during which the trajectory of interest is generated. It excludes setup and finalization overhead." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002114 ! computational performance metric
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000003 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label time unit
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002119
name: average integration step time
def: "A computational performance metric that represents the mean real-world time required to advance the simulation by one integration step. It is a convenient measure of per-step computational efficiency. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002114 ! computational performance metric
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000003 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label time unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002120
name: simulation throughput
def: "A computational performance metric that expresses how much simulated model time is produced per unit of real-world computing time, commonly reported as nanoseconds per day. It is a standard measure for comparing the practical speed of simulations. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002114 ! computational performance metric
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000280 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label rate unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002155
name: simulation protocol
def: "A plan specification that describes a sequential, multi-stage computational workflow, such as minimization, heating, equilibration, and production, applied to a molecular system. It organizes the individual stages and their ordering into a single reproducible procedure. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: IAO:0000104 ! plan specification

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002156
name: simulation stage
def: "A molecular dynamics process that constitutes one discrete, chronological phase within a larger simulation run, characterized by its own role and its own input and output files. Examples include a heating stage or a production stage. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000000 ! molecular dynamics process

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002157
name: simulation parameter schedule
def: "A simulation parameter that specifies how another parameter, such as target temperature, restraint force constant, or non-bonded cutoff, changes over the course of a run, whether across simulated time or across integration steps. It captures ramping and stepwise schedules applied during a stage. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001164 ! simulation parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002158
name: simulation continuity check
def: "A validation analysis that evaluates whether two consecutive simulation stages join without an unexpected break, by comparing the end time of one stage with the start time of the next. It flags gaps that may indicate missing segments or unit errors. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000353 ! validation analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002159
name: cross-source validation
def: "A validation analysis that checks whether metadata extracted from several distinct files describing the same stage, such as topology, input, output, and trajectory files, agree with one another. It surfaces inconsistencies such as mismatched atom counts or timesteps. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000353 ! validation analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002160
name: file parsing error
def: "An information content entity that records a failure, exception, or warning encountered while reading or extracting metadata from a simulation data file. It preserves the reason a file could not be fully processed. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: IAO:0000030 ! information content entity

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002161
name: file format convention
def: "A data format that designates a specific standardized schema variant that a file adheres to within a broader container format, such as the AMBER conventions used inside a NetCDF file. It identifies the precise rules for interpreting the file's contents. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000436 ! data format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002162
name: system classification label
def: "An information content entity that assigns a high-level descriptive category to a molecular system based on its overall composition, such as a protein-ligand complex in explicit water. It provides a concise, human-readable summary of what is being simulated. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: IAO:0000030 ! information content entity

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002163
name: atom selection mask
def: "An atom selection specification that defines a subset of atoms within a molecular system using a formal string or logical expression following the format of a specific software." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002251 ! atom selection specification
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002164
name: trajectory frame interval
def: "A simulation state time that represents the average amount of simulated time elapsed between consecutive saved frames of a trajectory. It reflects how finely the trajectory samples the simulated time coordinate. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002112 ! simulation state time
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:002165 ! inter-stage time gap
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000003 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label time unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002165
name: inter-stage time gap
def: "A simulation state time that represents the difference between the end time of one simulation stage and the start time of the next. A nonzero gap indicates a break in the continuous simulated-time coordinate across stages. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002112 ! simulation state time
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000003 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label time unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002166
name: hydrogen detection strategy
def: "An analysis algorithm that identifies which atoms in a molecular system are hydrogens, for the purpose of applying or detecting hydrogen mass repartitioning. Different strategies rely on different atomic attributes, such as atomic number or atom name. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001696 ! analysis algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002192
name: initial density
def: "A thermodynamic property that represents the mass density of the simulated system at the start of a run, computed from the topology mass and the initial periodic box volume. It provides a baseline for comparison against the equilibrated density reached during a constant-pressure run. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001293 ! thermodynamic property
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000052 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label mass density unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002196
name: atom count consistency check
def: "A cross-source validation that checks whether the atom count agrees across all files describing a system, such as topology, trajectory, etc. A mismatch indicates the files do not describe the same system." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002159 ! cross-source validation
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:002197 ! box consistency check
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002197
name: box consistency check
def: "A cross-source validation that checks whether periodic box information is consistently present or absent across the files describing a stage. It flags cases where, for example, a topology declares a box but a coordinate file does not. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002159 ! cross-source validation

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002198
name: timing consistency check
def: "A cross-source validation that checks whether step counts, timesteps, and total durations agree across the input, output, and trajectory files of a stage. It verifies that the recorded trajectory length matches the configured number of steps times the timestep. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002159 ! cross-source validation

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002199
name: sampling consistency check
def: "A cross-source validation that checks whether the coordinate write frequency configured in the input matches the frequency reflected in the output and trajectory. It confirms that sampling settings were applied as specified. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002159 ! cross-source validation

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002203
name: protein domain
def: "A polypeptide domain that occurs in a protein. It is a distinct, self-contained part of a protein that folds up on its own and usually carries out a particular job. Large proteins are often built from several domains." []
is_a: SO:0000417 ! polypeptide_domain
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002204
name: receptor-binding domain
def: "A protein domain whose function is to attach to a matching partner molecule called a receptor." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002203 ! protein domain
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002205
name: catalytic domain
def: "A protein domain that contains the active site, the pocket where an enzyme carries out its chemical reaction. It is the working part of an enzyme." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002203 ! protein domain
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002206
name: protein functional class label
def: "A system classification label that records the biological job of the main protein in a simulated system. Proteins do most of the work in living cells, and this label groups simulations by the kind of job their protein does. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002162 ! system classification label

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002207
name: enzyme classification label
def: "A protein functional class label for a system whose main protein is an enzyme, a protein that speeds up a chemical reaction in the cell. Enzyme simulations usually centre on the active site, so they often need a quantum description of the reacting groups. Knowing that a system is an enzyme tells a reader what the simulation was most likely set up to look at. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002206 ! protein functional class label
property_value: skos:relatedMatch OBI:0000427

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002208
name: transport protein classification label
def: "A protein functional class label for a system whose main protein is a transport protein, one that moves ions or molecules from place to place. These almost always sit in a membrane, so the system will contain a lipid bilayer as well as water. The property of interest is usually a rate of passage rather than a structure. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002206 ! protein functional class label
property_value: skos:relatedMatch GO:0005215

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002209
name: structural protein classification label
def: "A protein functional class label for a system whose main protein is a structural protein, one that gives shape, stiffness, or mechanical strength. These form long fibres or networks rather than compact globules, so a single copy is rarely the unit that matters. They are often studied with coarse-grained models for that reason. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002206 ! protein functional class label

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002210
name: regulatory protein classification label
def: "A protein functional class label for a system whose main protein is a regulatory protein, one that switches biological processes on or off. What is usually simulated is the change between its active and inactive shapes. Such changes are often too slow to observe directly, so enhanced sampling is commonly needed. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002206 ! protein functional class label

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002211
name: signaling protein classification label
def: "A protein functional class label for a system whose main protein is a signaling protein, one that passes messages within a cell or between cells. Binding at one site frequently alters behaviour at a distant one, which is the allosteric behaviour such simulations set out to trace. Many are membrane receptors, so the system will include a bilayer. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002206 ! protein functional class label
property_value: skos:relatedMatch GO:0038023

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002212
name: motor protein classification label
def: "A protein functional class label for a system whose main protein is a motor protein, one that turns chemical energy into movement. Their working cycle takes milliseconds or longer, far beyond what a direct simulation reaches, so they are studied in stages or with coarse-grained models. The coupling between chemistry at one site and motion elsewhere is the point of interest. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002206 ! protein functional class label

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002213
name: immune protein classification label
def: "A protein functional class label for a system whose main protein is an immune protein, one that helps recognise or fight off germs and other threats. Simulations of these usually concern how tightly and how specifically a target is recognised. The binding surfaces are often flexible loops, which makes sampling them the main difficulty. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002206 ! protein functional class label

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002214
name: storage protein classification label
def: "A protein functional class label for a system whose main protein is a storage protein, one that holds onto useful substances such as iron or amino acids until they are needed. They are usually large symmetric assemblies with a cavity inside. What is studied is how a substance enters, is held, and is released. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002206 ! protein functional class label

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002226
name: periodic box angles
def: "A system setup parameter that gives the three angles (commonly α, β, γ) between the edges of the simulation box. These are needed to describe boxes that are not simple rectangular blocks, for example triclinic or truncated-octahedral boxes. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001210 ! system setup parameter

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002230
name: SMILES code
def: "An identifier that encodes the structure of a molecule as a short line of text, using the SMILES notation (Simplified Molecular-Input Line-Entry System). It lets a small molecule be written, searched, and shared as plain text, and complements the InChI code. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000447 ! identifier
property_value: skos:closeMatch format:1196

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002232
name: compiler
def: "A software development and management tool that translates a program's source code into a runnable program. Which compiler was used can affect a simulation's speed and, occasionally, its numerical results. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000171 ! software development and management tool

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002233
name: atom index group
def: "A plan specification that defines a named group of atoms selected from the system, so the group can be referred to by name during setup or analysis. It is the concept behind a Gromacs index (.ndx) file, where groups such as Protein or Water are listed. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002251 ! atom selection specification

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002234
name: classical molecular dynamics
def: "A molecular dynamics method in which the forces between atoms come from a classical (empirical) force field rather than from quantum-mechanical calculations. It is the most common and computationally affordable form of molecular dynamics. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000843 ! molecular dynamics

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002235
name: source structure residue mapping
def: "An information content entity recording how the atoms and residues of a simulated system correspond to those of the experimental structure it was built from. The 2 rarely match: residues are renumbered, missing loops are built in, and hydrogens are added. Without this record, a simulation result cannot be related back to the numbering used in the literature. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: IAO:0000030 ! information content entity

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002236
name: oligomeric state
def: "A structural property that describes how many copies of a protein chain join together to form a working unit. Many proteins function only when several copies assemble into one complex. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001333 ! structural property

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002237
name: monomeric state
def: "An oligomeric state in which the protein works on its own as a single chain, not joined to copies of itself. A protein simulated as a single chain when it is really a pair will behave wrongly, because the surface that should be buried against its partner is exposed to water instead. The state is usually known from the experimental structure or from measurements in solution. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002236 ! oligomeric state
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:002238 ! dimeric state

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002238
name: dimeric state
def: "An oligomeric state in which 2 copies of a protein chain join together to form the working unit. The 2 copies bury a surface against each other that would otherwise face the solvent, so simulating only one gives a different answer. Many enzymes and most transcription factors work this way. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002236 ! oligomeric state

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002239
name: trimeric state
def: "An oligomeric state in which 3 copies of a protein chain join together to form the working unit. Such an assembly usually has 3-fold symmetry, so its subunits are equivalent and the whole can be built from one. Viral coat proteins and several membrane channels take this form. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002236 ! oligomeric state

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002240
name: tetrameric state
def: "An oligomeric state in which 4 copies of a protein chain join together to form the working unit. The 4 may be 4 copies of one chain or 2 copies each of 2 different ones, which is the arrangement haemoglobin takes. Cooperative behaviour, where binding at one subunit changes the others, requires an assembly of this kind. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002236 ! oligomeric state

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002241
name: higher-order oligomeric state
def: "An oligomeric state in which 5 or more copies of a protein chain join together to form the working unit. Assemblies this large are usually symmetric rings or shells, so the whole is built by repeating one subunit. They are often too large to simulate atom by atom, which is where coarse-grained models are used instead. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:002236 ! oligomeric state

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002246
name: spike opening conformational state
def: "A conformational state of a coronavirus spike protein describing how many of its receptor-binding domains are raised into the open position, ready to engage a host cell." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000105 ! conformational state
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002247
name: biological strain classification label
def: "A system classification label naming the specific strain or sequence variant of the organism that the simulated molecule comes from, for example a particular variant of the COVID-19 virus. It groups simulations by biological origin." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002162 ! system classification label
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002248
name: histone variant classification label
def: "A system classification label naming a non-standard version of a histone protein present in the structure (for example H2A.Z). Different histone versions can change how DNA is packaged and read." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002162 ! system classification label
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002249
name: DSSR
def: "A nucleic acid analysis tool that characterises RNA and DNA secondary structure and higher-order motifs directly from three-dimensional coordinates. Built on the x3DNA suite, it annotates base pairs, helices, stems, hairpin loops and multi-branch junctions, and produces schematic representations of the result. It is widely used for RNA structural bioinformatics and is integrated into viewers such as Jmol and PyMOL." []
synonym: "Dissecting the Spatial Structure of RNA" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001960 ! nucleic acid analysis tool
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-4303-9349

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002251
name: atom selection specification
def: "An information content entity that records which atoms of a molecular system a tool should act on. It may be a stored list of atom indices or an expression that is evaluated to produce that list. It says what to operate on, not what to do with it. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: IAO:0000030 ! information content entity

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002252
name: obsolete selection criteria
def: "OBSOLETE. An information content entity that records the conditions and factors used when choosing which items to include in a study, such as which ligands to simulate. It states what was considered rather than what was chosen." []
comment: Retired 2026-08-13, the day after it was minted. It was created to group three children of the retired MOLSIM:000310 plan specification, but only one of the three belonged: MOLSIM:002163 atom selection mask and MOLSIM:002233 atom index group went to MOLSIM:002251 atom selection specification instead, and MOLSIM:001035 validated ligand selection criteria turned out to be an object property that never belonged in a class tree. That left one child, MOLSIM:000143 ligand pairs selection criteria, which is itself the group its twelve criteria belong to. A search of the whole ontology found no other term that could join: every other label mentioning selection or criteria is a convergence threshold, an algorithm or an analysis, all correctly placed elsewhere. MOLSIM:000143 was re-parented to IAO:0000030 information content entity, where it sat before. Never present in a release file.
is_obsolete: true

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002255
name: molecular state
def: "A state that a molecule or molecular system occupies, characterised by its shape, its surroundings, its position on the energy surface, or its electronic configuration. It describes a condition the system is in, rather than a relationship to another molecule or a choice made when the system was built. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000006 ! model

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002264
name: acetyl capping group
def: "A molecular termini state in which the N-terminus of a polymer chain is closed off with an acetyl group, so that the end carries no electric charge. Capping this way makes a short peptide behave more like a piece cut from the middle of a longer chain. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "ACE" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001214 ! molecular termini state

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002265
name: N-methylamide capping group
def: "A molecular termini state in which the C-terminus of a polymer chain is closed off with an N-methylamide group, so that the end carries no electric charge. It is the usual partner to an acetyl group at the other end of the chain. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "NME" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001214 ! molecular termini state

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002266
name: amide capping group
def: "A molecular termini state in which the C-terminus of a polymer chain is closed off with a plain amide group, so that the end carries no electric charge. It is a smaller alternative to an N-methylamide cap. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "NHE" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:001214 ! molecular termini state

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002267
name: charged N-terminus
def: "A molecular termini state in which the N-terminus of a polymer chain is left uncapped and carries a positive charge, as a free amine group does at the pH of most simulations. This is the usual choice when the chain being simulated is a whole protein rather than a fragment of one. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001214 ! molecular termini state

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002268
name: charged C-terminus
def: "A molecular termini state in which the C-terminus of a polymer chain is left uncapped and carries a negative charge, as a free carboxylic acid group does at the pH of most simulations. This is the usual choice when the chain being simulated is a whole protein rather than a fragment of one. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001214 ! molecular termini state

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002269
name: van der Waals cutoff distance
def: "A non-bonded interaction parameter that specifies the distance beyond which van der Waals interactions are no longer calculated. Several programs set this separately from the electrostatic cut-off so that the two can take different values. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001185 ! non-bonded interaction parameter
relationship: IAO:0000039 UO:0000001 {all_only="true"} ! has measurement unit label length unit
property_value: IAO:0000119 "AMBER 26 Reference Manual, p. 499, entry vdw_cutoff. States that es_cutoff and vdw_cutoff control the cutoffs for vdw and electrostatic direct force interactions separately, that cut must not be given as well, and that vdw_cutoff must be greater than or equal to es_cutoff." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000119 "GROMACS 2026.3 Reference Manual, p. 53, entry rvdw, which gives the distance for the LJ or Buckingham cut-off." xsd:string
property_value: MOLSIM:002254 "rvdw" xsd:string {dcterms:source="MOLSIM:000247"}
property_value: MOLSIM:002254 "vdw_cutoff" xsd:string {dcterms:source="MOLSIM:000217"}

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002270
name: review article
def: "A publication that surveys and summarises existing published work on a topic rather than reporting new primary results." []
is_a: IAO:0000311 ! publication
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0003-4846-8051

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002271
name: book chapter
def: "A publication that forms one titled part of an edited book, usually written by different authors from the other parts." []
is_a: IAO:0000311 ! publication
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0003-4846-8051

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002272
name: thesis
def: "A document presenting the research carried out for an academic degree, submitted to and examined by the awarding institution. Simulation results are often reported here before they appear in any journal." []
is_a: IAO:0000310 ! document
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0003-4846-8051

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002273
name: conference proceeding
def: "A publication that is one of the collected contributions to a scientific meeting." []
is_a: IAO:0000311 ! publication
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0003-4846-8051

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002274
name: data source descriptor
def: "An information content entity that records one property of a data source, such as how its data was produced or who may see it. These are deliberately kept apart from the data source hierarchy itself, which sorts sources only by what kind of resource they are, so that a single source can carry several descriptors at once." []
is_a: IAO:0000030 ! information content entity
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0003-4846-8051

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002275
name: data origin
def: "A data source descriptor that records how the data held by a source was produced." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002274 ! data source descriptor
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0003-4846-8051

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002276
name: experimental data origin
def: "A data origin recording that the data was obtained by measurement in a laboratory rather than by calculation." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002275 ! data origin
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0003-4846-8051

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002277
name: computational data origin
def: "A data origin recording that the data was produced by calculation or simulation rather than by laboratory measurement." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002275 ! data origin
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0003-4846-8051

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002278
name: data access
def: "A data source descriptor that records who may obtain the data held by a source." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002274 ! data source descriptor
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0003-4846-8051

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002279
name: public access
def: "A data access descriptor recording that the data may be obtained by anyone without permission or licence." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002278 ! data access
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0003-4846-8051

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002280
name: restricted access
def: "A data access descriptor recording that the data may be obtained only under some condition, such as an institutional membership, a licence, an embargo period, or a direct request to its holder." []
is_a: MOLSIM:002278 ! data access
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0003-4846-8051

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002281
name: Extended PDB ID
def: "An Extended PDB ID is the unique twelve-character code composed of a 'pdb_' header followed by 8 alphanumeric characters. Every Extended PDB ID is assigned to a experimentally determined biomolecular structure deposited in the Protein Data Bank (PDB). This identifier serves to reference and retrieve PDB data. This format is the successor of the legacy four-character PDB ID." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000447 ! identifier
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:002282
name: InChIKey code
def: "An InChIKey is a fixed-length, 27-character alphanumeric hash derived from the InChI (International Chemical Identifier) code of a chemical structure, used to uniquely and compactly identify chemical compounds in databases and web searches." []
synonym: "InChiKey code" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000447 ! identifier
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010001
name: femtosecond
def: "An SI unit of time equal to 10^-15 seconds or one quadrillionth of a second. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "fs" EXACT []
is_a: UO:1000010 ! second based unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010002
name: atmosphere
def: "A unit of pressure defined as 101,325 pascals (Pa) or 1.01325 bar, approximately equal to the average atmospheric pressure at sea level on Earth. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "atm" EXACT []
is_a: UO:0000109 ! pressure unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010003
name: angstrom per nanosecond
def: "A unit of velocity, representing one angstrom (10^-10 meters) of distance traveled per nanosecond (10^-9 seconds) of time. It is commonly used in molecular dynamics simulations and studies of atomic-scale processes. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "Å/ns|angstrom/nanosecond" EXACT []
is_a: UO:0000060 ! speed/velocity unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010004
name: kilocalorie per mole
def: "A unit of energy per amount of substance, defined as one kilocalorie of energy (1000 thermochemical gram calories) per one mole of substance. It is commonly used in chemistry and biology for thermodynamic quantities. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "kcal/mol|kilocalorie/mole" EXACT []
is_a: UO:0000111 ! energy unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010005
name: kilocalorie per mole per square angstrom
def: "A unit of energy per amount of substance per area, commonly used in molecular dynamics simulations for expressing force constants and restraint weights. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "kcal/mol/Å^2|kilocalorie/mole/angstrom^2" EXACT []
is_a: UO:0000111 ! energy unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010006
name: elementary charge
def: "A unit of electric charge defined as the charge carried by a single proton. It is a fundamental physical constant, with a value of exactly 1.602176634 × 10^-19 coulombs. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "e" EXACT []
is_a: UO:0000219 ! electric charge

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010007
name: kinematic viscosity unit
def: "A unit that measures a fluid's resistance to flow under the influence of gravity. It is the ratio of the fluid's dynamic viscosity to its density. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: UO:0000000 ! unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010008
name: square centimeter per second
def: "A centimeter-gram-second (CGS) unit of kinematic viscosity, defined as the kinematic viscosity of a fluid that passes one square centimeter in one second. It is equivalent to the unit Stokes (St). (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "cm^2/s|stokes|St" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:010007 ! kinematic viscosity unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010009
name: electric dipole moment unit
def: "A unit that measures the separation of positive and negative electrical charges within a system, indicating the system's overall polarity. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: UO:0000000 ! unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010010
name: debye
def: "A centimeter-gram-second (CGS) unit of electric dipole moment, defined as 10^-18 statcoulomb-centimeters. One Debye is approximately equal to 3.33564 × 10^-30 coulomb-meters. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "D" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:010009 ! electric dipole moment unit

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010011
name: Kabsch RMSD algorithm
def: "An algorithm that finds the rotation bringing 2 matched sets of points into the closest possible agreement, by decomposing the matrix of their cross-correlations. It gives the rotation only, so the 2 sets must already have been centred on their averages. It is the standard way structures are superposed before any difference between them is measured. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001717 ! RMSD calculation algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010012
name: STRIDE algorithm
def: "An algorithm that assigns secondary structure to each residue of a protein from its atomic coordinates. It combines hydrogen bond energies with backbone angle preferences, where the older DSSP method uses hydrogen bonds alone. The extra criterion makes its assignments agree more closely with those a crystallographer would make by eye. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001745 ! secondary structure assignment algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010013
name: Gaussian mixture model algorithm
def: "A statistical algorithm that describes a distribution as a weighted sum of several bell-shaped components, fitting the position, width and weight of each. It suits data made of several overlapping groups, where one component would fit none of them. Each component can then be treated as a conformational state. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001751 ! statistical algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010014
name: parametric distribution fitting algorithm
def: "A statistical algorithm that fits a chosen family of distributions to data by finding the parameter values that make the data most likely, or most probable given a prior. Assuming a family lets a whole distribution be summarised by 2 or 3 numbers. The assumption is also the weakness: if the data do not follow that family, the fit is confidently wrong. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001751 ! statistical algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010015
name: spline-based estimation algorithm
def: "A statistical algorithm that estimates a distribution by fitting smooth polynomial pieces joined at chosen points, rather than assuming a named family. It can follow a shape that no standard distribution matches. Its accuracy depends on how many joining points are used, which must be chosen to avoid following noise. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001751 ! statistical algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010016
name: Shrake-Rupley algorithm
def: "An algorithm that computes the surface area of a molecule reachable by solvent, by placing test points over each atom's surface and counting those not buried by neighbouring atoms. The test points approximate rolling a solvent-sized sphere over the molecule. Its accuracy depends on how many test points are used, which is the one setting it has. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001715 ! surface area calculation algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010017
name: color Tanimoto score
def: "A similarity score giving how far the chemical features of 2 aligned molecules coincide, such as hydrogen bond donors, acceptors and charged groups. It complements a shape comparison, which cannot tell a hydrogen bond donor from an acceptor of the same size. \"Color\" here refers to feature type, not to any visual property. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000075 ! Tanimoto similarity algorithm
disjoint_from: MOLSIM:010018 ! shape Tanimoto score

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010018
name: shape Tanimoto score
def: "A similarity score giving how far the volumes of 2 aligned molecules overlap, as the shared volume divided by the volume either occupies. It ranges from 0 for no overlap to 1 for identical shape. It considers only shape, so 2 chemically unlike molecules that fill the same space score highly. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000075 ! Tanimoto similarity algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010019
name: Tanimoto combo score
def: "A similarity score adding the shape score and the chemical feature score, giving a value between 0 and 2. Adding them weights shape and chemistry equally, which suits searching for a molecule that both fits a site and makes the same contacts. Reporting the 2 parts separately alongside it is usual, since the sum hides which one is high. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000075 ! Tanimoto similarity algorithm

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010020
name: molecular trajectory analysis format
def: "A molecular trajectory analysis format is a specialized file structure designed to store processed data derived from the analysis of a molecular dynamics simulation. These formats typically contain derived quantities, such as secondary structure timelines, pairwise distance matrices, or principal component vectors, rather than raw atomic coordinates. They allow for the efficient storage and rapid retrieval of complex analysis results without the need to re-process the massive original trajectory files." []
is_a: MOLSIM:001085 ! molecular data format
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-2294-5393

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010021
name: solvent analysis format
def: "A data format that stores spatial or statistical data describing how solvent molecules are distributed around a solute and what properties they carry there. Files in these formats usually hold a 3-dimensional grid of values such as local solvent density, charge distribution, or interaction energy. They are used to visualize hydration shells and to calculate thermodynamic properties of solvation. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001085 ! molecular data format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010022
name: quantum chemistry format
def: "A data format that stores the results of an electronic structure calculation, such as molecular orbitals, electron densities, basis sets or electrostatic potentials. Files in these formats are how quantum chemistry programs hand their results to visualization software and to other analysis tools. The group covers both program-specific formats and interchange formats. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001085 ! molecular data format

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010023
name: electronic laboratory notebook source
def: "A data source that holds data, observations or protocols recorded directly in a digital laboratory notebook system used by a research group. Unlike a public database or a formal publication, it contains raw internal records of day-to-day work and of the exact conditions of an experiment. Citing it says where the data came from when that data sits inside a system owned by one institution and has not yet been publicly deposited or peer reviewed." []
synonym: "electronic lab journal source" EXACT []
is_a: MOLSIM:000688 ! data source
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0003-4846-8051

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010024
name: local computing cluster system
def: "A set of networked computers housed and administered within a single institution, used as one pooled resource. It differs from a national facility in being controlled locally, so access and software are decided by the group that runs it. Most routine simulation work is done on one of these rather than on a large shared machine. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:001862 ! computing system

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010025
name: effective energy analysis
def: "A free energy analysis method that estimates the free energy of a single conformation by adding its internal potential energy to its solvation free energy. It leaves out the solute's internal entropy, on the assumption that this cancels when 2 similar states are compared. It is the reasoning that the end-point binding free energy methods rest on. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000951 ! binding energy analysis

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010026
name: protein-peptide docking analysis
def: "A computational method that predicts the structure of a complex between a protein and a short peptide. It is harder than docking a small rigid molecule, because a peptide has many rotatable bonds and usually has no fixed shape of its own until it binds. Methods for it therefore search over the peptide's conformation as well as its position. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000255 ! static molecular interaction prediction modeling

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010027
name: membrane placement analysis
def: "Membrane placement analysis is a computational method used to determine the optimal position and orientation of a protein structure within a lipid bilayer. It calculates the most energetically favorable alignment by assessing the hydrophobicity of the protein surface and matching it to the hydrophobic core and polar interfaces of the membrane. This analysis is a critical prerequisite for setting up stable membrane protein simulations and for understanding how proteins anchor themselves in the cell membrane." []
is_a: MOLSIM:000328 ! system setup modeling
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986

[Term]
id: MOLSIM:010028
name: leap analysis
def: "A validation method that checks an assembled molecular system for chemical and topological errors before a simulation is set up. It reports missing force field parameters, a non-integer net charge, and atoms placed on top of one another. It is run as the last step of system preparation, because each of those faults makes the resulting topology unusable. (UNVERIFIED)" []
is_a: MOLSIM:000328 ! system setup modeling

