[Term]
id: UO:0000012
name: kelvin
def: "A thermodynamic temperature unit which is equal to the fraction 1/273.16 of the thermodynamic temperature of the triple point of water." [BIPM:BIPM, NIST:NIST]
synonym: "K" EXACT []
is_a: UO:0000045 ! base unit
is_a: UO:1000012 ! kelvin based unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000018
name: nanometer
def: "A length unit which is equal to one thousandth of one millionth of a meter or 10^[-9] m." [NIST:NIST]
synonym: "nanometre" EXACT []
synonym: "nm" EXACT []
is_a: UO:1000008 ! meter based unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000019
name: angstrom
def: "A length unit which is equal to 10 [-10] m." [NIST:NIST]
synonym: "Å" EXACT []
is_a: UO:1000019 ! angstrom based unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000028
name: millisecond
def: "A time unit which is equal to one thousandth of a second or 10^[-3] s." [NIST:NIST]
synonym: "ms" EXACT []
is_a: UO:1000010 ! second based unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000029
name: microsecond
def: "A time unit which is equal to one millionth of a second or 10^[-6] s." [NIST:NIST]
synonym: "us" EXACT []
is_a: UO:1000010 ! second based unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000030
name: picosecond
def: "A time unit which is equal to 10^[-12] s." [NIST:NIST]
synonym: "ps" EXACT []
is_a: UO:1000010 ! second based unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000045
name: base unit
def: "A unit which is one of a particular measure to which all measures of that type can be related." [NIST:NIST]
is_a: UO:0000000 ! unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000047
name: area unit
def: "A unit which is a standard measure of the amount of a 2-dimensional flat surface." [UOC:GVG]
is_a: UO:0000000 ! unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000051
name: concentration unit
def: "A unit which represents a standard measurement of how much of a given substance there is mixed with another substance." [UOC:GVG]
is_a: UO:0000000 ! unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000052
name: mass density unit
def: "A density unit which is a standard measure of the mass of a substance in a given volume." [UOC:GVG]
synonym: "mass per unit volume" EXACT []
is_a: UO:0000182 ! density unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000060
name: speed/velocity unit
def: "A unit which is a standard measure of the rate of movement. Speed is measured in the same physical units of measurement as velocity, but does not contain the element of direction that velocity has. Speed is thus the magnitude component of velocity." [Wikipedia:Wikipedia]
is_a: UO:0000000 ! unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000061
name: unit of molarity
def: "A concentration unit which is a standard measure of the number of moles of a given substance per liter of solution." [UOC:GVG]
is_a: UO:0000051 ! concentration unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000062
name: molar
def: "A unit of concentration which expresses a concentration of 1 mole of solute per liter of solution (mol/L)." [UOC:GVG]
synonym: "M" EXACT []
is_a: UO:1000062 ! molar based unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000063
name: millimolar
def: "A unit of molarity which is equal to one thousandth of a molar or 10^[-3] M." [UOC:GVG]
synonym: "mM" EXACT []
is_a: UO:1000062 ! molar based unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000094
name: meter per second
def: "A speed/velocity unit which is equal to the speed of an object traveling 1 meter distance in one second." [NIST:NIST]
synonym: "m/s" EXACT []
synonym: "metre per second" EXACT []
is_a: UO:1000094 ! meter per second based unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000095
name: volume unit
def: "A unit which is a standard measure of the amount of space occupied by any substance, whether solid, liquid, or gas." [NIST:NIST]
is_a: UO:0000000 ! unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000105
name: frequency unit
def: "A unit which is a standard measure of the number of repetitive actions in a particular time." [NIST:NIST]
is_a: UO:0000000 ! unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000106
name: hertz
def: "A frequency unit which is equal to 1 complete cycle of a recurring phenomenon in 1 second." [NIST:NIST]
synonym: "Hz" EXACT []
synonym: "s^1" EXACT []
is_a: UO:1000106 ! hertz based unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000107
name: force unit
def: "A unit which is a standard measure of the force is applied when a mass is accelerated." [NIST:NIST]
is_a: UO:0000000 ! unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000109
name: pressure unit
def: "A unit which is a standard measure of the force applied to a given area." [NIST:NIST]
is_a: UO:0000000 ! unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000111
name: energy unit
def: "A unit which is a standard measure of the work done by a certain force (gravitational, electric, magnetic, force of inertia, etc)." [NIST:NIST]
is_a: UO:0000000 ! unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000121
name: angle unit
def: "A unit which is a standard measure of the figure or space formed by the junction of two lines or planes." [Wikipedia:Wikipedia]
is_a: UO:0000000 ! unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000122
name: plane angle unit
def: "A unit which is a standard measure of the angle formed by two straight lines in the same plane." [Wikipedia:Wikipedia]
is_a: UO:0000121 ! angle unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000123
name: radian
def: "A plane angle unit which is equal to the angle subtended at the center of a circle by an arc equal in length to the radius of the circle, approximately 57 degrees 17 minutes and 44.6 seconds." [NIST:NIST]
synonym: "rad" EXACT []
is_a: UO:1000123 ! radian based unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000150
name: nanosecond
def: "A time unit which is equal to one thousandth of one millionth of a second or 10^[-9] s." [NIST:NIST]
synonym: "ns" EXACT []
is_a: UO:1000010 ! second based unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000182
name: density unit
def: "A unit which is a standard measure of the influence exerted by some mass." [Wikipedia:Wikipedia]
is_a: UO:0000000 ! unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000185
name: degree
def: "A plane angle unit which is equal to 1/360 of a full rotation or 1.7453310^[-2] rad." [Wikipedia:Wikipedia]
is_a: UO:1000185 ! degree based unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000186
name: dimensionless unit
def: "A unit which is a standard measure of physical quantity consisting of only a numerical number without any units." [Wikipedia:Wikipedia]
is_a: UO:0000000 ! unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000189
name: count unit
def: "A dimensionless unit which denotes a simple count of things." [MGED:MGED]
synonym: "count" EXACT []
is_a: UO:0000186 ! dimensionless unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000219
name: electric charge
def: "A unit which is a standard measure of the quantity of unbalanced electricity in a body (either positive or negative) and construed as an excess or deficiency of electrons." [WordNet:WordNet]
is_a: UO:0000000 ! unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000221
name: dalton
def: "An independently to the base SI units defined mass unit which is equal to one twelfth of the mass of an unbound atom of the carbon-12 nuclide, at rest and in its ground state." [Wikipedia:Wikipedia]
synonym: "amu" EXACT []
synonym: "Da" EXACT []
synonym: "u" EXACT []
synonym: "unified atomic mass unit" EXACT []
is_a: UO:1000221 ! dalton based unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000267
name: electric field strength unit
def: "The electric field strength is a unit which is a measure of the potential difference between two points some distance apart." [Wikipedia:Electric_field]
synonym: "E-field strength" EXACT []
is_a: UO:0000000 ! unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000268
name: volt per meter
def: "The volt per meter is a unit of electric field strength equal to the a potential difference of 1 volt existing between two points that are 1 meter apart." [Wikipedia:Electric_field]
synonym: "V/m" EXACT []
synonym: "volt per metre" EXACT []
is_a: UO:1000268 ! volt per meter based unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000280
name: rate unit
def: "A unit which represents a standard measurement occurrence of a process per unit time." [UOC:GVG]
is_a: UO:0000000 ! unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000324
name: square angstrom
def: "An area unit which is equal to an area enclosed by a square with sides each 1 angstrom long." [UOC:GVG]
synonym: "A^[2]" RELATED []
is_a: UO:0000047 ! area unit

[Term]
id: UO:0000325
name: megaHertz
def: "A frequency unit which is equal to one million hertz or 10^[6] V." [UOC:GVG]
synonym: "megahertz" RELATED []
synonym: "mH" RELATED []
is_a: UO:0000105 ! frequency unit

[Term]
id: UO:0010069
name: bar
def: "A pressure unit which is equal to 100,000 pascal or the pressure or stress on a surface caused by a force of 100,000 newtons spread over a surface of 1 m^[2]." [NIST:NIST]
is_a: UO:1000110 ! pascal based unit

[Term]
id: UO:1000008
name: meter based unit
is_a: UO:0000001 ! length unit

[Term]
id: UO:1000010
name: second based unit
is_a: UO:0000003 ! time unit

[Term]
id: UO:1000012
name: kelvin based unit
is_a: UO:0000005 ! temperature unit

[Term]
id: UO:1000019
name: angstrom based unit
is_a: UO:0000001 ! length unit

[Term]
id: UO:1000062
name: molar based unit
is_a: UO:0000061 ! unit of molarity

[Term]
id: UO:1000094
name: meter per second based unit
is_a: UO:0000060 ! speed/velocity unit

[Term]
id: UO:1000106
name: hertz based unit
is_a: UO:0000105 ! frequency unit

[Term]
id: UO:1000110
name: pascal based unit
is_a: UO:0000109 ! pressure unit

[Term]
id: UO:1000123
name: radian based unit
is_a: UO:0000122 ! plane angle unit

[Term]
id: UO:1000185
name: degree based unit
is_a: UO:0000122 ! plane angle unit

[Term]
id: UO:1000221
name: dalton based unit
is_a: UO:0000002 ! mass unit

[Term]
id: UO:1000268
name: volt per meter based unit
is_a: UO:0000267 ! electric field strength unit

[Typedef]
id: BFO:0000051
name: has part
def: "a core relation that holds between a whole and its part" []
property_value: IAO:0000116 "Everything has itself as a part. Any part of any part of a thing is itself part of that thing. Two distinct things cannot have each other as a part." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000116 "Occurrents are not subject to change and so parthood between occurrents holds for all the times that the part exists. Many continuants are subject to change, so parthood between continuants will only hold at certain times, but this is difficult to specify in OWL. See http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ro/docs/temporal-semantics/" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000116 "Parthood requires the part and the whole to have compatible classes: only an occurrent have an occurrent as part; only a process can have a process as part; only a continuant can have a continuant as part; only an independent continuant can have an independent continuant as part; only a specifically dependent continuant can have a specifically dependent continuant as part; only a generically dependent continuant can have a generically dependent continuant as part. (This list is not exhaustive.)\n\nA continuant cannot have an occurrent as part: use 'participates in'. An occurrent cannot have a continuant as part: use 'has participant'. An immaterial entity cannot have a material entity as part: use 'location of'. An independent continuant cannot have a specifically dependent continuant as part: use 'bearer of'. A specifically dependent continuant cannot have an independent continuant as part: use 'inheres in'." xsd:string
is_transitive: true

[Typedef]
id: BFO:0000063
name: precedes
def: "x precedes y if and only if the time point at which x ends is before or equivalent to the time point at which y starts. Formally: x precedes y iff ω(x) <= α(y), where α is a function that maps a process to a start point, and ω is a function that maps a process to an end point." []
is_transitive: true

[Typedef]
id: IAO:0000039
name: has measurement unit label
is_functional: true

[Typedef]
id: IAO:0000136
name: is about
def: "A (currently) primitive relation that relates an information artifact to an entity." []
property_value: IAO:0000112 "This document is about information artifacts and their representations" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000114 IAO:0000125
property_value: IAO:0000116 "7/6/2009 Alan Ruttenberg. Following discussion with Jonathan Rees, and introduction of \"mentions\" relation. Weaken the is_about relationship to be primitive. \n\nWe will try to build it back up by elaborating the various subproperties that are more precisely defined.\n\nSome currently missing phenomena that should be considered \"about\" are predications - \"The only person who knows the answer is sitting beside me\" , Allegory, Satire, and other literary forms that can be topical without explicitly mentioning the topic." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000117 "person:Alan Ruttenberg" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000119 "Smith, Ceusters, Ruttenberg, 2000 years of philosophy" xsd:string
domain: IAO:0000030 ! information content entity

[Typedef]
id: MOLSIM:000297
name: has periodic box type
def: "A relation that links a molecular simulation system to the geometric shape of the simulation cell used to apply periodic boundary conditions. Those conditions mimic an infinite system by making a particle that leaves one side re-enter from the opposite side. Common shapes are cubic, triclinic and rhombic dodecahedron, and the choice affects both computational cost and how isotropic the system is. (UNVERIFIED)" []
domain: MOLSIM:001887 ! molecular simulation system
range: MOLSIM:000032 ! box type

[Typedef]
id: MOLSIM:000504
name: has molecular dynamics suite utility
def: "A relation that links a computational process or analysis step to the utility program from a molecular dynamics software suite that was used to perform it. For example, a trajectory analysis may use a particular trajectory processing utility, or system preparation a particular solvation tool. It records the exact tool used within a larger workflow, where that tool is one component of a bigger software package. (UNVERIFIED)" []
domain: MOLSIM:000000 ! molecular dynamics process
range: MOLSIM:000001 ! software

[Typedef]
id: MOLSIM:000507
name: has alignment tool
def: "A relation that links a structural alignment procedure or analysis step to the software program used to perform the alignment. Structural alignment superimposes molecular structures such as proteins or nucleic acids, so that their conformations can be compared or conserved regions found. (UNVERIFIED)" []
domain: MOLSIM:000004 ! simulation analysis
range: MOLSIM:000001 ! software

[Typedef]
id: MOLSIM:000508
name: has protein structure source
def: "A relation that links a molecular structure to the origin from which its three-dimensional coordinates were obtained. The origin may be an entry in an experimental database such as the Protein Data Bank, the output of a computational prediction method such as homology modelling, or another defined source. Recording it lets a reader trace where a structure came from and judge its quality. (UNVERIFIED)" []
domain: MOLSIM:000904 ! molecular structure
range: MOLSIM:000688 ! data source

[Typedef]
id: MOLSIM:001033
name: has simulation environment
def: "A relation that links a molecular simulation system to the overall physical context or medium it represents, such as an aqueous solution, a lipid bilayer, a vacuum or a crystal lattice. That context shapes the choice of simulation parameters, including boundary conditions and dielectric treatment, and how the results should be read." []
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986
domain: MOLSIM:001887 ! molecular simulation system
range: MOLSIM:002067 ! simulation environment

[Typedef]
id: MOLSIM:001034
name: has template complex structure
def: "A relation that links a molecular simulation system to the initial three-dimensional structural model of the molecular complex used as its starting point. That structure is often taken from experimental data such as a PDB entry, or from earlier computational modelling such as a docking pose. (UNVERIFIED)" []
domain: MOLSIM:001887 ! molecular simulation system
range: MOLSIM:000904 ! molecular structure

[Typedef]
id: MOLSIM:001035
name: has validated ligand selection criteria
def: "A relation that links a plan specification to the rules, checks or conditions applied to confirm that the chosen ligands, and the alchemical transformations between them, are suitable for a relative binding free energy calculation. Those checks may cover structural similarity, consistency of charge and protonation state, or avoiding transformations that inappropriately break or form covalent bonds. (UNVERIFIED)" []
domain: IAO:0000104 ! plan specification
range: MOLSIM:000143 ! ligand pairs selection criteria

[Typedef]
id: MOLSIM:001036
name: has reaction coordinate
def: "A relation that links an enhanced sampling process to the geometric or collective variable along which the system is steered or biased, for example in steered molecular dynamics or umbrella sampling. Examples are the distance between two groups of atoms, an angle, a dihedral angle, or a more complex function of atomic coordinates." []
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0009-0007-1391-4986
domain: MOLSIM:000845 ! enhanced sampling
range: MOLSIM:001994 ! reaction coordinate

[Typedef]
id: MOLSIM:002167
name: has simulation stage
def: "A relation that links a molecular dynamics process to one of the discrete stages that make it up. The stages belong to the run rather than to the protocol, because one protocol may be followed by many runs. (UNVERIFIED)" []
domain: MOLSIM:000000 ! molecular dynamics process
range: MOLSIM:002156 ! simulation stage

[Typedef]
id: MOLSIM:002168
name: has parameter schedule
def: "A relation that links a molecular dynamics process to a schedule defining how one of its parameters varies over simulated time or integration steps. A parameter that changes during a run, such as a temperature being raised or a restraint being released, is not described by a single value. Without the schedule the record of the run would say only where it started. (UNVERIFIED)" []
domain: MOLSIM:000000 ! molecular dynamics process
range: MOLSIM:002157 ! simulation parameter schedule
is_a: MOLSIM:002202 ! has simulation parameter

[Typedef]
id: MOLSIM:002169
name: has continuity check
def: "A relation that links a simulation stage to a continuity check assessing its temporal join with an adjacent stage. A long simulation is usually run as a chain of shorter stages, and a gap or an overlap between 2 of them makes the combined trajectory wrong. The check is what establishes that the stages really do join end to end. (UNVERIFIED)" []
domain: MOLSIM:002156 ! simulation stage
range: MOLSIM:002158 ! simulation continuity check

[Typedef]
id: MOLSIM:002170
name: has parsing error
def: "A relation that links a simulation stage to an error encountered while loading or parsing one of its data files. Recording the error keeps a failed or partial read visible instead of silently producing incomplete metadata. A record with an error attached should not be treated as equivalent to one without. (UNVERIFIED)" []
domain: MOLSIM:002156 ! simulation stage
range: MOLSIM:002160 ! file parsing error

[Typedef]
id: MOLSIM:002171
name: has system classification
def: "A relation that links a molecular simulation system to a high-level classification label describing its composition. It lets systems be grouped and searched by what they contain rather than by their file names. The labels are coarse on purpose, so that a whole collection can be sorted without reading each entry. (UNVERIFIED)" []
domain: MOLSIM:001887 ! molecular simulation system
range: MOLSIM:002162 ! system classification label

[Typedef]
id: MOLSIM:002172
name: has format convention
def: "A relation that links a data format to the specific convention or schema variant that a file follows. One named format often covers several incompatible layouts, so naming the format alone does not say how to read a file. The convention is what a reader has to match. (UNVERIFIED)" []
domain: MOLSIM:000436 ! data format
range: MOLSIM:002161 ! file format convention

[Typedef]
id: MOLSIM:002173
name: has restraint mask
def: "A relation that links a molecular dynamics process to the atom selection mask defining which atoms are subject to restraints. The mask is what turns \"restrain the protein\" into a definite set of atoms. A mask that selects the wrong atoms produces a simulation that runs normally and means something else. (UNVERIFIED)" []
domain: MOLSIM:000000 ! molecular dynamics process
range: MOLSIM:002163 ! atom selection mask

[Typedef]
id: MOLSIM:002202
name: has simulation parameter
def: "A relation that links a molecular dynamics process to a simulation parameter that governs how it is carried out, such as the integration timestep, the non-bonded cutoff, or an output write interval. These settings are part of what a result means, not incidental detail. A simulation cannot be repeated or judged without them. (UNVERIFIED)" []
domain: MOLSIM:000000 ! molecular dynamics process
range: MOLSIM:001164 ! simulation parameter

[Typedef]
id: MOLSIM:002250
name: follows protocol
def: "A relation that links a molecular dynamics process to the simulation protocol it was carried out according to. The protocol is the reusable plan and the process is one execution of it, so a single protocol may be followed by many runs. (UNVERIFIED)" []
domain: MOLSIM:000000 ! molecular dynamics process
range: MOLSIM:002155 ! simulation protocol

[Typedef]
id: MOLSIM:002258
name: has water model
def: "A relation that links a molecular simulation system to the water model used to represent its solvent, such as TIP3P or SPC/E. The choice fixes the geometry and the charges of every water molecule, and it affects properties that depend on the solvent, including diffusion and the strength of hydrogen bonds. (UNVERIFIED)" []
domain: MOLSIM:001887 ! molecular simulation system
range: MOLSIM:000014 ! water model force field

[Typedef]
id: MOLSIM:002260
name: has termini state
def: "A relation that links a molecular simulation system to the chemical state chosen for the ends of its polymer chains, whether each end was closed off with a capping group or left uncapped and carrying a charge. The choice changes the total charge of the system, and it matters most for short peptides, where the two ends are a large part of the whole molecule. (UNVERIFIED)" []
synonym: "has capping group" EXACT []
domain: MOLSIM:001887 ! molecular simulation system
range: MOLSIM:001214 ! molecular termini state

[Typedef]
id: OBI:0000293
name: has specified input
def: "The inverse property of is specified input of" []
property_value: IAO:0000111 "has specified input" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000112 "see is_input_of example_of_usage" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000114 IAO:0000122
property_value: IAO:0000116 "8/17/09: specified inputs of one process are not necessarily specified inputs of a larger process that it is part of. This is in contrast to how 'has participant' works." xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000117 "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000117 "PERSON: Bjoern Peters" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000117 "PERSON: Larry Hunter" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000117 "PERSON: Melanie Coutot" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000412 http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/obi.owl
is_a: RO:0002233 ! has input
inverse_of: OBI:0000295 ! is specified input of

[Typedef]
id: OBI:0000295
name: is specified input of

[Typedef]
id: OBI:0000299
name: has specified output
def: "The inverse property of is specified output of" []
property_value: IAO:0000111 "has specified output" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000114 IAO:0000122
property_value: IAO:0000117 "PERSON: Alan Ruttenberg" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000117 "PERSON: Bjoern Peters" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000117 "PERSON: Larry Hunter" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000117 "PERSON: Melanie Courtot" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000412 http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/obi.owl
is_a: RO:0002234 ! has output
inverse_of: OBI:0000312 ! is specified output of

[Typedef]
id: OBI:0000312
name: is specified output of
def: "A relation between a completely executed planned process and a continuant participating in that process. The presence of the continuant at the end of the process is explicitly specified in the objective specification which the process realizes the concretization of." []
property_value: IAO:0000111 "is specified output of" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000114 IAO:0000122
property_value: IAO:0000117 "Alan Ruttenberg" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000117 "PERSON:Bjoern Peters" xsd:string
property_value: IAO:0000412 http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/obi.owl

[Typedef]
id: RO:0000056
name: participates in
def: "a relation between a continuant and a process, in which the continuant is somehow involved in the process" []

[Typedef]
id: RO:0000058
name: is concretized as
def: "A relationship between a generically dependent continuant and a specifically dependent continuant or process, in which the generically dependent continuant depends on some independent continuant or process in virtue of the fact that the specifically dependent continuant or process also depends on that same independent continuant. A generically dependent continuant may be concretized as multiple specifically dependent continuants or processes." []

[Typedef]
id: RO:0000086
name: has quality
def: "a relation between an independent continuant (the bearer) and a quality, in which the quality specifically depends on the bearer for its existence" []
property_value: IAO:0000116 "A bearer can have many qualities, and its qualities can exist for different periods of time, but none of its qualities can exist when the bearer does not exist." xsd:string

[Typedef]
id: RO:0002233
name: has input
def: "p has input c iff: p is a process, c is a material entity, c is a participant in p, c is present at the start of p, and the state of c is modified during p." []
comment: http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002233
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-6601-2165

[Typedef]
id: RO:0002234
name: has output
def: "p has output c iff c is a participant in p, c is present at the end of p, and c is not present in the same state at the beginning of p." []
property_value: IAO:0000117 orcid:0000-0002-6601-2165

